E["item:admiral-proudmoore-s-orders"] = {t="item",n="Admiral Proudmoore's Orders",z="durotar",s="Kul Tiras forces still hold the coast in Durotar, guided by Admiral Proudmoore's Orders. Written before Daelin Proudmoore fell at Theramore, the papers describe a campaign against the Horde.",h="Kul Tiras forces still hold the coast in Durotar, guided by Admiral Proudmoore's Orders.",sec={{t="A Legacy of Hatred",b="At Tiragarde Keep, Kul Tiras forces still mean to fight. Lieutenant Benedict's garrison holds papers detailing long-term maneuvers and fortifications against the Horde. Daelin Proudmoore's offensive in Durotar was an organized campaign, planned to continue after his death. For the Horde, these papers reveal Kul Tiras operations and possible reinforcements along its borders.",sp=0},{t="Delivery to Grommash Hold",b="Horde scouts carry the recovered orders to Grommash Hold in Orgrimmar. They bring them to Nazgrel in Thrall's chamber. The plans support Nazgrel's warning that humans cannot be trusted and remain an active danger. Horde leaders now have reason to prepare for more attacks along the coast.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What are Admiral Proudmoore's Orders?",a="Admiral Proudmoore's Orders are military directives Daelin Proudmoore drew up before he fell at Theramore. They direct the remaining Kul Tiras soldiers in Durotar to fortify coastal positions and wage war against the Horde.",al={"proudmoores orders","what are the orders","admirals orders item"},it="identity"},{q="Where were these orders recovered?",a="The orders were recovered at Tiragarde Keep in Durotar, during the struggle against Kul Tiras forces near the southeastern coast.",al={"where do i find the orders","orders location","who drops the orders"},it="origin"},{q="Who needs to see these orders?",a="Nazgrel needs to see the orders. He counsels Warchief Thrall inside Grommash Hold in Orgrimmar's Valley of Wisdom.",al={"who do i turn this into","who wants the orders","orders hand in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are Kul Tiras soldiers still fighting in Durotar?",a="Kul Tiras soldiers remain in Durotar because Lieutenant Benedict and others stayed devoted to Admiral Proudmoore's mission to exterminate the orcs. His orders gave the garrison plans to keep harassing Durotar without his direct oversight.",al={"why are humans in durotar","why tiragarde keep hostile","daelin dead why fight"},it="history"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, these papers support those who argued that human truces would not last. They show Kul Tiras forces intended a war of extermination from the moment they landed.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, these orders show that the human presence along the coast where your people make their home remains an immediate danger."},kw={"benedict","durotar","kul tiras","nazgrel","orders","orgrimmar","proudmoore","tiragarde"},rel={"quest:830","zone:durotar","subzone:grommash-hold","zone:orgrimmar","npc:thrall","topic:horde","topic:human"},src={"Admiral Proudmoore's Orders","The Admiral's Orders (2)"}}
E["item:burning-blade-medallion"] = {t="item",n="Burning Blade Medallion",z="durotar",s="In Durotar, the Burning Blade Medallion threatens the Horde's young warriors. Cultists carry it in the Valley of Trials, and Yarrog Baneshadow holds it deep in the Burning Blade Coven.",h="In Durotar, the Burning Blade Medallion threatens the Horde's young warriors.",sec={{t="A Mark of Corruption",b="Zureetha Fargaze's divinations lead to the medallion in the Burning Blade Coven. Yarrog Baneshadow serves the Burning Blade cult and carries it deep in the winding caverns. The trinket channels dark power among the cult's impish familiars and felstalkers. Defeating Yarrog and taking the medallion ends the cult's attempt to undermine the Horde's training grounds from within Durotar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Burning Blade Medallion?",a="Yarrog Baneshadow, an operative of the Burning Blade cult hiding in Durotar, carries the magical talisman. It focuses dark magic and marks the bearer's allegiance to the cult.",al={"burning blade talisman","coven medallion","yarrog's medallion"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants the medallion retrieved?",a="Zureetha Fargaze, an orc seer outside the Den in the Valley of Trials, wants the medallion retrieved. She hopes to root out demonic influence and study the cult's local plans.",al={"who takes the medallion","where do i turn in the medallion","zureetha fargaze quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the medallion found?",a="Yarrog Baneshadow holds the medallion deep inside the Burning Blade Coven, a hidden cave northwest of the Den in the Valley of Trials. He lurks along the cave's upper ledges.",al={"where is yarrog baneshadow","burning blade medallion location","how to find the medallion"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does the medallion's presence mean for Durotar?",a="The medallion confirms that the Burning Blade cult has placed operatives in the Horde's proving grounds. Its presence signals the cultists' broader, more dangerous ambitions across the orcish homeland.",al={"why are cultists in valley of trials","is burning blade in durotar"},it="threat"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, the medallion recalls the demonic corruption that once enslaved your race. That shadow now threatens young initiates before they leave the Valley of Trials.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock of the Horde, you practice dark magic under strict discipline. The medallion marks the Burning Blade's rogue, unbound fel craft, which threatens Durotar's stability."},kw={"burning blade coven","burning blade medallion","durotar","felstalker","talisman","valley of trials","yarrog baneshadow","zureetha fargaze"},rel={"npc:zureetha-fargaze","quest:794","subzone:burning-blade-coven","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:the-den","quest:792","zone:durotar"},src={"Burning Blade Medallion","Burning Blade Medallion (Classic)"}}
E["item:cactus-apple"] = {t="item",n="Cactus Apple",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Cactus Apples give orcs a rare source of moisture in Durotar’s dry heat.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Cactus Apples give orcs a rare source of moisture in Durotar’s dry heat.",sec={{t="Desert Harvest",b="Across the Valley of Trials, cactus apples grow in clusters around thick cactuses. Gathering them means working among the thorns, but the fruit eases the thirst of Durotar’s heat. Galgar, an orc in the valley, gathers the apples for Cactus Apple Surprise. Recruits enduring their early training can cool themselves with his treat.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do cactus apples grow?",a="Cactus apples grow wild in the Valley of Trials in southern Durotar. They cluster near the bases of stout cactus plants scattered across the basin.",al={"cactus apple locations","where to find cactus apple","cactus apple spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Cactus Apple Surprise?",a="Cactus Apple Surprise is a chilled dish Galgar prepares with freshly gathered cactus apples. The treat offers relief from Durotar’s desert heat.",al={"what is galgars surprise","cactus apple recipe","galgar treat"},it="purpose"},{q="Who asks for these apples?",a="Galgar, an orc in the Valley of Trials, asks young recruits to bring back six fresh apples. In return, he gives them portions of his cooling dessert.",al={"cactus apple quest giver","who wants cactus apples","galgar apples"},it="motive",gp=true},{q="What is a Cactus Apple?",a="A Cactus Apple is a crisp, refreshing wild fruit found flourishing beneath the thorny cactuses of the Valley of Trials in Durotar. Despite the harsh, arid conditions of the orcish homeland, these resilient plants produce succulent fruit that offers much-needed hydration and nourishment under the scorching desert sun.",al={"what is cactus apple","cactus apple lore","what are cactus apples"},it="identity",add="93b3f975"},{q="Where do Cactus Apples come from?",a="Cactus Apples are native desert fruits that grow naturally at the base of cacti scattered across Durotar's Valley of Trials. They are not crafted or cultivated by any single person, but rather sprout directly from the resilient flora adapted to the red canyons and dry climate of the region.",al={"where do cactus apples come from","cactus apple origin","who made cactus apples"},it="origin",add="e52e1b37"},{q="Why does Galgar want Cactus Apples?",a="Galgar gathers them to whip up batches of his famous Cactus Apple Surprise. The sweltering heat of the Valley of Trials takes a heavy toll on new recruits and seasoned warriors alike, and the sweet, cooling dessert made from these apples offers vital refreshment against the brutal midday sun.",al={"why gather cactus apples","why does galgar want cactus apples","cactus apple purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="0fea9150"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a wilderness cook in Durotar, you can make a hydrating meal from desert cactuses.",["race:Orc"]="As a young orc in Durotar, you learn to make use of every scarce bit of moisture the red canyon offers."},kw={"cactus apple","cactus apple surprise","desert fruit","durotar","galgar","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:galgar-s-cactus-apple-surprise","npc:galgar","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar"},src={"Cactus Apple","Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise"}}
E["item:canvas-scraps"] = {t="item",n="Canvas Scraps",z="durotar",s="At Razor Hill, Canvas Scraps go to Furl Scornbrow for travel sacks for new Horde recruits. The cloth comes from human invaders and centaur tribes in Durotar.",h="At Razor Hill, Canvas Scraps go to Furl Scornbrow for travel sacks for new Horde recruits.",sec={{t="Trophies of Durotar's Enemies",b="Kul Tiras marines and sailors carry canvas along Durotar’s eastern shore. Their gear and sails leave scraps behind. Inland, Kolkar centaur reuse coarse cloth taken from supply caravans and past conflicts. Their camps and gear hold scraps for salvage.",sp=0},{t="A Veteran's Craft",b="Furl Scornbrow watches for invaders from the Razor Hill watchtower. The aging veteran has left his fighting days behind, but puts cloth taken from enemies to use. He stitches it into sturdy carrying bags for younger soldiers. The bags help the new generation defend the Horde’s borders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do Canvas Scraps come from?",a="Canvas Scraps come from human and centaur foes across Durotar. Kul Tiras forces at Tiragarde Keep and along the eastern shore carry them, as do Kolkar centaur drudges and outrunners near their inland camps.",al={"who drops canvas scraps","where to get canvas scraps","canvas scraps farm"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Furl Scornbrow want these scraps?",a="Furl Scornbrow is an aging Orc veteran in the Razor Hill watchtower who can no longer fight on the front lines. He sews salvaged cloth into traveling sacks for young adventurers.",al={"who needs canvas scraps","what are canvas scraps used for","furl scornbrow canvas"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why do the Kul Tiras troops and centaur carry canvas?",a="Kul Tiras troops came to Durotar aboard warships and keep seaside camps, where sailcloth and woven canvas are everyday essentials. Kolkar centaur get coarse fabrics by raiding caravans, scavenging coastlines, and plundering travelers across the arid plains.",al={"why do centaur have canvas","human canvas scraps lore"}},{q="What are Canvas Scraps?",a="Canvas Scraps are pieces of heavy, woven fabric salvaged from the camps and gear of enemies across Durotar. Tougher than simple linen, canvas is widely used for heavy-duty military equipment, sails, and rugged tents. While scraps like these might look like mere refuse on the battlefield, their durable fibers can easily be repurposed by a skilled tailor or craftsman into practical supplies, such as sturdy carrying bags for warriors on the march.",al={"what are canvas scraps","canvas scrap item","what is canvas scraps"},it="identity",add="6d5b894e"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Each scrap taken from Kul Tiras invaders or Kolkar raiders helps supply new defenders answering Thrall’s call across Durotar.",["profession:Tailoring"]="Warriors gather woven canvas as raw salvage, and the rugged cloth can be made into practical bags for the harsh desert."},kw={"canvas scraps","carry your weight","durotar","furl scornbrow","kolkar","kul tiras","razor hill"},rel={"quest:791","npc:furl-scornbrow","subzone:razor-hill-watchtower","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:kul-tiras","topic:centaur","topic:horde"},src={"Canvas Scraps","Carry Your Weight"}}
E["item:durotar-tiger-fur"] = {t="item",n="Durotar Tiger Fur",z="durotar",s="Across the Echo Isles off Durotar's southeastern coast, Durotar Tiger Fur helps the growing Darkspear settlement endure. The trolls make blankets, tents, and armor from the pelts.",h="Across the Echo Isles off Durotar's southeastern coast, Durotar Tiger Fur helps the growing Darkspear...",sec={{t="A Vital Resource for the Darkspear",b="In Sen'jin Village, the Darkspear must make scarce supplies last. So they let local tigers thrive until their needs call for a cull. Trolls cure the thick hides into goods their settlement needs, including armor and warm blankets for changing seasonal weather.",sp=0},{t="Hunting the Echo Isles",b="The Echo Isles lie south of Durotar, across open water. The Darkspear once called the islands home, until the witch doctor Zalazane drove them out. Hunters face danger from Zalazane's thralls and from tigers among the thick foliage. Experienced hunters such as Vel'rin Fang speak of spending entire days motionless in the jungle brush to secure a single clean kill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are Durotar tiger furs obtained?",a="Hunters collect Durotar tiger fur from tigers across the Echo Isles, off Durotar's southeastern coast.",al={"where do tiger furs drop","durotar tiger fur location","how to get tiger furs"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the trolls of Sen'jin Village need these furs?",a="Vel'rin Fang gathers fur for the growing Darkspear settlement. The trolls use it to make blankets, tents, and protective leather armor against seasonal weather.",al={"why collect tiger pelts","who needs tiger fur","practical prey purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why don't the trolls overhunt the tigers?",a="The Darkspear let the tiger population thrive and cull only when their growing community's needs strain supplies of shelter and clothing.",al={"tiger conservation","cull the flock"}},{q="What is Durotar Tiger Fur?",a="Durotar Tiger Fur is the pelt harvested from the wild tigers prowling the Echo Isles off the southeastern coast of Durotar. Tough, warm, and resilient, these hides are an essential raw material for the Darkspear trolls of Sen'jin Village, who work them into everyday necessities to shelter their people from the harsh elements.",al={"what is durotar tiger fur","tiger fur durotar","what is this fur"},it="identity",add="e997b985"},{q="Where does Durotar Tiger Fur come from?",a="These furs are skinned directly from the Durotar tigers that stalk the dense underbrush of the Echo Isles. They are not crafted by artisans, but hunted in the wild by stalkers and scouts braving the waters south of Sen'jin Village.",al={"origin of durotar tiger fur","where do tiger furs come from","who makes durotar tiger fur"},it="origin",add="c85f7978"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For the Darkspear, tiger hides mean survival in Sen'jin Village. They also recall the painful loss of their homeland on the Echo Isles.",["class:Hunter"]="As a Hunter, stalking tigers in the Echo Isles calls for patience and camouflage. The hunt echoes classic troll hunting rites as you ambush the stealthy island predators."},kw={"durotar tiger","durotar tiger fur","echo isles","practical prey","sen'jin village","troll pelt","vel'rin fang"},rel={"quest:817","subzone:echo-isles","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","quest:808","subzone:razor-hill"},src={"Durotar Tiger Fur","Practical Prey"}}
E["item:encrypted-parchment"] = {t="item",n="Encrypted Parchment",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Encrypted Parchment calls promising young orc rogues to the Den. Gornek gives it to recruits after their first trials, and its cipher points to Rwag, the hidden trainer.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Encrypted Parchment calls promising young orc rogues to the Den.",sec={{t="A Summons from the Shadows",b="In the Valley of Trials, young orcs prove their strength beneath the open sun. Those gifted in stealth, deception, and bladecraft draw a different notice. After facing the local wildlife, promising orc rogues receive Encrypted Parchment from Gornek. Its coded words call to those who can read a message meant to stay hidden.",sp=0},{t="Ties to the Shattered Hand",b="The cipher guides a novice through the Den, past the other clan trainers, to Rwag. There, the recruit learns that the Shattered Hand arranged the summons. The order works within the Horde's covert network. Answering its call begins a rogue's training in espionage and shadowcraft.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Encrypted Parchment?",a="Encrypted Parchment is a coded summons that guides novice orc rogues to their trainer, Rwag, inside the Den in the Valley of Trials.",al={"what is encrypted parchment","parchment purpose","why encrypted parchment"},it="purpose"},{q="Who sends the parchment to you?",a="Gornek hands you the parchment after your first trials in the valley. Its message comes from Rwag, the rogue trainer.",al={"who wrote the parchment","parchment sender","who gave me parchment"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the message written in cipher?",a="Rwag and his contacts in the Shattered Hand favor secrecy. The cipher guides recruits suited to the subtle path of a rogue into their hidden ranks.",al={"why is it encrypted","why encrypted","secret message"},it="motive"},{q="What organization is behind the summons?",a="Rwag reveals that the Shattered Hand asked him to watch for capable recruits. The order trains rogues in stealth and espionage to serve the Horde from the shadows.",al={"who wants to train me","shattered hand rogue","what faction sent this"},it="ties"},{q="Can troll rogues use this parchment?",a="No. Troll rogues also begin in the Valley of Trials, but they receive an Encrypted Tablet instead.",al={"troll encrypted parchment","is it for trolls too"},gp=true},{q="What is the Encrypted Parchment?",a="The Encrypted Parchment is a coded letter delivered to promising young orc rogues who prove their mettle in the Valley of Trials. Written using thieves' cant or cipher to avoid prying eyes, it directs you to seek out your trainer, Rwag, concealed within the shadows of the Den.",al={"what is encrypted parchment","encrypted parchment item","what is this parchment"},it="identity",rc="Orc",add="268fdb07"},{q="Why is the Encrypted Parchment given to you?",a="The parchment is delivered to you because you have caught the attention of the Shattered Hand, the guild of assassins and scouts serving the Horde. They wish to bring you into their fold, instruct you in your lethal craft, and ensure you know where to find their covert operative, Rwag.",al={"why do i need encrypted parchment","why encrypted parchment","purpose of encrypted parchment"},it="why_wanted",rc="Orc",add="fa1aab52"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you receive a summons to train in the Horde's covert arts with mentors tied to the Shattered Hand.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you may favor open, honorable combat, but this missive welcomes those whose talents lie in the quieter, deadlier arts of survival."},kw={"durotar","encrypted parchment","gornek","orc rogue","rwag","shattered hand","the den","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:3088","npc:rwag","npc:gornek","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:the-den","quest:1858","quest:cutting-teeth","quest:3083"},src={"Encrypted Parchment","Encrypted Parchment (quest)"}}
E["item:encrypted-tablet"] = {t="item",n="Encrypted Tablet",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, a coded tablet sends novice troll rogues to Rwag. The rogue trainer inscribes the message and keeps his post inside the Den.",h="In the Valley of Trials, a coded tablet sends novice troll rogues to Rwag.",sec={{t="A Hidden Summons",b="Novice troll rogues receive the Encrypted Tablet when they reach the Valley of Trials. Its coded words direct them to Rwag, an orc trainer who lives in the Den’s shaded caves. The slate keeps the local shadow operatives’ business discreet and tests whether new recruits can understand its message.",sp=0},{t="Eyes of the Hand",b="The tablet brings recruits into contact with the Horde’s wider shadow network. When they report to Rwag, scouts learn that syndicates such as the Shattered Hand watch their progress. These syndicates rely on valley trainers to judge whether prospective cutpurses, spies, and assassins are sharp enough to serve the new nation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Encrypted Tablet used for?",a="The Encrypted Tablet directs young troll rogues to report to Rwag, the rogue trainer inside the Den in the Valley of Trials.",al={"tablet purpose","what does encrypted tablet do","why do i have encrypted tablet"},it="purpose"},{q="Who wrote the message on the tablet?",a="Rwag wrote the message on the tablet. The rogue trainer in the Valley of Trials oversees training for thieves, cutpurses, and assassins serving the Horde.",al={"who sent encrypted tablet","tablet author","who wrote this"},it="origin"},{q="Where do I find Rwag?",a="Rwag is inside the Den, a cavern complex along the northern ridge of the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",al={"where is rwag","rwag location","find rogue trainer valley of trials"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is 'the Hand' mentioned by Rwag?",a="The Hand is the Shattered Hand, a clandestine order in the Horde’s rogue network. Rwag reports to them on the readiness of new operatives from the Valley.",al={"what hand","who are the hand","shattered hand connection"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Encrypted Tablet?",a="The Encrypted Tablet is a coded stone slate delivered specifically to you upon beginning your training in the Valley of Trials. Encrypted to shield its contents from pryin' eyes, it serves as a summons to test your cleverness and direct you to the local rogue trainer.",al={"encrypted tablet","what is encrypted tablet","tablet item"},it="identity",add="395214f3"},{q="Why is the Encrypted Tablet wanted?",a="The rogue trainer Rwag sent the tablet to ensure that newly arrived scoundrels find their way to his den. By deciphering the encrypted message, you prove you have the wits required of a rogue and learn precisely where to seek his guidance.",al={"why want encrypted tablet","why is tablet needed","who wants encrypted tablet"},it="why_wanted",add="3f134c2e"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you receive the ciphered slate as your first step into the Horde’s formal ranks. It points you to Rwag’s training inside the Den.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll training in Durotar, you receive this tablet as proof that your agility and stealth have caught the Valley trainers’ attention."},kw={"durotar","encrypted tablet","rogue trainer","rwag","shattered hand","the den","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:3083","npc:rwag","topic:rogue","subzone:valley-of-trials","topic:troll","zone:durotar","subzone:the-den"},src={"Encrypted Tablet","Encrypted Tablet (quest)"}}
E["item:etched-parchment"] = {t="item",n="Etched Parchment",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Gornek sends new hunters to Jen'shan for their first lessons in Durotar.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Gornek sends new hunters to Jen'shan for their first lessons in Durotar.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Hunt",b="Young orcs and Darkspear trolls begin their rites in the Valley of Trials. As recruits prove themselves against local vermin, Gornek helps them find their calling. He gives the Etched Parchment to those who will wield bow, gun, and fang. Its message comes from Jen'shan, a skilled hunter trainer who seeks fresh eyes and steady hands.",sp=0},{t="The First Lesson",b="Taking the parchment to Jen'shan begins a hunter's training in Durotar. She teaches that the wild path demands dedication. Mastering the beasts of the desert takes as much effort as an arcanist's magic or a shaman's work with the spirits. Her summons brings new hunters to lessons in marksmanship and wilderness survival.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Etched Parchment for?",a="The Etched Parchment guides new hunters in the Valley of Trials to their trainer, Jen'shan.",al={"etched parchment use","what does etched parchment do"},it="purpose"},{q="Who hands out this parchment?",a="Gornek gives the parchment to young hunters near the Den in the Valley of Trials.",al={"who gives etched parchment","etched parchment questgiver"},gp=true},{q="Who wrote the Etched Parchment?",a="Jen'shan wrote the message. She is a troll hunter trainer in the Valley of Trials, ready to train new marksmen.",al={"who sent etched parchment","parchment author"},it="origin"},{q="Where can Jen'shan be found?",a="Jen'shan waits in the Valley of Trials in Durotar, near the training grounds, to instruct novice orc and troll hunters.",al={"where is jenshan","find jenshan"},gp=true},{q="What is the Etched Parchment?",a="The Etched Parchment is a written summons directed specifically to novice hunters arriving in the Valley of Trials. Handed to you by Gornek, it carries a direct call to seek out the local hunter trainer, Jen'shan, so you can begin learning how to survive the harsh red wastes of Durotar and master the wild beasts that roam them.",al={"what is etched parchment","etched parchment item","about etched parchment"},it="identity",add="ddc4492f"},{q="Why does Jen'shan want the Etched Parchment returned to her?",a="Jen'shan does not keep the parchment as a prized relic; she uses it as a formal summons to bring fledgling hunters before her. Delivering it confirms you have answered her call and are ready to be instructed in the deadly crafts of archery, marksmanship, and surviving alongside the fierce predators of Durotar.",al={"why bring etched parchment","why does jenshan want the parchment","etched parchment purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="f14a07d9"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you receive this missive as your first rite of passage in Durotar. It brings you to Jen'shan, who teaches tracking, ranged weapons, and survival.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you hone your craft. For a hunter, this parchment marks the first step toward feeding your clan and guarding Durotar's borders."},kw={"durotar","etched parchment","gornek","hunter","jen'shan","trainer","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:3087","npc:gornek","npc:jen-shan","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:hunter"},src={"Etched Parchment","Etched Parchment (Classic)"}}
E["item:felstalker-hoof"] = {t="item",n="Felstalker Hoof",z="durotar",s="In Durotar's Valley of Trials, young shaman face felstalkers to prove they are ready. Their hooves go to Canaga Earthcaller before they learn to commune with the earth spirits.",h="In Durotar's Valley of Trials, young shaman face felstalkers to prove they are ready.",sec={{t="A Shaman's Trial",b="Canaga Earthcaller sends young shaman to face the demonic taint threatening Durotar. North in the Valley of Trials, the Burning Blade Coven's vile familiars share the ground with roaming felstalkers. Taking a felstalker's hoof tests a shaman's endurance, resolve, and spirit. Those who subdue the beasts are ready to learn the secrets of the earth and prepare the ceremonial sapta for communing with elemental spirits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Felstalker Hoof used for?",a="You bring two Felstalker Hooves to Canaga Earthcaller in the Valley of Trials. They prove you have the strength and spirit to begin communing with the earth element.",al={"what does felstalker hoof do","hoof quest item","why get felstalker hooves"},it="purpose"},{q="Where do these hooves come from?",a="The hooves come from demonic Felstalkers inside and around the Burning Blade Coven, north in the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",al={"where to get felstalker hoof","felstalker hoof location","who drops hooves"},it="origin"},{q="Who requires these hooves?",a="Canaga Earthcaller, the shaman trainer near the Den in the Valley of Trials, asks for the hooves during the Call of Earth rite.",al={"who wants felstalker hooves","who turns in hoof","canaga earthcaller quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Can any adventurer collect these hooves?",a="Shaman undergoing elemental initiation seek Felstalker Hooves. Warriors, warlocks, and rogues face their own trials in the valley and have no need for them.",al={"can non shaman get hooves","is hoof shaman only"},gp=true},{q="What is a Felstalker Hoof?",a="A Felstalker Hoof is a physical trophy taken from the demonic felstalkers summoned by the Burning Blade cultists in Durotar. Rather than serving as a crafting component, it is taken as proof of combat prowess by young shamans seeking to commune with the spirits of the earth.",al={"what is felstalker hoof","felstalker hoof info","what are felstalker hooves"},it="identity",add="1af4909c"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you begin your path toward communion with the earth spirits by slaying demons and gathering their hooves. The trial tests the patience and stubborn resilience you need to wield an Earth Totem.",["faction:Horde"]="Demonic felstalkers in Durotar's training grounds remind the Horde that the Burning Blade's corruption still lingers on its lands."},kw={"burning blade coven","call of earth","canaga earthcaller","durotar","earth sapta","felstalker","felstalker hoof","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:1516","npc:canaga-earthcaller","subzone:burning-blade-coven","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:shaman","quest:792","quest:794"},src={"Felstalker Hoof","Call of Earth (Durotar)"}}
E["item:fire-tar"] = {t="item",n="Fire Tar",z="durotar",s="Across the eastern Barrens, Razormane spellcasters carry Fire Tar. Horde shamans bring it to Telf Joolam, who brews it into a Fire Sapta that lets them commune with fire spirits.",h="Across the eastern Barrens, Razormane spellcasters carry Fire Tar.",sec={{t="A Concoction of the Razormane",b="Razormane geomancers, mystics, and thornweavers carry Fire Tar. The quilboar use it in their harsh magic and rituals, where its power is tuned to flame. Shamanic instructors prize the substance as a worldly reagent. It helps mortal senses reach the raw fury of the elements.",sp=0},{t="The Path to the Fire Totem",b="Young orc and troll shamans travel high among Durotar's crags to Telf Joolam, where they forge their fire totems. Telf asks them to bring a reagent pouch taken from Burning Blade cultists and Fire Tar gathered from the Razormane. He brews the two ingredients into a fire sapta. A shaman who drinks it can perceive the fire spirits waiting atop the nearby peaks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Fire Tar used for?",a="Shamans bring Fire Tar to Telf Joolam in Durotar. He brews it with reagents from the Burning Blade into a Fire Sapta. The brew lets a shaman see and commune with fire spirits to earn a fire totem.",al={"fire tar use","what does fire tar do","why do i need fire tar"},it="purpose"},{q="Who carries Fire Tar?",a="Spellcasting Razormane quilboar carry Fire Tar in the eastern Barrens. They include Razormane Geomancers, Mystics, Thornweavers, and Water Seekers.",al={"who drops fire tar","fire tar mobs","where to get fire tar"},it="target"},{q="Why do shamans need ingredients tied to hostile spellcasters?",a="Saptas need physical components saturated with the matching element. Razormane casters and Burning Blade warlocks channel heat and destructive flame. Their everyday materials carry the fiery essence needed to awaken a shaman's elemental sight.",al={"why quilboar tar","why warlocks and quilboar"}},{q="Where does Telf Joolam brew the Fire Sapta?",a="Telf Joolam brews the Fire Sapta on a high cliff overlooking Durotar's crags. The cliff lies near the path between Razor Hill and the Barrens. He teaches initiates to balance flame's destructive and creative nature.",al={"where is telf joolam","turn in fire tar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Fire Tar?",a="Fire Tar is a volatile, elemental substance carried by spellcasters among the Razormane quilboar in the Barrens. Imbued with the fundamental essence of fire, this pungent pitch is prized by practitioners of elemental magic for its natural affinity to flame.",al={"what is fire tar","fire tar info","describe fire tar"},it="identity",add="1e4fc5f4"},{q="Where does Fire Tar come from, and who makes it?",a="Fire Tar is collected from the Razormane quilboar spellcasters inhabiting the eastern Barrens, including their geomancers, mystics, and thornweavers. Telf Joolam asks initiates to bring it as a component for his fire sapta.",al={"who makes fire tar","fire tar origin","where does fire tar come from"},it="origin",add="006bd002"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, gathering Fire Tar is an essential rite of passage. You seek elemental resonance in the wider world, then use it to brew the Fire Sapta and earn your Fire Totem.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you cross the Southfury River from Durotar into the Barrens to gather Fire Tar. There you face the aggressive Razormane tribes."},kw={"call of fire","fire sapta","fire tar","quilboar","razormane","shaman totem","telf joolam","the barrens"},rel={"quest:1524","npc:telf-joolam","topic:shaman","topic:quilboar","zone:barrens","zone:durotar","item:reagent-pouch-shaman","subzone:dustwind-cave"},src={"Fire Tar","Call of Fire (3)"}}
E["item:fizzle-s-claw"] = {t="item",n="Fizzle's Claw",z="durotar",s="In Thunder Ridge, Fizzle Darkstorm’s claw is carried to Razor Hill as proof of his death. The goblin warlock threatened the orcish homeland under the Burning Blade’s banner.",h="In Thunder Ridge, Fizzle Darkstorm’s claw is carried to Razor Hill as proof of his death.",sec={{t="A Grim Trophy",b="Orgnil Soulscar sent forces to root out shadow cults threatening the orcish homeland. He named Fizzle Darkstorm as an instigator spreading corruption in Thunder Ridge. Fizzle served the Burning Blade as a warlock. His claw now proves to Horde commanders that he has been slain.",sp=0},{t="The Threat in Thunder Ridge",b="Thunder Ridge lies just northwest of Razor Hill, close enough to threaten the surrounding lands. Horde scouts carried Fizzle’s claw back to Razor Hill. It confirms that his rituals and attempt to establish a Burning Blade foothold have been stopped.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who does this claw belong to?",a="The claw belonged to Fizzle Darkstorm, a goblin warlock affiliated with the Burning Blade.",al={"who is fizzle","fizzle darkstorm","claw owner"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Orgnil Soulscar want Fizzle's Claw?",a="Orgnil Soulscar wants proof that Fizzle is dead. The Burning Blade works in secret, and the claw confirms that this threat to Durotar has been removed.",al={"why need claw","orgnil soulscar claw","proof of death"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where was the claw found?",a="Fizzle Darkstorm’s claw was taken at his camp in Thunder Ridge, northwest of Razor Hill in Durotar.",al={"fizzle location","where is fizzle","thunder ridge claw"},it="place"},{q="What is the Burning Blade doing in Durotar?",a="The Burning Blade seeks to undermine the new orcish homeland through demonic corruption, dark sorcery, and civil unrest. Warlocks like Fizzle establish hidden camps to spread chaos across the region.",al={"burning blade durotar","why are cultists in thunder ridge"},it="threat"},{q="What is Fizzle's Claw?",a="Fizzle's Claw is the severed hand of Fizzle Darkstorm, a treacherous goblin warlock aligned with the Burning Blade cult. It serves as gruesome physical proof of his demise for Orgnil Soulscar in Razor Hill, confirming that the cultist ringleader stirring up trouble in Thunder Ridge has been permanently eliminated.",al={"what is fizzles claw","fizzles claw item","fizzle claw identity"},it="identity",add="0fb0af8e"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can present Fizzle’s claw in Razor Hill. It helps cleanse Durotar of shadow cults threatening the young nation’s safety.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you know Fizzle Darkstorm used fel arts in service of the Burning Blade. He turned his talents against the Horde."},kw={"burning blade","dark storms","durotar","fizzle darkstorm","fizzle's claw","orgnil soulscar","razor hill","thunder ridge"},rel={"quest:806","npc:orgnil-soulscar","subzone:thunder-ridge","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:warlock","topic:goblin"},src={"Fizzle's Claw","Dark Storms (quest)"}}
E["item:foreman-s-blackjack"] = {t="item",n="Foreman's Blackjack",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Foreman's Blackjack keeps Durotar's peons at work. Foremen use the leather-wrapped cosh to wake laborers who fall asleep during the Horde's early construction.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Foreman's Blackjack keeps Durotar's peons at work.",sec={{t="A Tool of Orcish Labor",b="Durotar needs stockpiles of lumber for the Horde's new home. In the Valley of Trials, peons do the work, and Foreman Thazz'ril keeps the crews moving with Foreman's Blackjack. Its weighted blow jolts laborers awake when they nap beneath the valley's shade trees. It is meant to wake them, not kill them. Peon life in the new Horde means hard, unglamorous work under an iron fist.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Foreman's Blackjack used for?",a="Overseers give the blackjack to young adventurers to discipline sleeping peons in the Valley of Trials. A strike jolts a napping peon awake, and they return to chopping and hauling wood.",al={"blackjack use","why use blackjack","peon club"},it="purpose"},{q="Who owns this blackjack?",a="Foreman Thazz'ril owns the blackjack. The labor taskmaster is stationed in the Valley of Trials, where he oversees the collection of raw timber for the young Orc settlement.",al={"who gives blackjack","foreman blackjack owner"},it="leader"},{q="Why do the peons keep falling asleep on the job?",a="Orcish peons work exhausting shifts gathering wood under Durotar's harsh sun. When exhaustion overtakes them, they often nap without permission beneath the valley's sparse trees.",al={"why are peons lazy","lazy peons sleeping"},it="motive"},{q="Can I keep the blackjack after finishing the task?",a="No. The overseer demands the tool back as soon as the shirkers have been disciplined. It stays with taskmasters who enforce labor quotas.",al={"keep blackjack","can i keep foreman blackjack"},gp=true},{q="What is the Foreman's Blackjack?",a="The Foreman's Blackjack is a heavy leather-wrapped truncheon carried by Foreman Thazz'ril in the Valley of Trials. It is an unglamorous tool of discipline, designed not to inflict grievous wounds in war, but to deliver a sharp, stinging blow that jolts sleeping workers back to their feet.",al={"what is the blackjack","foremans blackjack item","what is foremans blackjack"},it="identity",add="4e7ef009"},{q="Why does Foreman Thazz'ril want the blackjack back?",a="Foreman Thazz'ril relies on the blackjack to run his work crews in the Valley of Trials. Without it, he has little leverage to force the exhausted, unmotivated peons to keep chopping and hauling lumber for the Horde. Once you have helped knock the laborers back to their duties, he expects his essential tool returned.",al={"why return the blackjack","why does thazzril need the blackjack","why want the blackjack"},it="why_wanted",add="9e33a4a7"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For young orcs entering the Valley of Trials, wielding the blackjack offers an early lesson in Horde hierarchy. Those without a warrior's strength or spirit are sent to labor and kept in line by force.",["faction:Horde"]="The blackjack reflects the work needed to tame Durotar. Settling this harsh land requires every laborer to work without pause."},kw={"blackjack","durotar","foreman's blackjack","lazy peons","peon","thazzril","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:lazy-peons","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar"},src={"Foreman's Blackjack","Lazy Peons"}}
E["item:glowing-ember"] = {t="item",n="Glowing Ember",z="durotar",s="At the Shrine of Eternal Flame, a Glowing Ember awakens the brazier for a shaman’s trial. It comes from a Minor Manifestation of Fire on Durotar’s crags.",h="At the Shrine of Eternal Flame, a Glowing Ember awakens the brazier for a shaman’s trial.",sec={{t="Core of the Flame",b="A rising shaman drinks fire sapta to see the fiery spirits on the ridge near Telf Joolam. There, the initiate faces a Minor Manifestation of Fire. When the elemental falls, its physical form leaves only a smoldering ember. Raw elemental heat still pulses within it, carrying the spark needed to awaken the sacred brazier at the Shrine of Eternal Flame.",sp=0},{t="Igniting the Torch",b="When the Glowing Ember enters the mountain brazier’s cool basin, white-hot fire bursts to life. The brazier’s flame lets the initiate light the Torch of the Dormant Flame. That torch binds fire’s unruly essence in a vessel the initiate can carry down the mountain as proof of mastery over the elements.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does the Glowing Ember come from?",a="You recover the ember from a defeated Minor Manifestation of Fire at the summit above the Shrine of Eternal Flame in Durotar.",al={"how to get glowing ember","glowing ember drop","where find glowing ember"},it="origin"},{q="What is the ember used for?",a="You place the ember in the metal brazier at the Shrine of Eternal Flame. Its intense, rhythmic flame lights the ceremonial Torch of the Dormant Flame.",al={"what does glowing ember do","glowing ember use","brazier ember"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why do shamans need the fire sapta to acquire it?",a="The elemental spirits atop the mountain are beyond ordinary mortal sight. Drinking fire sapta attunes your senses to the elemental plane and reveals the Minor Manifestation of Fire, so you can challenge it.",al={"why need sapta","cant see fire elemental","fire sapta ember"}},{q="Who directs shamans to seek this ember?",a="Telf Joolam, a hermit in the crags of Durotar, brews the fire sapta and guides shaman initiates through the trial of defeating the flame spirit.",al={"who gives the quest","telf joolam ember","call of fire quest giver"}},{q="What is the Glowing Ember?",a="The Glowing Ember is the smoldering remnant harvested from a Minor Manifestation of Fire upon the peak overlooking Durotar. It is a concentrated piece of living flame left behind once the spirit is overcome, holding enough innate elemental heat to spark the dormant fires atop the mountain's sacred altar.",al={"what is glowing ember","glowing ember lore","glowing ember item"},it="identity",add="8d7073a8"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you test your resolve against living fire in this rite of passage before you command your totem."},kw={"call of fire","fire sapta","glowing ember","minor manifestation of fire","shrine of eternal flame","telf joolam","torch of the dormant flame"},rel={"quest:1524","npc:telf-joolam","item:torch-of-the-dormant-flame","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},src={"Glowing Ember","Call of Fire (4)"}}
E["item:glyphic-tablet"] = {t="item",n="Glyphic Tablet",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Gornek gives novice Darkspear troll mages the Glyphic Tablet. Its summons sends them to Mai'ah for instruction in arcane magic.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Gornek gives novice Darkspear troll mages the Glyphic Tablet.",sec={{t="A Mage's First Summons",b="Darkspear recruits with an affinity for arcane power receive the Glyphic Tablet in the Valley of Trials. Gornek hands it to young mages as they handle early tasks around the red canyons. On the slate, Mai'ah, a seasoned troll mage outside the Den, invites them to meet her.\n\nThe Darkspear follow arcane traditions unlike the scholarly academies of humans or high elves. Mai'ah offers instruction and a solemn warning. Raw magic corrupts and deceives, and its dangers to a mage's mind exceed those of any enemy soldier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Glyphic Tablet?",a="The Glyphic Tablet summons a novice troll mage to Mai'ah in the Valley of Trials for proper spellcasting training.",al={"what does glyphic tablet do","glyphic tablet use","why do i have glyphic tablet"},it="purpose"},{q="Who sends the Glyphic Tablet?",a="Mai'ah writes the tablet, and Gornek hands it to young troll recruits in the Valley of Trials.",al={"who wrote glyphic tablet","who gave me glyphic tablet"},it="origin"},{q="Why do troll mages need a warning about magic?",a="Mai'ah warns that arcane magic corrupts, feeds arrogance, and can make spellcasters feel invincible. Its unseen dangers are deadlier than physical rivals.",al={"what does mai'ah say","is magic dangerous"},it="motive"},{q="Can other Horde races receive this tablet?",a="Troll mages receive the Glyphic Tablet in the Valley of Trials. Orc mages receive a Glyphic Parchment that summons them to Mai'ah.",al={"can orcs get glyphic tablet","is glyphic tablet troll only"},it="for_you"},{q="What is the Glyphic Tablet?",a="The Glyphic Tablet is an inscribed message sent to novice troll mages beginning their trials in the Valley of Trials. Delivered through Gornek, it summons you to meet with Mai'ah, the local mage trainer, so you may formally commence your instruction in the arcane arts.",al={"what is glyphic tablet","glyphic tablet item","about glyphic tablet"},it="identity",add="be25ec39"},{q="Why does anyone want the Glyphic Tablet?",a="The tablet is not sought for power or wealth, but serves as a formal summons and token of introduction. It ensures young troll mages present themselves to Mai'ah, who uses the meeting to deliver crucial warnings regarding the corrupting dangers inherent to wielding arcane magic.",al={"why want glyphic tablet","who needs glyphic tablet","why keep glyphic tablet"},it="why_wanted",add="28b4f0b5"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you begin your Darkspear arcane instruction with Mai'ah's warning that magic's corrupting allure is your greatest peril.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you receive this tablet to begin your path alongside traditional shamanic and martial ways."},kw={"arcane","durotar","glyphic tablet","gornek","mai'ah","troll mage","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:3086","npc:mai-ah","npc:gornek","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:mage","topic:troll","subzone:the-den"},src={"Glyphic Tablet","Glyphic Tablet (quest)"}}
E["item:gnomish-tools"] = {t="item",n="Gnomish Tools",z="durotar",s="Along Durotar’s coast, Gnomish Tools from Proudmoore’s fleet are being recovered by the Horde. The salvaged devices may teach its craftsmen how Alliance engineering works and how to adapt it for survival.",h="Along Durotar’s coast, Gnomish Tools from Proudmoore’s fleet are being recovered by the Horde.",sec={{t="Sunken Salvage",b="Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore’s fleet brought vast supplies of modern equipment to Durotar. Proudmoore led Kul Tiras and Alliance forces to its shores, with sophisticated gear made by their gnomish allies aboard. After the fleet was destroyed along the Scuttle Coast, east of Tiragarde Keep, delicate mechanical kits sank beneath the waves. Waterproof toolboxes still lie among the rotting timbers and barnacle-encrusted hulls in the shallows.",sp=0},{t="Eyes in Orgrimmar",b="Gar'Thok, who oversees Razor Hill, sent Horde scouts to recover tools from the watery grave of Proudmoore’s navy. The orcs know humans and gnomes are skilled in engineering, especially siege engines, shipwrighting, and clockwork mechanics. So the kits travel by caravan to craftsmen and scholars in Orgrimmar. There, the Horde intends to study Alliance contraptions, learn to counter enemy war machines, and adapt foreign innovations for its own survival.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are gnomish tools lying off the coast of Durotar?",a="Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore’s fleet carried the tools when Kul Tiras assaulted Durotar. When the armada was shattered and sunk along the Scuttle Coast, east of Tiragarde Keep, its naval cargo settled on the ocean floor.",al={"why gnomish tools here","origin of gnomish tools","how did tools get in durotar"},it="origin"},{q="Why does the Horde want these tools?",a="Gar'Thok of Razor Hill wants the tools recovered and sent to Orgrimmar. By studying the intricate work of Alliance engineers, the Horde hopes to understand enemy machines and build better gear of its own.",al={"why does gar'thok want tools","horde use for gnomish tools","what are the tools for"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are the tools found?",a="The tools lie in toolboxes scattered in and around sunken wreckage along Durotar’s Scuttle Coast, just east of Tiragarde Keep. Many rest underwater or across half-submerged broken hulls.",al={"gnomish tools location","where to find gnomish tools","gnomish toolboxes location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What are these Gnomish Tools?",a="These are specialized mechanical implements crafted by the gnomes of the Alliance. Highly prized for their precision and intricate design, they represent some of the most sophisticated engineering in Azeroth. Carried aboard Grand Admiral Proudmoore's warships to maintain and repair advanced Alliance machinery, they were scattered across the ocean floor off Durotar's coast when his fleet met its ruin.",al={"what are gnomish tools","gnomish tools info","what are the gnomish tools"},it="identity",add="bc7dc32b"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can study these kits for insight into the precise craft of Alliance tinkers, clockwork assemblies, and miniaturization.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can help recover lost Alliance equipment for study. Learning enemy designs and foreign mechanisms may help the Horde defend against future naval invasions."},kw={"durotar","engineering","gar'thok","gnomish tools","proudmoore","razor hill","scuttle coast","tiragarde keep"},rel={"quest:825","subzone:scuttle-coast","npc:gar-thok","subzone:tiragarde-keep","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","topic:gnome"},src={"Gnomish Tools","From The Wreckage...."}}
E["item:hallowed-tablet"] = {t="item",n="Hallowed Tablet",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, the Hallowed Tablet calls young Darkspear priests to Ken'jai. Its words begin their lessons in communing with the spirits.",h="In the Valley of Trials, the Hallowed Tablet calls young Darkspear priests to Ken'jai.",sec={{t="A Summons from the Spirits",b="Gornek gives the Hallowed Tablet to a promising troll priest taking their first steps through the Valley of Trials. A personal invitation from Ken'jai, the priest trainer outside the Den, is written upon it. Ken'jai reads signs and hears the spirits' whispers.\n\nSo when young Darkspear with spiritual potential arrive in Durotar, the spirits make their coming known to him. The tablet tells the initiate to read its message and seek Ken'jai's guidance in channeling spiritual authority.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Hallowed Tablet?",a="In the Valley of Trials, Gornek gives novice troll priests an inscribed stone tablet. Its message directs them to Ken'jai, their priest trainer.",al={"what is this item","hallowed tablet lore","what does the tablet do"},it="identity"},{q="Who sent the tablet?",a="Ken'jai sent the tablet through Gornek. The spirits foretold a new acolyte's arrival, so Ken'jai, the priest trainer outside the Den, sent word.",al={"who wrote it","who gave me this","tablet author"},it="origin"},{q="Why do troll priests need to see Ken'jai?",a="Darkspear priests commune with and command the spirits. Ken'jai guides initiates as their spiritual connection deepens, helping ensure the spirits favor teaching them stronger abilities.",al={"what does kenjai do","why see kenjai"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For the Darkspear, priesthood means close communion with the spirits and loa. The tablet invites you into those ancestral spiritual traditions.",["class:Priest"]="The tablet begins your formal priest training in Durotar and establishes your bond with Ken'jai, your mentor."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","gornek","hallowed tablet","ken'jai","troll priest","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:3085","npc:gornek","topic:priest","topic:troll","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar"},src={"Hallowed Tablet","Hallowed Tablet (quest)"}}
E["item:kron-s-amulet"] = {t="item",n="Kron's Amulet",z="durotar",s="Along the Southfury River, Kron’s amulet recalls a young orc hunter who went missing.",h="Along the Southfury River, Kron’s amulet recalls a young orc hunter who went missing.",sec={{t="Tragedy on the Southfury",b="Kron was a headstrong young orc from a farmstead northwest of Razor Hill. He went to hunt the vicious Dreadmaw crocolisks along the Southfury River, on the border with the Barrens. His mother, Misha Tor'kren, warned him of the danger, but pride carried him onward. Kron never returned. His amulet was found inside one of the river’s predators, confirming he had been slain and devoured. It gives Misha painful confirmation of her son’s fate.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Kron?",a="Kron was a headstrong young orc hunter who lived with his mother, Misha Tor'kren, on a farmstead northwest of Razor Hill. He went alone to test his strength against the river beasts, despite warnings of their ferocity.",al={"who is kron","kron backstory","kron lore"},it="people"},{q="Where is Kron's Amulet found?",a="Dreadmaw Crocolisks and Corrupted Dreadmaw Crocolisks along the banks of the Southfury River in Durotar carry Kron's Amulet in their bellies.",al={"where do i find the amulet","kron's amulet location","who drops kron's amulet"},sp=1,it="item",gp=true},{q="Who wants Kron's Amulet returned?",a="Misha Tor'kren wants Kron's Amulet returned. She awaits word of her son at her farmstead northwest of Razor Hill, and the amulet gives her painful confirmation of his fate.",al={"who needs the amulet","where to turn in kron's amulet","misha tor'kren"},sp=1,it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Kron's Amulet?",a="This personal trinket belonged to Kron, an orc youth from a farmstead northwest of Razor Hill. Driven by pride and eager to prove his strength, he set out alone toward the Southfury River to hunt the ferocious Dreadmaw crocolisks along the border of the Barrens. Instead of returning in triumph, he fell prey to the beasts he sought to slay. Swallowed along with his remains, this talisman is the only surviving piece of the young hunter that can prove his grim demise.",al={"what is the amulet","krons amulet lore","who owns the amulet"},it="identity",add="5d838632"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, Kron's fate shows how pride and the pursuit of martial glory can lead one to ignore the wisdom of elders, with deadly consequences.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, Kron's fate is a stark lesson in the danger of underestimating vicious beasts in unfamiliar river territory."},kw={"amulet","dreadmaw crocolisk","kron","misha tor'kren","razor hill","southfury river"},rel={"quest:816","npc:misha-tor-kren","subzone:southfury-river","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","zone:barrens"},src={"Kron's Amulet","Lost But Not Forgotten (Classic)"}}
E["item:minshina-s-skull"] = {t="item",n="Minshina's Skull",z="durotar",s="On the Echo Isles, Minshina's soul remains bound to his skull by Zalazane's dark magic. Minshina was a Darkspear troll and Master Gadrin's brother. Zalazane seized the isles and drove the tribe away, then used Minshina's skull in his rituals.",h="On the Echo Isles, Minshina's soul remains bound to his skull by Zalazane's dark magic.",sec={{t="A Trapped Spirit",b="Minshina was captured and slain when Zalazane seized the Echo Isles and drove out the Darkspear. The traitorous witch doctor bound his soul to his severed skull instead of letting him pass into death. Now the skull lies within a circle of power on the southernmost isle, holding Minshina fast to Zalazane's magic.\n\nMaster Gadrin dreams of his brother calling to him, and seeks brave travelers to enter the occupied islands. He asks them to reclaim the skull and break Zalazane's hold over Minshina's spirit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Minshina?",a="Minshina was a Darkspear troll and the brother of Master Gadrin of Sen'jin Village. Zalazane murdered him amid his betrayal on the Echo Isles.",al={"minshina lore","who is minshina","master gadrin brother"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Minshina's soul trapped in his skull?",a="Zalazane used dark magic to bind Minshina's spirit inside his severed head. He placed the skull in a circle of power on the main isle, keeping Minshina bound to his will instead of passing to the ancestors.",al={"why trap his soul","zalazane skull ritual","soul trapped in skull"},it="power"},{q="Where is the skull located?",a="The skull lies on the largest and southernmost isle of the Echo Isles. It rests atop a hill in a circle of power, among candles, ritual markers and other skulls, guarded by Zalazane's thralls.",al={"where is minshinas skull","circle of power location","skull location echo isles"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens when the skull is brought to Master Gadrin?",a="When you return the skull to Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village, the dark enchantment breaks. Minshina's spectral form appears briefly, bows in gratitude and departs peacefully for the realm of the ancestors.",al={"freeing minshina","gadrin skull reward","what happens to minshina"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is Minshina's Skull?",a="Minshina's Skull is the physical remains of Minshina, a fallen Darkspear troll and the brother of Master Gadrin. Rather than resting peacefully in death, Minshina had his very soul bound into his severed skull through dark voodoo, leaving him trapped and crying out for release.",al={"what is minshina's skull","minshina skull identity","what is this skull"},it="identity",add="5c3b75e4"},{q="Where does Minshina's Skull come from, and who made it?",a="The skull belonged to Minshina, who was captured and killed by the traitorous witch doctor Zalazane on the Echo Isles. Using foul sorcery, Zalazane severed the head and bound Minshina's spirit directly to the bone, placing it within a circle of power alongside other remains to fuel his dark rituals.",al={"where did minshina's skull come from","who made minshina skull","minshina skull origin"},it="origin",add="1b71ee0f"},{q="Why does anyone want Minshina's Skull?",a="Master Gadrin seeks the skull to rescue his brother's tormented spirit. Minshina constantly calls out to Gadrin in his dreams, unable to find rest while imprisoned by Zalazane's magic. Recovering the skull from the circle of power on the Echo Isles is the only way to break the binding and grant his soul freedom.",al={"why want minshina skull","why collect minshina skull","who wants minshina skull"},it="why_wanted",add="b6c5f4d1"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For the Darkspear, Zalazane's desecration of Minshina breaks ancestral tradition. Recovering his skull is a matter of tribal honor.",["faction:Horde"]="Recovering the skull strikes an early blow against Zalazane's hold over the Echo Isles, just off Durotar's coast."},kw={"circle of power","darkspear","echo isles","gadrin","minshina","sen'jin village","skull","zalazane"},rel={"quest:808","npc:master-gadrin","subzone:echo-isles","quest:826","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Minshina's Skull","Minshina's Skull (quest)"}}
E["item:reagent-pouch-shaman"] = {t="item",n="Reagent Pouch",z="durotar",s="In Durotar, Burning Blade cultists carry reagents for a shaman's first fire sapta. Telf Joolam mixes them with fire tar from Razormane quilboar to make a draught that lets a young shaman see the realm of fire.",h="In Durotar, Burning Blade cultists carry reagents for a shaman's first fire sapta.",sec={{t="Components of the Flame",b="Burning Blade cultists carry reagents for a young shaman's first fire sapta. The hermit Telf Joolam mixes the powders and oils from their pouches with fire tar from Razormane quilboar. Together, these ingredients make a draught that grants sight into the realm of fire and attunes the shaman to the spirits of flame.",sp=0},{t="Tainted Sources, Pure Vision",b="Burning Blade cultists turn flame toward destruction and fel sorcery. Yet the elements in their pouches still belong to heat and combustion. Shaman teach that elemental forces exist in tension: fire creates as well as destroys. A shaman can use the cultists' tools to awaken true communion with the spirits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the reagent pouch used for?",a="Telf Joolam uses the reagents with fire tar from Razormane quilboar to brew a fire sapta. Drinking it grants a shaman visionary sight to seek the elemental spirits and claim the Fire Totem.",al={"reagent pouch use","what does reagent pouch do","reagent pouch shaman quest"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Where do I find a reagent pouch?",a="You can recover a pouch from Burning Blade cultists in Dustwind Cave, in the rocky heights northeast of Razor Hill in Durotar.",al={"reagent pouch drop","where to get reagent pouch","burning blade pouch location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does a shaman need warlock reagents?",a="Burning Blade cultists stock their pouches with ingredients tied to fire magic. Their flame rituals make the reagents useful catalysts for brewing a fire sapta.",al={"why warlock items","why burning blade reagents","shaman using fel items"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Reagent Pouch?",a="It is a small satchel carried by cultists of the Burning Blade, packed with the ritual herbs, ashes, and occult catalysts they use to fuel their dark spells. While meant for dark sorcery, the sheer concentration of fiery components makes the entire pouch a potent bundle of raw elemental materials.",al={"what is reagent pouch","reagent pouch lore","burning blade reagent pouch"},it="identity",add="ad39cae0"},{q="Where does the Reagent Pouch come from?",a="The pouches are assembled and carried by Burning Blade cultists hiding within the caves of Durotar and the Barrens. These warlocks gather and store specific components needed for their destructive rites, keeping them close at hand whenever casting flame and shadow magic.",al={"reagent pouch origin","who made the reagent pouch","where did reagent pouch come from"},it="origin",add="2a611680"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, retrieving the pouch is a rite of passage toward earning your Fire Totem. It teaches that corrupted elemental forces can be reclaimed to serve balance.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you recognize the pouches as sorcerous supplies for fel cultists. Their ritual elements are meant for demonic pyromancy, not communion with nature."},kw={"burning blade","call of fire","durotar","dustwind cave","fire sapta","fire totem","reagent pouch","telf joolam"},rel={"quest:1524","npc:telf-joolam","item:fire-tar","subzone:dustwind-cave","zone:durotar","topic:shaman","topic:warlock"},src={"Reagent Pouch (shaman)","Call of Fire (3)"}}
E["item:rough-quartz"] = {t="item",n="Rough Quartz",z="durotar",s="In Durotar, a shaman receives Rough Quartz from a Minor Manifestation of Earth. An elder binds the stone into the shaman’s first Earth Totem.",h="In Durotar, a shaman receives Rough Quartz from a Minor Manifestation of Earth.",sec={{t="Heart of the Earth Totem",b="In Durotar or Mulgore, a Minor Manifestation of Earth gives Rough Quartz to a shaman who communes with the spirits. To an untrained eye, the stone looks like an ordinary desert pebble. It represents endurance, patience, and unwavering strength.\n\nAt the Valley of Trials, Canaga Earthcaller binds the quartz into carved wood to make an Earth Totem. The stone becomes the spiritual focus that joins a young shaman to Azeroth’s living soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Rough Quartz?",a="An elder shaman binds Rough Quartz into an initiate’s first Earth Totem as its spiritual core. It also shows that the novice has communed with the elemental earth spirit.",al={"what does rough quartz do","rough quartz use","why do i need rough quartz"},it="purpose"},{q="Who gives you the Rough Quartz?",a="A Minor Manifestation of Earth grants you Rough Quartz after you commune with the spirit during the Call of Earth ritual in Durotar or Mulgore.",al={"where do i get rough quartz","who drops rough quartz"},it="origin"},{q="Who do I bring this stone to in Durotar?",a="Bring Rough Quartz to Canaga Earthcaller, the shaman trainer in the Valley of Trials. Canaga fashions it into your Earth Totem.",al={"where to turn in rough quartz","rough quartz turn in","who takes rough quartz"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Is this quartz used for anything else?",a="No. Rough Quartz is a sacred ritual object used to make an Earth Totem. It has no use in common trade.",al={"can i sell rough quartz","is rough quartz used in crafting"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What is Rough Quartz?",a="Rough Quartz is a small elemental pebble given to aspiring shaman by a Minor Manifestation of Earth. Though modest in size and appearance, the stone represents an initiate's passing of the rite of earth and communion with the elemental spirit, serving as tangible proof of their bond.",al={"what is rough quartz","rough quartz item","rough quartz meaning"},it="identity",add="f25f16be"},{q="Why does Canaga Earthcaller want the Rough Quartz?",a="Canaga Earthcaller requires the Rough Quartz as proof that you have heeded the call and communed with the elemental spirit. He uses the pebble as the heart of your first Earth Totem, allowing you to commune further with the earth and cast spells tied directly to its power.",al={"why need rough quartz","rough quartz purpose","why bring rough quartz to canaga"},it="why_wanted",add="871e2ee1"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, Rough Quartz marks your first communion with the element of earth. It anchors your spells and marks your path as a conduit of the spirits."},kw={"call of earth","canaga earthcaller","earth totem","minor manifestation of earth","rough quartz","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:1516","npc:canaga-earthcaller","npc:minor-manifestation-of-earth","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","zone:mulgore","topic:shaman"},src={"Rough Quartz","Call of Earth (Durotar 3)"}}
E["item:rune-inscribed-parchment"] = {t="item",n="Rune-Inscribed Parchment",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Gornek gives aspiring orc shamans a summons from Shikrik. It calls them to guide their people and commune with elemental spirits.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Gornek gives aspiring orc shamans a summons from Shikrik.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Spirits",b="New orc shamans train under veteran overseers in the Valley of Trials. During an initiate’s first trials, Gornek gives them a rune-covered message from Shikrik, the local shamanic instructor. It calls them to deepen their bond with the elements.\n\nAmong the orcs, shamans mediate between the living and their ancestors. The message marks a turn from brute strength toward disciplined reverence for ancestral ways.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Rune-Inscribed Parchment?",a="In the Valley of Trials, Gornek gives novice orc shamans a handwritten message. It directs them to report to Shikrik for formal instruction.",al={"rune parchment","what is this item","shaman parchment"},it="identity"},{q="Who wrote the parchment?",a="Shikrik, the shaman trainer in the Valley of Trials, wrote the parchment. It instructs young initiates in the ways of the elements and ancestral spirits.",al={"who sent the parchment","parchment author"},it="origin"},{q="Why are shamans considered chosen among the orcs?",a="Orc shamans guide their people as spiritual leaders. They listen to elemental spirits and act as conduits for their ancestors. Shikrik teaches apprentices to mend allies and wield the elements’ fury against their foes.",al={"why be a shaman","orc shaman role"}},{q="Why does Shikrik want you to read the Rune-Inscribed Parchment?",a="Shikrik dispatched this message through Gornek to summon you directly to her. Having recognized that you are chosen to guide the spiritual lives of your people, she intends to begin your formal training in communion with ancestors, elemental mastery, and the rites of an orc shaman.",al={"why read rune inscribed parchment","why does shikrik send parchment","purpose of rune-inscribed parchment"},it="why_wanted",rc="Orc",add="00232829"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you take your first step on the path of the elements. Under Shikrik’s guidance, you learn ancestor worship and mastery of the elements.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you carry ancestral wisdom in Durotar. The rediscovery of shamanic tradition is central to the new Horde."},kw={"durotar","gornek","parchment","rune-inscribed parchment","shaman","shikrik","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:3089","npc:gornek","topic:shaman","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar"},src={"Rune-Inscribed Parchment","Rune-Inscribed Parchment (Classic)"}}
E["item:rune-inscribed-tablet"] = {t="item",n="Rune-Inscribed Tablet",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Gornek gives a stone message to young Darkspear troll shamans. It sends promising mystics to Shikrik for formal spiritual instruction.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Gornek gives a stone message to young Darkspear troll shamans.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Spirits",b="Gornek gives a rune-carved stone to initiates who prove their mettle in the Valley of Trials. The troll shaman Ishi-yo sends it to Shikrik, the shaman trainer. For Darkspear trolls, the tablet begins a shared path with the orcs. Their old spiritual traditions join the shamanic heritage Warchief Thrall has renewed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Rune-Inscribed Tablet used for?",a="Gornek gives the tablet to young troll shamans in the Valley of Trials. It directs them to Shikrik for formal spiritual education.",al={"tablet purpose","what does the tablet do","rune tablet use"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who sends the tablet?",a="The troll shaman Ishi-yo sends the tablet. It directs the initiate to Shikrik, the orc shaman trainer just outside the Den in the Valley of Trials. Shikrik knows they are coming.",al={"who wrote the tablet","tablet sender","who carved it"},it="origin"},{q="Who receives this tablet?",a="Gornek gives the tablet to newly arrived Darkspear troll shamans as their first class summons in Durotar.",al={"who gets rune-inscribed tablet","which class gets the tablet"},it="target"},{q="What is the Rune-Inscribed Tablet?",a="The Rune-Inscribed Tablet is a written summons directed to aspiring troll shamans training within the Valley of Trials. Marked with shamanic runes, it serves as a personal message passed through Gornek to introduce promising recruits directly to their local trainer.",al={"what is rune-inscribed tablet","rune inscribed tablet lore","what is this tablet"},it="identity",rc="Troll",add="cd2cca59"},{q="Why does Shikrik want you to receive the Rune-Inscribed Tablet?",a="The tablet actually comes from Ishi-yo, the troll shaman who gave you your first lessons; Gornek only guesses it came from Shikrik. Ishi-yo sends you on to Shikrik, who already expects you. She wants to ground you in the elements and the spirits of your ancestors, so that one day you can guide and protect the Horde's villages and towns just as Thrall guides the Horde itself.",al={"why does shikrik send the tablet","why do i need this tablet","shikrik rune inscribed tablet"},it="why_wanted",rc="Troll",add="33b46b09"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, the tablet marks your first official step toward mastering earth, fire, water, and air. Your strength flows from ancestral spirits.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you answer an orc trainer's summons. It marks a growing bond and shared spiritual path between your people and their new Horde allies."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","gornek","rune-inscribed tablet","shaman","shikrik","trainer","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:3084","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","npc:gornek","topic:shaman","topic:troll","npc:thrall","topic:horde"},src={"Rune-Inscribed Tablet","Rune-Inscribed Tablet (quest)"}}
E["item:sack-of-supplies"] = {t="item",n="Sack of Supplies",z="durotar",s="Across Razorwind Canyon, the sacks of supplies bound for Rezlak lie scattered among harpy roosts. Dustwind harpies seized the goods as they crossed Durotar.",h="Across Razorwind Canyon, the sacks of supplies bound for Rezlak lie scattered among harpy roosts.",sec={{t="A Plundered Caravan",b="Rezlak needs a steady supply of goods for his work outside Orgrimmar. Gazlowe contracted the goblin engineer from Ratchet to build for the Horde. A caravan carrying a promised shipment passed near the canyon road south of Orgrimmar. Dustwind harpies ambushed it and dragged the cargo into their roosts in Razorwind Canyon, scattering sacks beside their nests in the dirt and scree.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside these supply sacks?",a="The sacks hold construction materials and trade goods for Gazlowe's engineering work. They are meant to support Orcish building projects near Orgrimmar. Without them, Rezlak cannot finish his work.",al={"supply sack contents","what are in the sacks","rezlak supplies"},it="identity"},{q="Who stole the supplies?",a="Dustwind harpies stole the supplies. This savage avian race infests the high crevices and ravines of Razorwind Canyon.",al={"who took the supplies","who stole the sacks"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Rezlak?",a="Rezlak is a goblin engineer Gazlowe sent from Ratchet to help the Horde build and maintain line infrastructure in Durotar.",al={"who is rezlak","rezlak lore"},it="people"},{q="Where do these sacks of supplies come from?",a="These sacks were part of a shipment sent to Durotar on behalf of Gazlowe and his goblin engineers. Intended to aid the orcs in building and maintaining their settlements, the caravan carrying them was ambushed and looted along the road before it could reach its destination.",al={"sack of supplies origin","where did the supplies come from","who made supply sack"},it="origin",add="812e6d27"},{q="Why does Rezlak want these supply sacks?",a="Rezlak cannot carry out the construction work Gazlowe assigned him without proper gear and materials. Harpies from Razorwind Canyon plundered the caravan carrying his tools and provisions, leaving the goblin foreman completely stalled until someone recovers the stolen cargo.",al={"why rezlak wants supplies","why need supply sacks","winds in the desert supplies why"},it="why_wanted",add="55ee41bd"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Recovering the supplies from local predators keeps frontier construction around Orgrimmar moving without costly delays."},kw={"durotar","dustwind harpies","gazlowe","razorwind canyon","rezlak","sack of supplies"},rel={"quest:834","quest:835","npc:rezlak","subzone:razorwind-canyon","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:razor-hill"},src={"Sack of Supplies","Winds in the Desert"}}
E["item:sarkoth-s-mangled-claw"] = {t="item",n="Sarkoth's Mangled Claw",z="durotar",s="Across the southern bluffs of the Valley of Trials, Sarkoth's Mangled Claw bears the mark of a wounded hunter. Hana'zua crushed the scorpid's pincer before its venomous sting struck him down.",h="Across the southern bluffs of the Valley of Trials, Sarkoth's Mangled Claw bears the mark of a wounded hunter.",sec={{t="A Trophy of Vengeance",b="Hana'zua, a young Darkspear troll, met Sarkoth while hunting in the Valley of Trials. The massive scorpid pierced his chest with its venomous stinger, leaving him bleeding beneath a nearby tree.\n\nBefore the sting, Hana'zua crushed the beast's pincer. The battered claw proves Sarkoth has been slain. For the wounded hunter, its scar shows that his desperate strike found its mark and preserves his warrior's honor as venom courses through his veins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the claw mangled?",a="Sarkoth's pincer was crushed in a desperate duel with Hana'zua, a troll hunter. Sarkoth stung Hana'zua in the chest, but the troll struck before the beast's claw could close around his leg.",al={"why broken claw","who crushed sarkoth claw","mangled claw lore"}},{q="Who wants Sarkoth's Mangled Claw?",a="Hana'zua asks for the claw. Badly wounded beneath a tree in the Valley of Trials, he fears he will die there. He wants Sarkoth slain to uphold his honor; seeing the deed done steels him to endure until Gornek sends aid.",al={"who needs sarkoth claw","who turned in to","hanazua claw"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where did this claw come from?",a="The claw came from Sarkoth, a large, aggressive scorpid prowling the elevated plateau along the southern cliffs of the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",al={"sarkoth location","where is sarkoth","where to get mangled claw"},it="origin"},{q="What is Sarkoth's Mangled Claw?",a="It is the severed pincer of Sarkoth, an unusually large and vicious scorpid prowling the southern plateau above the Valley of Trials. The claw bears severe, splintering damage inflicted by the badly wounded Darkspear troll Hana'zua during their desperate struggle, serving as undeniable proof that the monstrous beast has finally been slain.",al={"what is sarkoths mangled claw","sarkoth claw identity","mangled claw"},it="identity",add="5a9dc5fc"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a troll, bringing the claw to Hana'zua gives a dying Darkspear kinsman some dignity. He learns his final strike scarred the beast before the end.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, claiming the trophy in the Valley of Trials marks an early test of courage and martial strength in Durotar's harsh wilds."},kw={"claw","durotar","hana'zua","mangled claw","sarkoth","scorpid","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:804","npc:hana-zua","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Sarkoth's Mangled Claw","Sarkoth (quest)"}}
E["item:searing-collar"] = {t="item",n="Searing Collar",z="durotar",s="At Skull Rock in Durotar, Searing Collars burn the Burning Blade cultists who wear them. The heated torcs help attune them to demonic power.",h="At Skull Rock in Durotar, Searing Collars burn the Burning Blade cultists who wear them.",sec={{t="Instruments of Corruption",b="The Burning Blade gathers at Skull Rock, just east of Orgrimmar, for dark rites. Cultists, neophytes, and thugs wear Searing Collars around their necks. The metal brands and sears their skin as they endure its heat.\n\nMargoz, a hermit, studies the cruel devices. He suspects their burning and enchantments attune the wearers to demonic energies. What part do the collars play in the corruption spreading through orc society under the Horde’s nose?",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Searing Collar?",a="Burning Blade cultists wear Searing Collars around their necks in rituals. The heated metal burns their flesh and helps attune them to demonic power.",al={"what are searing collars","searing collar lore","what does the collar do"},it="identity"},{q="Who wears these collars?",a="Members of the Burning Blade hiding inside Skull Rock wear the collars. They include cultists, fanatics, thugs, apprentices, and neophytes.",al={"who uses them","who drops searing collars","burning blade collars"},it="people"},{q="Why do the cultists burn their own flesh?",a="The Burning Blade uses the searing metal in its rituals. By enduring the burns and demonic enchantment, cultists attune their bodies and spirits to demonic power.",al={"why burn their flesh","why wear searing collar","purpose of collar"},it="purpose"},{q="Who wants to inspect the Searing Collars?",a="Margoz, an investigator camping in Durotar, collects Searing Collars to study their enchantments and uncover the Burning Blade’s influence.",al={"who needs searing collars","who is studying the collars","margoz collars"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you may know Searing Collars as crude conduits that channel fel corruption into mortal flesh.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, finding cultists using these collars on Durotar’s doorstep is a grim reminder that the shadow of demonic servitude still lingers."},kw={"burning blade","demon","durotar","fel","margoz","searing collar","skull rock"},rel={"quest:827","quest:828","quest:809","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Searing Collar","Skull Rock (Classic)"}}
E["item:simple-tablet"] = {t="item",n="Simple Tablet",z="durotar",s="At the Valley of Trials, Gornek gives new troll warriors a message to carry to Frang.",h="At the Valley of Trials, Gornek gives new troll warriors a message to carry to Frang.",sec={{t="A Summons to Battle",b="Gornek gives new troll warriors a message from Tar'sere, addressed to Frang, the warrior trainer near the Den. It introduces the recruit to combat training in Durotar and asks them to present themselves to Frang. The message calls them to take up weapons for the Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Simple Tablet?",a="In the Valley of Trials, Gornek gives aspiring troll warriors a message directing them to Frang for combat training.",al={"simple tablet","what is this tablet","troll warrior tablet"},it="identity"},{q="Who sends the tablet?",a="Tar'sere signs the message and directs the recruit to Frang, the warrior trainer outside the Den in the Valley of Trials.",al={"who sent simple tablet","who wrote the tablet","tablet sender"},it="origin"},{q="Where do I take the tablet?",a="Take the Simple Tablet to Frang, who rests outside the Den in the Valley of Trials.",al={"who do i give simple tablet to","where to bring tablet","frang location"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Who receives this tablet?",a="The Simple Tablet goes to troll warriors beginning their rites of passage in the Valley of Trials.",al={"can anyone get simple tablet","which class gets simple tablet"},it="target"},{q="Why does Frang send you the Simple Tablet?",a="Frang doesn't actually write it. Gornek guesses it came from Frang, but the tablet is signed by the troll Tar'sere, who sends you to Frang outside the Den. Frang needs cunning troll warriors to show the orcs how to fight with more than muscle, and he can train you for the Horde's battles ahead.",al={"why simple tablet","why does frang want me","purpose of simple tablet"},it="why_wanted",rc="Troll",add="219776b3"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, the message introduces you to Frang for combat training.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll in Durotar, this summons calls you to strengthen the Horde's frontline ranks alongside the orcs."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","frang","gornek","simple tablet","the den","valley of trials","warrior trainer"},rel={"quest:3065","npc:gornek","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:warrior","topic:troll","subzone:the-den"},src={"Simple Tablet","Simple Tablet (quest)"}}
E["item:taming-rod"] = {t="item",n="Taming Rod",z="durotar",s="In Durotar, Taming Rods help new hunters learn to command beasts. Trainers lend them to students for practice before they form lasting bonds with animal companions.",h="In Durotar, Taming Rods help new hunters learn to command beasts.",sec={{t="A Guide's Training Implement",b="In Razor Hill, trainers such as Thotar give Taming Rods to orc and troll hunters who are just beginning. The enchantment helps them practice before they can bind a wild creature for good. A rod pacifies a local predator, such as a dire mottled boar or an armored scorpid. The hunter learns to give commands and fight beside an animal companion, but the bond lasts only briefly.",sp=0},{t="A Step Toward Mastery",b="Each Taming Rod's magic fades after a short time, and each is attuned to certain kinds of wild beasts. Novices face trials against different temperaments, from docile foragers to aggressive venomous hunters. Once a student shows they can command these beasts, the rod goes back to the trainer. Then the trainer teaches them to tame, call, and dismiss lifelong companions without an artifact.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Taming Rod used for?",a="Hunters use a Taming Rod to practice commanding a beast in battle. A trainer lends it to a young hunter, and its magic briefly pacifies and charms the creature.",al={"what does taming rod do","taming rod use","why do i have a taming rod"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Do I keep the pet I tame with the rod?",a="No. A beast under a Taming Rod's influence is there only for training. The bond ends when the magic fades or you return the rod, and after your trials you learn to tame a lasting companion.",al={"is the pet permanent","do i keep the boar","do i keep the scorpid"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Can I use any Taming Rod on any animal?",a="No. Each Taming Rod is attuned to a particular target creature for that stage of training, such as a dire mottled boar or an armored scorpid.",al={"does the rod work on anything","taming rod targets"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Can I keep the Taming Rod after completing the training?",a="No. You return the Taming Rod to your hunter trainer after your assignment. After your final trial, the trainer teaches you to tame, summon, and dismiss beasts on your own.",al={"keep taming rod","can i save the rod"},it="motive",gp=true},{q="What is a Taming Rod?",a="A Taming Rod is an instructional implement entrusted to novice hunters by their trainers. Enchanted to temporarily bend a wild creature's will to your own, it serves as a training aid. Wielding it allows an aspiring hunter to experience the delicate connection required to command wildlife in battle without permanently bonding before their fundamental skills are fully mastered.",al={"what is a taming rod","taming rod item","taming rod lore"},it="identity",add="c3dba9d3"},{q="Why does a hunter want a Taming Rod?",a="Novice hunters require the rod to prove their developing authority over nature. By successfully subduing dangerous beasts like boars or scorpids, you demonstrate the determination and composure necessary to control a feral mind. Once you have shown your trainer that you can direct these creatures in combat, you are taught the true, lasting arts of beast companionship.",al={"why need taming rod","purpose of taming rod","why use taming rod"},it="why_wanted",add="da578f9f"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you use a Taming Rod to practice before you can form lasting bonds with wild beasts.",["faction:Horde"]="In Durotar and Mulgore, trainers such as Thotar use Taming Rods to test whether young recruits have the discipline to master Kalimdor's harsh wildlife."},kw={"armored scorpid","dire mottled boar","hunter pet","razor hill","taming rod","taming the beast","thotar"},rel={"quest:6061","npc:thotar","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:6081","quest:6065","topic:hunter"},src={"Taming Rod","Taming the Beast (Orc and Troll 1)","Taming the Beast (Orc and Troll 3)"}}
E["item:torch-of-the-dormant-flame"] = {t="item",n="Torch of the Dormant Flame",z="durotar",s="At the Shrine of the Dormant Flame, a shaman stands ready to kindle the Torch of the Dormant Flame. Its fire waits on an ember won atop a mountain in Durotar.",h="At the Shrine of the Dormant Flame, a shaman stands ready to kindle the Torch of the Dormant Flame.",sec={{t="Vessel of Awakening",b="A shaman carries the unlit Torch of the Dormant Flame up the peaks above Durotar, seeking fire's favor. With fire sapta, the shaman sees a Minor Manifestation of Fire atop the mountain and challenges it. When the spirit falls, its glowing ember is placed in the weathered brazier at the Shrine of the Dormant Flame. Then the shaman touches the torch's head to the white-hot blaze, and the wood awakens as a burning emblem of elemental mastery.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Torch of the Dormant Flame?",a="Shaman undertaking the Call of Fire trial receive the unlit ceremonial torch. After a manifestation of fire is defeated, its ember goes into the shrine's brazier. The shaman dips the torch into the white-hot flames, kindling it with elemental power.",al={"what is dormant flame torch","why do i have this unlit torch","what does the torch do"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does this torch get lit?",a="The torch is lit atop the mountain near Telf Joolam in Durotar. After the Minor Manifestation of Fire is defeated, the shaman kindles it at the brazier of the Shrine of the Dormant Flame.",al={"where to light torch of dormant flame","shrine of dormant flame torch","how to ignite dormant torch"},gp=true},{q="Who provides the unlit torch?",a="Kranal Fiss, the shaman living north of the Crossroads, gives initiates the unlit torch and sends them to Telf Joolam, keeper of the Shrine of the Dormant Flame. Telf Joolam recognizes it as the mark of one attempting to tame fire.",al={"who gives torch of dormant flame","dormant torch source","call of fire torch giver"},it="origin"},{q="What is the Torch of the Dormant Flame?",a="It is a ceremonial, unlit torch crafted for a shaman's trial during the Call of Fire. Built to receive the wild essence of elemental flame, it remains completely cold and dormant until plunged into the consecrated brazier atop the Shrine of the Dormant Flame, where it catches fire from the essence of a defeated fire manifestation.",al={"torch of the dormant flame","what is dormant torch","dormant flame torch"},it="identity",add="5b4644ae"},{q="Why does Telf Joolam need the Torch of the Dormant Flame?",a="The torch serves as the vessel to capture and prove your mastery over fire. By igniting its dormant tip in the sacred brazier with the ember of a vanquished manifestation, you bind the elemental spark into a portable flame. Carrying that newly kindled torch back completes your spiritual communion with the element of fire.",al={"why need torch of dormant flame","why want dormant torch","purpose of dormant flame torch"},it="why_wanted",add="c6982489"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you begin with an unproven torch. Defeat a living manifestation of flame to kindle it and earn the right to summon a Fire Totem."},kw={"call of fire","durotar","fire sapta","shaman","shrine of the dormant flame","telf joolam","torch of the dormant flame"},rel={"quest:1524","npc:telf-joolam","item:glowing-ember","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},src={"Torch of the Dormant Flame","Call of Fire (4)"}}
E["item:ukor-s-burden"] = {t="item",n="Ukor's Burden",z="durotar",s="At the Valley of Trials, Ukor’s rejected provisions leave him needing help to carry them back to Razor Hill.",h="At the Valley of Trials, Ukor’s rejected provisions leave him needing help to carry them back to Razor Hill.",sec={{t="A Well-Intentioned Mistake",b="Ukor, an orc peon, rarely acts on his own. Yet he carried provisions from the inn in Razor Hill to feed young recruits in the Valley of Trials. The journey took him through Durotar’s red dust and dangerous wildlife.\n\nThe overseers and instructors refused the food, believing hardship and hunger make true warriors. Now Ukor waits outside the canyon’s mouth, afraid of the beasts on the trail back. He has entrusted the sack to passing travelers and asks them to return it to Innkeeper Grosk.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside Ukor's Burden?",a="Ukor’s Burden holds food and supplies from the Razor Hill inn. Ukor hoped to feed the young orcs and trolls in training, but the Valley of Trials refuses outside provisions.",al={"what is in the pack","ukors burden contents","what food is it"},it="item"},{q="Why did the Valley of Trials reject the food?",a="The overseers in the Valley of Trials believe hardship and hunger build character in young warriors. Innkeeper Grosk says hunger gives recruits spirit, so they refuse outside charity.",al={"why valley of trials refused food","why didnt they want the food","why wasnt the food needed"},it="motive"},{q="Where does the burden need to go?",a="Take the sack back to Innkeeper Grosk at the inn in Razor Hill. He will put the provisions back on the shelves and offer a drink to whoever brings them home.",al={"where do i take ukors burden","who wants ukors burden","ukors burden delivery"},it="target"},{q="What is Ukor's Burden?",a="Ukor's Burden is a heavy load of provisions and foodstuffs originally gathered from the inn in Razor Hill. An earnest peon named Ukor packed the bundle himself, intending to deliver relief to the young warriors training in the harsh crags of the Valley of Trials.",al={"what is ukors burden","ukor's burden","ukors burden item"},it="identity",add="97aa3ffc"},{q="Where does Ukor's Burden come from, and who made it?",a="The burden originated at the Razor Hill inn under the care of Innkeeper Grosk. Ukor, a well-meaning orc peon, hauled the load all the way down the road past dangerous scorpions and spiders to reach the proving grounds, only to find his efforts were unwanted.",al={"where did ukors burden come from","who made ukors burden","origin of ukor burden"},it="origin",add="1b425e9c"},{q="Why does anyone want Ukor's Burden?",a="After the trainers in the Valley of Trials turned down the provisions, Innkeeper Grosk needs the food returned to stock back on the shelves in Razor Hill. Terrified of the wild beasts prowling the Durotar wilderness, Ukor relies on passing travelers to carry it safely home.",al={"why does grosk want ukors burden","why return ukors burden","who wants ukor's burden"},it="why_wanted",add="32c1e657"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see how Durotar’s harsh trials shape new soldiers. Even a kind offer must yield to the demands of their training."},kw={"durotar","grosk","peon","rations","razor hill","ukor","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:ukor","npc:innkeeper-grosk","quest:2161","subzone:razor-hill","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},src={"Ukor's Burden","A Peon's Burden"}}
E["item:uncloven-satyr-hoof"] = {t="item",n="Uncloven Satyr Hoof",z="durotar",s="In Ashenvale, Uncloven Satyr Hooves hold the power satyrs steal from the ancient forest. Ula'elek uses that power to forge armor in Sen'jin Village.",h="In Ashenvale, Uncloven Satyr Hooves hold the power satyrs steal from the ancient forest.",sec={{t="Leeched Power",b="Satyrs haunt the corrupted groves of northeastern Ashenvale, feeding on the ancient forest’s magic. The more they consume, the more corruption twists their demonic bodies. Their hooves swell and lose their cleft, becoming dense stores of the energy they have absorbed. Skilled shamans and leatherworkers can harvest that volatile power.",sp=0},{t="Crafting the Brutal Armor",b="At Sen'jin Village on Durotar’s coast, Ula'elek turns demonic corruption into strength for Horde champions. The troll armorer takes hooves from satyrs that have fed on the forest and draws out their trapped magic. Then he channels that stolen power into brutal gauntlets, armor for young warriors facing the rigors of Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are these satyr hooves uncloven?",a="Satyrs in Ashenvale feed on the forest’s sacred magic and corrupt it as they leech its power. Those that gorge themselves most develop swollen hooves that lose their cleft and hold the dense, stolen energy inside.",al={"why are they not cloven","uncloven hoof meaning","swollen hooves"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Uncloven Satyr Hooves be found?",a="Satyrs in the corrupted ruins and tainted groves of northeastern Ashenvale carry these hooves, including those near Satyrnaar and Night Run.",al={"where to farm hooves","satyr hoof location","which satyrs drop hooves"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants these hooves in Durotar?",a="Ula'elek, an armorer in Sen'jin Village on Durotar’s southern coast, asks for seven hooves so he can draw out their stored magic.",al={"who needs satyr hooves","satyr hoof quest giver","what to do with hooves"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What are the hooves used to craft?",a="Ula'elek draws corrupt forest power from the hooves to forge a pair of sturdy, magic-infused brutal gauntlets.",al={"what are they used for","hoof crafting reward","brutal gauntlets materials"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does an Uncloven Satyr Hoof come from?",a="These hooves are taken directly from the satyrs lurking in northeastern Ashenvale. Rather than being crafted, they are natural body parts warped by dark gluttony. Satyrs in the forest gorge themselves on Ashenvale's pure natural energies, and the demons that consume the greatest surplus of this stolen magic develop distinctive swollen, uncloven hooves.",al={"where do uncloven satyr hooves come from","who made uncloven satyr hoof","source of satyr hooves"},it="origin",add="81ca4f2a"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a young warrior seeking renown, you can prove your martial prowess by hunting Ashenvale’s satyrs and commissioning specialized armor from Horde trainers in Sen'jin Village.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you share the Darkspear crafters’ skill at turning dark or hostile energies into useful gear. Ula'elek leeches power from demonic foes instead of letting it go to waste."},kw={"ashenvale","durotar","gauntlets","hoof","satyr","sen'jin","ula'elek","uncloven"},rel={"quest:1842","npc:ula-elek","quest:1843","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:ashenvale","zone:durotar","topic:satyr"},src={"Uncloven Satyr Hoof","Satyr Hooves"}}
E["item:venomtail-antidote"] = {t="item",n="Venomtail Antidote",z="durotar",s="In Durotar, Rhinag lies stricken by scorpid venom, and time is running short. Kor'ghan brews the antidote in Orgrimmar for the scout near the northwestern border.",h="In Durotar, Rhinag lies stricken by scorpid venom, and time is running short.",sec={{t="A Race Against the Venom",b="A deep sting from Durotar's venomtail scorpids can kill a warrior within an hour. Rhinag, a troll scout, was envenomed near the northwestern border, far from aid. His only hope is a remedy from Kor'ghan, an apothecary in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow.",sp=0},{t="Kor'ghan's Cure",b="Kor'ghan works beneath Orgrimmar, where he knows desert toxins and harsh remedies. He prepares a vial to purge the venom before it turns fatal. The draught stops the poison and spares Rhinag a humiliating death in the wilderness. Even so, Kor'ghan demands further trials and hunts from the scout to atone for his carelessness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Venomtail Antidote used for?",a="Venomtail Antidote counters the deadly venom of venomtail scorpids. Rhinag, an envenomed troll near Durotar's northwestern border, needs it before the poison kills him.",al={"antidote purpose","who needs venomtail antidote","what does venomtail antidote do"},it="purpose"},{q="Who brews the Venomtail Antidote?",a="Kor'ghan brews the antidote in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar. He knows Durotar's scorpid toxins and how to counter their stings.",al={"who makes the antidote","where to get venomtail antidote","kor'ghan antidote"},it="origin"},{q="Why is time so critical when obtaining the antidote?",a="Venomtail poison can kill Rhinag within an hour of the sting. You must secure the antidote and rush it back across Durotar to save his life.",al={"why hurry antidote","how long does rhinag have","venomtail poison timer"},it="danger"},{q="Why is Rhinag hesitant to seek help in Sen'jin Village?",a="Rhinag is embarrassed to have fallen to a common scorpid. He fears his kin in Sen'jin Village will mock his carelessness and stupidity if he returns weakened.",al={"why not go to sen'jin","rhinag pride","why hide in durotar"},it="motive"},{q="What is Venomtail Antidote?",a="Venomtail Antidote is a specialized concoction crafted to neutralize the deadly poison of Durotar's venomtail scorpids. Without it, anyone stung deeply by these aggressive beasts faces a rapid and agonizing death as the toxin spreads through their blood.",al={"what is venomtail antidote","venomtail antidote info","venomtail cure"},it="identity",add="ba1b91bb"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you know pride runs deep. Rhinag would rather risk dying alone in the wastes than face open mockery in Sen'jin Village for being bested by a scorpid.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face Durotar's unforgiving desert. Saving Rhinag calls for swift coordination between wilderness scouts and city apothecaries."},kw={"antidote","cleft of shadow","cure","durotar","kor'ghan","orgrimmar","rhinag","scorpid","venomtail"},rel={"quest:812","quest:813","npc:rhinag","npc:kor-ghan","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Venomtail Antidote","Need for a Cure"}}
E["item:venomtail-poison-sac"] = {t="item",n="Venomtail Poison Sac",z="durotar",s="In Durotar, a scorpion's venom can bring a hunter near death, and its poison sac holds what alchemists need for a cure.",h="In Durotar, a scorpion's venom can bring a hunter near death, and its poison sac holds what alchemists need...",sec={{t="A Deadly Toxin and Its Remedy",b="Scorpids roam Durotar’s red rocks. Venomtail Scorpids, Corrupted Scorpids, and the Death Flayer all carry sacs filled with fast-acting venom. Left untreated, the poison can overwhelm even seasoned warriors. Yet those same sacs hold the chief compounds alchemists need for an antidote.\n\nWhen a scorpion stung the hunter Rhinag outside Orgrimmar, local alchemists needed four fresh poison sacs. They would use them to make a remedy and neutralize the venom in his veins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures carry these poison sacs?",a="Durotar’s scorpids carry these poison sacs, especially Venomtail Scorpids near Orgrimmar. Corrupted Scorpids and the rare Death Flayer carry them too.",al={"who drops venomtail poison sac","where to get venomtail poison sac","which scorpids have poison sacs"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="What is the poison sac used for?",a="Kor'ghan in Orgrimmar uses the sacs to distill a specialized antidote. Rhinag needs it after being stung and poisoned while hunting without proper preparation.",al={"venomtail sac use","why do i need venomtail poison sac"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who can brew the antidote from these sacs?",a="Kor'ghan in Orgrimmar can refine the raw venom from four intact sacs into a curative draft. He must do so before the poison proves fatal.",al={"who brews the antidote","where to turn in venomtail sacs","kor'ghan venomtail"}},{q="What is a Venomtail Poison Sac?",a="A Venomtail Poison Sac is the venom-producing organ harvested from the dangerous scorpids that prowl Durotar, most notably the venomtail scorpids lurking near the gates of Orgrimmar. The fluid inside carries an exceptionally potent and fast-acting toxin, making the creatures a deadly threat to any careless hunter who wanders the arid red wastes.",al={"what is venomtail poison sac","venomtail poison sac lore","about venomtail sac"},it="identity",add="7ee9d5ba"},{q="Where does a Venomtail Poison Sac come from?",a="These sacs are harvested directly from the scorpids indigenous to the harsh plains of Durotar, including venomtail scorpids, corrupted scorpids, and death flayers. They are natural anatomical organs of the beasts, biological reservoirs developed by the scorpids to subdue prey and defend against predators in the unforgiving wasteland.",al={"where do venomtail poison sacs come from","who drops venomtail sac","venomtail poison sac origin"},it="origin",add="c7932c21"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a young Horde adventurer in Durotar, you learn that local toxins can kill those who rush into the red wastes unprepared.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, take Rhinag’s misfortune as a warning. Pursuing dangerous beasts without knowing their venom or carrying a remedy can cost you your life."},kw={"antidote","durotar","kor'ghan","poison","rhinag","sac","scorpid","venomtail"},rel={"quest:813","quest:812","item:venomtail-antidote","npc:kor-ghan","npc:rhinag","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Venomtail Poison Sac","Finding the Antidote"}}
E["item:vile-familiar-head"] = {t="item",n="Vile Familiar Head",z="durotar",s="Near the Burning Blade Coven, Vile Familiar Heads test young Horde warlocks. Under Ruzan's guidance, novices gather six gruesome trophies to prove they are ready to bind their first demonic minions. The trial calls for discipline and respect for the danger of the beings they mean to summon.",h="Near the Burning Blade Coven, Vile Familiar Heads test young Horde warlocks.",sec={{t="A Gruesome Lesson in Demonology",b="In the Valley of Trials, Ruzan asks novices who seek to learn summoning to bring him six Vile Familiar Heads. The fiery imps called vile familiars lurk outside the Burning Blade Coven. Their elemental cunning makes them dangerous foes. To pass, novices must face and defeat them, proving they can master demonic life rather than be overcome by it.\n\nWarlocks are barely tolerated within Thrall's Horde, so their training demands care. A novice slain by a conjured creature would deepen the dishonor and suspicion cast upon those who practice the dark arts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Vile Familiar Heads used for?",a="The heads prove a novice warlock's readiness in the Valley of Trials. Ruzan requires six before teaching an apprentice to summon a first imp minion.",al={"vile familiar head purpose","what are these heads for","ruzan quest item"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where do vile familiars come from?",a="Vile familiars gather at the mouth and inside a cave northeast within the Valley of Trials. The cave holds the secretive and malevolent Burning Blade Coven.",al={"vile familiar location","where to find vile familiars","burning blade coven cave"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Ruzan make young warlocks collect these heads?",a="Ruzan expects a warlock to overpower a creature before summoning it. Imps deceive their foes and hurl volatile fire, so defeating them face-to-face teaches apprentices the danger of the demons they mean to command.",al={"why collect heads","ruzan motive","why kill familiars first"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How does the Horde view warlocks who collect such trophies?",a="The modern Horde tolerates warlocks without embracing them. Betrayals tied to fel magic left deep distrust, so Ruzan and other trainers insist apprentices study with discipline and discretion.",al={"are warlocks accepted","horde warlock reputation","distrusted warlocks"},it="conflict"},{q="What is a Vile Familiar Head?",a="It is the severed head of a vile familiar, one of the minor impish demons found lurking outside the Burning Blade Coven in the Valley of Trials. For a novice warlock studying in Durotar, carrying these grisly trophies serves as proof of having defeated an imp in direct combat.",al={"what is vile familiar head","vile familiar head item","vile familiar trophy"},it="identity",add="07ac30a7"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="For a warlock, collecting these heads is an early step toward mastery over the Nether and the right to summon and bind an imp into servitude.",["faction:Horde"]="Even in Durotar's training grounds, warlocks practice on the fringes, mindful of the lingering suspicion with which the Horde watches their demonic pursuits."},kw={"burning blade coven","durotar","imp","ruzan","valley of trials","vile familiar","vile familiar head","warlock quest"},rel={"quest:792","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:burning-blade-coven","topic:warlock","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},src={"Vile Familiar Head","Vile Familiars (Warlock)"}}
E["item:zalazane-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Zalazane's Head",z="durotar",s="Master Gadrin seeks proof that Zalazane has fallen. The Darkspear long for relief from the witch doctor who drove them from the Echo Isles.",h="Master Gadrin seeks proof that Zalazane has fallen.",sec={{t="Proof of the Traitor's End",b="Master Gadrin asks you to prove that Zalazane is dead. The witch doctor betrayed the Darkspear and seized their island home with hexes that enslaved minds. His magic drove Vol'jin's people to Durotar's shores.\n\nFrom the Echo Isles, Zalazane still sends hexed thralls across the water to seize more victims. Sen'jin Village needs proof that his rule has ended. His severed head confirms his defeat and brings the displaced tribe some peace, with hope of reclaiming their stolen islands one day.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks for Zalazane's Head?",a="Master Gadrin asks for Zalazane's Head as proof that Zalazane has been slain. He is a witch doctor in Sen'jin Village on Durotar's southern coast.",al={"who wants zalazane head","zalazane quest giver","gadrin zalazane"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why was Zalazane targeted?",a="Zalazane was once a respected sorcerer among the Darkspear. His lust for power led him to enslave his kin with mind-controlling magic, drive the tribe from the Echo Isles, and raid the mainland for more Darkspear to bind as thralls.",al={"why kill zalazane","what did zalazane do","zalazane lore"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Zalazane found?",a="Zalazane lives on the largest of the Echo Isles, off Durotar's southeastern coast. Hexed and voodoo trolls bound to his service surround him.",al={"where is zalazane","zalazane location","echo isles zalazane"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does bringing the head reclaim the Echo Isles?",a="Killing Zalazane ends the immediate threat of his raids and brings relief to Sen'jin Village. Yet the Echo Isles remain dangerous and filled with lingering voodoo thralls, and the Darkspear remain largely based on the mainland.",al={"do trolls get echo isles back","is echo isles reclaimed","echo isles safe"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Zalazane's Head?",a="It is the severed head of the witch doctor Zalazane, taken after striking him down on the Echo Isles. More than a grim trophy, it serves as undeniable proof that the rogue sorcerer who betrayed the Darkspear tribe and drove them from their island home has finally been slain.",al={"zalazane head what is it","what is zalazanes head","zalazane head item"},it="identity",add="a9dad833"},{q="Where does Zalazane's Head come from?",a="It comes directly from the traitorous witch doctor Zalazane himself, claiming it after defeating him at his camp on the largest of the Echo Isles. It was not crafted, but taken by force to put an end to his enslavement of fellow Darkspear trolls.",al={"who made zalazane head","where do you get zalazanes head","origin of zalazanes head"},it="origin",add="c704c705"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, claiming Zalazane's head is an act of vengeance and justice against the traitor who drove your people into exile and enslaved your brothers.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure Durotar's southern coast by eliminating Zalazane and stopping his dark magic from undermining Thrall's newly founded territories."},kw={"darkspear","echo isles","gadrin","hexed troll","sen'jin village","voodoo troll","zalazane","zalazane's head"},rel={"quest:826","subzone:echo-isles","subzone:sen-jin-village","topic:darkspear-tribe","quest:808","zone:durotar","npc:vol-jin"},src={"Zalazane's Head","Zalazane (quest)"}}
E["npc:canaga-earthcaller"] = {t="npc",n="Canaga Earthcaller",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Canaga Earthcaller guides new Horde shamans toward the land's spirits and their first totems.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Canaga Earthcaller guides new Horde shamans toward the land's spirits and their...",sec={{t="Voice of the Land",b="From the red bluffs of the Valley of Trials, Canaga Earthcaller guides Darkspear trolls and orcs as they begin the shaman’s path. He teaches them to quiet their minds and listen to Kalimdor’s rumblings. Then they prepare earth sapta to commune with the spirits.",sp=0},{t="The First Totem",b="Canaga sends each novice to gather sacred reagents and travel to the local spirit rock in Durotar. There, they drink earth sapta and see the elemental spirits firsthand. With his guidance, they earn their Earth Totem.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Canaga Earthcaller?",a="Canaga Earthcaller is a Darkspear troll shaman who mentors young shamans in the Valley of Trials as they take their first steps in the Horde.",al={"canaga lore","who is canaga","canaga earthcaller npc"},it="identity"},{q="What does Canaga teach young shamans?",a="Canaga guides Horde shamans through the Call of Earth ritual chain in Durotar. He brews Earth Sapta so initiates can perceive and speak with the local earth elemental spirit as they seek their first totem.",al={"shaman quest durotar","call of earth durotar","canaga quests"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Earth Sapta Canaga prepares?",a="Earth Sapta is a spiritual draught Canaga brews from regional reagents. Shamans drink it to open their senses to the land’s hidden spirits and speak with elemental manifestations.",al={"what is earth sapta","sapta lore"},it="item"},{q="Why is a troll training shamans in an orcish proving ground?",a="After the Third War, the Darkspear tribe joined closely with Thrall’s Horde and settled alongside the orcs in Durotar. Troll shamans and warriors now train beside young orcs in the Valley of Trials.",al={"why troll in valley of trials","darkspear in valley of trials"},it="why_here"},{q="Where can Canaga Earthcaller be found?",a="Canaga sits on rock plateaus overlooking the Valley of Trials’ eastern paths, just south of the main training hub.",al={"canaga location","where is canaga"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Canaga Earthcaller on?",a="Canaga serves the Horde, guiding fledging shamans of both the Darkspear trolls and the orcs. Stationed in the Valley of Trials, he aids young initiates in forging their initial communion with the elemental spirits of Durotar on behalf of Warchief Thrall's newly established realm.",al={"canaga earthcaller faction","is canaga horde","who does canaga serve"},it="side",add="9fbe2a10"},{q="What does Canaga Earthcaller want?",a="Canaga seeks to ensure that emerging shamans properly attune to the spirits of the earth. He tests hopeful initiates by tasking them to gather sacred reagents, drink the Earth Sapta, and commune directly with local elemental manifestations.",al={"what does canaga want","canaga earthcaller goal","canaga purpose"},it="wants",add="911868d9"},{q="Who is Canaga Earthcaller tied to?",a="Canaga belongs to the Darkspear tribe and collaborates directly with the orcish shamanic teachers in the Valley of Trials, guiding young trolls and orcs alike through the Call of Earth.",al={"canaga earthcaller ties","who does canaga work with","canaga allies"},it="ties",add="f7883336"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you meet Canaga as your first spiritual mentor in Durotar. He prepares Earth Sapta so you can commune with the elements and claim your Earth Totem.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you find Canaga among the prominent Darkspear figures in the Valley of Trials. He guides young troll shamans as they begin their path with the spirits.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you find Canaga working alongside orcish instructors in the valley. He helps young orcs bind their spirits to the harsh soil of their new homeland."},kw={"call of earth","canaga","darkspear","durotar","earth sapta","earthcaller","shaman","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:1516","quest:1462","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Canaga Earthcaller"}}
E["npc:elder-runetotem"] = {t="npc",n="Elder Runetotem",z="durotar",s="During the Lunar Festival, Elder Runetotem appears outside Razor Hill in Durotar. The tauren spirit offers travelers wisdom and a blessing.",h="During the Lunar Festival, Elder Runetotem appears outside Razor Hill in Durotar.",sec={{t="A Spirit in Durotar",b="Elder Runetotem appears beside Razor Hill, far from Mulgore's grassy plains and sacred burial grounds. Her presence brings the ancient traditions of the Shu'halo to the Horde's home along the Great Sea.",sp=0},{t="Ancestral Honors",b="During the Lunar Festival, spirits of great leaders, shamans, and heroes appear throughout the world to commune with the living. Elder Runetotem bears a name from a line that reveres the Earth Mother and seeks spiritual communion. Travelers who honor her receive ancestral tokens and her blessing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Runetotem?",a="Elder Runetotem is a tauren ancestor who appears near Razor Hill in Durotar during the Lunar Festival. She greets travelers and offers ancestral blessings.",al={"elder runetotem lore","who is the tauren ghost in razor hill","runetotem ghost"},it="identity"},{q="Why is a tauren spirit located in Durotar?",a="Most tauren ancestral spirits are rooted in Mulgore, but Lunar Festival spirits travel across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms. In Razor Hill, Horde travelers passing through Durotar can pay their respects to the wisdom of the Earth Mother's children.",al={"why is runetotem in razor hill","tauren ghost durotar"},it="why_here"},{q="What connection does she have to the Runetotem tribe?",a="Elder Runetotem bears the name of the Runetotem clan, a prominent tauren lineage known for its shamans, spiritual guides, and ties to the natural world.",al={"runetotem tribe elder","runetotem family"},it="ties"},{q="What does speaking with her grant?",a="Speaking with Elder Runetotem during the Lunar Festival honors her memory and grants a Coin of Ancestry and a temporary blessing from the spirits.",al={"what does elder runetotem give","runetotem reward"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Elder Runetotem on?",a="Elder Runetotem takes no side in the wars of the living. As an honored ancestral spirit of the tauren, she offers her ancient wisdom and blessings to any adventurer, Horde or Alliance, who respects the ways of the ancestors.",al={"is elder runetotem horde","elder runetotem faction","elder runetotem side"},it="side",add="c76d680b"},{q="What does Elder Runetotem want?",a="She seeks to share the remembrance and reverence of the tauren people with travelers passing through Razor Hill. By reaching out to the living, she reminds travelers of the ancestral spirits watching over the lands and keeping ancient traditions alive.",al={"what does elder runetotem seek","why talk to elder runetotem","elder runetotem goal"},it="wants",add="021a9c1d"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, finding a venerable ancestor of the Runetotem tribe far from Mulgore reminds you that the spirits of the Shu'halo watch over their allies across all lands.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can find Elder Runetotem outside Razor Hill. Her presence reflects the spiritual alliance between the orcs of Durotar and the tauren of Mulgore."},kw={"coin of ancestry","durotar","elder runetotem","lunar festival","razor hill","runetotem","tauren ghost"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:8670","topic:tauren","zone:mulgore","subzone:red-rocks"},src={"Elder Runetotem"}}
E["npc:foreman-thazz-ril"] = {t="npc",n="Foreman Thazz'ril",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Foreman Thazz'ril keeps the peons at work. Crews gather what the encampment and young warriors need, but sleepers and nearby cultists test his patience.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Foreman Thazz'ril keeps the peons at work.",sec={{t="Keeping the Peons in Line",b="In the Valley of Trials, Foreman Thazz'ril directs peons as they chop lumber and gather materials for the encampment and young warriors. Durotar's harsh red rock demands steady labor, but the peons often nap beneath the desert sun. So Thazz'ril sends newly arrived recruits to rouse them with his blackjack and keep construction moving.",sp=0},{t="A Lost Pick in Dangerous Hands",b="Thazz'ril was scouting the Burning Blade Coven for mineral resources when dark cultists drove him to flee. In his haste, he left behind his treasured enchanted pick. Warlocks and their demonic minions now gather in the cave. Too cautious to retrieve it himself, Thazz'ril depends on young Horde aspirants to venture into the depths and bring it back.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Foreman Thazz'ril?",a="Foreman Thazz'ril is an orc labor supervisor in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. He manages work crews, oversees lumber chopping, and scouts the region for resources to aid the Horde's settlement.",al={"who is thazzril","thazzril valley of trials","foreman thazzril lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Thazz'ril give players a blackjack?",a="The peons under Thazz'ril's watch often sleep instead of gathering lumber. He gives recruits an enchanted wooden blackjack to rouse them and send them back to work.",al={"why hit lazy peons","thazzril blackjack","lazy peons quest lore"}},{q="Why is Thazz'ril's pick inside the Burning Blade cave?",a="Thazz'ril left his enchanted pick in the Burning Blade Coven while scouting for mineral veins. He fled when he encountered the cultists inside.",al={"thazzril pick","why is pick in coven","burning blade pick"}},{q="What is his role in the Horde?",a="Thazz'ril is a civilian overseer, not a frontline soldier or shaman. He supervises manual labor, keeps construction supplies ready, and keeps the peons productive.",al={"is thazzril a soldier","thazzril rank"}},{q="Whose side is Foreman Thazz'ril on?",a="Thazz'ril is loyal to Thrall's Horde. Stationed in the Valley of Trials, he oversees the fundamental labor and resource gathering that helps build Durotar and sustain the training grounds for incoming orc and troll recruits.",al={"foreman thazzril allegiance","thazzril horde","thazzril faction"},it="side",add="607050fc"},{q="What does Foreman Thazz'ril want?",a="Thazz'ril primarily wants his workers to actually work. Exasperated by lazy peons slacking off around the valley, he recruits young adventurers to wake them up. He also seeks the recovery of his prized enchanted pick, which he unfortunately abandoned near the Burning Blade's coven.",al={"thazzril goals","what does thazzril need","thazzril quest motive"},it="wants",add="f77b2dd2"},{q="Why is Foreman Thazz'ril here?",a="He is assigned to the Valley of Trials to direct peon labor and manage local mining and wood-gathering efforts. Maintaining the settlement and keeping raw materials flowing is essential to preparing young warriors before they venture into the wider lands of Durotar.",al={"why is thazzril in the valley of trials","thazzril location reason"},it="why_here",add="ee1167cb"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As a young orc coming of age, you see how Horde strength on the battlefield depends on disciplined labor.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can see how much Thazz'ril values his equipment. He is desperate to recover his enchanted pick from the Burning Blade Coven."},kw={"blackjack","burning blade","durotar","foreman","lazy peons","thazzril","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:lazy-peons","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:burning-blade-coven","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},src={"Foreman Thazz'ril"}}
E["npc:furl-scornbrow"] = {t="npc",n="Furl Scornbrow",z="durotar",s="Northwest of Razor Hill, Furl Scornbrow keeps watch over Durotar. Too old for the front lines, he makes sturdy packs for young travelers.",h="Northwest of Razor Hill, Furl Scornbrow keeps watch over Durotar.",sec={{t="Watchman of the Ridge",b="From a wooden tower northwest of Razor Hill, Furl Scornbrow watches Durotar’s central plains. In the tense days after Orgrimmar was founded, sentries like him sounded their horns against hostile quilboar, centaur, and Kul Tiras interlopers. Since then, Durotar has grown more stable, and Razor Hill has secured its borders. Emergencies come less often, leaving Furl long, quiet hours at his post.",sp=0},{t="A Useful Pair of Hands",b="Furl says his old bones and fading strength keep him from fighting. Yet an orc does not easily surrender their purpose. He puts his hands to work making canvas sacks and packs for fresh recruits who carry supplies. In exchange for coarse thread and practical materials, he equips green adventurers setting out to prove their worth to the Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Furl Scornbrow?",a="Furl Scornbrow keeps watch from a lookout tower atop the bluffs northwest of Razor Hill. Too old for the front lines, he watches for danger and makes bags for young travelers.",al={"who is furl","furl scornbrow lore","furl in razor hill"},it="identity"},{q="What is Furl's role in Durotar?",a="Furl mans the signal horn tower and watches for invaders approaching Razor Hill. With Durotar more secure under Horde control, he sounds the alarm less often and spends quiet hours helping recruits organize their gear.",al={"what does furl do","furl purpose"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Furl ask travelers for materials?",a="Furl asks travelers for materials because he believes every member of the Horde must carry their weight. Unable to fight, he stitches practical travel packs for newer warriors and asks only for basics such as coarse thread.",al={"carry your weight quest lore","why does furl want thread"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Furl Scornbrow on?",a="Furl stands firmly with the Horde. Positioned high above Razor Hill, he keeps watch over Durotar to protect the young orcish realm from potential invaders and aids travelers who serve the Warchief.",al={"furl scornbrow faction","furl scornbrow horde","is furl horde"},it="side",add="1ce1cc0b"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Furl shows the orcish belief that age need not end a warrior’s service. Though he has lost his strength in battle, he continues to serve the Horde with honor.",["faction:Horde"]="Furl’s watch along the ridges outside Razor Hill reflects the vigilance needed to protect Durotar’s young settlements from lingering threats."},kw={"carry your weight","durotar","furl scornbrow","lookout","orc","razor hill","watchtower"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:791"},src={"Furl Scornbrow"}}
E["npc:galgar"] = {t="npc",n="Galgar",z="durotar",s="Near the Den in the Valley of Trials, Galgar feeds young Horde recruits. He asks newcomers to gather wild cactus apples for his Cactus Apple Surprise.",h="Near the Den in the Valley of Trials, Galgar feeds young Horde recruits.",sec={{t="A Cook in the Valley",b="Galgar cooks by the Den's fire in the Valley of Trials. He feeds young orcs and trolls through their first rites of passage. Durotar is a dry, harsh red wasteland, so food must be found across the land. Galgar sends novice warriors to gather ripe cactus fruit, testing their attention and resilience while stocking his kitchen.",sp=0},{t="Cactus Apple Surprise",b="Galgar calls his specialty Cactus Apple Surprise. He says gathering spiny desert fruit is a simple way to ease fresh recruits into adventuring. The dish still feeds hungry trainees. Every Horde warrior begins somewhere, and Galgar starts them by foraging in the desert.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Galgar?",a="Galgar is near the central campfire and cooking area outside the Den, in the Valley of Trials. The canyon lies in southwestern Durotar and is where orcs and trolls begin.",al={"galgar location","where is galgar","galgar coordinates"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Galgar ask adventurers to do?",a="Galgar asks new adventurers to gather ripe cactus apples from wild cacti scattered across the Valley of Trials. He uses them to prepare his Cactus Apple Surprise.",al={"galgar quest","what does galgar want"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why does Galgar send new recruits to pick fruit?",a="Galgar says the task is simple. It gives fledgling fighters an early chore to learn the valley and practice self-sufficiency in Durotar's harsh wilderness.",al={"why cactus apples","galgar test"},it="motive"},{q="What is Cactus Apple Surprise?",a="Cactus Apple Surprise is Galgar's signature recipe. He makes it with fresh cactus apples gathered from Durotar's native desert plants to feed novice recruits.",al={"what is cactus apple surprise","galgar food"},it="item"},{q="Who is Galgar?",a="Galgar is an orc cook stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. Rather than training warriors in brute combat, he supports the settlement by preparing hearty provisions for the young recruits, most notably his well-known cactus apple surprise.",al={"who is galgar","galgar lore","who galgar"},it="identity",add="115dfff8"},{q="Whose side is Galgar on?",a="Galgar is loyal to Thrall's Horde. Serving inside the Valley of Trials, he tends directly to the fledgling orcs and trolls taking their first steps in service to Durotar.",al={"galgar faction","is galgar horde","galgar allegiance"},it="side",add="7f3ad096"},{q="What does Galgar want?",a="Galgar wants fresh ingredients—primarily the ripe cactus apples that grow across the arid valley—so he can brew batches of his signature cactus apple surprise to keep the young recruits fed and energized.",al={"what does galgar need","galgar goal","galgar wants"},it="wants",add="d4d57a6c"},{q="Why is Galgar here in the Valley of Trials?",a="Galgar is stationed in the Valley of Trials to support the encampment's kitchen. While trainers instruct aspirants in the art of war, Galgar ensures the grounds remain supplied with food and introduces new arrivals to basic field work.",al={"why is galgar here","galgar valley of trials reason","why is galgar in durotar"},it="why_here",add="50f967f0"},{q="Why is Galgar famous?",a="Galgar is known throughout the Valley of Trials for his famous recipe, Cactus Apple Surprise. Almost every young recruit passing through the den tastes his cooking while performing introductory chores for him.",al={"is galgar famous","what is galgar known for","galgar fame"},it="fame",add="2e1d8215"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Galgar cooks in the Horde's practical, rustic way. He uses Durotar's sparse natural resources to feed recruits and keep them ready for battle.",["race:Orc"]="As a young orc in the Valley of Trials, you gather fruit for Galgar as a familiar rite of passage before facing fiercer wilderness threats."},kw={"cactus apple surprise","cactus apples","cook","durotar","galgar","horde recruit","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:galgar-s-cactus-apple-surprise","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},src={"Galgar"}}
E["npc:gar-thok"] = {t="npc",n="Gar'Thok",z="durotar",s="At Razor Hill, Gar'Thok directs recruits from the Valley of Trials as they help secure Durotar. The veteran orc warrior survived the Kul Tiras landings on Durotar's coast. Now he coordinates the defense against human encroachers and native threats.",h="At Razor Hill, Gar'Thok directs recruits from the Valley of Trials as they help secure Durotar.",sec={{t="A Veteran of the Red Wastes",b="After the Third War, Gar'Thok marched to Durotar under Warchief Thrall. In the first days of building the new homeland, he served as a lieutenant under Nazgrel.\n\nWhen Rexxar, the half-ogre wanderer, arrived in Durotar, Gar'Thok warned him that quilboar were raiding the settlement's perimeter. He enlisted the beastmaster to protect the fragile new settlement.",sp=0},{t="Surviving the Admiral's Invasion",b="Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's Kul Tiras fleet landed on Durotar's eastern shores, and Gar'Thok's resolve was tested. At an outlying watch post, he saw naval marines overwhelm and slaughter his garrison. His forces were decimated, but Gar'Thok survived.\n\nThe surprise assault left him vigilant. Surviving marines still occupy Tiragarde Keep and the coastal shipwrecks.",sp=0},{t="Defense of Razor Hill",b="From Razor Hill's barracks, Gar'Thok oversees the defense of central Durotar. He sends emerging Horde warriors, shamans, and scouts to drive out hostile Kul Tiran remnants, reclaim salvaged supplies, and recover military orders left in the coastal ruins.\n\nDurotar's safety is far from assured. Gar'Thok keeps pressure on those who challenge the Horde's right to this soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gar'Thok?",a="At Razor Hill, Gar'Thok is an orc officer who organizes Durotar's military response to hostile forces. A veteran of the Third War, he served under Nazgrel during the founding of Orgrimmar.",al={"garthok lore","who is garthok","razor hill commander"},it="identity"},{q="Where did Gar'Thok fight before coming to Razor Hill?",a="Before reaching Razor Hill, Gar'Thok served as Nazgrel's lieutenant at a frontier outpost in Durotar. He worked with Rexxar to quell early quilboar raids. Kul Tiran sailors overran the post and slew his men.",al={"garthok past","garthok mount hyjal","garthok history"},it="history"},{q="Why does Gar'Thok hate the humans in Durotar so much?",a="During Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's invasion, Kul Tiras sailors ambushed Gar'Thok's coastal outpost and butchered his men. Gar'Thok survived and remains dedicated to eradicating the remaining marine encampments.",al={"why garthok hates kul tiras","garthok humans","tiragarde keep garthok"},it="motive"},{q="What threats does Gar'Thok send adventurers to fight?",a="Gar'Thok sends recruits against hostile Kul Tiran sailors at Tiragarde Keep, to reclaim supplies from coastal shipwrecks, push back invading quilboar, and uncover orders left by human commanders.",al={"garthok quests","what does garthok want","razor hill quests"},it="threat"},{q="What is his relationship with Nazgrel and Thrall?",a="Gar'Thok served as Nazgrel's trusted lieutenant during the first colonizing expeditions in Durotar, under Warchief Thrall. Together, they helped secure the borders of the newly claimed territory.",al={"garthok nazgrel","garthok thrall","garthok rank"},it="ties"},{q="Where can Gar'Thok be found?",a="Gar'Thok can be found outside Razor Hill's main watchtower and barracks. Razor Hill is Durotar's central settlement, south of Orgrimmar.",al={"garthok location","where is garthok","find garthok"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Gar'Thok on?",a="Gar'Thok is wholly loyal to the Horde and Warchief Thrall. Stationed in Durotar under the command of Nazgrel, he works tirelessly to defend the nascent orc homeland and ensure newly arrived warriors are prepared to protect the Horde's borders.",al={"gar'thok faction","is gar'thok horde","who does garthok serve"},it="side",add="61b8b646"},{q="What does Gar'Thok want?",a="Gar'Thok wants Durotar firmly secured against all threats. Having watched his outpost slaughtered by Kul Tiras invaders, he seeks vengeance against the remaining human sailors on the coast and demands the suppression of encroaching quilboar that harass the settlement.",al={"gar'thok goal","what does garthok want","garthok motives"},it="wants",add="7b499593"},{q="Why is Gar'Thok here?",a="Following the devastation of his coastal outpost by Kul Tiran forces, Gar'Thok took up a post in Razor Hill. From this central settlement, he organizes the defense of Durotar and directs budding Horde champions against hostile incursions.",al={"why is gar'thok in razor hill","why is garthok here","garthok duty razor hill"},it="why_here",add="007248aa"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For young orcs leaving the Valley of Trials, Gar'Thok represents the stern discipline of the veteran generation that bled to win Durotar.",["faction:Horde"]="For fresh recruits of every Horde race, Gar'Thok shows how precarious their new territory is and directs them to repel invasive Alliance remnants.",["class:Warrior"]="As a frontline commander who survived a brutal naval ambush, Gar'Thok expects martial fortitude and unhesitating obedience from fellow warriors."},kw={"daelin","durotar","gar'thok","garthok","kul tiras","nazgrel","razor hill","rexxar","tiragarde"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:kul-tiras","quest:784","quest:830","quest:825","topic:quilboar","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Gar'Thok"}}
E["npc:gornek"] = {t="npc",n="Gornek",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Gornek oversees new orc and Darkspear troll recruits preparing to prove their worth to the New Horde.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Gornek oversees new orc and Darkspear troll recruits preparing to prove their worth...",sec={{t="Welcoming the Unproven",b="At the Valley of Trials, Gornek assesses new Horde recruits and gives them their first test of discipline. Warchief Thrall's order is clear: every youth and newcomer must earn a place through grit and perseverance. Gornek reads their introductory orders and directs them to trainers around the compound. Whether they carry an encrypted scrawl, a glyphic parchment, or a simple tablet, he receives their credentials and sends them onto a hard path of survival.",sp=0},{t="A Life in Service to Durotar",b="The valley's arid canyons test battle skill and teach the New Horde's communal ways. Gornek keeps novices from lingering, pointing them toward nearby scorpid burrows, feral boar dens, and veteran instructors. Those who survive the training grounds and slay the threats in the red rock gullies receive his final acknowledgment. Then he sends them into Durotar's wider, perilous landscape.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gornek?",a="Gornek is an orc greeter and taskmaster who oversees new Horde recruits in the Valley of Trials. He reads their induction documents and guides them to their class trainers.",al={"gornek","who is this orc","who is gornek"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Gornek?",a="Gornek stands near the center of the Valley of Trials in southwestern Durotar, inside the Den where young orcs and Darkspear trolls begin their journeys.",al={"gornek location","where is gornek","gornek map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do new recruits report to him?",a="New arrivals bring training scrolls and tablets naming their chosen discipline. Gornek evaluates these letters of introduction, confirms their eligibility, and sends them to the proper mentors in the valley.",al={"why visit gornek","parchment quest","tablet quest"},it="why_me"},{q="What is his role in the New Horde?",a="Gornek coordinates entry into Thrall's New Horde. He ensures recruits learn honor, survival, and martial readiness before they enter Durotar's broader lands.",al={"gornek horde role","what does gornek do"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Gornek on?",a="Gornek is fiercely loyal to Thrall's New Horde. Stationed in Durotar, he serves as an overseer within the Valley of Trials, ensuring that every newly awakened orc and visiting troll recruit embraces the discipline, strength, and survival mindset necessary to defend their fledgling nation.",al={"gornek faction","who does gornek serve","gornek horde or alliance"},it="side",add="a3ac85eb"},{q="What does Gornek want?",a="Gornek wants you to prove yourself worthy of the Horde. Durotar is a harsh land crawling with predators and hostile infiltrators, and he refuses to waste resources on undisciplined recruits. He tasks young warriors with hunting dangerous beasts and rooting out local threats to forge them into capable fighters.",al={"gornek goal","what does gornek need","gornek quest motive"},it="wants",add="e623e91b"},{q="Why is Gornek in the Valley of Trials?",a="The Valley of Trials is the designated proving ground for the Horde's newest blood. Gornek is stationed here to direct fresh arrivals, evaluate their early capabilities, and introduce them to the trainers and trials that will prepare them for the challenges of Durotar and beyond.",al={"why is gornek here","gornek valley of trials role","why is gornek in durotar"},it="why_here",add="a6376a9f"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For young orcs, reporting to Gornek is their first step toward leaving childhood behind and earning an honorable place in Durotar.",["race:Troll"]="As allies sheltered by Thrall, Darkspear trolls present their credentials to Gornek and prove they are capable equals alongside their orc brothers."},kw={"den","durotar","gornek","parchment","the new horde","valley of trials"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","quest:787","subzone:the-den","quest:98576","topic:new-horde","topic:horde"},src={"Gornek"}}
E["npc:hana-zua"] = {t="npc",n="Hana'zua",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Hana'zua waits wounded on the canyon ridges for help from young Horde initiates.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Hana'zua waits wounded on the canyon ridges for help from young Horde initiates.",sec={{t="A Scout Fallen to Venom",b="Above the Valley of Trials, Hana'zua lies wounded on the ridges. The Darkspear scout met Sarkoth, a vicious scorpid that stalks the cliffs. Its venomous sting nearly killed him. Unable to move or return to camp, he waits in the dust for passing recruits. He needs them to kill Sarkoth and carry word of his plight to the Den.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hana'zua?",a="In the Valley of Trials in Durotar, Hana'zua is a wounded Darkspear troll scout. Beasts on the ridges ambushed and poisoned him.",al={"hanazua","who is hanazua","injured troll valley of trials"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to Hana'zua?",a="Sarkoth struck Hana'zua down on the crags above the training grounds. The large scorpid's venom left him unable to move or return to safety.",al={"why is hanazua hurt","who poisoned hanazua","hanazua injury"},it="why_here"},{q="What does he ask travelers to do?",a="Hana'zua asks travelers to kill Sarkoth and bring back the beast's claw as proof. He also asks them to carry word of his condition to the instructors at the Den.",al={"hanazua quest","what does hanazua want"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Hana'zua on?",a="Hana'zua is loyal to the Horde and his fellow Darkspear trolls. Like other young orcs and trolls who come through the Valley of Trials, he ventured into the proving grounds to demonstrate his strength and readiness to serve Thrall's new nation.",al={"hanazua faction","who does hanazua serve","is hanazua horde"},it="side",add="eb2d80d7"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear initiate beginning your journey in Durotar, you may find a wounded kinsman amid the dangers of local wildlife. Protect your new allies.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, helping Hana'zua survive and avenge his wound is an early test of your loyalty and readiness to fight."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","hana'zua","hanazua","sarkoth","scorpid","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:804","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:troll","subzone:the-den"},src={"Hana'zua"}}
E["npc:innkeeper-grosk"] = {t="npc",n="Innkeeper Grosk",z="durotar",s="At Razor Hill, Innkeeper Grosk welcomes travelers on the road between the Valley of Trials and Orgrimmar. His inn offers food, drink, and a place to rest in central Durotar.",h="At Razor Hill, Innkeeper Grosk welcomes travelers on the road between the Valley of Trials and Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="Hospitality in the Red Wastes",b="Razor Hill joins Durotar’s southern training grounds to Orgrimmar’s high walls. Innkeeper Grosk gives warriors, scouts, and peons shelter at his inn. Beneath its sturdy timbers, travelers can find basic provisions, hearty meats, and cool water.",sp=0},{t="A Peon's Respite",b="Innkeeper Grosk also helps the laborers who keep Durotar running. Ukor, a timid peon, carried food to the Valley of Trials, only to learn it was not needed. He asks travelers to bring the load back to Grosk’s inn in Razor Hill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Innkeeper Grosk located?",a="Innkeeper Grosk is inside the inn at Razor Hill, in central Durotar on the main road north to Orgrimmar.",al={"innkeeper grosk location","where is grosk","razor hill innkeeper"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What services does Innkeeper Grosk provide?",a="Grosk offers Horde travelers a place to bind their Hearthstone in Razor Hill. He also sells basic food, water, and meat to replenish health and mana between travels.",al={"what does grosk do","grosk vendor","can i bind hearthstone at razor hill"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Does Innkeeper Grosk offer any quests?",a="Grosk receives the food Ukor asks travelers to carry back to Razor Hill. Ukor feared Durotar’s beasts too much to bring it himself.",al={"innkeeper grosk quests","a peons burden turn in"},gp=true},{q="Who is Innkeeper Grosk?",a="Innkeeper Grosk is the orc proprietor of the tavern in Razor Hill. As travelers, grunts, and wandering adventurers pass through Durotar on their way to or from Orgrimmar, Grosk offers them shelter, provisions, and a hearth to rest their weary bones.",al={"who is grosk","innkeeper grosk","who is innkeeper grosk"},it="identity",add="490d29ee"},{q="Whose side is Innkeeper Grosk on?",a="Grosk is a steadfast member of the Horde, welcoming orcs, trolls, tauren, and Forsaken into his establishment. He ensures that those fighting for Warchief Thrall's new realm have a reliable base of rest and resupply in Durotar.",al={"is grosk horde","innkeeper grosk allegiance","innkeeper grosk faction"},it="side",add="10a7c15b"},{q="What does Innkeeper Grosk want?",a="Grosk wants to keep his inn running smoothly, catering to travelers across the arid plains of Durotar. He trades hearty food and drink, binds wandering adventurers to his hearthstone, and occasionally looks after the needs of the town's laborers and guards.",al={"what does grosk want","grosk motive","innkeeper grosk goals"},it="wants",add="29305f72"},{q="Why is Innkeeper Grosk in Razor Hill?",a="Razor Hill serves as the primary crossroad and garrison town between the Valley of Trials, Sen'jin Village, and the capital of Orgrimmar. Grosk established his tavern here to provide essential lodging and supplies at the beating heart of Durotar's frontier life.",al={"why is grosk here","why razor hill innkeeper","grosk razor hill role"},it="why_here",add="7fe37467"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For newly blooded orcs, trolls, and visiting tauren, Grosk’s inn is the first true town and hearth location on the road north from the Valley of Trials or Sen'jin Village toward Orgrimmar."},kw={"durotar","grosk","innkeeper","innkeeper grosk","orgrimmar","peon's burden","razor hill"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:2161","zone:orgrimmar","npc:magga"},src={"Innkeeper Grosk"}}
E["npc:jen-shan"] = {t="npc",n="Jen'shan",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Jen'shan prepares young hunters for the wild. The Darkspear jungle troll teaches orc and troll marksmen to track, fight at range, and survive.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Jen'shan prepares young hunters for the wild.",sec={{t="Mentor of the Red Sands",b="Jen'shan trains new hunters in the Valley of Trials. Young orcs and Darkspear trolls find her by following inscribed tablets and parchments. She teaches archery, marksmanship, and wilderness survival, readying them for the scorpids and boars on the canyon floor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Jen'shan?",a="Jen'shan is a Darkspear jungle troll who trains hunters in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. She teaches young Horde hunters to track, understand the wilderness, and fight at range.",al={"jenshan lore","who is jenshan","valley hunter trainer"},it="identity"},{q="What quests involve Jen'shan?",a="Young hunters go to Jen'shan for their first training. Orcs bring her an Etched Tablet, while trolls seek her with an Etched Parchment.",al={"jenshan quests","etched tablet jenshan","etched parchment jenshan"},gp=true},{q="Why is a troll training hunters in an orc proving ground?",a="The Valley of Trials trains orc recruits and the Darkspear trolls who share Durotar. Troll scouts like Jen'shan prepare hunters and warriors of both races for service to the Horde.",al={"why is a troll in valley of trials","troll trainer in durotar"},it="why_here"},{q="Whose side is Jen'shan on?",a="Jen'shan is loyal to the Horde and her people, the Darkspear tribe. Stationed in the Valley of Trials, she serves alongside the orcs to ensure that new recruits, whether troll or orc, are properly prepared for the harsh realities of surviving in Durotar and fighting for the warchief.",al={"jenshan faction","is jenshan horde","jenshan loyalty"},it="side",add="9968b478"},{q="What does Jen'shan want?",a="Jen'shan seeks to drill fledging hunters in marksmanship, survival, and the wild instincts needed to endure. She wants promising young scouts to hone their craft quickly so they can handle the fierce beasts roaming the red wastes and protect the fledgling Horde from its enemies.",al={"jenshan motive","jenshan goal","what does jenshan need"},it="wants",add="f50adc74"},{q="Who is Jen'shan tied to?",a="Jen'shan belongs to the Darkspear trolls led by Sen'jin's son, Vol'jin. Because the Darkspear share Durotar with Thrall's orcs, she works closely with the trainers of the Valley of Trials to guide fresh recruits of both races into the ranks of the Horde.",al={"jenshan connections","jenshan darkspear ties","who does jenshan serve"},it="ties",add="ece1555d"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a young orc or troll hunter, you meet Jen'shan first. She teaches you ranged techniques before you leave the red canyons of the Den.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you see Jen'shan carry on the Darkspear tradition of tracking and scouting. She teaches young trolls their ancestral hunting ways in their new home on this continent."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","etched parchment","etched tablet","hunter trainer","jen'shan","jenshan","troll","valley of trials"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:troll","quest:3082","quest:3087"},src={"Jen'shan"}}
E["npc:kali-remik"] = {t="npc",n="Kali Remik",z="durotar",s="In Sen'jin Village, Kali Remik sends young hunters on toward further training. She is a Darkspear troll hunter who knows Durotar's tracking and survival ways.",h="In Sen'jin Village, Kali Remik sends young hunters on toward further training.",sec={{t="A Guide for the Hunt",b="Kali Remik guides young scouts in Sen'jin Village, where they begin life beyond the Valley of Trials. A Darkspear troll tracker, she knows Durotar's dry lands and the Horde's settlements. When novices are ready to leave the local training grounds, she sends promising hunters to Thotar in Razor Hill. There they learn to tame beasts and strengthen the Horde's frontier ranks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kali Remik?",a="Kali Remik is a Darkspear troll hunter and scout who guides young hunters ready to advance beyond local training.",al={"kali remik lore","who is kali remik","kali remik npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Kali Remik be found?",a="Kali Remik can be found in Durotar, especially around Sen'jin Village, aiding her people.",al={"where is kali remik","kali remik location","find kali remik"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What guidance does she offer to hunters?",a="Kali Remik sends young orc and troll hunters who have proven their basic skills to Razor Hill. There, Thotar begins their training in taming a beast companion.",al={"the hunters path quest","kali remik hunter quest","what does kali teach"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Kali Remik on?",a="Kali Remik is loyal to the Darkspear tribe and stands firmly with Thrall's Horde. She aids her people and their allies by guiding young wilderness scouts and marksmen toward proper training and service to their new homeland.",al={"kali remik faction","who does kali remik serve","kali remik horde"},it="side",add="f072d80b"},{q="Why is Kali Remik in Sen'jin Village?",a="Kali Remik stays in Sen'jin Village to watch over the emerging defenders of the Darkspear tribe. In these coastal shallows, she helps identify promising young hunters among the orcs and trolls who pass through, directing them to the mentors who can hone their survival skills.",al={"why is kali remik here","kali remik sen'jin village role","what brought kali remik here"},it="why_here",add="bd47d9e0"},{q="What does Kali Remik want?",a="Kali Remik wants to see Durotar protected by capable scouts and stalkers. She seeks out aspiring hunters to ensure they do not wander unprepared, pointing them along the proper paths to find the trainers who can teach them the ways of the wild.",al={"what does kali remik want","kali remik motive","what is kali remik's goal"},it="wants",add="a3912784"},{q="Who is Kali Remik tied to?",a="She is closely bound to the Darkspear trolls of Sen'jin Village and works in tandem with the hunter trainers of Durotar. Her duties link her to the broader survival network of the Horde, ensuring new recruits connect with established mentors across their territory.",al={"who is kali remik tied to","kali remik connections","kali remik allies"},it="ties",add="528bbb7d"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a young orc or troll hunter, you can turn to Kali Remik when your skills outgrow village drills. She sends you to Thotar in Razor Hill.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you share Kali Remik's tribe. She watches over her kin as they rebuild their lives along Durotar's coast and settle in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","kali remik","sen'jin village","the hunter's path","tracker","valley of spirits"},rel={"quest:6065","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:valley-of-spirits","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","topic:troll","topic:horde","quest:8355"},src={"Kali Remik"}}
E["npc:kaltunk"] = {t="npc",n="Kaltunk",z="durotar",s="In Durotar's Valley of Trials, Kaltunk welcomes young orcs and points them toward their first duties for the Horde.",h="In Durotar's Valley of Trials, Kaltunk welcomes young orcs and points them toward their first duties for the...",sec={{t="The First Step",b="Kaltunk watches over new arrivals in the Valley of Trials. He directs them to Gornek and the path of discipline. Trainers and elders set trials and hunting rites, while Kaltunk gives recruits clear orders so they know where to go.",sp=0},{t="Keeper of the Valley",b="The Valley of Trials was chosen to test the strength and resilience of youths walking its canyon floors. Kaltunk brings the same rugged practicality to his work. He offers no grand speeches or coddling. Each orc must find a place in the world and serve the warchief.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kaltunk?",a="Kaltunk is an orc overseer in the Valley of Trials. Newly awakened orc adventurers meet him first, and he points them toward their mentors and the start of their training.",al={"kaltunk role","who is this orc","kaltunk npc"},it="identity"},{q="What does Kaltunk do for new adventurers?",a="Kaltunk gives new recruits their initial task: speak with Gornek elsewhere in the valley so their training can begin.",al={"kaltunk quest","what does kaltunk want","first quest valley of trials"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can I find Kaltunk?",a="Kaltunk stands near the central training tent and campfire in the secluded Valley of Trials, in southern Durotar.",al={"kaltunk location","find kaltunk","where is kaltunk"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is he stationed in the Valley of Trials?",a="Kaltunk welcomes incoming orc recruits, keeps them organized, and sets them on a path of service to Thrall's Horde.",al={"why is kaltunk here","kaltunk purpose"},it="why_here"},{q="Whose side is Kaltunk on?",a="Kaltunk serves the Horde and stands firmly under the authority of Warchief Thrall. He is stationed in the Valley of Trials specifically to welcome fresh orc recruits and guide their first steps into service for the new nation of Durotar.",al={"kaltunk faction","who does kaltunk serve","is kaltunk horde"},it="side",add="7b0fd1f8"},{q="What does Kaltunk want?",a="Kaltunk wants you to prove yourself to the Horde. He ensures that untested newcomers do not linger idle, directing you immediately to Gornek and the overseers in the Valley of Trials so your training and service to Durotar can begin without delay.",al={"what does kaltunk need","kaltunk goal","kaltunk motive"},it="wants",add="5cbb3fad"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc stepping out into Kalimdor, Kaltunk's gruff instructions are the first words you hear as you begin earning your honor.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see how Kaltunk helps maintain order in Durotar's harsh proving grounds."},kw={"durotar","gornek","kaltunk","orc starter","valley of trials","your place in the world"},rel={"quest:your-place-in-the-world","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar"},src={"Kaltunk"}}
E["npc:kaplak"] = {t="npc",n="Kaplak",z="durotar",s="In Razor Hill, Kaplak prepares young rogues for the Horde's quieter work. He teaches orc and troll students before sending them north to Orgrimmar.",h="In Razor Hill, Kaplak prepares young rogues for the Horde's quieter work.",sec={{t="A Mentor in the Shadows",b="Kaplak trains new Horde rogues in Razor Hill. Though orcish custom favors open combat and roaring charges, he teaches skills that call for patience. His students learn to stalk unseen, pick locks, and strike from behind.\n\nWhen they outgrow his lessons in Durotar's red ravines, Kaplak sends them north to Orgrimmar. There, senior guild operatives can deepen their craft.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kaplak?",a="Kaplak is an orc rogue trainer in Razor Hill, Durotar. He teaches early rogue skills to young orc and troll rogues from the Valley of Trials, then sends them to higher trainers in Orgrimmar.",al={"who is kaplak","kaplak lore","kaplak razor hill"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Kaplak be found?",a="Kaplak can be found in Razor Hill, Durotar's central settlement. He usually rests in or around the local barracks with other class trainers.",al={"where is kaplak","kaplak location","find kaplak"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests does Kaplak offer?",a="Kaplak guides rogue adventurers toward advanced trainers and assignments. He may send them to find Therzok in Orgrimmar.",al={"kaplak quests","quests from kaplak"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Kaplak on?",a="Kaplak is loyal to the Horde and serves the orcs of Durotar. Stationed in Razor Hill, he guides the fledgling stalkers and scouts of Thrall's realm, honing their abilities so they can defend orcish lands from centaur raids, Kul Tiras infiltrators, and any other threats to the growing nation.",al={"kaplak faction","kaplak alliance or horde","who does kaplak serve"},it="side",add="c5a92913"},{q="Why is Kaplak in Razor Hill?",a="Kaplak is stationed in Razor Hill to train young orcs and trolls who practice the subtle arts of stealth, poisoning, and ambush. As recruits venture out from the Valley of Trials, he sharpens their rogue crafts before sending capable scouts forward to the capital city of Orgrimmar.",al={"why is kaplak here","kaplak purpose durotar","what is kaplak doing in razor hill"},it="why_here",add="d6e62700"},{q="What does Kaplak want?",a="Kaplak seeks to strengthen the ranks of the Horde's rogues. He looks for cunning, discipline, and swift blades among the newly arrived recruits, directing promising scouts onward to senior mentors like Therzok in Orgrimmar once their preliminary training is complete.",al={"kaplak motives","kaplak goals","what does kaplak need"},it="wants",add="044206c1"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a young orc or troll rogue leaving the Valley of Trials, you can learn your first trade from Kaplak. Then he directs you to the covert networks in Orgrimmar.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can count on Kaplak to train scouts, spies, and assassins. They guard Durotar and work beyond ordinary battle lines."},kw={"durotar","kaplak","orc","orgrimmar","razor hill","rogue trainer","stealth","therzok"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:1859","quest:2380","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Kaplak"}}
E["npc:kzan-thornslash"] = {t="npc",n="Kzan Thornslash",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Kzan Thornslash equips new Horde recruits for their first trials. The orc merchant supplies weapons in Durotar.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Kzan Thornslash equips new Horde recruits for their first trials.",sec={{t="Armorer to the Recruits",b="Kzan Thornslash supplies weapons to young orcs and Darkspear trolls in the Valley of Trials. They are taking their first steps as Horde warriors. He offers basic hand axes, shortswords, clubs, and staves for recruits facing local wildlife and hazards.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kzan Thornslash?",a="Kzan Thornslash supplies weapons to new Horde trainees in the Valley of Trials. He is an orc merchant, and his wares prepare recruits for their first combat trials.",al={"kzan thornslash","who is kzan","valley of trials weapon vendor"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Kzan Thornslash?",a="You can find Kzan Thornslash inside the Den, a cave in southwestern Durotar's Valley of Trials. Novice adventurers and their training instructors gather there.",al={"kzan location","where is kzan thornslash","kzan thornslash map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What kind of equipment does Kzan sell?",a="Kzan sells basic weapons for recruits, including axes, swords, daggers, staves, and bludgeons. They offer reliable iron until recruits acquire forged or found gear.",al={"what does kzan sell","kzan items","kzan weapons"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Kzan Thornslash on?",a="Kzan Thornslash stands firmly with the Horde. Operating within the Valley of Trials, he answers to the authority of Orgrimmar and Thrall's new nation, outfitting the young orcs and trolls who arrive to prove their strength and loyalty in Durotar.",al={"kzan thornslash faction","who does kzan serve","is kzan horde"},it="side",add="feb30cb2"},{q="Why is Kzan Thornslash in the Valley of Trials?",a="Kzan stays in the Valley of Trials to arm aspiring recruits and warriors embarking on their initial trials. In a harsh, arid proving ground overrun by scorpids, boars, and vile familiars, an unproven fighter needs reliable steel, clubs, and blades to survive their testing.",al={"why is kzan thornslash here","kzan valley of trials role","what does kzan do"},it="why_here",add="1bbcac80"},{q="What does Kzan Thornslash want?",a="Kzan aims to supply recruits with the arms they need while maintaining his trade in Durotar. Through his dealings with young warriors, he ensures that the fledgling defenders of the Horde are adequately equipped with basic weaponry to defend their newly settled lands.",al={"what does kzan want","kzan thornslash motive","kzan thornslash goal"},it="wants",add="c4565150"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a young warrior starting with a chipped blade, you can find blunt and edged weapons from Kzan to suit different combat disciplines.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see its nascent armies begin with merchants like Kzan, who supply steel for every capable hand."},kw={"durotar","horde","kzan","orc","thornslash","valley of trials","weapon vendor","weapons"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","quest:97279"},src={"Kzan Thornslash"}}
E["npc:lar-prowltusk"] = {t="npc",n="Lar Prowltusk",z="durotar",s="Southwest of Sen'jin Village, Lar Prowltusk keeps watch over Durotar's frontier. He guards the young troll settlement and sends travelers against nearby threats.",h="Southwest of Sen'jin Village, Lar Prowltusk keeps watch over Durotar's frontier.",sec={{t="Watcher on the Coast",b="Lar Prowltusk watches the coast southwest of Sen'jin Village. As a Darkspear sentinel, he helps guard the tribe's new home after its people fled their sunken island chain. Hostile neighbors still harass Sen'jin Village as the trolls work to secure a permanent home.\n\nSo Lar directs scouts and warriors to watch the coast and curb these attacks. He pays special attention to the Kolkar centaur, giving the settlement room to breathe.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lar Prowltusk?",a="Lar Prowltusk guards the outskirts of Sen'jin Village in Durotar. The Darkspear sentinel sends Horde travelers against regional threats before they reach the settlement.",al={"lar prowltusk","who is lar prowltusk","lar prowltusk durotar"},it="identity"},{q="What threats does Lar Prowltusk focus on?",a="Lar Prowltusk watches Durotar's frontier for danger, especially marauding Kolkar centaur packs pushing into troll territory.",al={"lar prowltusk quests","what does lar prowltusk want"},it="wants"},{q="Where can Lar Prowltusk be found?",a="Lar Prowltusk keeps watch along the paths southwest of Sen'jin Village in southern Durotar.",al={"lar prowltusk location","where is lar prowltusk"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Lar Prowltusk on?",a="Lar Prowltusk is loyal to the Darkspear tribe and the Horde. Stationed along the harsh coast of Durotar southwest of Sen'jin Village, he acts in defense of his people's new home, looking out for encroaching enemies that threaten the safety of the Darkspear trolls and their orc allies.",al={"lar prowltusk faction","who does lar prowltusk serve","lar prowltusk horde or alliance"},it="side",add="7aeb1fbe"},{q="Why is Lar Prowltusk out here?",a="You find Lar Prowltusk keeping watch southwest of Sen'jin Village to guard the Darkspear settlement from regional perils. Durotar's southern reaches face constant pressure from aggressive neighbors, and Lar stays posted near the wild coast to help direct defenders against these local threats before they strike the village.",al={"why is lar prowltusk in durotar","lar prowltusk location reason","why is lar southwest of senjin"},it="why_here",add="ffd46d6a"},{q="Who is Lar Prowltusk tied to?",a="Lar Prowltusk is closely tied to the troll settlement of Sen'jin Village, coordinating with the village defenders and wandering Horde adventurers to safeguard troll territory.",al={"lar prowltusk allies","lar prowltusk relations","lar prowltusk mate"},it="ties",add="9e56c7c1"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you depend on scouts like Lar Prowltusk to guard your tribe's fragile new home in Durotar from aggressive centaur clans and encroaching human forces.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you share Lar Prowltusk's struggle to secure Durotar's borders against threats near your fledgling capital."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","kolkar","lar prowltusk","northwatch","sen'jin village","troll"},rel={"subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","quest:786","topic:troll","topic:alliance"},src={"Lar Prowltusk"}}
E["npc:magga"] = {t="npc",n="Magga",z="durotar",s="Near the Den in the Valley of Trials, Magga welcomes new arrivals. She greets Horde travelers beginning their journey through the valley in Durotar.",h="Near the Den in the Valley of Trials, Magga welcomes new arrivals.",sec={{t="A Welcoming Face in the Valley of Trials",b="Young orcs and Darkspear trolls first meet the wider world in the Valley of Trials. Near the Den, Magga welcomes those arriving there. Trainers and recruits keep busy nearby, while she helps bring the small camp together.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Magga?",a="Magga is an orc civilian near the Den in the Valley of Trials, Durotar. She welcomes new Horde travelers.",al={"magga durotar","magga valley of trials","who is magga"},it="identity"},{q="What is Magga's connection to Innkeeper Grosk?",a="Magga has no special tie to Innkeeper Grosk. She stays in the Valley of Trials, while Innkeeper Grosk keeps the inn at Razor Hill. Travelers can find food, drink, and a place to bind their hearthstones there.",al={"magga and grosk","magga innkeeper"},it="ties"},{q="Does Magga offer any quests?",a="Magga receives the 'Welcome!' errand. Adventurers bring her a Valley of Trials Gift Voucher, and she welcomes them to Azeroth with a small companion as a gift.",al={"magga quests","welcome quest"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Magga on?",a="Magga is a loyal member of the Horde, dwelling alongside her fellow orcs in the Valley of Trials. She welcomes newcomers arriving in the valley, proudly supporting the people and defense of Durotar under Thrall's leadership.",al={"magga faction","is magga horde","magga allegiance"},it="side",add="7d8c5102"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a fresh Horde recruit in the harsh Valley of Trials, you receive a reassuring welcome to Durotar from Magga."},kw={"durotar","horde","innkeeper grosk","magga","orc","valley of trials","welcome"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","npc:innkeeper-grosk"},src={"Magga"}}
E["npc:mai-ah"] = {t="npc",n="Mai'ah",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Mai'ah guides young Darkspear trolls as they begin their study of magic. She prepares new spellcasters for their path among the Horde.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Mai'ah guides young Darkspear trolls as they begin their study of magic.",sec={{t="Arcane Mentor of the Den",b="Young Darkspear trolls come to Mai'ah in the Valley of Trials to learn magic. Orcs favor the elements or the warrior's path, while trolls have a rare gift for arcane study. Candidates bring glyphic inscriptions, and Mai'ah teaches them to shape raw power into controlled incantations. That control matters in Durotar, where danger waits beyond the den.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mai'ah?",a="Mai'ah trains Darkspear troll mages in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. She gives new spellcasters their first guidance and instruction before they travel into the wider lands of the Horde.",al={"who is maiah","maiah lore","troll mage trainer"},it="identity"},{q="Why is there a troll mage trainer in an orc starting area?",a="Young Darkspear trolls take their coming-of-age trials alongside orc youths after fleeing their sinking island home and settling in Durotar with Thrall's orcs. Orc culture largely shuns arcane magic because of past demon corruption, so troll mages such as Mai'ah guide their own kind.",al={"why troll mage here","valley of trials troll trainer","troll mage durotar"},it="why_here"},{q="What role does she play in training new mages?",a="New troll mages bring Mai'ah written instructions, such as glyphic parchments, and she begins their formal training. She teaches the fundamentals of spellcasting so they can defend the Valley of Trials from local beasts and rogue Burning Blade infiltrators.",al={"what does maiah do","glyphic parchment maiah","maiah quests"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Mai'ah on?",a="Mai'ah is loyal to the Darkspear tribe and the Horde. Stationed in the Valley of Trials, she works under Warchief Thrall's new regime to foster the Horde's future spellcasters, dedicating her arcane knowledge to bolstering young troll and allied mages.",al={"mai'ah allegiance","who does mai'ah serve","is mai'ah horde"},it="side",add="4a36b72a"},{q="What does Mai'ah want?",a="Mai'ah wants to train aspiring practitioners in the fundamentals of the arcane. She seeks to guide young novices through their introductory spells and glyphs, ensuring they possess the discipline and magical power needed to survive Durotar and serve the Horde.",al={"what does mai'ah need","mai'ah goals","why does mai'ah teach"},it="wants",add="648de549"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Darkspear spellcaster, you begin your magical journey with Mai'ah. She teaches the discipline to weave fire, frost, and arcane energy beneath Durotar's harsh sun.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear youth, you can find cultural mentorship in the Valley of Trials from Mai'ah, who teaches an art rarely practiced by your orcish allies."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","mage trainer","mai'ah","maiah","troll","valley of trials"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","quest:98576","topic:troll"},src={"Mai'ah"}}
E["npc:master-gadrin"] = {t="npc",n="Master Gadrin",z="durotar",s="In Sen'jin Village, Master Gadrin guides the Darkspear through exile and grief. Once a teacher of priests and mages, he now serves his people and seeks to lift the dark curse over their home on the Echo Isles.",h="In Sen'jin Village, Master Gadrin guides the Darkspear through exile and grief.",sec={{t="Mentor of the Darkspear",b="Before the Darkspear came to Kalimdor, Master Gadrin guided his people across generations in the South Seas. He served as a witch doctor on their island home and taught the tribe its mystical ways.",sp=0},{t="The Betrayal of Zalazane",b="On the Echo Isles, Master Gadrin trained the tribe's priests and mages with the young witch doctor Zalazane. But the dark voodoo Zalazane sought to wield took hold of him, and madness followed. He enslaved his people's minds and drove Vol'jin and the uncorrupted Darkspear to Durotar's mainland.\n\nNow Gadrin lives in Sen'jin Village with the grief of seeing his companion become a tyrant. He works to lay slain tribesfolk to rest and bring Zalazane's rule to an end.",sp=0},{t="Keeper of Ancient Lore",b="Master Gadrin knows more of troll spiritualism and loa lore than almost anyone alive in the Horde. Scholars, shamans, and the Royal Apothecary Society seek his counsel on arcane and alchemical mysteries. When the Burning Blade threatens Durotar or distant researchers need forgotten rites, Gadrin draws on that knowledge.\n\nHe sends adventurers to Zul'Farrak to read the tablet bearing Shadra the spider loa's true name. Then he crafts the binding the rite requires.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Master Gadrin?",a="Master Gadrin guides the Darkspear as a witch doctor and elder spiritual leader. He lives in Sen'jin Village on Durotar's coast and advises Chieftain Vol'jin.",al={"master gadrin lore","who is gadrin","gadrin npc"},it="identity"},{q="What is Gadrin's history with Zalazane?",a="Master Gadrin and the young witch doctor Zalazane once trained the Darkspear's priests and mages on the Echo Isles. Gadrin watched Zalazane fall to dark magic, lose his reason, and drive the tribe from its island home.",al={"gadrin and zalazane","how does gadrin know zalazane","zalazane mentor"},it="ties"},{q="Why is Gadrin staying in Sen'jin Village?",a="Master Gadrin remains in Sen'jin Village, the refuge survivors built on Durotar's southern coast after Zalazane's curse drove them from the Echo Isles. He counsels refugees, watches for local threats, and directs strikes against Zalazane's forces.",al={"why is gadrin here","what is gadrin doing in senjin village"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Minshina?",a="Minshina was Master Gadrin's brother. He died amid the turmoil on the Echo Isles, and his restless spirit began calling to Gadrin in dreams. Gadrin asks trusted adventurers to recover his brother's skull so Minshina's soul can find peace.",al={"minshina brother","minshinas skull quest lore","who was minshina"}},{q="Does Gadrin help with the Burning Blade cult?",a="Yes. After Zureetha Fargaze reports the Burning Blade's infiltration of the Valley of Trials, Master Gadrin watches for the cult near Sen'jin Village. Seeing the danger to Durotar, he sends recruits north to report to Orgnil Soulscar in Razor Hill.",al={"burning blade durotar gadrin","orgnil soulscar gadrin"}},{q="What does Gadrin know about the loa Shadra?",a="Master Gadrin knows the old teachings of troll theology. When the Forsaken Apothecary Lydon seeks a potent venom used by the Hinterlands Witherbark trolls, Gadrin identifies it as a gift from Shadra the spider loa. He sends adventurers to Zul'Farrak to read the tablet bearing her true name, which he needs to write a summoning spell.",al={"shadra spider loa gadrin","gadrin spider god"}},{q="Whose side is Master Gadrin on?",a="Master Gadrin is loyal to the Darkspear tribe and the Horde. Having journeyed from the Darkspear islands after Thrall saved his people from the Sea Witch, he serves as a senior elder, mystical teacher, and trusted advisor to Chieftain Vol'jin.",al={"gadrin faction","is gadrin horde","who does gadrin serve"},it="side",add="48c543c3"},{q="What does Master Gadrin want?",a="Master Gadrin seeks the death of the traitorous witch doctor Zalazane and the liberation of the Echo Isles. He wishes to free his cursed kin from Zalazane's mind control, reclaim his deceased brother Minshina's skull so the spirits may rest, and protect Sen'jin Village from emerging dangers across Durotar.",al={"what does gadrin want","gadrin goal","master gadrin motive"},it="wants",add="d3faca51"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you have in Master Gadrin a living link to your ancestral home and Sen'jin's traditions. He has shaped your tribe's spiritual leaders for generations and grieves like a father over the tragedy of the Echo Isles.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you share the traditions Master Gadrin taught the Darkspear: communion with spirits and the loa, shaped by the shadow and faith of jungle trolls.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you follow a path Master Gadrin opened by teaching the Darkspear arcane arts after the Third War. His teaching showed troll magic could reach beyond raw ritual mojo.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can look to Master Gadrin as one of Vol'jin's most trusted advisors. He watches coastal Durotar and warns Razor Hill when dark cults threaten Durotar's young nation."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","echo isles","gadrin","master gadrin","minshina","sen'jin village","vol'jin","witch doctor","zalazane"},rel={"npc:vol-jin","subzone:sen-jin-village","quest:826","subzone:echo-isles","quest:808","npc:orgnil-soulscar","topic:darkspear-tribe","zone:durotar"},src={"Master Gadrin"}}
E["npc:master-vornal"] = {t="npc",n="Master Vornal",z="durotar",s="In Sen'jin Village, Master Vornal brews for the Darkspear and guards the craft he has mastered. Though age has touched him, the elderly jungle troll refuses to teach an apprentice.",h="In Sen'jin Village, Master Vornal brews for the Darkspear and guards the craft he has mastered.",sec={{t="The Stubborn Brewer of Sen'jin",b="Master Vornal makes draughts and spirits for his fellow Darkspear trolls in Sen'jin Village. Age is catching up with him, yet he will not give up his independence. He refuses to train an apprentice and mixes every remedy and volatile brew himself.",sp=0},{t="A Solvent Spirit",b="At times, Master Vornal sends young adventurers into the surrounding lands for harsh or unusual ingredients. He uses them in solvents and other mixtures, and rewards those who bring them back. Yet he keeps his methods and recipes to himself, doing all the brewing by his own hand.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Master Vornal?",a="Master Vornal is an elderly Darkspear jungle troll who brews spirits and remedies in Sen'jin Village. He insists on working without an apprentice.",al={"master vornal","vornal","sen'jin master vornal","who is vornal"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Master Vornal?",a="Master Vornal can be found among the huts of Sen'jin Village, on Durotar's southern coast just north of the Echo Isles.",al={"vornal location","where is master vornal","find master vornal"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Master Vornal refuse to take apprentices?",a="Master Vornal says no troll or orc worthy of his teaching has come forward. His eyesight is failing, and he leans more on alchemy, yet he would rather work alone than teach someone unworthy.",al={"vornal apprentice","why no apprentice","vornal students"}},{q="What tasks does he offer adventurers?",a="Master Vornal sends wanderers across the region to gather raw ingredients for his solvent mixtures. He depends on travelers to bring the materials, then keeps the brewing to himself.",al={"master vornal quest","a solvent spirit","vornal quest"},it="wants",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Master Vornal on?",a="Master Vornal is loyal to the Darkspear tribe and the Horde. He makes his home in Sen'jin Village, lending his craft and experience to help secure the young settlement against surrounding perils.",al={"vornal allegiance","who does master vornal serve","master vornal faction"},it="side",add="e0bd334a"},{q="Why is Master Vornal in Sen'jin Village?",a="Master Vornal resides along the coast of Durotar to aid his kin as they carve out a new existence in exile. From his home in Sen'jin Village, he practices his trade and tasks travelers with gathering the potent reagents he requires.",al={"why is master vornal here","why is vornal in senjin village","vornal purpose in durotar"},it="why_here",add="27223be8"},{q="What does Master Vornal want?",a="Though aging, Master Vornal prefers to work independently and refuses to burden himself with apprentices. Instead, he looks to capable adventurers to run his errands and collect rare distillations and solvents across Durotar.",al={"what does vornal want","master vornal goal","what is vornal looking for"},it="wants",add="faf3afd9"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you can see Master Vornal among the stubborn elder craftspeople who helped establish Sen'jin Village after the tribe fled its island home.",["profession:Herbalism"]="With Herbalism, you can recognize Master Vornal's search for rare catalysts and harsh natural reagents to make his solvents."},kw={"a solvent spirit","darkspear","durotar","master vornal","sen'jin village","troll","vornal"},rel={"subzone:sen-jin-village","quest:818","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Master Vornal"}}
E["npc:misha-tor-kren"] = {t="npc",n="Misha Tor'kren",z="durotar",s="At the Tor'kren Farm in western Durotar, Misha Tor'kren waits for word of her son. Kron went west toward the Southfury River to hunt crocolisks, but has not returned.",h="At the Tor'kren Farm in western Durotar, Misha Tor'kren waits for word of her son.",sec={{t="A Mother's Vigil",b="Misha Tor'kren tends her farm southeast of Thunder Ridge, near the ridge. Her son Kron went west toward the Southfury River to hunt crocolisks and prove his mettle. He never came home. Durotar's frontier dangers stretch the orcish watchtowers thin, and Misha has heard no word of him. She needs travelers to search the riverbanks for signs of her son.",sp=0},{t="A Grim Token",b="Kron fell to the Southfury River's crocolisks. Misha can receive only his salvaged amulet. It is a bitter reminder of the dangers young orcs face while trying to prove their strength in Kalimdor's wilderness.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Misha Tor'kren?",a="Misha Tor'kren tends the Tor'kren Farm in western Durotar, southeast of Thunder Ridge.",al={"misha torkren","who is misha","torkren farm owner"},it="identity"},{q="Where did her son Kron go?",a="Kron went west toward the Southfury River to hunt crocolisks and prove himself as a hunter. He did not return home.",al={"where is kron","what happened to kron","misha son"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens when you look for Kron?",a="Misha asks travelers to search for Kron along the river. His disappearance weighs heavily on her, and she needs someone to investigate.",al={"is kron dead","find kron","lost but not forgotten"},sp=1},{q="Is she related to Rexxar's bear Misha?",a="No. Misha is an orc farmer in Durotar, distinct from Rexxar's loyal bear companion, who shares her name.",al={"misha bear","rexxar bear misha","is she the bear"}},{q="Whose side is Misha Tor'kren on?",a="Misha Tor'kren is a loyal member of the Horde, living as a humble orc settler in Durotar. She makes her home at Tor'kren Farm, working the harsh red soil and relying on Horde travelers and local champions to assist her family in times of crisis.",al={"misha tor'kren faction","who does misha tor'kren serve","misha torkren horde"},it="side",add="971252e3"},{q="What does Misha Tor'kren want?",a="Misha wants desperately to find her lost son, Kron. The young orc went missing while out hunting along the dangerous banks of the Southfury River, and she pleads with passing adventurers to search the waters, discover what became of him, and bring back any sign of his fate.",al={"what does misha want","misha tor'kren goal","why does misha need help"},it="wants",add="b9e15925"},{q="Who is Misha Tor'kren tied to?",a="Misha is deeply tied to her family, most notably her missing son Kron. She manages the Tor'kren homestead southeast of Thunder Ridge, where their livelihoods depend on surviving the perils of Durotar's wilderness.",al={"misha tor'kren family","who is misha related to","misha torkren son"},it="ties",add="8e838196"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know the cost of youthful pride when Kron tries to prove his strength against Durotar's wildlife.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know river predators can be dangerous before a hunter has mastered the wild."},kw={"crocolisk","kron","lost but not forgotten","misha","misha tor'kren","southfury river","thunder ridge","tor'kren farm"},rel={"quest:816","subzone:tor-kren-farm","subzone:southfury-river","subzone:thunder-ridge","zone:durotar","npc:misha"},src={"Misha Tor'kren"}}
E["npc:orgnil-soulscar"] = {t="npc",n="Orgnil Soulscar",z="durotar",s="At Razor Hill, Orgnil Soulscar watches for danger among the orcs of Durotar. He gathers reports and helps direct defenses, with the Burning Blade cult in the canyons foremost in his thoughts.",h="At Razor Hill, Orgnil Soulscar watches for danger among the orcs of Durotar.",sec={{t="Watcher of Razor Hill",b="Orgnil Soulscar watches for hidden threats across Durotar from Razor Hill. Grunt patrols guard against Alliance forces and centaur raiders, while he searches for danger among the orcs themselves. Scouts bring reports from across the region. Orgnil studies them for signs of corrupt rites and secret gatherings.",sp=0},{t="Hunting the Shadow Council's Remnants",b="Orgnil Soulscar hunts the Burning Blade cult, whose warlocks hide in caves such as Skull Rock. Fel magic devastated the orcish people in past generations, and Orgnil will not let demon worship gain ground near Orgrimmar. He sends trusted recruits to confront cultists and gather ritual talismans. He also sends them to seek counsel from local hermits and shamans such as Margoz about the dark magic at work.",sp=1,bt={"q5726.3"}}},faq={{q="Who is Orgnil Soulscar?",a="Orgnil Soulscar directs defense from Razor Hill, investigating threats and guiding warriors and scouts against dangers to the newly settled orc lands.",al={"who is orgnil","orgnil soulscar lore","razor hill quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="What threat is Orgnil most worried about?",a="Orgnil Soulscar is intent on rooting out the Burning Blade cult. Its hidden presence in Durotar's caverns and its corrupting fel magic threaten the fresh start Thrall envisions for the Horde.",al={"what does orgnil want","orgnil enemies","who does orgnil fight"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Orgnil send travelers to Margoz?",a="Margoz is a knowledgeable hermit living north of Razor Hill who understands the Burning Blade's signs and rituals. Orgnil sends scouts to him to read the cult's movements and investigate the spreading magical corruption.",al={"why margoz","orgnil and margoz","who is margoz to orgnil"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can Orgnil Soulscar be found?",a="Orgnil Soulscar is stationed outdoors in Razor Hill, near Durotar's central crossroads.",al={"orgnil location","where is orgnil","find orgnil soulscar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Burning Blade in Durotar?",a="The Burning Blade is a cult bound to demonic masters and the Shadow Council. Its members hide in ravines such as Skull Rock and Dustwind Cave, seeking to poison Durotar's wildlife and draw young orcs back into demonic service.",al={"burning blade durotar","burning blade cult","who are burning blade"},sp=1,bt={"q5726.3"}},{q="Does Orgnil work directly for Thrall?",a="Orgnil Soulscar serves in the regional defense force based in Razor Hill, carrying out the Warchief's order to protect Durotar from sedition and demonic influence.",al={"orgnil thrall","is orgnil warchief guard"},it="leader"},{q="Whose side is Orgnil Soulscar on?",a="Orgnil is entirely loyal to the Horde and the defense of Durotar. Stationed in Razor Hill, he acts as an enforcer of local order and security, dedicating his efforts to protecting young orcish settlements from insidious internal threats like the Burning Blade cultists lurking in the canyon shadows.",al={"orgnil soulscar faction","who does orgnil serve","orgnil allegiance"},it="side",add="68dd86eb"},{q="What does Orgnil Soulscar want?",a="Orgnil wants to root out and eradicate the shadow of the Burning Blade within Durotar. He seeks reliable intelligence on cultist activity, tasking capable adventurers with cutting down their warlocks, reclaiming stolen talismans, and consulting local hermits like Margoz to untangle the demonic corruption spreading across the land.",al={"what does orgnil want","orgnil goals","orgnil purpose"},it="wants",add="07ede484"},{q="Why is Orgnil Soulscar here in Razor Hill?",a="Razor Hill serves as the central hub of defense and logistics in Durotar outside of Orgrimmar. Orgnil is stationed here as an investigative authority and protector, perfectly positioned to monitor suspicious stirrings across the dry valleys and mobilize travelers against encroaching cultists and tainted beasts.",al={"why is orgnil in razor hill","orgnil role razor hill","why is orgnil here"},it="why_here",add="9d37257b"},{q="Who is Orgnil Soulscar tied to?",a="Orgnil works with the local Horde defenders against the Burning Blade and directs adventurers to Margoz, who lives northeast of Razor Hill.",al={"orgnil allies","orgnil connections","who does orgnil work with"},it="ties",add="05bd4129"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As a young orc, you can look to Orgnil as a guard against the demonic taint that once enslaved the clans. His work reminds new recruits to stay alert and keep their homeland pure.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, tread carefully around Orgnil. He hunts uncontrolled demonic corruption within Durotar.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can count on Orgnil to guard its heartland from cultists while the Horde builds its new nation."},kw={"burning blade","durotar","margoz","orgnil soulscar","razor hill","shadow council","skull rock"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:828","quest:823","quest:806"},src={"Orgnil Soulscar"}}
E["npc:rezlak"] = {t="npc",n="Rezlak",z="durotar",s="Along Durotar’s roads south of Orgrimmar, Rezlak waits for help keeping his supplies moving. The goblin belongs to the Tinkers’ Union and hires travelers to recover lost goods and drive off harpies.",h="Along Durotar’s roads south of Orgrimmar, Rezlak waits for help keeping his supplies moving.",sec={{t="A Pragmatic Tinkers' Union Agent",b="Rezlak waits beside the canyon road between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar. He represents the Tinkers’ Union, a goblin syndicate devoted to engineering, supply lines, and practical business. While trade runs smoothly, the factional tensions of Kalimdor matter little to him. Dustwind harpies have raided his cargo caravans and made the routes unsafe. So Rezlak stays at his post and hires passersby to recover supplies and deal with the harpies for profit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rezlak?",a="Rezlak is a goblin merchant and engineer with the Tinkers’ Union. One of Gazlowe’s men, he was sent to help the orcs of Durotar. He waits along the main northern road for help securing supply lines and reclaiming gear from local pests.",al={"rezlak lore","who is rezlak","rezlak durotar"},it="identity"},{q="What is Rezlak doing in Durotar?",a="Rezlak works along the trade routes between the central plains and the canyon pass to Orgrimmar. Dustwind harpies ambushed his caravans and scattered cargo across the arid canyons, making the routes unsafe.",al={"why is rezlak in durotar","rezlak purpose","rezlak mission"},it="why_here"},{q="Which quests does Rezlak offer?",a="Rezlak offers two jobs. ‘Winds in the Desert’ asks you to recover sacks of lost supplies scattered across the canyon floor. ‘Securing the Lines’ asks you to thin the nearby Dustwind harpies.",al={"rezlak quests","what quests does rezlak give"},gp=true},{q="What is the Tinkers' Union?",a="The Tinkers’ Union is a goblin trade organization for mechanics, inventors, and logistical work. Like other goblin cartels and guilds, its members put profitable trade and practical solutions ahead of political loyalty.",al={"tinkers union","rezlak faction"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Rezlak on?",a="Rezlak represents goblin commercial enterprise rather than partisan loyalty. Although he is stationed along a major Durotar roadway deep within Horde territory and is affiliated with the Tinkers' Union, he maintains the pragmatic neutrality typical of his race, prioritizing engineering contracts and salvaged equipment over factional politics.",al={"rezlak faction","is rezlak horde","rezlak horde or alliance"},it="side",add="910e2401"},{q="What does Rezlak want?",a="Rezlak needs his caravans kept safe. Dustwind harpies from Razorwind Canyon snatched his last shipment, so he hires able adventurers to recover the lost sacks of supplies and to thin out the harpies in Drygulch Ravine so the routes are safe again.",al={"what does rezlak need","rezlak goals","rezlak quest motive"},it="wants",add="dba9f262"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you understand why Rezlak prizes mechanical efficiency, useful tools, and salvaged components.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you meet Rezlak just outside Orgrimmar. His dealings reflect the transactional ties between neutral goblin guilds and the fledgling Horde."},kw={"durotar","dustwind harpies","rezlak","securing the lines","tinkers union","winds in the desert"},rel={"quest:834","quest:835","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","topic:goblin","topic:horde"},src={"Rezlak"}}
E["npc:rhinag"] = {t="npc",n="Rhinag",z="durotar",s="Near Durotar’s northwestern border, Rhinag waits among the rocks, weakened by scorpids’ venom. The Darkspear troll needs a remedy from a passing traveler before the poison takes its toll.",h="Near Durotar’s northwestern border, Rhinag waits among the rocks, weakened by scorpids’ venom.",sec={{t="A Venomous Peril",b="Among the rocks near Durotar’s northwestern border, Rhinag lies weak after a Venomtail Scorpid stung him. The poison has left the Darkspear troll isolated. He needs a venomtail antidote, and his survival depends on whether a passing traveler can find one in time.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rhinag?",a="Rhinag is a Darkspear jungle troll traveler, stranded and weakened near Durotar’s northwestern border after a scorpion’s sting.",al={"who is rhinag","rhinag lore","troll at rocktusk"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Rhinag be found?",a="Rhinag rests among the rocks near Durotar’s northwestern border.",al={"rhinag location","where is rhinag","rocktusk farm troll"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happened to him?",a="A Venomtail Scorpid stung Rhinag while he crossed Durotar. Its poison left him incapacitated, and he needs an antidote before it proves fatal.",al={"why is rhinag sick","what poisoned rhinag","need for a cure backstory"}},{q="Whose side is Rhinag on?",a="Rhinag is allied with the Horde. A Darkspear troll lying stricken near Durotar's northwestern border, he relies on travelers and Horde champions passing by to assist him in his time of need.",al={"rhinag faction","is rhinag horde","rhinag allegiance"},it="side",add="37e11902"},{q="What does Rhinag want?",a="Rhinag desperately needs an antidote. Having suffered the sting of a local venomtail scorpid, he requires a timely cure before the venom takes full toll on his body.",al={"rhinag quest","what does rhinag need","rhinag help"},it="wants",add="cc642833"},{q="Why is Rhinag here?",a="Rhinag has taken shelter among the rocks near Durotar's northwestern border after falling victim to a venomtail scorpid sting, waiting there for aid before the poison completely overwhelms him.",al={"why is rhinag here","where is rhinag","what brought rhinag here"},it="why_here",add="ffa3558a"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you may find a kinsman brought low by Durotar’s native wildlife. The Darkspear tribe faces many trials as it makes a home alongside the Horde."},kw={"antidote","durotar","need for a cure","rhinag","venomtail scorpid"},rel={"quest:812","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Rhinag"}}
E["npc:rwag"] = {t="npc",n="Rwag",z="durotar",s="In the Den, Rwag teaches newcomers the first steps of a rogue's craft. The orc trains newly arrived orcs and trolls in stealth, subterfuge, and dirty fighting in Durotar's Valley of Trials, under the Horde's watch.",h="In the Den, Rwag teaches newcomers the first steps of a rogue's craft.",sec={{t="Shadows of the Valley",b="Deep in the Den, Rwag trains young rogues, cutpurses, and thieves before they leave the cave and venture into Durotar. The new Horde honors martial skill and valor in battle. Yet Rwag knows subtlety, poisons, and a well-placed dagger can still mean survival in the unforgiving desert.\n\nRwag keeps watch over affairs in the Valley. He distrusts the dark practitioners sheltering in the cave, especially the warlock Nartok.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rwag?",a="Rwag trains orc and troll rogues inside the Den in the Valley of Trials. There, he teaches them the first steps of their training in Durotar.",al={"who is rwag","rwag valley of trials","orc rogue trainer"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Rwag?",a="Rwag can be found deep inside the Den, a cavern cut into the rocky cliffs of Durotar's Valley of Trials. Several other class trainers are there too.",al={"rwag location","where is rwag","find rwag"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Rwag think of the warlocks in the Den?",a="Rwag distrusts the warlocks who share the Den, especially Nartok. He watches the warlock closely.",al={"rwag nartok","why does rwag distrust warlocks","rwag encrypted parchment"},it="conflict"},{q="Which classes does Rwag train?",a="Rwag trains rogues in early techniques such as Eviscerate. At the Shattered Hand's request, he watches new recruits and passes along anything the Hand might need to know about them.",al={"what does rwag teach","can rwag train me"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Rwag on?",a="Rwag serves the Horde, stationed in the Valley of Trials to instruct fledgling orc and troll cutpurses. His deeper loyalty is to the Shattered Hand, which he believes will see the Horde to its former glory, unhindered by what he calls the timidness of the Warchief.",al={"rwag faction","is rwag horde","who does rwag serve"},it="side",add="864b6a89"},{q="What does Rwag want?",a="Rwag aims to hone the stealth, cunning, and martial skill of aspiring rogues starting out in the Valley of Trials. He expects his pupils to master silent footfalls, precise strikes, and keen vigilance—all while keeping a wary eye on untrustworthy figures lurking nearby.",al={"what does rwag want","rwag goal","rwag motives"},it="wants",add="c0621c2a"},{q="Why is Rwag here?",a="Rwag makes his post inside the Den so he can evaluate and instruct new recruits eager to walk the path of shadows. Durotar requires scouts and discreet blades just as much as frontline warriors, and he ensures those with a knack for theft and subterfuge are properly disciplined.",al={"why is rwag in the den","rwag valley of trials role","why is rwag in durotar"},it="why_here",add="4b9fa3b0"},{q="Who is Rwag tied to?",a="Rwag works alongside the other class mentors in the Valley of Trials, though he keeps a suspicious distance from the warlock trainer Nartok, whom he openly distrusts. His ties remain with the Horde's network of rogue trainers and the young scouts he sends out across Durotar.",al={"rwag connections","who does rwag know","rwag nartok"},it="ties",add="0a3d842f"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a young orc or troll rogue in the Valley of Trials, you meet Rwag as your first mentor in skulduggery. He teaches early offensive techniques and how to decipher secret ciphers.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you see in Rwag the practical edge of survival. Even in Thrall's honorable new Horde, shadows and cold steel remain vital."},kw={"durotar","nartok","rogue","rwag","the den","trainer","valley of trials"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:the-den","quest:3083","quest:3088","zone:durotar"},src={"Rwag"}}
E["npc:tai-jin"] = {t="npc",n="Tai'jin",z="durotar",s="At the Razor Hill barracks, Tai'jin teaches young Darkspear priests the balance of light and shadow. She passes on troll spiritual traditions and rites such as the Hex of Weakness.",h="At the Razor Hill barracks, Tai'jin teaches young Darkspear priests the balance of light and shadow.",sec={{t="Priestess of Razor Hill",b="Tai'jin guides young priests from the Razor Hill barracks as they set out across Durotar. Orcs here chiefly follow shamanism or warlock arts. Darkspear trolls bring their communion with spirits and loas to the Horde. Tai'jin teaches the first principles of priesthood and the balance of light and shadow, rooted in troll heritage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Tai'jin?",a="Tai'jin can be found on the ground floor of the Razor Hill Barracks in central Durotar, beside the other class trainers.",al={"tai'jin location","where is tai'jin","taijin razor hill"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Tai'jin teach?",a="Tai'jin teaches new priests spells, ranks, and abilities as they gain experience. Her lessons include early instruction for troll initiates.",al={"taijin trainer","what does taijin train","priest spells razor hill"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why is a troll priest stationed in an orc settlement?",a="Razor Hill trains young Horde adventurers leaving the Valley of Trials and Sen'jin Village. Orcs do not practice priestly arts, so Tai'jin brings Darkspear spiritual traditions to the settlement.",al={"why is taijin in razor hill","trolls in razor hill barracks"},it="why_here"},{q="What special rites does Tai'jin provide for troll priests?",a="Tai'jin guides Darkspear priests through introductory spiritual rites, including the Hex of Weakness. The rite channels ancestral curses.",al={"hex of weakness quest","taijin quests"},gp=true},{q="Who is Tai'jin?",a="Tai'jin is a Darkspear jungle troll priest trainer stationed in the barracks of Razor Hill. Devoted to guiding those who channel spiritual and divine energies, she instructs young acolytes of the Horde—particularly troll and undead priests—in mastering their spiritual arts, prayers, and traditional troll rites.",al={"taijin identity","who is taijin","taijin lore"},it="identity",add="5b5c447a"},{q="Whose side is Tai'jin on?",a="Tai'jin is loyal to the Darkspear tribe and the Horde. Stationed in Durotar alongside orc warriors and shamans, she works in service to Warchief Thrall's united forces, ensuring that spiritual practitioners are prepared to defend Horde territory.",al={"taijin faction","who does taijin serve","taijin allegiance"},it="side",add="1746c020"},{q="What does Tai'jin want?",a="Tai'jin seeks to guide novice priests in understanding their spiritual gifts and deepening their devotion. She tasks budding acolytes with proving their discipline, meditation, and communion with spiritual forces so they can properly support their allies across Durotar and beyond.",al={"what does taijin want","taijin goal","taijin purpose"},it="wants",add="dfe85d14"},{q="Who is Tai'jin tied to?",a="As a spiritual mentor within Razor Hill, Tai'jin is tied closely to the Darkspear trolls led by Sen'jin's legacy, as well as the local Horde garrison under the authority of Orgrimmar. She works alongside fellow trainers and defenders in Durotar to foster strong, faithful acolytes.",al={"taijin ties","taijin connections","who is taijin allied with"},it="ties",add="ab897349"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a Horde priest training in Durotar, you learn from Tai'jin before heading to Orgrimmar's grand halls.",["race:Troll"]="As a young Darkspear troll, you can learn distinctive spells from Tai'jin, including the Hex of Weakness."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","hex of weakness","priest trainer","razor hill","tai'jin","taijin"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:troll","quest:5654","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Tai'jin"}}
E["npc:telf-joolam"] = {t="npc",n="Telf Joolam",z="durotar",s="At the Shrine of the Dormant Flame, Telf Joolam guides Horde initiates in the ways of fire. The Darkspear shaman teaches them to commune with and command this volatile element.",h="At the Shrine of the Dormant Flame, Telf Joolam guides Horde initiates in the ways of fire.",sec={{t="Keeper of the Flame",b="Among the crags above the borderlands, Telf Joolam tends the Shrine of the Dormant Flame. Fire spirits call for sharp discipline and a steady mind. Earth offers calm certainty, and water asks for patience. Telf prepares young shamans for trials where wild embers can consume the unready.",sp=0},{t="The Path of Fire",b="Under Telf's guidance, initiates brew and drink a ritual Fire Sapta. It opens their mortal eyes to the unseen elemental planes. Then he sends them up the rocky summits to face burning spirits. Those who earn the flame must honor its ravenous hunger and master their pride.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Telf Joolam?",a="Telf Joolam, a Darkspear troll shaman, tends the Shrine of the Dormant Flame. He guides young shamans who seek communion with fire.",al={"telf joolam","who is telf","shrine of dormant flame troll"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Telf Joolam be found?",a="Telf Joolam can be found at the Shrine of the Dormant Flame, high on the rocky ridge between Durotar and the Barrens.",al={"telf joolam location","where is telf","how to find telf joolam"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of the Fire Sapta he asks for?",a="The Fire Sapta opens an initiate's spiritual vision, so they can perceive and speak with elemental fire spirits unseen by mortal eyes.",al={"what is fire sapta","fire sapta use","why drink sapta"},it="purpose"},{q="What element does Telf Joolam teach?",a="Telf Joolam teaches fire. He tests shamans' strength and will, so they can control flame without yielding to its destructive nature.",al={"what element does telf teach","telf joolam element","fire totem quest guy"}},{q="Why is a troll overseeing shamanic rites here?",a="Since joining Thrall's Horde, many Darkspear trolls have taken up shamanism alongside orcs and tauren. Experienced shamans such as Telf guide the next generation.",al={"why troll shaman","darkspear shamanism"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens after completing Telf Joolam's tasks?",a="After proving mastery over the flame spirits on the nearby peak, initiates gain the knowledge and blessing to forge their permanent Fire Totem.",al={"call of fire reward","what does telf give you"},it="next_step"},{q="Whose side is Telf Joolam on?",a="Telf Joolam stands proudly with the Horde and the Darkspear tribe. As a revered shaman keeper, his allegiance lies with Thrall's new shamanic traditions, guiding both orc and troll initiates who walk the path of the elements.",al={"telf joolam faction","is telf joolam horde","telf joolam allegiance"},it="side",add="6bc0eb27"},{q="What does Telf Joolam want?",a="Telf Joolam seeks to test aspiring shamans seeking communion with fire. He tasks initiates with gathering the reagents for a Fire Sapta, demanding proof of resolve and harmony before granting communion with the dormant elemental flame.",al={"telf joolam goal","what does telf want","why talk to telf joolam"},it="wants",add="6f75c3b9"},{q="Who is Telf Joolam tied to?",a="Telf Joolam works in concert with the shaman trainers across Durotar and the Barrens, acting as a vital link in the Call of Fire trials. Through his sacred duties at the shrine, he serves the greater spiritual revival of the Horde.",al={"telf joolam connections","who does telf work with","telf joolam allies"},it="ties",add="b42da7bb"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you follow Telf Joolam's guidance through the Fire Sapta trials and learn to master your Fire Totem.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you see a Darkspear elder guiding initiates in shamanic ways shared across the Horde.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see elders like Telf guard sacred elemental shrines throughout the borderlands and strengthen the Horde's spiritual roots."},kw={"barrens","call of fire","darkspear","durotar","fire sapta","shaman","shrine of the dormant flame","telf joolam"},rel={"subzone:shrine-of-the-dormant-flame","quest:1524","zone:durotar","zone:barrens","topic:troll"},src={"Telf Joolam"}}
E["npc:thotar"] = {t="npc",n="Thotar",z="durotar",s="In Razor Hill, Thotar prepares young Horde hunters for Durotar’s wilds. Orcs and trolls come to him after leaving the Valley of Trials to learn tracking and beast taming.",h="In Razor Hill, Thotar prepares young Horde hunters for Durotar’s wilds.",sec={{t="A Mentor in Razor Hill",b="Thotar trains Horde hunters in Razor Hill for the wilderness of Durotar. After learning the basics in the Valley of Trials, new recruits come to him to face more dangerous predators. He teaches marksmanship and the respect needed to live alongside and direct Kalimdor’s deadliest creatures. Orcs have passed these traditions down through generations.",sp=0},{t="Taming the Wilds",b="Thotar sends young hunters into arid canyons to learn the ancient art of taming beasts. There, they calm and bond with native creatures, from venomous scorpids and armored surf crawlers to cunning boars. His lessons teach Horde trackers to build a bond with nature instead of relying on force.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Thotar?",a="Thotar trains hunters in Razor Hill. He teaches traditional wilderness lore, marksmanship, and beast taming.",al={"who is thotar","thotar lore","what does thotar do"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Thotar be found?",a="Thotar can be found in Razor Hill, the Horde settlement in central Durotar, just north of the Valley of Trials.",al={"thotar location","where is thotar","find thotar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What traditions does Thotar teach?",a="Thotar teaches hunting and tracking traditions passed down through generations of orcs. His lessons cover weapon mastery, wilderness survival, and patient bonds with animal companions.",al={"what does thotar teach","hunter traditions","thotar training"},it="purpose"},{q="Does Thotar only train orcs?",a="Thotar trains hunters aligned with the Horde who come to Razor Hill. He mentors Darkspear trolls and wandering tauren passing through Durotar.",al={"can trolls train with thotar","thotar tauren","who does thotar train"},it="people"},{q="What tasks does Thotar give to young hunters?",a="Thotar sends novice hunters to track native Durotar wildlife, including boars, surf crawlers, and scorpids. They use a taming rod to earn the beasts’ trust and obedience.",al={"thotar quests","taming the beast thotar","what does thotar send you to do"},it="target"},{q="Why is beast taming so important in his training?",a="A beast companion can help a Horde hunter survive in battle and in the wild. Thotar teaches hunters to bond with their beasts so they become loyal defenders of the Horde.",al={"why tame beasts","hunter pet lore","purpose of beast taming"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Whose side is Thotar on?",a="Thotar stands firmly with the Horde. Stationed in Razor Hill, he dedicates his craft to strengthening the Horde's ranks by training newly arrived orc, troll, and tauren hunters to survive the wild and defend their lands.",al={"thotar faction","is thotar horde","thotar allegiance"},it="side",add="07bd0b61"},{q="What does Thotar want?",a="Thotar seeks to pass down ancestral hunting traditions to a new generation. He expects aspiring hunters to prove their respect for the wilderness by mastering the arts of tracking, survival, and beast taming.",al={"what does thotar want","thotar goal","thotar purpose"},it="wants",add="83013f85"},{q="Why is Thotar in Razor Hill?",a="Razor Hill serves as the primary gathering settlement for young adventurers venturing out of the Valley of Trials. Thotar remains here alongside other trainers to prepare emerging hunters before they head deeper into the perils of Durotar and the wider world.",al={"why is thotar here","why is thotar in razor hill","thotar razor hill"},it="why_here",add="0fc388b7"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a Horde hunter, you learn beast taming rites and wilderness skills after leaving the starter valleys.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you follow Thotar’s traditional hunting customs and ancestral respect for tracking and beast companionship.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear hunter leaving Sen’jin Village, you learn Horde survival skills for Durotar’s dangers.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can learn from Thotar in Razor Hill to patrol Durotar’s borders with sharp eyes and a well-bonded combat beast."},kw={"durotar","hunter","hunter trainer","kaplak","orc","razor hill","taming the beast","thotar"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:6061","quest:6081","quest:6065","npc:kaplak","topic:troll","topic:tauren"},src={"Thotar"}}
E["npc:ukor"] = {t="npc",n="Ukor",z="durotar",s="Outside the Valley of Trials, Ukor rests after carrying food south from Razor Hill. The grounds had enough provisions already, but he hopes his people can still use them.",h="Outside the Valley of Trials, Ukor rests after carrying food south from Razor Hill.",sec={{t="A Peon's Errand",b="Ukor rests by the eastern road outside the Valley of Trials, tired after carrying food south from Razor Hill. Orc peons spend their days cutting lumber or hauling rocks for harsh taskmasters. Ukor chose to bring provisions to the recruits on his own initiative.\n\nHe crossed Durotar’s red plains, where scorpids and boars prowl, only to find the training grounds already well stocked. His bundle was not needed. Now he asks passing young adventurers to carry it north to Innkeeper Grosk.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ukor?",a="Ukor rests along the road leading east from the Valley of Trials in southern Durotar. He is an earnest orc peon.",al={"ukor lore","who is ukor","what does ukor do"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Ukor standing by the road with a sack of food?",a="Ukor carried rations south from Razor Hill to feed the young warriors training in the Valley of Trials. When he arrived, he found plenty of provisions already there, and the sack was not needed.",al={"why is ukor here","ukor quest reason","ukor food bundle"},it="why_here"},{q="What does Ukor ask passing travelers to do?",a="Ukor asks travelers heading north toward Razor Hill to return the bundle to Innkeeper Grosk. He is too afraid of the beasts along the road to carry it back himself.",al={"ukor task","what does ukor want","peons burden quest"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Ukor on?",a="Ukor is a loyal peon of the Horde. Humble and dutiful, he serves Durotar and his kin by hauling supplies and running errands between settlements like Razor Hill and the Valley of Trials, braving wild beasts without a complaint.",al={"ukor faction","is ukor horde","who does ukor serve"},it="side",add="5f505ef5"},{q="Who is Ukor tied to?",a="Ukor answers to Innkeeper Grosk back in Razor Hill. He undertook the journey to the Valley of Trials on Grosk's behalf to deliver fresh provisions, and he relies on passing adventurers to return surplus stock to the innkeeper.",al={"ukor allies","who does ukor know","ukor innkeeper grosk"},it="ties",add="2e03bca7"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Orc peons do the hard physical labor that helps build the new Horde. Ukor shows that even humble laborers want to support Durotar's warriors.",["faction:Horde"]="For new recruits emerging from their trials, helping Ukor is an early chance to support the everyday movement of supplies between Horde settlements."},kw={"a peon's burden","durotar","grosk","peon","razor hill","ukor","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:2161","npc:innkeeper-grosk","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar"},src={"Ukor"}}
E["npc:ula-elek"] = {t="npc",n="Ula'elek",z="durotar",s="In Sen'jin Village, Ula'elek forges armor for warriors across the Horde. This Darkspear smith works with Thun'grim Firegaze, shaping specialized gear through traditional troll craft and trophies gathered across Kalimdor.",h="In Sen'jin Village, Ula'elek forges armor for warriors across the Horde.",sec={{t="Smith of the Darkspear",b="Ula'elek serves the Darkspear as an armorsmith in Sen'jin Village. Nearby quilboar and sea crawlers threaten the coastal settlement, so the tribe needs sturdy armor and sound blades. Ula'elek's skill also brings seasoned warriors from across the Horde to his forge.",sp=0},{t="Forging the Brutal Armor",b="Young warriors who visit Thun'grim Firegaze at his overlook in the Barrens are sent south to Sen'jin Village. The veteran trusts Ula'elek to forge Brutal Gauntlets for battle-hardened fighters. The work calls for rare materials, especially swollen, uncloven hooves from the satyrs draining the forest's magic in northeastern Ashenvale.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ula'elek?",a="Ula'elek is a Darkspear troll armorsmith in Sen'jin Village. Horde veterans trust him to make specialized armor for promising frontline fighters.",al={"who is ula'elek","ula'elek lore","ulaelek background"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Ula'elek be found?",a="Ula'elek can be found in Sen'jin Village on Durotar's southeastern coast, south of Razor Hill.",al={"ula'elek location","where is ula'elek","find ulaelek"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Thun'grim Firegaze send warriors to Ula'elek?",a="Thun'grim Firegaze sends warriors to Ula'elek because he trusts the troll smith to forge Brutal Gauntlets for warriors who have earned his respect.",al={"thungrim and ulaelek","why go to ula'elek"},it="motive"},{q="What materials does Ula'elek need to make the gauntlets?",a="Ula'elek needs warriors to hunt satyrs in northeastern Ashenvale and gather their swollen, uncloven hooves for the Brutal Gauntlets.",al={"ula'elek materials","brutal gauntlets ingredients"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What kind of gear does Ula'elek craft?",a="Ula'elek specializes in heavy combat armor. He makes the Brutal Gauntlets, part of the Brutal Armor set for promising Horde warriors.",al={"what does ula'elek make","ula'elek rewards"},it="purpose"},{q="Why do the gauntlets require satyr hooves?",a="Satyrs in northeastern Ashenvale drain the forest's magic, and the most potent among them have swollen, uncloven hooves. Ula'elek draws power from those hooves and puts it into the gauntlets.",al={"why satyr hooves","hooves for gauntlets"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Whose side is Ula'elek on?",a="Ula'elek is a Darkspear troll loyal to the Horde. Based out of Sen'jin Village on the coast of Durotar, he plies his craft for the benefit of Horde champions, partnering with orcish smiths like Thun'grim Firegaze to forge sturdy armor for warriors who defend their shared lands.",al={"ulaelek faction","is ulaelek horde","ulaelek allegiance"},it="side",add="3fd6027c"},{q="What does Ula'elek want?",a="Ula'elek wants capable materials to practice his craft and fashion sturdy armor. When called upon by Thun'grim, he tasks rising warriors with gathering exotic components—such as satyr hooves—so that he can forge brutal gauntlets worthy of proven fighters.",al={"ulaelek goal","what does ula'elek need","what does ulaelek want"},it="wants",add="c0ac20d7"},{q="Why is Ula'elek here in Sen'jin Village?",a="Ula'elek resides in Sen'jin Village to serve his tribe and the Horde as an armorsmith. Working by the coast of Durotar, he remains close to his Darkspear kin while lending his forge to train and equip the Horde's frontline warriors.",al={"why is ulaelek in senjin","ulaelek location reason","why is ula'elek here"},it="why_here",add="a7c1ab84"},{q="Who is Ula'elek tied to?",a="Ula'elek is closely allied with Thun'grim Firegaze, an accomplished orc armorsmith stationed in the Barrens. Thun'grim trusts Ula'elek's skill enough to send promising warriors straight to his anvil in Sen'jin Village to have their gauntlets crafted.",al={"ulaelek connections","who does ulaelek know","ula'elek allies"},it="ties",add="e890a681"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you rely on Ula'elek to forge your Brutal armor set. At Thun'grim Firegaze's direction, he shapes hard-won satyr hooves into rugged gauntlets.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you see Darkspear smiths equipping the young Horde with frontline gear on Sen'jin Village's open shores.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you see Horde smiths turn beast and demon trophies to practical use in warrior armor, beyond traditional foundries."},kw={"brutal gauntlets","darkspear","durotar","satyr hooves","sen'jin village","smith","thun'grim firegaze","ula'elek"},rel={"quest:1839","quest:1842","quest:1843","quest:1502","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","topic:satyr","topic:troll"},src={"Ula'elek"}}
E["npc:vol-jin"] = {t="npc",n="Vol'jin",z="durotar",s="In Orgrimmar, Vol'jin counsels Warchief Thrall and seeks a lasting home for his people. The Darkspear chieftain is a master shadow hunter.",h="In Orgrimmar, Vol'jin counsels Warchief Thrall and seeks a lasting home for his people.",sec={{t="Chieftain of the Darkspear",b="After his father Sen'jin dies on their ancestral island, Vol'jin leads the Darkspear. Sea witch-worshipping murlocs and human forces nearly destroy the isolated tribe. Thrall's orcs intervene, and a deep bond forms between the orcs and trolls. Fleeing the ruined islands, Vol'jin pledges his people to the New Horde and leads them across the Great Sea to Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="Council in the Valley of Wisdom",b="The Darkspear settle in Durotar, but Zalazane betrays them on the Echo Isles. Many refugees flee to the mainland and Sen'jin Village. Vol'jin spends much of his time in Grommash Hold in Orgrimmar, giving Thrall strategic counsel and the benefit of his shadow hunter skill. From the orcish capital, he watches over the young Horde and works to reclaim his people's lands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Vol'jin?",a="Vol'jin leads the Darkspear troll tribe and advises Warchief Thrall in Orgrimmar. A skilled shadow hunter, he speaks for his people among the Horde's leaders.",al={"who is the troll leader","voljin lore","darkspear leader"},it="identity"},{q="Where does Vol'jin live?",a="Vol'jin lives in Grommash Hold, in Orgrimmar's Valley of Wisdom, beside Warchief Thrall.",al={"where is voljin","voljin location","find voljin"},it="place"},{q="Why did the Darkspear join the Horde?",a="During the Third War, Thrall's fleet washed ashore on the Darkspear Islands. The orcs allied with the trolls against hostile humans and a fanatical murloc army. After Sen'jin died, Vol'jin pledged his tribe to Thrall, and the Darkspear followed the Horde to Kalimdor.",al={"why are trolls horde","darkspear horde history","thrall and voljin"}},{q="Why aren't the Darkspear living on their own islands?",a="After settling on the Echo Isles off Durotar, the witch doctor Zalazane was driven mad by dark magic. He enslaved his fellow tribesmen, forcing Vol'jin and the surviving Darkspear to flee to Sen'jin Village on the mainland.",al={"what happened to echo isles","why are trolls in senjin village","zalazane betrayal"}},{q="Whose side is Vol'jin on?",a="Vol'jin is entirely devoted to the Horde and his own exiled Darkspear trolls. Ever since Thrall and the orcs rescued his tribe from slaughter in their island homeland, Vol'jin has honored his father's oath of allegiance. He serves as one of Thrall's most trusted confidants, offering wise counsel and tactical guidance from within the heart of Orgrimmar.",al={"voljin faction","who does voljin serve","is voljin horde"},it="side",add="00b3c7ef"},{q="What does Vol'jin want?",a="Vol'jin wants above all to secure a stable and prosperous future for the Darkspear tribe, fulfilling the dying vision of his father, Sen'jin. He works closely with Thrall to cement the Horde's foothold across Durotar, striving to protect his displaced people from the hostile threats of Kalimdor and preserve their ancestral traditions.",al={"voljin goals","what are voljin's motives","what does voljin seek"},it="wants",add="9b5f7e47"},{q="Why is Vol'jin in Orgrimmar?",a="Vol'jin resides in Grommash Hold beside Thrall to represent the Darkspear trolls at the very center of Horde leadership. In addition to guiding his people, he acts as a chief strategist and spiritual advisor to the Warchief, coordinating tribal defenses and strengthening the vital alliance between troll and orc.",al={"why is voljin in orgrimmar","why is voljin here","what is voljin doing in orgrimmar"},it="why_here",add="ee20a7f7"},{q="Who is Vol'jin tied to?",a="Vol'jin is the son and successor of the revered witch doctor Sen'jin, whose sacrifice saved the Darkspear. He shares an unshakeable bond with Warchief Thrall, whom he advises daily, and his ties to the loa guide his path as a shadow hunter.",al={"voljin allies","voljin connections","who is voljin related to"},it="ties",add="df7c3222"},{q="Why is Vol'jin famous?",a="Vol'jin is renowned as both the chieftain of the Darkspear tribe and an accomplished shadow hunter, deeply attuned to the loa. He led his people through devastating murloc raids, human invasions, and exile, earning the eternal respect of trolls and the highest esteem among the founders of the new Horde.",al={"why is voljin revered","voljin reputation","is voljin famous"},it="fame",add="779e986b"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you have Vol'jin for a chieftain. He guides the displaced Darkspear through hardship with spiritual wisdom and tactical resolve.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you have Vol'jin beside Thrall, offering cunning counsel and the fierce loyalty of the jungle trolls."},kw={"darkspear","grommash hold","orgrimmar","sen'jin","shadow hunter","thrall","vol'jin","zalazane"},rel={"npc:thrall","topic:darkspear-tribe","topic:troll","zone:orgrimmar","quest:826","npc:master-gadrin","topic:horde","zone:durotar"},src={"Vol'jin"}}
E["npc:zjolnir"] = {t="npc",n="Zjolnir",z="durotar",s="In Sen'jin Village, Zjolnir raises raptors for Darkspear riders and trusted Horde champions. These trained mounts carry deep cultural pride for troll riders.",h="In Sen'jin Village, Zjolnir raises raptors for Darkspear riders and trusted Horde champions.",sec={{t="Breeder of the Darkspear Raptors",b="Near Sen'jin Village, Zjolnir tends the pens where he raises the fierce raptors favored by the Darkspear. Their wild nature calls for an expert hand before they can be raised and saddled for war.\n\nHe gives these prized mounts freely to fellow trolls who have learned the riding arts. Other Horde members must first earn exalted trust with the Darkspear tribe before he will entrust them with a raptor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Zjolnir?",a="Zjolnir tends the raptor pens in Sen'jin Village, a Darkspear settlement on Durotar's southern coast.",al={"zjolnir location","where is zjolnir","raptor vendor location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Zjolnir sell?",a="Zjolnir sells whistle-summoned raptors, the Darkspear trolls' racial mounts. He offers several breeds and colors for newly trained riders and seasoned veterans.",al={"zjolnir vendor","what does he sell","troll mount vendor"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Can non-trolls buy raptors from him?",a="Yes. Non-trolls must earn exalted standing with the Darkspear Trolls before Zjolnir will sell them a raptor. Trolls may buy once they have the required riding skill.",al={"can orcs buy raptors","who can buy mounts from zjolnir","horde raptor mount"},it="for_you",gp=true},{q="Who is Zjolnir?",a="Zjolnir is a Darkspear jungle troll handler and breeder who tends to the tribe's prized raptors. Stationed in Sen'jin Village on the Durotar coast, he provides sturdy raptor mounts to his fellow trolls and trusted champions of the Horde who have proven their dedication to the Darkspear tribe.",al={"who is zjolnir","zjolnir lore","who is the raptor vendor"},it="identity",add="a5db9414"},{q="Whose side is Zjolnir on?",a="He is fiercely loyal to the Darkspear tribe and the Horde. Residing in Sen'jin Village under the leadership of Chieftain Vol'jin, he offers his carefully trained beasts exclusively to his kin and to outsiders who have earned exalted standing with the Darkspear.",al={"zjolnir faction","who does zjolnir serve","is zjolnir horde"},it="side",add="324eb78a"},{q="Why is Zjolnir here?",a="Sen'jin Village serves as the primary coastal haven for the Darkspear trolls following their exile from the Echo Isles. Zjolnir stays here to raise, care for, and supply the tribe's fierce raptor mounts for scouts, raiders, and riders defending their new home in Durotar.",al={"why is zjolnir in senjin village","what is zjolnir doing here"},it="why_here",add="58f60087"},{q="What does Zjolnir want?",a="Zjolnir aims to see the Darkspear tribe well-mounted and strong. He seeks capable riders worthy of handling the tribe's predatory raptors, entrusting the deadly beasts only to fellow trolls or allies whose service and loyalty to the Darkspear have been proven beyond question.",al={"what does zjolnir want","zjolnir goals"},it="wants",add="4b978e02"},{q="Who is Zjolnir tied to?",a="He is bound directly to the Darkspear trolls and serves the community established in Sen'jin Village. His work directly supports the tribe's defense and mobility under Chieftain Vol'jin and the wider Horde alliance founded alongside Thrall.",al={"zjolnir affiliations","who does zjolnir work with"},it="ties",add="bad296c7"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you can ride the swift, clawed beasts at the heart of your heritage and fighting traditions. Zjolnir provides raptors for your people.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde warrior, you can earn the right to ride one of Zjolnir's raptors into battle by proving your steadfast devotion to the Darkspear tribe."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","mount","raptor","sen'jin village","troll mount","zjolnir"},rel={"subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Zjolnir"}}
E["npc:zureetha-fargaze"] = {t="npc",n="Zureetha Fargaze",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Zureetha Fargaze watches for threats to young Horde recruits. Alongside Foreman Thazz'ril, she sends them to uncover and root out the Burning Blade cult hidden in Durotar.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Zureetha Fargaze watches for threats to young Horde recruits.",sec={{t="Eyes in the Valley",b="Zureetha Fargaze watches for dangers beyond the work and discipline Foreman Thazz'ril oversees. The Burning Blade cult has entered the Valley of Trials in secret. It has corrupted lesser demons and gathered strength in the nearby Burning Blade Coven. She sends untested adventurers to recover medallions from cultists, confirm the danger and disrupt the cult's early efforts. Then she directs seasoned recruits farther into Durotar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zureetha Fargaze?",a="Zureetha Fargaze watches over the Valley of Trials in Durotar. She keeps watch near Foreman Thazz'ril for threats to the training grounds.",al={"zureetha fargaze lore","who is zureetha","fargaze valley of trials"},it="identity"},{q="Why is she concerned about the Burning Blade?",a="The Burning Blade cult has taken root in a nearby cave. It gathers foul familiars and corrupts the peaceful trial grounds, so Zureetha sends recruits to recover cultist medallions as proof and weaken its ranks.",al={"burning blade valley of trials","why does zureetha want medallions","burning blade cult durotar"},it="wants"},{q="Where does she send recruits after their initial trials?",a="After young orcs and trolls prove themselves against local threats, Zureetha sends them southeast across the ridge to Sen'jin Village. There they aid the Darkspear tribe.",al={"where do i go after zureetha","zureetha next quest","report to sen'jin"},it="next_step"},{q="Whose side is Zureetha Fargaze on?",a="Zureetha stands firmly with Thrall's Horde. Stationed in the Valley of Trials alongside Foreman Thazz'ril, her duty is to guide young recruits and safeguard the training grounds from internal corruption and hidden enemies.",al={"zureetha fargaze faction","who does zureetha serve","is zureetha horde"},it="side",add="b30f15ad"},{q="Why is Zureetha Fargaze here in the Valley of Trials?",a="She is posted in the Valley of Trials to watch over the newly arrived orcs and trolls as they begin their training. More urgently, she remains vigilant against the shadowy reach of the Burning Blade cult, which has begun creeping into the valley's nearby caves.",al={"why is zureetha in valley of trials","zureetha purpose durotar","why is zureetha here"},it="why_here",add="497b9432"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As a young orc taking your first steps into the world, you see in Zureetha the vigilance needed to keep the demonic taint of the past from polluting your new homeland.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock in the Valley of Trials, you encounter Zureetha's early tasks and face the vile familiars corrupted by the Burning Blade's dark summonings."},kw={"burning blade","burning blade medallion","durotar","foreman thazz'ril","valley of trials","zureetha fargaze"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","subzone:sen-jin-village"},src={"Zureetha Fargaze"}}
E["quest:1463"] = {t="quest",n="Earth Sapta",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Earth Sapta is lost, and an initiate can ask Canaga Earthcaller for another. The replacement lets the young shaman commune with the spirits of the land, with a warning to guard sacred draughts carefully.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Earth Sapta is lost, and an initiate can ask Canaga Earthcaller for another.",sec={{t="A Second Chance with the Elements",b="An initiate who loses the Earth Sapta may lose the chance to commune with the spirits of stone and soil. Rituals prepare the elemental brew, which thins the veil between the physical realm and the spirits. If the draught is lost or spilled while traveling through Durotar, Canaga Earthcaller prepares another in good faith. He warns the novice to guard sacred gifts with greater care.",sp=0},{t="Canaga's Guidance",b="Canaga Earthcaller watches over fledgling shamans emerging from the Den in the Valley of Trials. Young orcs and trolls can stumble amid their early trials, but elemental spirits do not take kindly to negligence. Accepting a second sapta brings a small lesson in humility. Power granted by the earth must be guarded and respected.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is an Earth Sapta?",a="The Earth Sapta is a ceremonial draught prepared for shaman initiates. Drinking it grants spiritual sight, so they can perceive and speak with elemental earth spirits unseen by ordinary eyes.",al={"what is sapta","earth sapta use","purpose of sapta"},it="item"},{q="Why does Canaga Earthcaller offer this quest?",a="Canaga Earthcaller offers another Earth Sapta when an initiate loses or misplaces theirs before completing the communion ritual during the Call of Earth trials. He provides a replacement in good faith so the acolyte can finish the spiritual task.",al={"why canaga gives sapta","lost my earth sapta"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this ritual take place?",a="The exchange takes place in the Valley of Trials, a sun-scorched canyon in southwestern Durotar. Young orcs and trolls begin their journeys of discipline and honor there.",al={"where is canaga","valley of trials sapta location"},it="place"},{q="Is losing the sapta seen poorly by the spirits?",a="Canaga warns initiates that careless handling of sacred draughts shows a lack of focus. A true shaman treats every elemental gift with reverence.",al={"does losing sapta matter","lore of losing sapta"}},{q="Who can undertake this communion?",a="Shamans seeking to attune themselves to their first elemental totem, the Earth Totem, may prepare and drink the Earth Sapta.",al={"who can get earth sapta","classes for sapta"},it="people"},{q="What happens after an initiate drinks the sapta?",a="Drinking the draught opens an initiate's inner vision. They can then find and speak with a local manifestation of the earth spirit tucked away in the crags of the Valley of Trials.",al={"what does sapta do when drunk","after earth sapta"},it="next_step"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As an initiate shaman, you learn discipline when you lose the sapta. Communion with the elements calls for steady focus and careful hands.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you learn the ancient ways of shamanism in Durotar's arid crags. Your dedication is tested against the ancestors and the earth beneath your boots.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you learn to balance traditional loa worship with reverence for the elemental spirits in the Valley of Trials."},kw={"call of earth","canaga earthcaller","draught","durotar","earth sapta","shaman","totem","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:canaga-earthcaller","quest:1516","quest:1462","zone:durotar"},m={start="Canaga Earthcaller",level="4",faction="Horde",cl={"SHAMAN"},id=1463},src={"Earth Sapta (Durotar)"}}
E["quest:1485"] = {t="quest",n="Vile Familiars",z="durotar",s="Near the Den, Vile Familiars threaten warlocks who seek the power of demons. Ruzan asks you to prove your strength by bringing back their heads. This is the first dangerous step toward mastering fel power under the Horde’s watchful eyes.",h="Near the Den, Vile Familiars threaten warlocks who seek the power of demons.",sec={{t="A Precarious Place in the Horde",b="Warlocks have an uneasy place in Thrall’s new Horde. Demonic corruption and blood pacts once brought ruin to the orcs, leaving deep scars and distrust. Durotar tolerates fel magic, but its practitioners are neither loved nor welcomed. Many warlocks live apart and practice in shadowed places like the Den, away from prying eyes. There, they teach the few initiates daring enough to follow their path.",sp=0},{t="The Trial of Mastery",b="Ruzan asks you to prove your strength before he teaches you the dangerous rites for bending an imp to your will. Vile Familiars lurk near a cave northeast of the Den and hurl bolts of flame at those who approach. Slay these lesser demons and bring their heads back to Ruzan. They will show him you can overcome the fiery creatures you hope to control. Only then can you face the danger of the magic you seek to command.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Ruzan send warlocks to fight vile familiars?",a="Ruzan sends you to face an imp’s fiery nature and danger before you try to summon one. Warlocks are few and distrusted, so he asks you to prove you can defeat such creatures before teaching you demon summoning.",al={"why kill vile familiars","ruzan test","imp trial"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the vile familiars found?",a="Vile Familiars gather around and inside a cave northeast of the Den in the Valley of Trials, beyond the roaming boars and scorpids. The cave is an encampment for the Burning Blade Coven.",al={"vile familiar location","where are familiars","ruzan cave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How does the Horde view warlocks in Durotar?",a="Warlocks face deep suspicion across the Horde because demonic corruption once scarred the orcs. Thrall’s government tolerates them and sees their value in battle, yet many still live apart.",al={"are warlocks hated","horde warlock lore","why distrust warlocks"},it="conflict"},{q="What reward does completing this trial offer?",a="Bringing Ruzan the heads of slain Vile Familiars proves you have the strength and discipline to command demons. He can then teach you to summon an imp minion.",al={"what do i learn","quest reward ruzan","imp spell"},it="for_you",gp=true},{q="Are vile familiars actual demons?",a="Yes. Vile Familiars are minor demonic imps tied to fel magic. Though small, they are formidable foes who hurl fireballs at their enemies.",al={"what are vile familiars","are familiars imps","familiar demon type"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Ruzan?",a="Ruzan is an orc warlock trainer in the Den in the Valley of Trials. He teaches new orc warlocks to harness fel energy safely and control summoned servants.",al={"ruzan","who is ruzan","valley of trials warlock"},it="people"},{q="What are the Vile Familiar Heads for?",a="Ruzan requires the heads as physical proof of your triumph over the creatures in combat. Because so few novices choose the warlock's path, he refuses to teach you the hazardous art of demon summoning until you can prove you possess the power and will to dominate them.",al={"vile familiar head use","why collect vile familiar heads","ruzan vile familiar heads"},it="item",add="2f864f20"},{q="What are the vile familiars doing in the Valley of Trials?",a="These vicious, imp-like creatures cluster around a cave northeast of the Den known as the Burning Blade Coven. Drawn by corrupt magics or bound by lurking cultists, they serve as a lethal proving ground for fledgling warlocks to test their resolve against minor demonic minions.",al={"why are vile familiars here","vile familiars valley of trials","cave vile familiars"},it="target",add="58d905b2"},{q="Why does Ruzan send you instead of dealing with the familiars himself?",a="This is a personal trial of mastery, not a public defense task. If Ruzan or the Grunts dispatched the familiars, it would teach you nothing. A warlock who cannot overpower a basic demon in direct combat will inevitably be consumed or destroyed the moment they attempt to summon one.",al={"why doesn't ruzan kill them","why me ruzan","why does ruzan test me"},it="why_me",add="cca9ea14"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you face this first trial to prove you can subdue demonic fire before learning the rite to summon an imp of your own.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you meet your people’s dark history each day. You must prove your control and loyalty in a society that remembers the horrors of fel corruption.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can train as a warlock in Durotar, though the dark arts remain confined to isolated places like the Den."},kw={"burning blade coven","durotar","imp","ruzan","the den","valley of trials","vile familiars","warlock"},rel={"quest:792","subzone:burning-blade-coven","subzone:the-den","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},m={start="Ruzan",level="4",faction="Horde",cl={"WARLOCK"},id=1485,ri={"Vile Familiar Head"}},src={"Vile Familiars (Warlock)"}}
E["quest:1499"] = {t="quest",n="Vile Familiars",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Ruzan tests warlock initiates against vile familiars. After you slay them, you report to Zureetha Fargaze, who directs the effort against the Burning Blade.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Ruzan tests warlock initiates against vile familiars.",sec={{t="A Matter of Discipline",b="Warriors and scouts in the Valley of Trials answer to Zureetha Fargaze. She sends them to curb the Burning Blade Coven. Warlock initiates answer first to Ruzan, their shadowy mentor. He demands proof that you can master lesser demons before sending you back to aid the Horde's defense. Your work helps the warlocks and keeps the Den safe.",sp=0},{t="The Threat of the Coven",b="Zureetha Fargaze watches the northern cavern above the Valley of Trials. Vile familiars hide within, the weakest pets of the Burning Blade cultists. Their presence insults the orcs and threatens the sacred training grounds. When you report your success, you show that those who practice fel magic are ready to defend Durotar from corruption.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Ruzan send me to Zureetha Fargaze instead of rewarding me himself?",a="Zureetha Fargaze directs the defense and the effort to cull the Burning Blade in the Valley of Trials. Ruzan tests your control over lesser fel creatures, then sends you to her so she can recognize your service and include it in the Valley's defense.",al={"why see zureetha","ruzan to zureetha","why talk to zureetha"},it="motive"},{q="Who are the vile familiars?",a="Vile familiars are minor demonic imps and minions bound to the Burning Blade Coven. They serve darker masters deep inside the cavern overlooking the Valley of Trials.",al={"what are vile familiars","vile familiar lore","familiars burning blade"},it="target"},{q="Where can I find Zureetha Fargaze?",a="Zureetha Fargaze is out in the open near the center of the Den in the Valley of Trials. She is a short walk up from the trainers' camp where Ruzan resides.",al={"where is zureetha","zureetha fargaze location","zureetha map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is there another quest with the exact same name?",a="Most adventurers receive Vile Familiars directly from Zureetha Fargaze and hunt the creatures for her. Warlocks receive a separate task from Ruzan, then report to Zureetha when they finish.",al={"two vile familiars quests","duplicate vile familiars","warlock vile familiars"},gp=true},{q="What is the Burning Blade doing in the Valley of Trials?",a="The Burning Blade cult operates in secret pockets across Durotar, seeking to undermine Thrall's new Horde from within. Its members prey on unproven novices from a cavern inside the Valley of Trials, spreading demonic corruption under the eyes of the orcish overseers.",al={"burning blade valley of trials","why are cultists in the den"},it="threat"},{q="Does slaying these familiars wipe out the cult?",a="No. Vile familiars are pets and scouts for the darker powers inside the coven. Defeating them begins the effort to uncover and cleanse the deeper cultist threat in the Valley.",al={"is burning blade defeated","are cultists gone"},it="next_step"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you face vile familiars to prove you can dominate and dismantle wild fel creatures without falling prey to them.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know demonic familiars recall the dark pacts that once enslaved your people. Removing them from Durotar's soil matters to your people's survival.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you share the Valley of Trials with others who view demonic magic with deep suspicion. You show your loyalty by standing against rogue cultists."},kw={"burning blade coven","durotar","imps","ruzan","the den","valley of trials","vile familiars","warlock quest","zureetha fargaze"},rel={"npc:zureetha-fargaze","quest:792","subzone:the-den","subzone:burning-blade-coven","zone:durotar"},m={start="Ruzan",["end"]="Zureetha Fargaze",level="4",faction="Horde",cl={"WARLOCK"},id=1499},src={"Vile Familiars (Warlock 2)"}}
E["quest:1505"] = {t="quest",n="Veteran Uzzek",z="durotar",s="Just south of Far Watch Post, recruits turn to Veteran Uzzek for lessons in combat. His years of experience teach young Horde warriors that strength calls for discipline and study.",h="Just south of Far Watch Post, recruits turn to Veteran Uzzek for lessons in combat.",sec={{t="The Path of the Warrior",b="Strength alone cannot make a Horde warrior a champion. The finest fighters stay humble students of their craft. Through discipline and study, they sharpen their instincts. Young warriors ready to pass beyond basic training seek veterans who have survived the trials of war.",sp=0},{t="The Veteran at the Border",b="Between Durotar and the Barrens, young fighters seek deeper guidance in combat. Far Watch Post watches the eastern frontier. Just south of the orc garrison, Veteran Uzzek teaches promising recruits combat and survival tactics. He has endured countless bloody conflicts and now guides the next generation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Veteran Uzzek?",a="Near the Durotar and Barrens frontier, Veteran Uzzek teaches young Horde warriors combat. He shares lessons learned through countless conflicts from his camp.",al={"who is uzzek","uzzek lore","who is the veteran"}},{q="Where can Uzzek be found?",a="Uzzek is south of Far Watch Post, the orc garrison on the eastern border between Durotar and the Barrens.",al={"where is uzzek","uzzek location","find uzzek"}},{q="What is Far Watch Post?",a="Far Watch Post is an orc garrison on the Barrens' eastern frontier. It guards the crossing from Durotar and protects the Horde's border.",al={"what is the far watch post","far watch post purpose"}},{q="Why are young warriors sent to Uzzek?",a="Young warriors seek Uzzek for combat instruction. The Horde prizes strength, but its finest fighters also master discipline, study, and martial technique.",al={"why visit uzzek","what does uzzek teach","warrior instruction"}},{q="What does Uzzek say when you arrive?",a="Uzzek welcomes young warriors to his post. He is ready to assess their commitment and teach them the ways of war.",al={"what happens when you speak to uzzek","uzzek quest turn in"}},{q="How does the Horde view its warriors?",a="The Horde honors warriors for their strength and devotion to battle. Its traditions also teach that mastery takes discipline and learning from seasoned veterans.",al={"who honors warriors","horde warrior culture"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you learn from Uzzek that brute force is not enough. True strength comes from disciplined study of combat.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you honor martial skill and rely on veteran fighters at frontier outposts to guide the next generation."},kw={"barrens","combat instruction","durotar","far watch post","horde","uzzek","veteran uzzek","warrior"},rel={"npc:uzzek","subzone:far-watch-post","zone:barrens","zone:durotar","topic:warrior","topic:horde"},m={faction="Horde",cl={"WARRIOR"},id=1505,xg=1505},src={"In-game quest text: Veteran Uzzek"},fv=true}
E["quest:1506"] = {t="quest",n="Gan'rul's Summons",z="durotar",s="Ophek brings Gan'rul's Summons to young Horde warlocks in Razor Hill. Gan'rul Bloodeye calls them to the Cleft of Shadow to advance their training. There, they take the first step toward summoning a voidwalker.",h="Ophek brings Gan'rul's Summons to young Horde warlocks in Razor Hill.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Shadows",b="In Durotar, novice warlocks do not go unnoticed for long. When a practitioner shows enough mastery over an initial imp, word reaches the deep caverns beneath Orgrimmar. Ophek carries messages for the senior dark casters from his post in Durotar. He finds warlocks with an urgent demand to leave their work and report to the Cleft of Shadow.",sp=0},{t="The Senior Warlock",b="Gan'rul Bloodeye oversees the training of young orc warlocks within the Horde. From the hidden caverns beneath Orgrimmar, he hones their lethal fel power while keeping these dangerous arts from the Warchief's disapproving gaze. A call to his circle means simple fire spells and imps are no longer enough. The apprentice is ready to bind a creature from the Twisting Nether.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ophek?",a="Ophek is an associate of the warlocks stationed in Durotar. He watches for rising practitioners and carries orders from senior mentors such as Gan'rul Bloodeye.",al={"ophek","who gives this quest","quest starter"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Gan'rul Bloodeye located?",a="Gan'rul Bloodeye is in the Cleft of Shadow, a dark cavern system beneath Orgrimmar's rocky plateaus.",al={"where is ganrul","gan'rul location","find gan'rul bloodeye"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Gan'rul Bloodeye want to see me?",a="Gan'rul considers you ready to advance your warlock studies and begin the dangerous rites to summon and bind a voidwalker.",al={"why summons","what does ganrul want","quest reason"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens after reporting to Gan'rul?",a="Reporting to Gan'rul begins Creature of the Void. You are sent to find the components and knowledge needed to draw a void entity into Azeroth.",al={"next quest","what comes after gan'rul's summons"},it="next_step"},{q="Why do the warlocks stay in the Cleft of Shadow?",a="Warlocks practice volatile fel magic, which Thrall and the traditional shamanic Horde regard with deep suspicion. The Cleft of Shadow lets them perform rituals out of public view.",al={"why cleft of shadow","why are warlocks hiding","warlock cave orgrimmar"},it="why_here"},{q="Can any class take this quest?",a="No. Only Horde warlocks who have reached the tenth circle of their training can receive the summons.",al={"is this warlock only","who gets this quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Ophek send you to Gan'rul?",a="Ophek acts simply as an errand runner and messenger for Gan'rul Bloodeye. Senior warlocks in the Cleft of Shadow do not wander Orgrimmar hunting down apprentices themselves; they send lackeys to fetch who they need. Ophek knows better than to delay Gan'rul's summons, warning you that keeping a warlock master waiting rarely ends well.",al={"why does ophek send me","ophek motive","why is ophek delivering the summons"},it="motive",add="f5421555"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, this summons marks your path beyond basic imp conjuration. It opens the way to command a voidwalker's sturdy protection.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know warlocks hold an uneasy place in Thrall's new Horde. Their pragmatic power is tolerated, while they remain secluded beneath Orgrimmar."},kw={"bloodeye","cleft of shadow","gan'rul","ophek","orgrimmar","summons","voidwalker","warlock quest"},rel={"npc:gan-rul-bloodeye","quest:1473","quest:1471","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Ophek",["end"]="Gan'rul Bloodeye",level="10",faction="Horde",cl={"WARLOCK"},id=1506,xg=1478},src={"Gan'rul's Summons"}}
E["quest:1516"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Earth",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Canaga Earthcaller tests novice Horde shamans through endurance and patience. Their hunt for felstalkers prepares a ritual sapta.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Canaga Earthcaller tests novice Horde shamans through endurance and patience.",sec={{t="The First Bond",b="A shaman first learns to bond with each element. For orcs and trolls, that path begins with earth, the bedrock of life, endurance, and patience. In the Valley of Trials, Canaga Earthcaller guides new shamans. He teaches them that earth demands respect and steadfastness before it grants protection.",sp=0},{t="A Cleansing Hunt",b="North of the Valley of Trials, the Burning Blade cult works dark magic in the ravines. Its spells summon felstalkers, corrupt hounds from beyond this plane. Hunting them tests whether a shaman can defend the land from unnatural decay. Canaga uses their hooves to brew an Earth Sapta, a sacred draft that opens mortal eyes to the elemental plane.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this trial?",a="The trial begins a shaman’s study of elemental mysteries and tests patience and spiritual discipline before the earth spirits. It prepares them to commune with those spirits and earn an Earth Totem.",al={"why do call of earth","what does call of earth give","purpose of quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Canaga Earthcaller?",a="Canaga Earthcaller is a troll shaman trainer in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. He guides young orc, troll, and visiting tauren shamans toward elemental mastery.",al={"who is canaga","canaga earthcaller lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Canaga need felstalker hooves?",a="Canaga uses felstalker hooves to prepare an Earth Sapta. The potion lets a mortal shaman perceive and speak with elemental spirits.",al={"why felstalker hooves","hooves purpose"},it="item"},{q="Where are the felstalkers located?",a="Felstalkers haunt the cave and surrounding bluffs north of the training grounds in the Valley of Trials. They are within the Burning Blade Coven.",al={"felstalker location","where to find felstalkers"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Can other Horde races undertake this version of the trial?",a="Yes. The trial is mainly for orc and troll shamans coming of age in Durotar. Tauren shamans traveling from Red Cloud Mesa can also undertake it in the Valley of Trials.",al={"can tauren do this","is this orc only"},gp=true},{q="What virtues does the earth represent to a shaman?",a="In shamanic tradition, earth is the foundation of life. It embodies great strength, stamina, and eternal patience, yet can be stubbornly fickle when not respected.",al={"virtues of earth","shaman earth meaning"},it="power"},{q="Why does Canaga Earthcaller want this done?",a="Canaga serves as a guide for young shaman taking their first steps on the spiritual path. He senses that a time of conflict approaches and that you possess the enduring spirit required to commune with the earth. Before he can prepare the sacred sapta and share the earth's mysteries, he must test your resolve, strength, and patience against dangerous adversaries to ensure you are ready to heed the element's call.",al={"canaga earthcaller motive","why does canaga test you","canaga earthcaller why"},it="motive",add="a9a10a24"},{q="Why are the felstalkers in the Valley of Trials?",a="These demonic hounds haunt the northern reaches of the valley, summoned and bound by the shadowy warlocks of the Burning Blade Coven who have hidden themselves within the local caverns. Their foul presence defiles the surrounding land, making them both an immediate threat to young initiates and a fitting test of courage and martial strength for a budding shaman.",al={"why are there felstalkers here","felstalkers valley of trials","what are the felstalkers"},it="target",add="3057b25e"},{q="Why must you face the felstalkers instead of the valley's guards?",a="This is a personal spiritual trial, not a standard military operation. A shaman must establish their own harmony with the elements through personal trial and demonstrated strength. Having warriors or guards gather the hooves would prove nothing to the stubborn spirits of the earth, who demand that you face danger directly and prove your own patience, endurance, and capability before granting their power.",al={"why me call of earth","why not send guards felstalkers","why must i hunt the felstalkers"},it="why_me",add="dddcc185"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you begin formal communion with the elements here. This lays the foundation for your Earth Totem.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc under Thrall’s Horde, you honor ancient clan traditions from before the demonic corruption by returning to the shamanic path.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you follow Darkspear witch doctors and spiritualists in embracing earth spirits. They support your people’s new home alongside the orcs."},kw={"burning blade","call of earth","canaga earthcaller","earth totem","felstalker","sapta","shaman trial","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:canaga-earthcaller","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:burning-blade-coven","quest:792","quest:794","zone:durotar","zone:mulgore"},m={start="Canaga Earthcaller",["end"]="Canaga Earthcaller",level="4",faction="Horde",cl={"SHAMAN"},id=1516,ri={"Felstalker Hoof"},xg=1516},src={"Call of Earth (Durotar)"}}
E["quest:1517"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Earth",z="durotar",s="At Spirit Rock, Canaga Earthcaller guides young shaman through their first communion with the elements. An Earth Sapta lets them see the Minor Manifestation of Earth on sacred ground.",h="At Spirit Rock, Canaga Earthcaller guides young shaman through their first communion with the elements.",sec={{t="The Power of the Sapta",b="A sapta is a rare draught known to only a few shaman masters. Elemental magic lets it bridge mortal sight and the spiritual plane, granting Sapta Sight to the strong-willed. Since it binds the drinker's spirit directly to an element, tradition forbids drinking it outside consecrated holy ground.",sp=0},{t="Pilgrimage to Spirit Rock",b="To commune with earth, you leave the Valley of Trials and climb the Hidden Path into Durotar's southern crags. Spirit Rock waits at the trail's end, an elevated sanctuary above the rugged wasteland. Drink the sapta there, and you can see what ordinary eyes cannot: an elemental presence among the stone.",sp=0},{t="Patience of the Earth",b="The Minor Manifestation of Earth asks for neither bloodshed nor submission. It asks only that you stand humbly before the world. Fire, water, and air bear turbulent, volatile, often chaotic spirits, while earth teaches steadiness. Mountains endure, and plains teach boundless patience.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is an Earth Sapta?",a="An Earth Sapta is a potion brewed by veteran shaman to attune a drinker's spirit temporarily to earth. It grants the inner sight needed to see and speak with hidden elemental spirits.",al={"what is sapta","earth sapta meaning","what does sapta do"},it="item"},{q="Where is Spirit Rock located?",a="Spirit Rock lies in the craggy mountains southwest of the Den in the Valley of Trials. Follow the Hidden Path into the hills south of the valley floor to reach it.",al={"where is spirit rock","spirit rock location","how to find spirit rock"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why must the sapta be consumed at Spirit Rock?",a="Shamanic tradition allows a sapta to be drunk only in a designated holy place. Sacred sites like Spirit Rock are natural thin places between the mortal realm and elemental spirits.",al={"why drink at spirit rock","can i drink sapta anywhere"},it="place"},{q="Who is the Minor Manifestation of Earth?",a="The Minor Manifestation of Earth is an elemental spirit dwelling at Spirit Rock. Only Sapta Sight can reveal it, and the spirit greets young shaman to test their humility and teach the first lessons of elemental balance.",al={"manifestation of earth","who is the earth spirit"},it="identity"},{q="Can any Horde shaman undertake this trial?",a="Young orc and Darkspear troll shaman training in Durotar chiefly undertake this rite. Tauren shaman who travel here may also complete it, though their equivalent rite takes place on Red Cloud Mesa.",al={"can tauren do this quest","who can do call of earth"},it="people"},{q="How does the earth spirit react to the initiate?",a="Unlike the volatile manifestations of fire or air, the earth spirit welcomes initiates who approach with humble respect. It bestows its blessing without demanding a contest of strength.",al={"what does the earth spirit say","is the earth spirit hostile"}},{q="Why does Canaga Earthcaller want this done?",a="Canaga Earthcaller is guiding you along the spiritual path of the shaman. Having proven your readiness by gathering the necessary ritual components, he now requires you to drink the Earth Sapta at Spirit Rock. His purpose is to forge your bond with the elemental spirits of the land, allowing your vision to pierce the veil and commune directly with the earth.",al={"canaga motive","why send to spirit rock","why drink earth sapta"},it="motive",add="1aaf4733"},{q="Why does Canaga Earthcaller send you instead of going himself?",a="This journey is a sacred rite of passage that every aspiring shaman must undertake personally. The Earth Sapta binds the drinker's own spirit to the element, granting vision that cannot be experienced through a surrogate. Canaga already commands this communion; you must stand before the earth humbly yourself to earn its blessing.",al={"why me canaga","why send player to spirit rock","why must i drink the sapta"},it="why_me",add="99304602"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you take your first step toward attunement with the elements. True mastery begins with earth's quiet patience.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs returning to ancestral ways after generations of fel corruption, communion through the Earth Sapta is a sacred rediscovery of their people's traditional bond with the spirits.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you embrace these earthen rites to adapt your deep ancestral ties to Durotar's harsh, sun-baked landscape."},kw={"call of earth","canaga earthcaller","earth sapta","hidden path","minor manifestation of earth","sapta sight","spirit rock","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:canaga-earthcaller","npc:minor-manifestation-of-earth","subzone:spirit-rock","subzone:hidden-path","quest:1462","quest:1516","subzone:the-den","zone:durotar"},m={start="Canaga Earthcaller",["end"]="Minor Manifestation of Earth",level="4",faction="Horde",cl={"SHAMAN"},id=1517},src={"Call of Earth (Durotar 2)"}}
E["quest:1518"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Earth",z="durotar",s="In Durotar, you seek the earth spirit’s favor and return to Canaga Earthcaller with rough quartz. He shapes it into your first elemental totem.",h="In Durotar, you seek the earth spirit’s favor and return to Canaga Earthcaller with rough quartz.",sec={{t="Heart of the Stone",b="A novice shaman seeks the earth through patience and humility. Brute strength will not win the spirit’s favor. The Minor Manifestation of Earth gives you rough quartz. That small stone proves the spirit has accepted your pledge, and it holds the seed of power.",sp=0},{t="The First of Four Paths",b="You complete the trial when you bring the quartz to Canaga Earthcaller in the Valley of Trials. Canaga shapes it into an Earth Totem, the focus through which you channel the ground’s steadfast protection and strength.\n\nEarth begins your path through the four elemental disciplines. The rite lays the foundation for a lifetime of communion with the natural world.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the rough quartz used for?",a="The rough quartz is a token from the Minor Manifestation of Earth and proof that you have communed with the spirit. Canaga Earthcaller sets it into your Earth Totem as its heart and as a focus for your earth spells.",al={"rough quartz","what does quartz do","purpose of quartz"},it="item"},{q="Who is Canaga Earthcaller?",a="Canaga Earthcaller trains shaman in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. He guides young orc and troll initiates through their earliest trials, preparing them to commune with elemental spirits and shaping their first totems.",al={"canaga","canaga earthcaller","who is canaga"},it="identity"},{q="Can tauren do this quest?",a="Yes. Tauren usually complete their trial of earth with their own elders at Red Cloud Mesa in Mulgore. Any Horde shaman who travels to the Valley of Trials can undergo the ritual with Canaga Earthcaller.",al={"can tauren do durotar call of earth","tauren shaman durotar","tauren call of earth"},gp=true},{q="What does receiving the Earth Totem signify?",a="Receiving an Earth Totem signifies that the spirit of the earth has recognized you. It marks your standing among shaman and gives you a physical focus for earth-based blessings and wards.",al={"why get earth totem","shaman earth totem meaning"},it="purpose"},{q="What virtues does the earth demand from a shaman?",a="The spirit asks an initiate for patience, strength, and wisdom. Even the smallest pebble can outlast mountains through endurance. The earth teaches shaman to respect the ground, so it will support them in turn.",al={"earth spirit lessons","what does earth ask"}},{q="Where does the shaman path go after this?",a="Earth is the first of the four elements a shaman must master. As your training continues, you are called to seek communion with the spirits of fire, water, and air.",al={"what totem next","after earth totem","four paths shaman"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does the Minor Manifestation of Earth give you the rough quartz?",a="Having tested your resolve and acknowledged your communion, the spirit grants you the rough quartz as tangible proof of your bond. It wants you to take this small stone back to Canaga Earthcaller so it can serve as the living heart of your first totem, binding the enduring strength and patience of the earth directly to your spiritual practice.",al={"minor manifestation of earth motive","why rough quartz","manifestation of earth why send"},it="motive",add="946f939a"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, this rite gives you your first totem. It lets you ground yourself in the elements and call upon the soil for aid.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you take part in the revival of orcish shamanism in Durotar. You turn back toward elemental balance after decades of demonic corruption.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you learn beside the orcs in the Valley of Trials. You adapt the Darkspear witch doctors’ and spiritualists’ traditional communion to include the four elemental paths.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Kalimdor’s elements are wild and untamed. The bond Horde shaman forge with them is essential to the survival of their new settlements."},kw={"call of earth","canaga earthcaller","durotar","earth totem","minor manifestation","rough quartz","shaman","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:canaga-earthcaller","npc:minor-manifestation-of-earth","quest:1516","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:troll","zone:mulgore","topic:tauren"},m={start="Minor Manifestation of Earth",["end"]="Canaga Earthcaller",level="4",faction="Horde",cl={"SHAMAN"},id=1518},src={"Call of Earth (Durotar 3)"}}
E["quest:1521"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Earth",z="durotar",s="In Mulgore, a young tauren shaman returns to Camp Narache bearing a gift from the earth. The Earth Sapta lets the initiate speak with a spirit and receive raw stone, beginning the path through the four elements.",h="In Mulgore, a young tauren shaman returns to Camp Narache bearing a gift from the earth.",sec={{t="A Gift from the Mountain",b="After drinking the Earth Sapta, you meet the Minor Manifestation of Earth on the crags near Red Cloud Mesa. The spirit gives you Rough Quartz, a plain stone that marks your pact with the element and its endurance. Patience and strength are the virtues earth demands. Through mutual respect, the spirit promises harmony with the land.",sp=0},{t="The First Totem",b="At Camp Narache, Seer Ravenfeather shapes the gifted quartz into your first Earth Totem. More than a mark of status, it is a lasting anchor for body and spirit. Through this carved focus, you channel the earth’s grounding and protective magic. It is your first true step along the fourfold elemental path.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Rough Quartz?",a="The Rough Quartz is a token the Minor Manifestation of Earth gives you as proof of communion. Seer Ravenfeather makes it the spiritual heart of your new Earth Totem.",al={"why do i need rough quartz","what is the quartz for","rough quartz use"},it="item"},{q="Why is an Earth Totem so important to a shaman?",a="Totems let a shaman channel elemental power. Without an Earth Totem as a focus, a shaman cannot call on the land spirits for spells and protective wards.",al={"why do i need earth totem","what does earth totem do","earth totem lore"},it="power"},{q="Who is Seer Ravenfeather?",a="Seer Ravenfeather is the spiritual guide and shaman trainer at Camp Narache on Red Cloud Mesa. She oversees young tauren’s elemental trials, guides them through their first visions, and crafts their sacred implements.",al={"who is ravenfeather","seer ravenfeather lore","camp narache seer"},it="identity"},{q="What are the four paths Seer Ravenfeather mentions?",a="Seer Ravenfeather means the four primal elements a shaman must master: Earth, Fire, Water, and Air. Earth is the foundation, and its endurance and steadfastness make it the initiate’s first trial.",al={"four paths","four elements shaman","what are the paths"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does this communion take place?",a="The communion takes place among the rugged cliffs bordering Red Cloud Mesa in Mulgore. You can reach the Minor Manifestation of Earth only after drinking the Earth Sapta.",al={"where do i find the earth spirit","manifestation location","where is the spirit"},it="place"},{q="Do other Horde shamans undertake a similar rite?",a="Yes. Orcs and Darkspear trolls in Durotar undertake their own Call of Earth in the Valley of Trials. They seek communion with local elemental manifestations and carve their first totems.",al={"do orcs do call of earth","troll call of earth","do all shamans get earth totem"},it="people"},{q="Why does the Minor Manifestation of Earth send you back to Seer Ravenfeather?",a="The elemental spirit has tested your resolve and deemed you worthy to walk the path of earth. By bestowing a piece of itself—the rough quartz—it provides tangible proof of your communion and mutual respect. It bids you return to Seer Ravenfeather so the stone can form the heart of your first totem, binding the spirits of earth to your service as you uphold patience, strength, and wisdom.",al={"minor manifestation of earth motive","why send rough quartz","manifestation of earth purpose"},it="motive",add="43ccddec"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, this rite gives you your first totem. Carrying it grounds your spiritual identity and lets you cast essential earth-aligned wards.",["race:Tauren"]="Tauren culture holds the Earth Mother in profound reverence. This trial binds an initiate to the living rock and soil of their ancestral homeland.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde shaman, you serve as a spiritual anchor and advisor, bridging the mortal races with Kalimdor’s volatile elemental forces."},kw={"call of earth","camp narache","earth totem","minor manifestation of earth","mulgore","red cloud mesa","rough quartz","seer ravenfeather","tauren shaman"},rel={"npc:seer-ravenfeather","npc:minor-manifestation-of-earth","quest:1520","subzone:camp-narache","zone:mulgore"},m={start="Minor Manifestation of Earth",["end"]="Seer Ravenfeather",level="4",faction="Horde",cl={"SHAMAN"},id=1521},src={"Call of Earth (Mulgore 3)"}}
E["quest:1525"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Fire",z="durotar",s="Telf Joolam sends you through Durotar and the eastern Barrens to gather what he needs for a Fire Sapta. The draught prepares an initiate to see and speak with fire spirits.",h="Telf Joolam sends you through Durotar and the eastern Barrens to gather what he needs for a Fire Sapta.",sec={{t="Brewing the Fire Sapta",b="A Fire Sapta opens a shaman’s senses to the Eternal Flame. Like the draught for earth, it lets you see and speak with spirits hidden from mortal sight. Telf Joolam sends you across Durotar and into the eastern Barrens for ingredients bound to heat and flame.",sp=0},{t="Enemies and Elements",b="Razormane quilboar spellcasters in the eastern Barrens carry fire tar, made in their earthy rituals. Burning Blade cultists carry the other ingredient in Dustwind Cave, in the ravines northeast of Razor Hill. They use fire for destruction and demonic chaos, yet the reagents in their pouches have a natural tie to the element.",sp=0},{t="The Nature of Flame",b="Telf Joolam teaches that fire brings more than destruction and ruin. It gives warmth and light, and makes creation possible. A wise shaman sees how opposing forces give meaning to each other, then uses contrasting elements together instead of wielding fire only as a weapon.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a Fire Sapta?",a="A Fire Sapta is a ritual draught made with ingredients tied to fire. Drinking it briefly aligns your spirit and vision with the plane of fire, revealing its spirits so you can speak with them.",al={"what is fire sapta","fire sapta meaning","why drink sapta"},it="item"},{q="Where do I find the Fire Tar?",a="Razormane quilboar spellcasters carry fire tar in the eastern Barrens, across the Southfury River from Durotar. Geomancers, Seers, Mystics, and Thornweavers often carry pots of the thick, flammable mixture for tribal rites.",al={"fire tar location","who drops fire tar","fire tar quilboar"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where is the Reagent Pouch found?",a="Burning Blade cultists carry the reagent pouch in Dustwind Cave, above the ravines northeast of Razor Hill in Durotar. The cave is distinct from Skull Rock, farther north near the coast.",al={"reagent pouch location","which cave has reagent pouch","burning blade pouch"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why does a shaman use items from warlocks?",a="Telf Joolam needs ingredients saturated with fire for the Sapta. Burning Blade cultists invoke destructive demonic flames, and their spell pouches hold potent reagents tied to fire.",al={"why use burning blade reagents","warlock items for shaman","warlock fire"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Telf Joolam?",a="Telf Joolam is a solitary troll shaman whose camp lies atop Durotar’s crags, south of Razor Hill. He oversees the trials of fire for Horde initiates and guides them in balancing destruction with creation.",al={"telf joolam lore","who is telf joolam"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after this quest?",a="After Telf Joolam makes the Fire Sapta from the gathered ingredients, he sends you to the fiery heights of the nearby dormant peak. You drink it there, face the elemental spirit, and earn your fire totem.",al={"next quest call of fire","after getting reagents","what to do with fire sapta"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Telf Joolam send you on this quest?",a="Telf Joolam is guiding your initiation into the deeper arts of the elements. To wield the power of fire and earn your Fire Totem, you must drink a specialized concoction known as a fire sapta, which temporarily aligns your spiritual senses with the realm of fire. Telf cannot brew this draught from thin air; he requires you to retrieve reagents deeply attuned to flame so he can prepare the mixture and set you upon the path of the Eternal Flame.",al={"why does telf joolam want this","telf joolam purpose","why help telf joolam"},it="motive",add="8d79977d"},{q="What is the Fire Tar for?",a="Fire tar is one of two vital catalysts required by Telf Joolam to brew a fire sapta. Carried by the spellcasting quilboar of the Razormane tribe in the eastern Barrens, the tar carries inherent volatile properties aligned with fire magic, giving the draught the potency needed to attune your senses to the elemental spirits.",al={"why do i need fire tar","fire tar purpose","use of fire tar"},it="item",add="08a6380d"},{q="What is the Reagent Pouch for?",a="The reagent pouch provides the volatile components needed to complete the fire sapta. Telf Joolam has you claim it from the Burning Blade cultists lurking northeast of Razor Hill because these warlocks regularly gather materials intrinsically tied to fire for their own dark sorcery. Rather than hunting across the lands for rare, scattered catalysts, the cultists' personal caches contain the exact reagents required to bridge your spirit to flame.",al={"why need reagent pouch","reagent pouch purpose","shaman reagent pouch use"},it="item",add="52c07fd8"},{q="Who are the Burning Blade cultists in Durotar?",a="The cultists are mortal agents of the Burning Blade, a shadowy remnant of the old demonic cults that once served the Shadow Council. Lurking in hidden caves above the ravines northeast of Razor Hill, these warlocks practice forbidden fel magic right beneath the Horde's nose, drawing on chaotic fire powers that make their reagent pouches prime sources for elemental brewing.",al={"burning blade target","who are the cultists","burning blade durotar"},it="target",add="65d894ad"},{q="Why must you gather the reagents yourself instead of Telf Joolam?",a="The journey itself is part of your spiritual trial. A shaman must prove capable of facing danger, confronting corrupt magic, and demonstrating resolve before claiming communion with fire. Telf Joolam serves as a mentor and guide on this remote peak, but the communion with the element cannot be handed to you—you must personally seize the components that bind you to the flame.",al={"why can't telf get them","why me fire quest","why shaman gather reagents"},it="why_me",add="f71fa686"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you face a trial in balancing opposing forces. Flame can bring vitality and light as well as wrath when wisdom guides it.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde defender, you face threats on the borders: Razormane quilboar encroaching in the Barrens and Burning Blade cultists hidden within Durotar.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you confront the Burning Blade and the warlock magic that once corrupted your people. Reclaiming fire as a natural element is an act of cultural restoration."},kw={"burning blade","call of fire","dustwind cave","fire sapta","fire tar","razormane","reagent pouch","telf joolam"},rel={"npc:telf-joolam","subzone:dustwind-cave","subzone:razor-hill","topic:quilboar","zone:barrens","zone:durotar","quest:1524","quest:827"},m={start="Telf Joolam",level="12",faction="Horde",cl={"SHAMAN"},id=1525,ri={"Fire Tar","Reagent Pouch (shaman)"}},src={"Call of Fire (3)"}}
E["quest:1526"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Fire",z="durotar",s="On Durotar's peaks, Call of Fire puts a shaman to a trial of flame. Telf Joolam sends the initiate to drink fire sapta, face a Minor Manifestation of Fire, and claim its ember.",h="On Durotar's peaks, Call of Fire puts a shaman to a trial of flame.",sec={{t="Eyes of the Flame",b="On Durotar's summit, fire spirits remain hidden from untrained eyes. Drink fire sapta, a draught made from reagents gathered across the barrens and coast, and your senses sharpen to the unseen. Minor spirits and manifestations appear among the summit crags.",sp=0},{t="Confronting the Manifestation",b="A Minor Manifestation of Fire waits atop the mountain. Once the sapta takes hold, it knows you can see it and awaits your challenge. Fire answers strength and decisive action, so strike without delay. The longer the fight lasts, the more fiercely the elemental fire burns.",sp=0},{t="The Brazier of the Dormant Flame",b="After the manifestation falls, you claim its lingering heat as a glowing ember. At the summit shrine, place it in the Brazier of the Dormant Flame. The inscribed metal stays cool beneath Durotar's sun and winds until the ember meets the bowl. Then white-hot flame kindles the ritual torch.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this trial?",a="You prove your strength by facing a manifestation of fire and capturing its heat in a ritual torch. The trial earns you the right to fashion a Fire Totem.",al={"why do call of fire","fire totem quest meaning","call of fire trial"},it="purpose"},{q="Why do I need to drink the fire sapta?",a="You drink fire sapta to see and touch the fire elementals atop the mountain, normally beyond mortal sight.",al={"what does fire sapta do","why sapta","cant see fire elemental"}},{q="Where is the Minor Manifestation of Fire found?",a="The Minor Manifestation of Fire waits at the mountain ridge's highest peak above Telf Joolam's perch in Durotar, near the Shrine of Eternal Flame.",al={"manifestation location","where is the fire elemental","where do i go"},gp=true},{q="Who is Telf Joolam?",a="Telf Joolam is an eccentric shaman hermit who lives high on a rocky ridge in Durotar. He guides young Horde initiates through dangerous, temperamental rites to understand fire.",al={"telf joolam role","telf joolam lore","who is the hermit"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the manifestation grow stronger during the fight?",a="Fire gathers strength and burns hotter as time passes. Strike decisively, since hesitation lets the spirit grow stronger.",al={"why is the fire elemental so strong","manifestation scaling","swift strike fire"}},{q="What happens after the brazier is lit?",a="Lighting the brazier kindles the ceremonial torch. Carry its sacred flame down the mountain to complete your Fire Totem.",al={"what after dormant flame","next quest call of fire","where to take lit torch"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Telf Joolam send you on this trial?",a="Telf Joolam is your mentor in the ways of the elements, tasked with guiding young shamans through their communion with fire. Fire is tempestuous, destructive, and unpredictable; the spirits will not grant you their power or respect unless you prove yourself capable of confronting and commanding their essence directly. Telf sends you up the peak not to rid the mountain of a threat, but to forge your spirit in battle and earn the right to carry the flame.",al={"telf joolam motive","why does telf joolam want this","why do this trial"},it="motive",add="e554f055"},{q="What is the Glowing Ember for?",a="The Glowing Ember is the pure elemental remnant harvested from the slain Minor Manifestation of Fire. To complete your rite, you must carry this fiery core to the Shrine of Eternal Flame and place it within the dormant brazier. Rekindling the cold basin with the elemental's living essence ignites a sacred, white-hot flame, which in turn lights your Dormant Torch and seals your connection to the element of fire.",al={"glowing ember use","why do i need glowing ember","purpose of glowing ember"},it="item",add="e534729d"},{q="What is the Minor Manifestation of Fire, and why is it here?",a="The Minor Manifestation of Fire is an elemental spirit lingering atop the mountain peak near the Shrine of Eternal Flame. Visible only to those whose senses are opened by the sacred fire sapta, it embodies the raw, aggressive nature of the flame. It remains perched upon the crag as an eternal guardian and test for aspiring shamans, challenging all who seek to master fire to subdue its burning wrath.",al={"minor manifestation of fire lore","who is the manifestation","why is the fire elemental here"},it="target",add="8a082e57"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you learn that fire is volatile and destructive, unlike solid, unyielding earth. It consumes an indecisive caller, so focus and authority are needed to master it.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde shaman, you join orc and troll shamans climbing Durotar's red crags to prove their communion with the land's fiery spirits."},kw={"brazier of the dormant flame","call of fire","durotar","fire sapta","fire totem","minor manifestation of fire","shaman trial","shrine of eternal flame","telf joolam"},rel={"npc:telf-joolam","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},m={start="Telf Joolam",["end"]="Brazier of the Dormant Flame",level="13",faction="Horde",cl={"SHAMAN"},id=1526,ri={"Glowing Ember"}},src={"Call of Fire (4)"}}
E["quest:1842"] = {t="quest",n="Satyr Hooves",z="durotar",s="In Sen'jin Village, Ula'elek sends warriors north to Ashenvale for Satyr Hooves. He needs their strange power to forge brutal gauntlets.",h="In Sen'jin Village, Ula'elek sends warriors north to Ashenvale for Satyr Hooves.",sec={{t="Harnessing Corrupted Essence",b="Ula'elek sends you into Ashenvale's ancient woods to gather what his craft requires. Demonic corruption still clings to the satyr covens there. For armor meant to rival Kalimdor's fiercest forces, he needs more than iron and leather.",sp=0},{t="The Bloat of Ashenvale's Magic",b="In northeastern Ashenvale, satyrs feed on the forest's lingering purity and twist it into foul power. Those that take in the most grow swollen hooves without the usual cloven split. Ula'elek plans to draw out that concentrated magic and weave it into his gauntlets.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Ula'elek need satyr hooves?",a="Ula'elek needs the hooves to empower the brutal gauntlets he is making. He means to draw out the forest magic the satyrs have drained and corrupted.",al={"why satyr hooves","hoof purpose","what are the hooves for"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the satyrs found?",a="Satyrs dwell in northeastern Ashenvale among corrupted ancient ruins. There, they drain the deep forest's lingering magic.",al={"where are satyrs","satyr location","where to find satyr hooves"},gp=true},{q="What makes an uncloven hoof special?",a="A hoof without a cloven split marks a satyr that has gorged itself on Ashenvale's pure magic. The stolen power swells its feet.",al={"uncloven hoof lore","why uncloven","swollen hooves"},it="item"},{q="Who is Ula'elek?",a="Ula'elek is a skilled Darkspear troll armor craftsman in Sen'jin Village, in southern Durotar. He helps warriors craft trial gear.",al={"who is ulaelek","quest giver","troll in senjin"},it="identity"},{q="What armor is Ula'elek forging?",a="Ula'elek is preparing a pair of Brutal Gauntlets. This heavy hand armor is imbued with stolen magic for rising Horde warriors.",al={"what are brutal gauntlets","gauntlet quest","reward armor"},it="purpose"},{q="Do the satyrs serve the Burning Legion here?",a="Yes. Satyrs are ancient night elves transformed by demonic pacts. The covens lingering in Kalimdor's woodlands still wield fel corruption in service to demonic powers.",al={"satyr allegiance","are satyrs legion"},it="threat"},{q="Why are the satyrs in northeastern Ashenvale?",a="Satyrs haunt northeastern Ashenvale to gorge themselves on the ancient forest's purity. By leeching and corrupting its latent enchantments, they empower their wicked rituals and warp their own bodies. The ones who feast most heavily on Ashenvale's natural magic develop grotesque, swollen uncloven hooves, becoming living vessels of concentrated arcane strength.",al={"why satyrs ashenvale","satyr hooves target lore","who are we hunting for hooves"},it="target",add="749a1d7b"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face cunning demonic ambushers in your rite of progression. The trial tests your martial resilience and earns you personalized armor.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde warrior, you leave Durotar's arid plains and travel deep into contested night elf territory in Ashenvale.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you can see Darkspear craft in Ula'elek's methods. He draws raw essence from fallen magical foes instead of relying only on conventional smithing."},kw={"ashenvale","brutal gauntlets","durotar","hooves","satyr","sen'jin village","ula'elek","uncloven"},rel={"npc:ula-elek","quest:1843","quest:1839","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:ashenvale","zone:durotar","topic:satyr"},m={start="Ula'elek",level="30",faction="Horde",cl={"WARRIOR"},id=1842,ri={"Uncloven Satyr Hoof"}},src={"Satyr Hooves"}}
E["quest:1843"] = {t="quest",n="Brutal Gauntlets",z="durotar",s="In Durotar, Ula'elek has finished Brutal Gauntlets for a seasoned Horde warrior. Rare materials from distant lands went into the work, meant to honor both maker and bearer.",h="In Durotar, Ula'elek has finished Brutal Gauntlets for a seasoned Horde warrior.",sec={{t="A Craftsman's Masterpiece",b="In Durotar, Ula'elek brings his lineage and skill to armor for a seasoned frontline warrior. He shapes brutal gauntlets from hardened trophies taken from dangerous foes. The finished armor can withstand fierce blows and strengthen the wearer's attacks.",sp=0},{t="Ancestral Honor",b="Among orcs and trolls, fine arms and armor carry the forge's prestige and the maker's spirit into battle. When Ula'elek presents the finished gauntlets, he entrusts a warrior with his ancestors' legacy. He expects a champion who wears them to answer that craft with courage, martial discipline, and strength.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ula'elek?",a="Ula'elek is a Durotar craftsman who makes tailored armor for Horde warriors. He asks for exotic materials so his work honors his trade and ancestral traditions.",al={"ulaelek","who gives brutal gauntlets","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Why were satyr hooves needed for these gauntlets?",a="Satyr hooves are swollen and uncloven, and hold power leeched from Ashenvale's magic. Ula'elek draws out that power and puts it into the gauntlets, giving them great magic.",al={"why satyr hooves","satyr parts","materials used"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What does wearing the gauntlets signify to Ula'elek?",a="To Ula'elek, the gauntlets are the finest work of his craft. Giving them to a worthy warrior honors his trade and ancestors, and ties his labor to the Horde's victories in battle.",al={"honor ancestors","ula'elek honor"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this task take place?",a="The forging ends in Durotar, the arid homeland of the orcs and Darkspear trolls. There Ula'elek inspects the recovered materials and presents the finished armor.",al={"location","where is brutal gauntlets turned in"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is this trial intended for all adventurers?",a="The trial is meant for frontline warriors who have proved their stamina and martial dedication. It marks their rise into more seasoned combat roles within the Horde.",al={"is this warrior only","class requirement"},it="why_me"},{q="What comes after receiving the gauntlets?",a="Receiving the gauntlets completes this crafting trial. The warrior is equipped to face greater threats across Azeroth's war-torn battlefields.",al={"next quest","brutal gauntlets follow up"},it="next_step"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you carry gauntlets made for heavy melee combat. They mark a step toward disciplined martial leadership.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you carry your craftworkers' tradition and martial pride into battle. Their work bears spiritual weight and honor."},kw={"armor forging","brutal gauntlets","durotar","horde","satyr hooves","ula'elek","warrior armor"},rel={"quest:1842","npc:ula-elek","zone:durotar"},m={start="Ula'elek",level="30",faction="Horde",cl={"WARRIOR"},id=1843},src={"Brutal Gauntlets (quest)"}}
E["quest:1859"] = {t="quest",n="Therzok",z="durotar",s="In Orgrimmar, Therzok awaits a promising rogue sent from Durotar. Kaplak has seen your skill in violence and stealth, and sends you to the Cleft of Shadow to meet a Shattered Hand operative.",h="In Orgrimmar, Therzok awaits a promising rogue sent from Durotar.",sec={{t="A Whispered Summons",b="The new Horde honors Thrall, yet not all its servants fight openly beneath his banner. Word reaches Orgrimmar of a fighter skilled in violence and stealth, one willing to bend the rules of open warfare. The underground guild takes notice.",sp=0},{t="Into the Cleft of Shadow",b="Kaplak sends you beneath Orgrimmar's red stone cliffs to the Cleft of Shadow. Therzok waits there, hidden from the city's grunts. Lone cutpurses and ambushers are brought into the Shattered Hand, the Horde's covert network of daggers in the dark.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Therzok?",a="In Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, Therzok serves the Shattered Hand. He meets promising young rogues from Durotar's training grounds and brings them into the guild's service.",al={"who is therzok","therzok lore","npc therzok"},it="target"},{q="Why does Kaplak send me to him?",a="Kaplak has seen your skill in combat and your talent for stealth and subterfuge. Knowing the Shattered Hand seeks capable scoundrels, he sends you to Therzok with a request to recruit you.",al={"why send me to therzok","kaplak quest","why go to orgrimmar"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Shattered Hand in Orgrimmar?",a="In Orgrimmar, the Shattered Hand is a secret guild of assassins, spies, and thieves who serve the Horde. They undertake difficult work that Thrall's honorable warriors cannot perform openly.",al={"what is shattered hand","shattered hand orgrimmar","horde rogue guild"},it="people"},{q="Where is the Cleft of Shadow located?",a="The Cleft of Shadow is a cavern beneath central Orgrimmar. Dark passages descend to it from the Valley of Strength and the Drag. It shelters the city's warlocks and rogues from public scrutiny.",al={"where is cleft of shadow","how to find therzok","cleft of shadow location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What comes after meeting Therzok?",a="After you greet Therzok, he explains the duties of Shattered Hand service. Then he assigns work to test your capability, stealth, and loyalty to the network.",al={"next quest","what does therzok want","after therzok"},it="next_step"},{q="Do non-rogues receive this quest?",a="No. Only rogues receive this summons after gaining a certain amount of experience. It marks their passage from local skirmishes into the Horde's intelligence network.",al={"can other classes do this","is this rogue only","rogue quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Kaplak choose you for this meeting?",a="Kaplak was explicitly ordered to scout for individuals matching your description. Word has reached the guild that you know how to hold your own in combat and are not above using stealth, deception, or less honorable means when necessary. Therzok has business in mind that requires someone with your specific, flexible set of talents.",al={"why me kaplak","why send me to therzok","why did kaplak pick me"},it="why_me",add="89f659b0"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, this summons brings you into the Shattered Hand. Your solitary work in Durotar now connects to the Horde's organized spy network.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Thrall preaches honor and the warrior spirit. Therzok's network shows the Horde also depends on unseen blades and secret gatherers of intelligence."},kw={"assassin","cleft of shadow","durotar","kaplak","orgrimmar","rogue","shattered hand","therzok"},rel={"quest:1858","npc:kaplak","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:cleft"},m={start="Kaplak",["end"]="Therzok",level="10",faction="Horde",cl={"ROGUE"},ra={"Orc","Troll"},id=1859},src={"Therzok (quest)"}}
E["quest:1884"] = {t="quest",n="Ju-Ju Heaps",z="durotar",s="On the Echo Isles, Un'thuwa asks you to destroy Zalazane's ju-ju heaps. Their corruption threatens Durotar's flow of magic.",h="On the Echo Isles, Un'thuwa asks you to destroy Zalazane's ju-ju heaps.",sec={{t="Tainted Heaps",b="From Sen'jin Village, Un'thuwa asks you to destroy the heaps Zalazane placed among his huts on the main Echo Isle. The tainted fetishes corrupt wildlife and strengthen warlocks and infernal creatures. Left alone, they may change Durotar's flow of magic forever.",sp=0},{t="Un'thuwa's Sense",b="Un'thuwa senses the heaps have been destroyed. With time and luck, she believes Durotar's magic will return to its normal flow. She praises your deed for your people and says you have proved your worth to the Horde's classes.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who placed the ju-ju heaps?",a="Zalazane, a warlock of the Echo Isles, placed the tainted heaps among his huts on the main isle.",al={"who made the heaps","zalazane heaps","ju ju source"}},{q="What do the heaps do?",a="The heaps corrupt wildlife and strengthen warlocks and infernal creatures.",al={"what are juju heaps","heaps effect","why destroy juju"}},{q="Where are the ju-ju heaps?",a="Zalazane placed them among his huts on the main Echo Isle.",al={"where heaps","echo isle heaps","ju ju location"}},{q="Who asks me to destroy them?",a="Un'thuwa in Sen'jin Village asks you to destroy the ju-ju heaps.",al={"who gives this","unthuwa request","who wants heaps gone"}},{q="Why does Durotar's magic matter here?",a="The heaps disrupt Durotar's normal flow of magic. If they remain, that flow may change forever.",al={"magic flow","durotar magic","why care about magic"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Un'thuwa calls this a deed for your people and says you have proved your worth to the Horde's classes."},kw={"durotar","echo isles","ju-ju heaps","magic","sen'jin village","tainted fetishes","un'thuwa","zalazane"},rel={"quest:826","subzone:echo-isles","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","topic:horde","topic:warlock"},m={faction="Horde",cl={"MAGE"},id=1884,xg=1882},src={"In-game quest text: Ju-Ju Heaps"},fv=true}
E["quest:2161"] = {t="quest",n="A Peon's Burden",z="durotar",s="Ukor waits outside the Valley of Trials with provisions he cannot carry home. The recruits in the red canyon refused his food, so he asks travelers to take it back to Razor Hill.",h="Ukor waits outside the Valley of Trials with provisions he cannot carry home.",sec={{t="A Misplaced Delivery",b="Ukor left Razor Hill carrying provisions for the fresh recruits training in the red canyon. He thought they needed the food, but the taskmasters sent him away. They keep rations meager, believing hardship teaches young Horde warriors discipline and endurance. Innkeeper Grosk later explains that hunger is part of their training.",sp=0},{t="Perils of the Red Waste",b="Ukor reached the pass, but fears crossing Durotar on the way back. Scorpids, venomous spiders, and prowling boars haunt the rocky trail. He has no weapons or armor, and lacks the fighting spirit expected of an orcish grunt.\n\nSo Ukor waits along the path and asks travelers leaving the proving grounds to carry his heavy provisions back to the inn in Razor Hill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ukor?",a="Ukor is a timid orc peon waiting on the road out of the Valley of Trials. He set out from Razor Hill with provisions, but fears the local wildlife too much to make the return journey alone.",al={"ukor","who is the peon on the road","peon near valley of trials"},it="identity"},{q="Why didn't the trainers in the Valley of Trials want the food?",a="The taskmasters keep the trainees hungry because they believe hardship teaches discipline and endurance. Innkeeper Grosk explains that meager rations are part of their training, so Ukor's provisions were refused.",al={"why refuse food","why did ukor carry food","innkeeper grosk starvation"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does this delivery need to go?",a="Carry the provisions north along Durotar's main thoroughfare to Razor Hill. Give them to Innkeeper Grosk inside the settlement's tavern.",al={"where is razor hill","who do i give the food to","where to deliver ukor's burden"},it="place"},{q="What makes the journey dangerous for a peon?",a="Scorpids, venomous crawler spiders, and wild boars roam Durotar's rocky wastes. Ukor is an unarmored, untrained laborer, while seasoned recruits can handle such vermin.",al={"why is ukor scared","durotar road dangers"},it="danger"},{q="What is the role of peons in the Horde?",a="Peons hold the lowest place in orcish society and do menial work, from hauling supplies and chopping timber to raising fortifications. Grunts and champions receive praise and glory, while peons are often overlooked, though they keep settlements fed and maintained.",al={"orc peons lore","peon status","what are peons"},it="people"},{q="Who is Innkeeper Grosk?",a="Innkeeper Grosk runs the inn in Razor Hill and manages its lodgings and supplies. He offers traveling warriors food, drink, and a hearth, and reminds recruits to rest before facing the wider world.",al={"innkeeper grosk","grosk razor hill","razor hill innkeeper"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Ukor want the food delivered back to Razor Hill?",a="Ukor genuinely meant well when he hauled supplies out from Razor Hill, hoping to aid the young recruits training under the harsh sun of the Valley of Trials. Finding that the trainers turned the rations away, he cannot simply abandon the supplies or let them spoil on the road. The food belongs back on the shelves of Innkeeper Grosk's pantry, but after barely surviving the trek past the region's scorpids and spiders, Ukor is terrified of making the perilous return trip alone.",al={"why return the food","ukor motive","why give food to grosk"},it="motive",add="777a74e1"},{q="Why does Ukor ask you to carry the burden instead of doing it himself?",a="Ukor is an ordinary peon, unaccustomed to violence and unarmed against the wilderness. While he managed to brave the scorpions and spiders on the road leading out from Razor Hill, the sheer terror of facing those savage predators again has frozen him in place. Spotting you emerging victorious from the Valley of Trials, he sees a capable hero who fears nothing, hoping you will gladly carry the burden on your way to Razor Hill.",al={"why can't ukor carry it","why me peon's burden","why ask me ukor"},it="why_me",add="fe82ef3c"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Orcish culture prizes physical might and courage, leaving peons like Ukor at the bottom of the social order. Helping with his delivery shows how humble labor keeps Durotar's fledgling nation working.",["faction:Horde"]="You leave the proving grounds for Razor Hill, the center of Horde defense and supplies in southern Durotar."},kw={"durotar","food","innkeeper grosk","peon","razor hill","supplies","ukor","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:ukor","npc:innkeeper-grosk","subzone:razor-hill","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},m={start="Ukor",["end"]="Innkeeper Grosk",level="5",faction="Horde",id=2161},src={"A Peon's Burden"}}
E["quest:2380"] = {t="quest",n="To Orgrimmar!",z="durotar",s="Kaplak sends a young rogue from Razor Hill north to Orgrimmar. You are to find Shenthul in the Cleft of Shadow and enter the Shattered Hand's network.",h="Kaplak sends a young rogue from Razor Hill north to Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Shadows",b="Kaplak sends you north from Razor Hill to Orgrimmar. Your growing skill has drawn the notice of handlers with greater standing, though your craft is still rough. You leave Durotar's red crags behind and make for the capital.",sp=0},{t="Under Thrall's Watchful Eye",b="Shenthul receives you in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar. He watches Warchief Thrall's political reforms with unease. The Shattered Hand cannot guard its interests by force or open defiance alone. Patience, subterfuge, and deception help it survive and preserve its influence.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this quest?",a="Kaplak, the rogue trainer in Razor Hill, sends you north after your skills draw the notice of more senior handlers in Orgrimmar.",al={"quest giver","who gives to orgrimmar","kaplak quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I find Shenthul?",a="You find Shenthul in the Cleft of Shadow, an underground district beneath Orgrimmar where rogues, warlocks, and other outcasts gather.",al={"shenthul location","where is shenthul","cleft of shadow shenthul"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Shattered Hand's agenda in Orgrimmar?",a="The Shattered Hand is an intelligence and assassination guild within the Horde. Shenthul watches Thrall's honorable reforms with unease, and the guild relies on stealth to survive and preserve its influence.",al={"shattered hand motives","why shattered hand in orgrimmar","shattered hand thrall"},it="conflict"},{q="Why am I being sent specifically at this stage?",a="Your early reconnaissance and skirmishes have shown you are capable, so you are entering more formal guild service. It begins with lockpicking and covert fieldwork in the capital.",al={"level 16 rogue quest","why go to orgrimmar now","rogue training summons"},it="why_me"},{q="Does this quest differ from 'Find the Shattered Hand'?",a="Both paths lead rogues to Shenthul in Orgrimmar. Which one you receive depends on where you train or take orders, and each advances the same training chain.",al={"find the shattered hand vs to orgrimmar","alternate breadcrumb quest"},gp=true},{q="What happens after reporting to Shenthul?",a="Shenthul tests your competence and sends you farther along the chain. You meet contacts such as Zando'zan, then take on covert work with goblin contacts in Ratchet.",al={"next quest after to orgrimmar","what does shenthul give"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Kaplak want me to go to Orgrimmar?",a="Kaplak is acting under direct orders from above. While he acknowledges you are far from a true master of stealth, your budding talents have caught the attention of Shenthul himself. The Shattered Hand needs cunning operatives trained for their covert agenda, and Kaplak's duty is to channel promising rogues like you into the deeper shadows of the capital where your true training can begin.",al={"why does kaplak send me","kaplak motive","why go to orgrimmar"},it="motive",add="a9995c5c"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you enter the capital's covert network under Shenthul's watch. The work turns to poisons, thievery, and deception beyond the frontier skirmishes.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you hear the friction between Thrall's honorable new path and the older clan organizations that endure beneath Orgrimmar."},kw={"cleft of shadow","kaplak","razor hill","rogue","shattered hand","shenthul","to orgrimmar"},rel={"npc:shenthul","npc:kaplak","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","quest:2378","quest:2379","quest:2382","quest:2381","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Kaplak",["end"]="Shenthul",level="16",faction="Horde",cl={"ROGUE"},id=2380,xg=2378},src={"To Orgrimmar!"}}
E["quest:2383"] = {t="quest",n="Simple Parchment",z="durotar",s="A message waits for you in the Valley of Trials, sent while you were away. Frang, your class trainer, is outside the Den.",h="A message waits for you in the Valley of Trials, sent while you were away.",sec={{t="A Message from Frang",b="The parchment asks you to read its words and speak with Frang. Your class trainer waits outside the Den in the Valley of Trials.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sent the parchment?",a="The parchment appears to have come from Frang, your class trainer.",al={"parchment sender","who wrote it"}},{q="Where can I find Frang?",a="Frang waits outside the Den in the Valley of Trials.",al={"where's Frang","Frang location"}},{q="What does Frang want?",a="Frang has words for you when you are ready.",al={"why Frang wants me","parchment message"}},{q="What should I do with the parchment?",a="Read the parchment, then speak with Frang in the Valley of Trials.",al={"read parchment","simple parchment"}}},kw={"class trainer","den","frang","parchment","simple parchment","valley of trials"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials"},m={faction="Horde",cl={"WARRIOR"},ra={"Orc"},id=2383},src={"In-game quest text: Simple Parchment"},fv=true}
E["quest:2936"] = {t="quest",n="The Spider God",z="durotar",s="Master Gadrin sends you to uncover the name of the spider god worshipped by the Witherbark tribe. To learn it, you must decipher the ancient writings carved upon the Tablet of Theka.",h="Master Gadrin sends you to uncover the name of the spider god worshipped by the Witherbark tribe.",sec={{t="Words on Stone",b="The Tablet of Theka preserves lore that Master Gadrin needs to understand the faith of the Witherbark trolls. Seeking out the stone tablet will reveal which ancient entity holds sway over their rituals, before you journey back to the witch doctor with your discovery.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks you to find the name of the spider god?",a="Master Gadrin seeks the name of the deity worshipped by the forest trolls.",al={"who gives the spider god","where to return","spider god quest giver"}},{q="Where is the spider god's name recorded?",a="You find the name by reading from the Tablet of Theka.",al={"what tablet","where is the name","how to learn the spider god name"}},{q="Which tribe worships the spider god?",a="The Witherbark tribe of forest trolls reveres the spider god.",al={"which trolls worship the spider god","spider god tribe"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a troll, uncovering the ancient names revered by the Witherbark brings you face to face with the darker loa worshipped among distant tribes."},kw={"master gadrin","spider god","tablet of theka","the spider god","troll loa","witherbark"},rel={"npc:master-gadrin"},m={faction="Horde",id=2936},src={"In-game quest text: The Spider God"},fv=true}
E["quest:2937"] = {t="quest",n="Summoning Shadra",z="durotar",s="At Shadra'Alor, you read Master Gadrin's parchment and call Shadra from the Witherbark realm.",h="At Shadra'Alor, you read Master Gadrin's parchment and call Shadra from the Witherbark realm.",sec={{t="Call of the Spider God",b="Master Gadrin sends you deep into the Witherbark realm of the Hinterlands. At Shadra'Alor, you read his parchment at the altar, and Shadra the spider god answers. Defeat her there, then carry her venom to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who provides the parchment to summon Shadra?",a="Master Gadrin gives you the parchment.",al={"who gives summoning shadra","summoning shadra questgiver"}},{q="Where is Shadra summoned?",a="You summon Shadra at the altar of Shadra'Alor, deep in the Witherbark realm of the Hinterlands.",al={"where to summon shadra","altar of shadra'alor location","shadra location"}},{q="Who receives the venom once Shadra is defeated?",a="After Shadra is defeated, you take her venom to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.",al={"who do i turn the venom into","summoning shadra turn in","apothecary lydon location"}}},kw={"apothecary lydon","hinterlands","master gadrin","shadra","shadra'alor","spider god","tarren mill","witherbark"},rel={"quest:2938","npc:master-gadrin","zone:hinterlands","subzone:tarren-mill"},m={start="Master Gadrin",["end"]="Apothecary Lydon",level="55",faction="Horde",id=2937,ri={"Shadra's Venom"}},src={"Summoning Shadra (Classic)"}}
E["quest:2985"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="durotar",s="Swart sends an initiate from Razor Hill toward Islen Waterseer on the Barrens coast. Earth and fire have tested the shaman; water asks for another kind of understanding.",h="Swart sends an initiate from Razor Hill toward Islen Waterseer on the Barrens coast.",sec={{t="A Shift in the Elements",b="Swart, the shaman trainer in Razor Hill, guides initiates through the elements. Earth teaches endurance, and fire tests their command. Once an initiate can wield flame without being consumed, Swart judges them ready to seek the teachings of water.",sp=0},{t="The Recluse of the Merchant Coast",b="Islen Waterseer lives on the Barrens coast beyond Ratchet. Travel south along the Southfury River into the Barrens, then east to the shore near a massive shark's carcass. Islen dwells where the waves meet the land, apart from the trainers in Durotar's towns. She guides the Horde in communion with water.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Swart, the orc shaman trainer in Razor Hill, sends you onward after you prove your command of earth and fire.",al={"quest giver","who starts call of water","swart"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="Where can I find Islen Waterseer?",a="Islen Waterseer lives on the eastern coast of the Barrens, just south of Ratchet. Follow the Southfury River south from Durotar, then head for the shore and look for her camp beside a large beached shark.",al={"where is islen","islen location","how to find islen waterseer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why must a shaman learn the elements in a specific order?",a="Shamanic tradition asks an initiate to build spiritual balance step by step. Earth grounds the soul, and fire tempers it for water's shifting nature.",al={"element order","why water after fire","shaman progression"},it="purpose"},{q="Is this quest available to other classes?",a="No. Shamans alone seek the favor of the water spirits and seek to manifest their Water Totem.",al={"can non shaman do this","is call of water shaman only"},gp=true},{q="What landmark should I look for when searching for Islen?",a="Look for a massive beached shark on the shore south of Ratchet. Islen lives beside it.",al={"shark landmark","how to spot islen's camp","islen coast"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after reaching Islen Waterseer?",a="Speaking with Islen begins the trials of water. The shaman must travel across Kalimdor and Lordaeron, gather pure drops of water, and confront spirits before earning the totem.",al={"next step","what does islen do","after call of water"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Swart send you to Islen Waterseer?",a="Swart recognizes your mastery over the flame and sees that your spiritual journey as a shaman must continue. He cannot teach you the ways of water himself—mastering the fluid, pure element requires guidance from Islen Waterseer, a dedicated elder dwelling along the Barrens coast. Swart sends you onward so you may commune with water and expand your bond with the elements.",al={"why does swart want this done","swart motive","why send me to islen"},it="motive",add="80a0e7c7"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you turn from earth and fire toward water's restorative power, opening a spiritual path to healing totems.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde shaman, you are directed to Islen Waterseer on the Barrens coast to undertake your communion with water."},kw={"call of water","islen waterseer","ratchet","razor hill","shaman","southfury river","swart","the barrens","water totem"},rel={"npc:islen-waterseer","subzone:razor-hill","zone:barrens","subzone:ratchet","subzone:southfury-river"},m={start="Swart",["end"]="Islen Waterseer",level="20",faction="Horde",cl={"SHAMAN"},id=2985},src={"Call of Water (Durotar)"}}
E["quest:3065"] = {t="quest",n="Simple Tablet",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, a marked parchment sends you to Frang after you prove yourself against local beasts. The warrior trainer waits outside the Den.",h="In the Valley of Trials, a marked parchment sends you to Frang after you prove yourself against local beasts.",sec={{t="A Summons to Arms",b="After you prove yourself against the Mottled Boars, Gornek gives you a parchment marked for you alone. Durotar is harsh, so the Horde gives its fighters guidance quickly. The parchment sends you to Frang, the veteran warrior trainer outside the Den.",sp=0},{t="Under the Shade of the Den",b="Frang shelters in the shade outside the Den and watches recruits come from the red scrubland. He judges each arrival with a seasoned eye, then teaches the fundamentals with a heavy axe or a spear. He prepares each recruit to defend the young Horde's fragile settlements.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Simple Tablet?",a="The Simple Tablet guides young warriors in the Valley of Trials to Frang, the resident warrior trainer.",al={"simple tablet","what is this tablet","warrior note"}},{q="Who sends the tablet?",a="Frang sends the message. The veteran warrior trainer waits outside the Den for emerging fighters.",al={"who wrote the tablet","who sent simple tablet"}},{q="Where can I find Frang?",a="Frang waits outside the Den in the Valley of Trials, sheltered from the desert sun beneath rock overhangs.",al={"frang location","where is frang","find warrior trainer"}},{q="Why does Frang mention spears and axes?",a="Frang recognizes that Horde recruits fight in different ways. Orcs favor heavy choppers such as greataxes, while trolls and other fighters often choose spears and lighter polearms. Both serve well in battle.",al={"frang spear quote","why spears"}},{q="Do other classes get this quest?",a="No. Warriors receive the Simple Tablet, while other classes receive no such message and are directed to their own mentors by a parchment, rune, or scroll.",al={"is simple tablet warrior only","class quests in valley of trials"}},{q="What is the purpose of the Den?",a="The Den is a sheltered cavern complex in the Valley of Trials. Trainers, supplies, and resting recruits gather there, away from the blazing heat and wandering beasts.",al={"what is the den","the den durotar"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, this summons marks your first step on Durotar's warrior path. Frang teaches you foundational stances and strikes.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you join its steady stream of hardened front-line fighters. They are sent to secure Durotar's precarious borders against centaur, quilboar, and human interlopers.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll training in the valley, you may hear Frang's gruff observations about your preference for spears over orcish axes. He respects anything that kills."},kw={"durotar","frang","gornek","simple tablet","the den","valley of trials","warrior"},rel={"npc:gornek","quest:cutting-teeth","subzone:the-den","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Frang",level="1",faction="Horde",cl={"WARRIOR"},ra={"Troll"},id=3065},src={"Simple Tablet (quest)"}}
E["quest:3082"] = {t="quest",n="Etched Tablet",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Gornek sends a carved tablet to young hunters. Jen'shan's mark calls them to train in the wild.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Gornek sends a carved tablet to young hunters.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Hunt",b="After young hunters prove themselves against the boars near the Den, Gornek brings them a carved tablet. Jen'shan's mark is cut into the stone. She is a skilled troll huntswoman stationed nearby, and her message shows that seasoned hunters have noticed the recruit's grit. Now the lesson turns from surviving local dangers to disciplined training in the wild.",sp=0},{t="The Sharing of Survival",b="Jen'shan teaches that orcs and trolls have a long history within the Horde. Orcs brought renowned traditions of warriors and shamans. The Darkspear trolls carried ancient skills in stalking, tracking, and survival, which helped orcs endure life on Azeroth. As Jen'shan trains new hunters, the two peoples share what they know, bound by respect for the hunt.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends the Etched Tablet?",a="Jen'shan sends the inscribed stone, and Gornek delivers it after you prove yourself in the Valley of Trials.",al={"who wrote etched tablet","tablet sender","who gave me this tablet"}},{q="Where can Jen'shan be found?",a="Jen'shan is in northern Durotar's Valley of Trials, among the other class instructors near the Den.",al={"jen'shan location","where is jenshan","find jenshan"}},{q="Why do troll trainers teach orc hunters here?",a="Jen'shan says the Horde turned to trolls for hunting lore while struggling to survive on Azeroth. Orcs already knew the ways of warriors and shamans, and the two peoples still share their skills.",al={"why troll hunter trainer","troll teaching orc","darkspear hunters"}},{q="What happens after turning in this tablet?",a="Jen'shan accepts you as her student and offers to teach you the basic techniques, shots, and survival practices of Horde hunters as you gain experience.",al={"what next after tablet","etched tablet reward lore","jenshan follow up"}},{q="What prerequisite must be finished before getting this tablet?",a="You must first finish Gornek's initial task, Cutting Teeth, by slaying mottled boars to prove your endurance.",al={"tablet prereq","how to unlock etched tablet","prerequisites for etched tablet"}},{q="Can any class complete this quest?",a="Only novice hunters can receive this training summons in the Valley of Trials. Gornek gives other classes different summons.",al={"who can get etched tablet","etched tablet class requirement","is this hunter only"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you find your first place among Horde hunters and begin learning from your local trainer in the wilderness.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you can see how Darkspear hunting lore helped the Horde survive on Kalimdor and support its allies.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you learn refined stalking and tracking from your Darkspear allies, adding to your people's warrior traditions.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see orcs and trolls share their distinct strengths to help both peoples survive."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","etched tablet","gornek","hunter","jen'shan","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:jen-shan","npc:gornek","quest:cutting-teeth","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Jen'shan",level="1",faction="Horde",cl={"HUNTER"},ra={"Troll"},id=3082},src={"Etched Tablet (quest)"}}
E["quest:3083"] = {t="quest",n="Encrypted Tablet",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Gornek sends new rogues to Rwag with a coded message. The summons leads them into the Den, where rogue training is bound to the Shattered Hand.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Gornek sends new rogues to Rwag with a coded message.",sec={{t="A Coded Summons",b="Gornek gives the Encrypted Tablet to initiates who prove their mettle against the local wildlife. Its message is written in cipher, a test and safeguard for those trained in stealth, poison, and subterfuge. The summons sends each recruit into the Den to meet Rwag, trainer of the Horde’s rogues, thieves, and cutpurses.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow of the Hand",b="Inside the Den, Rwag trains new rogues as an agent aligned with the Shattered Hand. He says the guild will not dictate every breath, yet the Hand holds him to account if an apprentice fails to perform. The fledgling Horde is surrounded by foes, so it depends on silent scouts and agile cutpurses to gather intelligence and strike from the shadows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Encrypted Tablet?",a="The Encrypted Tablet summons novice rogues from the Valley of Trials to meet their trainer, Rwag, inside the Den.",al={"what does the tablet do","encrypted tablet purpose","why encrypted tablet"}},{q="Who delivers the tablet to the player?",a="Gornek, who oversees trials in the valley, gives you the tablet after you prove yourself in your first combat trial by killing Mottled Boars.",al={"who gives the encrypted tablet","tablet quest giver","gornek tablet"}},{q="Where can Rwag be found?",a="Rwag can be found deep inside the Den, the cavern complex along the Valley of Trials’ northern cliffside.",al={"rwag location","where is rwag","find rwag"}},{q="What is 'the Hand' mentioned by Rwag?",a="Rwag means the Shattered Hand, a covert network and guild of assassins, spies, and rogues serving Warchief Thrall’s Horde.",al={"what is the hand","shattered hand rwag","who is the hand"}},{q="Why is the tablet written in an encrypted cipher?",a="The cipher hides sensitive rogue business and handlers’ identities from prying eyes. It also tests whether an initiate can handle discreet messages.",al={"why encrypted","why cipher","rogue tablet code"}},{q="Can any class undertake this quest?",a="No. Only troll rogues beginning their journey in the Valley of Trials receive the Encrypted Tablet.",al={"is encrypted tablet rogue only","can warriors do encrypted tablet","tablet class restriction"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you meet your first mentor, Rwag, through the tablet and encounter the Shattered Hand’s reach in Durotar.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you come from a culture that honors open battlefield combat. Orc rogues serve the modern Horde as scouts and infiltrators.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you bring jungle tracking instincts to the bladecraft taught by mentors in the Den. This gives you quiet utility among your orc allies."},kw={"durotar","encrypted tablet","gornek","rogue trainer","rwag","shattered hand","the den","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:rwag","npc:gornek","quest:cutting-teeth","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:the-den","zone:durotar"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Rwag",level="1",faction="Horde",cl={"ROGUE"},ra={"Troll"},id=3083},src={"Encrypted Tablet (quest)"}}
E["quest:3084"] = {t="quest",n="Rune-Inscribed Tablet",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Shikrik calls promising initiates to formal shaman training. The tablet's runes carry the summons to study the spirits and the elements: earth, fire, water, and air.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Shikrik calls promising initiates to formal shaman training.",sec={{t="A Call to the Spirits",b="After showing early discipline in the Valley of Trials' dusty grounds, fledgling shamans receive a carved stone tablet from Gornek. Its runes carry an invitation from Shikrik, the local shaman trainer. The summons says each initiate is ready to look beyond physical combat and heed the deeper currents of the natural world.",sp=0},{t="Spiritual Leadership in the New Horde",b="Shamanism holds a sacred place in the revitalized Horde. Shikrik teaches that shamans draw power from the four elements and strength from ancestral spirits. They follow Warchief Thrall's example as spiritual guides and sources of wisdom for their communities. Across Durotar, they protect the settlements taking root.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Rune-Inscribed Tablet?",a="Gornek gives novice shamans in the Valley of Trials an inscribed stone tablet bearing a summons from Shikrik. Its runes call the young adventurer to formal training in spiritual and elemental arts.",al={"rune inscribed tablet","tablet item","shaman tablet"}},{q="Who is Shikrik?",a="Shikrik is the shaman trainer near the mouth of the Den in the Valley of Trials. She guides new orc and troll shamans in mastering the elements and learning their duty as spiritual leaders within the Horde.",al={"shikrik","who is shikrik","shaman trainer valley of trials"}},{q="Why does Shikrik invoke Thrall when speaking to new shamans?",a="Warchief Thrall led the revival of ancestral shamanism after demonic corruption consumed the Old Horde. Shikrik points to him as an example of a shaman's duty to keep elemental harmony while guiding and protecting their people.",al={"why thrall","shikrik mentioning thrall"}},{q="Where is Shikrik located?",a="Shikrik is just outside the Den's entrance on the eastern side of the Valley of Trials, ready to teach novice shamans their early techniques.",al={"where is shikrik","find shikrik"}},{q="Who hands out the tablet?",a="Gornek oversees the first trials of newcomers arriving in the Valley of Trials. He gives the tablet to an initiate who has proved their basic mettle.",al={"who gives the tablet","gornek tablet"}},{q="What core philosophy does Shikrik teach?",a="Shikrik teaches that a shaman draws power from fire, earth, water, and air, and endurance and resolve from ancestral spirits. Shamans are expected to offer wisdom and defense to the towns or warbands they join.",al={"shikrik philosophy","shaman teachings"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you receive this tablet as your formal initiation into the path. It charges you to balance elemental powers and guide others through ancestral wisdom.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you see in this tablet the return to ancestral shamanism championed by Thrall, leaving behind the demonic past's warlock legacy.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you find common ground in shamanism with orc mentors like Shikrik. You join your ancestral communion with the Horde's shared elemental traditions.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you share a tradition of shamanism that offers honor and balance across the harsh frontier."},kw={"durotar","elements","gornek","shaman","shikrik","tablet","thrall","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:gornek","subzone:valley-of-trials","quest:cutting-teeth","subzone:the-den","zone:durotar","npc:thrall","topic:horde"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Shikrik",level="1",faction="Horde",cl={"SHAMAN"},ra={"Troll"},id=3084},src={"Rune-Inscribed Tablet (quest)"}}
E["quest:3085"] = {t="quest",n="Hallowed Tablet",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, the Hallowed Tablet carries Ken'jai's call to young priests after their first test. It points them toward the Darkspear way of communing with spirits.",h="In the Valley of Trials, the Hallowed Tablet carries Ken'jai's call to young priests after their first test.",sec={{t="A Message from Ken'jai",b="After you prove yourself against the boars under Gornek's watch, he gives you an inscribed stone: the Hallowed Tablet. Ken'jai's mark is on its message. The Darkspear mystic waits outside the Den, where he watches over newcomers drawn to faith and spiritual magic.",sp=0},{t="Communing with the Spirits",b="Darkspear priests among the Horde seek communion with spirits and loa. Across the sea, human and dwarven priests follow the Holy Light. Ken'jai welcomes you to Durotar and teaches that spiritual discipline makes your power grow. He will guide you in greater rites as your bond with the spirits matures.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Hallowed Tablet?",a="The Hallowed Tablet carries a message from Ken'jai, the troll priest trainer, for young priests in the Valley of Trials. Gornek keeps it until you prove your basic abilities in the valley.",al={"what is hallowed tablet","hallowed tablet item","tablet lore"}},{q="Who is Ken'jai?",a="Ken'jai is a Darkspear troll priest trainer outside the Den in the Valley of Trials. He teaches young initiates to commune with spirits and learn healing and shadowy spiritual arts.",al={"kenjai","who is kenjai","ken'jai trainer"}},{q="Why does a priest start out fighting mottled boars?",a="You prove basic self-reliance and survival skills before a specialist instructor spends time training you. Every initiate in the Valley of Trials faces this test, whatever their calling.",al={"why kill boars","cutting teeth connection"}},{q="How does Ken'jai's priesthood differ from the Holy Light?",a="Darkspear priests call on spirits and loa, while human and dwarven churches worship the Holy Light. Ken'jai teaches you to keep favor with these unseen powers and live in harmony with them.",al={"troll priest lore","horde priests","spirits vs light"}},{q="Where is the Den?",a="The Den is a hollowed cave settlement in the Valley of Trials in southern Durotar. Trainers and trial-masters use it as a hub for new Horde recruits.",al={"the den durotar","where is the den","kenjai location"}},{q="Can orcs become priests through this quest?",a="No. Only Darkspear trolls in the Valley of Trials have the spiritual traditions to train as priests under Ken'jai. Orcish culture instead follows shamanism and warlock magic.",al={"orc priests","can orcs be priests","orc hallowed tablet"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you leave the valley's ordinary trials and begin formal spiritual instruction with Ken'jai outside the Den.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you follow Darkspear traditions that honor ancestral spirits and loa, rather than the dogmatic ways of foreign priests.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help keep spiritual rites and the will of the spirits central as your people settle Durotar."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","gornek","hallowed tablet","ken'jai","priest","spirits","the den","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:cutting-teeth","npc:gornek","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:the-den","zone:durotar"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Ken'jai",level="1",faction="Horde",cl={"PRIEST"},ra={"Troll"},id=3085},src={"Hallowed Tablet (quest)"}}
E["quest:3086"] = {t="quest",n="Glyphic Tablet",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, a Glyphic Tablet calls young Horde mages to Mai'ah. Gornek gives it to them after they prove their strength, and the troll trainer waits outside the Den.",h="In the Valley of Trials, a Glyphic Tablet calls young Horde mages to Mai'ah.",sec={{t="A Message in Inscribed Stone",b="You have proved your strength against the Valley of Trials' wildlife. Gornek gives you an inscribed tablet sent by Mai'ah, the valley's mage trainer. When you are ready to begin your arcane studies, she asks you to meet her by the Den's entrance.",sp=0},{t="The Dangers of the Unseen",b="Mai'ah speaks plainly about a mage's power and its danger. Magic's unseen pull toward corruption, she warns, is a greater threat than rival warriors or enemy races. Humility and patience matter. Without them, unchecked sorcery can make a mage believe they have mastered more than they have.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who delivers the Glyphic Tablet to the player?",a="Gornek gives you the tablet after you clear the mottled boars in the Valley of Trials.",al={"who gives glyphic tablet","where do i get glyphic tablet","glyphic tablet starter"}},{q="Who is Mai'ah?",a="Mai'ah is a Darkspear troll mage trainer outside the Den in the Valley of Trials. She teaches beginning Horde mages early spells and warns them about arcane corruption.",al={"who is maiah","mai'ah lore","troll mage trainer"}},{q="Where is Mai'ah located?",a="Mai'ah waits just outside the Den's entrance, to the right of the tunnel mouth in the northern Valley of Trials.",al={"where is maiah","maiah location","find maiah"}},{q="What warning does Mai'ah give about magic?",a="Mai'ah warns that magic can corrupt those who wield it. She says mages should fear its unseen temptations and delusions of power more than physical enemies such as orcs, elves, or dwarves.",al={"maiah warning","magic corruption lore","what does maiah say"}},{q="Do other classes receive the Glyphic Tablet?",a="No. The Glyphic Tablet is for novice mages. Other classes receive different introductory summons, such as runes, scrolls, or sigils, suited to their trainers.",al={"can other classes get glyphic tablet","is glyphic tablet mage only"}},{q="What prerequisite must be met to receive this tablet?",a="You must first complete Gornek's opening task by slaying mottled boars across the red dirt flats of the Valley of Trials.",al={"glyphic tablet requirements","prereq for glyphic tablet"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you receive a formal welcome among Horde spellcasters from the valley's trainer. Mai'ah teaches you the discipline needed to control raw magic.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, your training with Mai'ah reflects your tribe's growing use of formal spellcasting alongside its traditional spiritual rites.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you take up a rare path under Mai'ah. Orcish culture has long been shaped by shamans and warriors, and few of your people have tried the arcane."},kw={"arcane","durotar","glyphic tablet","gornek","mage","mai'ah","the den","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:mai-ah","npc:gornek","quest:cutting-teeth","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:dwarf"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Mai'ah",level="1",faction="Horde",cl={"MAGE"},ra={"Troll"},id=3086},src={"Glyphic Tablet (quest)"}}
E["quest:3087"] = {t="quest",n="Etched Parchment",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Gornek delivers Jen'shan's summons to a young hunter. It comes after the initiate's first blooding and opens the way to wilderness training in Durotar.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Gornek delivers Jen'shan's summons to a young hunter.",sec={{t="A Summons from the Wild",b="After proving themselves against mottled boars, hunters in the Valley of Trials receive a parchment from Gornek. Jen'shan, a skilled Darkspear hunter, sent it after watching new arrivals from the edges of the encampment. Her note welcomes the initiate to formal training and recognizes the instincts needed to master Durotar's untamed beasts and harsh land.",sp=0},{t="The Hunter's Way",b="Reporting to Jen'shan marks the move from recruit to dedicated stalker. She warns that hunting is no easier than the arcane arts or ancestral shamanism. Mastering Durotar's predators, keeping ranged weapons in good order, and surviving on unforgiving land all demand discipline.\n\nJen'shan sends her apprentices to aid the valley's other inhabitants and test their abilities. Then they return to learn more advanced ways to survive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Etched Parchment?",a="The parchment is a written summons from Gornek on behalf of Jen'shan, the hunter trainer. It calls promising recruits to her for specialized martial and wilderness instruction in the Valley of Trials.",al={"what is this parchment","etched parchment note","hunter parchment"}},{q="Who delivers this summons to the player?",a="Gornek gives you the parchment after your first trial, when you slay mottled boars in the Valley of Trials.",al={"who gives etched parchment","where do i get the quest"}},{q="Who is Jen'shan?",a="Jen'shan is a Darkspear troll hunter stationed in the Valley of Trials. She evaluates new orc and troll hunters and teaches ranged warfare, tracking, and beastcraft.",al={"jen'shan lore","who is jenshan"}},{q="Why does Jen'shan compare hunters to mages and shamans?",a="Jen'shan warns that many mistake hunting for an easier path than ancestral spirits or arcane magic. Lethal marksmanship and mastery of wild beasts demand equal dedication and carry equal danger.",al={"why hunters not easy","jen'shan dialogue meaning"}},{q="What happens after reporting to Jen'shan?",a="Jen'shan introduces you to advanced hunter techniques and sends you to aid the Valley of Trials' other inhabitants. You practice your newly acquired skills through practical survival.",al={"what next after etched parchment","hunter quest continuation"}},{q="Who can receive this quest?",a="Only newly created orc hunters training in the Valley of Trials can receive it.",al={"who gets etched parchment","is this hunter only"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, this summons points you to Jen'shan to refine your aim and understand the wild.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear recruit, studying under Jen'shan keeps alive the ancient jungle tracking traditions carried from the Echo Isles.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you rely on mentors like Jen'shan to adapt clan hunting methods to Durotar's arid crags and deadly beasts.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde hunter, you scout the borders and feed the camps. Early training helps keep Durotar supplied and guarded."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","etched parchment","gornek","hunter trainer","jen'shan","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:jen-shan","npc:gornek","quest:cutting-teeth","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Jen'shan",level="1",faction="Horde",cl={"HUNTER"},ra={"Orc"},id=3087},src={"Etched Parchment (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3088"] = {t="quest",n="Encrypted Parchment",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Encrypted Parchment calls proven novice orc rogues toward the Den. Its cipher leads them to Rwag, an agent of the Shattered Hand.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Encrypted Parchment calls proven novice orc rogues toward the Den.",sec={{t="A Coded Summons",b="Gornek gives the coded parchment to novice orcs who have proved themselves against the local wildlife. Other trainers recruit pupils openly in the clearing, but rogue instructor Rwag sends his summons by cipher. The message leads you past the sunlit camp and deep into the cavern called the Den.",sp=0},{t="Eyes in the Shadows",b="You find Rwag watching among the rocks inside the Den. Warlocks lurk deeper in the cave, and Rwag tells you he watches recruits for the Shattered Hand. Orcish society prizes open honor and glory in battle. The Shattered Hand works in secret as the Horde's network of spies, cutthroats, and gatherers of intelligence.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends the Encrypted Parchment?",a="Rwag, the rogue trainer in the Valley of Trials, writes the parchment. He has Gornek deliver its coded message to promising young orcs after their first trials.",al={"who wrote the parchment","who gave me encrypted parchment","who sent note"}},{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="The parchment guides orc rogues to Rwag in the Den, where their formal training begins. He teaches stealth, lockpicking, and martial subterfuge.",al={"why do i need encrypted parchment","what does this quest do"}},{q="Where is Rwag located?",a="Rwag hides inside the Den, a dark cavern on the northern side of the Valley of Trials. He keeps near the entrance, wary of the warlocks deeper inside.",al={"where is rwag","find rwag","rwag location"}},{q="Why is the parchment encrypted?",a="The cipher keeps wandering brutes and curious outsiders from reading the summons. It also tests whether an initiate can decode a covert message.",al={"why cipher","why is note coded"}},{q="Who are the Shattered Hand?",a="The Shattered Hand began as an infamous orc clan known for self-mutilation. In Thrall's Horde, it is an organization of scouts, assassins, and covert agents that works from the shadows to protect Horde interests.",al={"shattered hand horde","what is shattered hand"}},{q="Why does Rwag distrust Nartok?",a="Nartok is a warlock trainer deeper in the Den. Rwag distrusts the dark spellcasters who openly conduct fel rituals in the cave's deepest corners.",al={"rwag nartok","why does rwag hate warlocks"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, this parchment marks your induction into the Horde's covert ranks. It introduces you to Rwag and your first professional training.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you balance ancestral discipline with the quiet cunning demanded by the Shattered Hand. Warriors instead seek open, bloodthirsty glory.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know that even an honorable warchief like Thrall needs spies and scouts to protect Durotar's young lands from hidden threats."},kw={"durotar","encrypted parchment","gornek","orc rogue","rwag","shattered hand","the den","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:rwag","npc:gornek","quest:cutting-teeth","subzone:the-den","quest:1858","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","quest:3083"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Rwag",level="3",faction="Horde",cl={"ROGUE"},ra={"Orc"},id=3088,ri={"Encrypted Parchment"}},src={"Encrypted Parchment (quest)"}}
E["quest:3089"] = {t="quest",n="Rune-Inscribed Parchment",z="durotar",s="At the Valley of Trials, Gornek gives new shamans Rune-Inscribed Parchment, a summons from Shikrik. It begins their training in communion with spirits and the elements.",h="At the Valley of Trials, Gornek gives new shamans Rune-Inscribed Parchment, a summons from Shikrik.",sec={{t="A Summons from the Spirits",b="New orc shamans prove they can survive against local wildlife. Then Gornek, who oversees the Valley of Trials, gives them a rune-inscribed summons. Shikrik, the valley's shaman trainer, wrote its mystical message and asks to meet each newly arrived initiate.",sp=0},{t="The Path of the Shaman",b="Meeting Shikrik begins a shaman's sacred duty to the Horde. She teaches that shamans serve as conduits for ancestral spirits and wield the wrath of the elements. Under her guidance, new shamans learn to channel spiritual energies, mend wounds, and call on Kalimdor's natural forces.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Rune-Inscribed Parchment?",a="Gornek gives new shamans in the Valley of Trials a written summons to seek formal instruction from Shikrik, their trainer.",al={"what is this quest","parchment quest","shaman starter note"}},{q="Who sends the parchment?",a="Shikrik wrote the message. She trains shamans near the dens in the Valley of Trials and awaits those chosen to guide their people spiritually.",al={"who wrote the parchment","shikrik note","who is shikrik"}},{q="Where do I take the parchment?",a="You take the parchment a short walk within the Valley of Trials. Shikrik waits beneath the red crags to train orc and troll shamans.",al={"where do i go","where is shikrik","turn in location"}},{q="Why was my character chosen to receive it?",a="Shikrik says those drawn to shamanism are chosen to serve as conduits for the ancestors and speak with the world's elemental forces.",al={"why shaman","why chosen","shaman calling lore"}},{q="What happens after presenting the parchment?",a="Shikrik accepts you as her student. She introduces you to elemental magic, communion with ancestors, and the basics of healing and combat.",al={"next step","what does shikrik do","after parchment"}},{q="Can any class complete this quest?",a="Only new shamans receive the Rune-Inscribed Parchment. Other classes receive distinct summons to their own trainers.",al={"is this shaman only","who gets this parchment","parchment for warriors"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, this parchment marks your first step on a spiritual path. It binds you to the spirits and Durotar's raw elements.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, your return to shamanism honors Draenor's ancestral traditions. The Old Horde's demonic corruption nearly extinguished them.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you bring your natural communion with spirits and reverence for ancestors into the Horde's shared shamanic traditions."},kw={"ancestors","durotar","elements","gornek","rune-inscribed parchment","shaman","shikrik","valley of trials"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","npc:gornek","quest:cutting-teeth","zone:durotar"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Shikrik",level="1",faction="Horde",cl={"SHAMAN"},ra={"Orc"},id=3089},src={"Rune-Inscribed Parchment (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3090"] = {t="quest",n="Tainted Parchment",z="durotar",s="A tainted parchment waits for you after your absence, and your teacher Nartok asks to speak with you. Its words challenge Thrall’s rule and warn of the dangers warlocks face.",h="A tainted parchment waits for you after your absence, and your teacher Nartok asks to speak with you.",sec={{t="A message waits",b="The tainted parchment is believed to come from Nartok, your new teacher. Read it, then speak with him in the Den in the Valley of Trials. He calls the orcs a proud people and says Thrall turns away from power that could make the land theirs.",sp=0},{t="A place among them",b="Nartok says you have joined their ranks, yet warlock power will not make you welcome. Thrall allows warlocks into Orgrimmar because they remain orcs. Nartok warns that recklessness can be fatal. He remains ready to teach you spellcasting if you need instruction.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sent the parchment?",a="The parchment is believed to come from Nartok, your new teacher.",al={"who sent this","parchment from who"}},{q="Where can I speak with Nartok?",a="Nartok is in the Den in the Valley of Trials.",al={"where is nartok","nartok location"}},{q="What does Nartok think of Thrall?",a="Nartok says Thrall turns away from power that could make the land theirs.",al={"thrall opinion","why criticize thrall"}},{q="Why does Thrall allow warlocks into Orgrimmar?",a="Nartok says Thrall allows warlocks into Orgrimmar because they are still orcs.",al={"warlocks in orgrimmar","why thrall allows warlocks"}},{q="What warning does Nartok give?",a="Nartok warns that warlock power does not ensure acceptance, and recklessness can be fatal.",al={"nartok warning","warlock danger"}},{q="Can Nartok teach me spells?",a="Nartok remains available if you need instruction in spellcasting.",al={"spell lessons","warlock training"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you face the danger Nartok warns of: wielding your power recklessly may prove fatal."},kw={"den","nartok","orgrimmar","spellcasting","tainted parchment","thrall","valley of trials","warlock"},rel={"npc:thrall","zone:orgrimmar"},m={faction="Horde",cl={"WARLOCK"},ra={"Orc"},id=3090},src={"In-game quest text: Tainted Parchment"},fv=true}
E["quest:5648"] = {t="quest",n="Garments of Spirituality",z="durotar",s="In Razor Hill, new priests put their healing to the test in the field. They seek Grunt Kor'ja, wounded while fighting Kul Tiras survivors, and tend her injuries. Those who succeed earn ceremonial vestments and recognition among the Horde's spiritual practitioners.",h="In Razor Hill, new priests put their healing to the test in the field.",sec={{t="A Healer's Trial",b="South of Razor Hill, the Horde still fights remnants of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's forces. Tai'jin, the troll priest trainer, tests new priests in the work of battle triage. She sends them to find Grunt Kor'ja, a warrior badly wounded while repelling human infiltrators. You tend her injuries and strengthen her before she succumbs.",sp=0},{t="Vestments of the Faithful",b="Healing Kor'ja proves a young priest is ready to serve the Horde's spiritual tradition. Tai'jin awards the Garments of Spirituality for saving a frontline defender. To orcs and Darkspear trolls alike, the robes mark their wearer as more than an apprentice of incantations. They can be trusted to keep Horde warriors alive in battle.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Grunt Kor'ja and why does she need healing?",a="Grunt Kor'ja is a Horde warrior posted just south of Razor Hill. She was wounded fighting soldiers who survived Admiral Proudmoore's Kul Tiras expedition and still harass the Durotar coastline.",al={"grunt korja","who is korja","injured grunt south"},it="target"},{q="Where can I find Tai'jin?",a="Tai'jin is in Razor Hill, Durotar. She mentors young Horde priests leaving the Valley of Trials.",al={"taijin location","who gives garments of spirituality","priest trainer razor hill"},gp=true},{q="What powers are required to heal Kor'ja?",a="Use Lesser Heal to tend Kor'ja's injuries, then strengthen her endurance with Power Word: Fortitude before returning to Tai'jin.",al={"which spells to use","how to complete garments of spirituality","korja spells"},gp=true},{q="Why are Kul Tiras soldiers still fighting in Durotar?",a="After Grand Admiral Proudmoore's invasion was defeated, remnants of his fleet scattered along Durotar's eastern coast. They still launch desperate raids and hold places such as Tiragarde Keep.",al={"proudmoore troops durotar","why humans in razor hill","kul tiras remnants"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the significance of the garments awarded?",a="The robes Tai'jin awards mark an initiate's passage into active service as a Horde healer. Passing this practical test earns the student the right to wear the vestments of their calling.",al={"garments reward lore","why give a robe","priest vestments razor hill"},it="item"},{q="What quest precedes Garments of Spirituality?",a="The trial follows In Favor of Spirituality. Ken'jai sends a young priest from the Valley of Trials to Tai'jin in Razor Hill.",al={"prerequisite quest","before garments of spirituality","how to start garments"},gp=true},{q="Why does Tai'jin want Kor'ja healed?",a="Tai'jin sees this trial as both practical defense and spiritual duty. Grunt Kor'ja took heavy wounds defending the settlement from Daelin Proudmoore's lingering Kul Tiras remnants, and without healing, she cannot survive to guard Razor Hill. For you, the task serves as your first true test: by mending her body and bestowing ancestral blessings, you prove your mastery of the priestly arts and demonstrate that you are ready to advance along the spiritual path.",al={"why does taijin help korja","taijin motive","why heal korja"},it="motive",add="ef970fef"},{q="Why does Tai'jin send you instead of tending to Kor'ja herself?",a="Tai'jin remains in Razor Hill to guide aspiring priests, and Kor'ja's plight offers the perfect trial to assess your growth. A priest's true worth is proven outside comfortable sanctuaries, in the dust where blood is spilled and frontline defenders falter. By tasking you to mend Kor'ja and fortify her spirit, Tai'jin requires you to demonstrate that your faith and training can endure the harsh realities facing the Horde.",al={"why send me","why doesnt taijin heal korja","why must i heal korja"},it="why_me",add="2bdbaeb4"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you face an early test of field healing in Durotar and earn your first vestments.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you learn from Tai'jin to put Darkspear spirituality to work protecting allies in battle.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help keep Grunt Kor'ja alive as Razor Hill faces nearby Kul Tiras aggressors."},kw={"durotar","fortitude","garments of spirituality","grunt kor'ja","lesser heal","proudmoore","razor hill","tai'jin"},rel={"quest:5649","npc:tai-jin","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:human"},m={start="Tai'jin",level="4",faction="Horde",cl={"PRIEST"},ra={"Troll"},id=5648},src={"Garments of Spirituality"}}
E["quest:5649"] = {t="quest",n="In Favor of Spirituality",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, young Darkspear priests begin their lives beyond the training grounds. Under Ken'jai's direction, they travel to Tai'jin in Razor Hill and meet Durotar's wider challenges. Their path holds both ancestral troll ways and service in the Horde.",h="In the Valley of Trials, young Darkspear priests begin their lives beyond the training grounds.",sec={{t="Leaving the Red Canyon",b="Darkspear acolytes leave the Valley of Trials after learning their basic rites from Ken'jai. The road from those secluded grounds leads to Razor Hill, a crossroads settlement in Durotar. There, a young priest steps beyond survival drills and begins to shoulder the spiritual and cultural duties of the tribe.",sp=0},{t="Old Faiths and New Alliances",b="Ken'jai speaks plainly about the Darkspear's place in Thrall's Horde. The trolls value the orcs' loyalty and lessons of honor, though some ancestral traditions sit uneasily among their allies. So Darkspear spiritual leaders teach their pupils to preserve their heritage quietly while serving the Horde.\n\nAt Razor Hill, Tai'jin welcomes the acolytes. He guides them toward self-sufficiency and strength within the community.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest In Favor of Spirituality?",a="Ken'jai, the troll priest trainer in the Den, directs you from the Valley of Trials.",al={"who starts in favor of spirituality","quest giver in favor of spirituality","kenjai priest quest"},gp=true},{q="Where can I find Tai'jin?",a="Tai'jin is in the barracks at Razor Hill, east of the town center along Durotar's main road.",al={"tai'jin location","where is tai jin","find tai'jin"},gp=true},{q="What classes can accept this quest?",a="Only troll priests beginning their journey in Durotar can take this path.",al={"is this quest priest only","who can take in favor of spirituality","priest class quest razor hill"},gp=true},{q="Why does Ken'jai emphasize keeping some traditions secret?",a="Ken'jai says the orcs are loyal allies who value honor, but do not welcome every ancient troll ritual or custom. He teaches young priests to honor their ancestral heritage discreetly and preserve harmony within the Horde.",al={"why secret troll traditions","orc troll friction religion","why practice in secret"},it="motive"},{q="What does Tai'jin teach the young priest upon arrival?",a="Tai'jin teaches that the Darkspear grew stronger by adapting to life in the Horde. The tribe prepares beforehand and enters battle already empowered, rather than waiting to draw strength directly from fallen foes.",al={"taijin speech","what does tai jin say","darkspear adaptation"},it="purpose"},{q="What quest immediately follows In Favor of Spirituality?",a="After you report to Tai'jin, she offers Garments of Spirituality. You go to help a wounded Horde soldier in the field.",al={"what comes after in favor of spirituality","in favor of spirituality follow up","next priest quest after taijin"},it="next_step",gp=true}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you leave the novice canyon and receive formal training and vestments from Tai'jin in Razor Hill.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you balance loyalty to the Horde with the preservation of ancient tribal spirituality.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see diverse cultures work together in Durotar, joining the wild traditions of the Echo Isles with Razor Hill's martial outpost."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","in favor of spirituality","ken'jai","priest","razor hill","tai'jin","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:tai-jin","quest:5648","subzone:razor-hill","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","npc:ukor","quest:2161","topic:horde"},m={start="Ken'jai",["end"]="Tai'jin",level="4",faction="Horde",cl={"PRIEST"},ra={"Troll"},id=5649},src={"In Favor of Spirituality"}}
E["quest:5654"] = {t="quest",n="Hex of Weakness",z="durotar",s="From Razor Hill to Orgrimmar, Hex of Weakness marks a young Darkspear priest’s next step. Tai'jin sends an initiate north to Ur'kyo, who welcomes new students into the tribe’s spiritual circle and teaches the loa’s darker arts.",h="From Razor Hill to Orgrimmar, Hex of Weakness marks a young Darkspear priest’s next step.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Circle",b="Tai'jin watches over young Darkspear priests as they study in Razor Hill’s barracks. When an acolyte has mastered spiritual communion and shadow magic, those first lessons come to an end. Tai'jin sends the promising priest north across Durotar’s red dirt canyons to Orgrimmar, the Horde capital. There, elder practitioners teach the tribe’s wider magical traditions.",sp=0},{t="The Old Ways in the Valley of Spirits",b="In Orgrimmar’s Valley of Spirits, the Darkspear keep a sanctuary apart from the orcs’ forges and warrior grounds. Ur'kyo, an elder priest, welcomes new initiates there. Joining his circle means honoring the loa and learning the ancestral ways of the jungle trolls. It also means mastering potent curses and hexes that sap an enemy’s strength in battle.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="The rite marks an initiate’s advancement in the Darkspear priesthood. Tai'jin sends developing troll priests from Durotar’s coast to Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar, where they join the tribe’s inner circle of spiritual practitioners.",al={"why do this quest","hex of weakness purpose","what does hex of weakness quest do"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Tai'jin?",a="Tai'jin is a troll priest trainer in the barracks of Razor Hill in Durotar. She guides young Darkspear spellcasters through their early trials before sending them onward to the capital.",al={"who is quest giver","tai'jin lore","taijin"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Ur'kyo?",a="Ur'kyo is an elder troll priest trainer in Orgrimmar’s Valley of Spirits. He oversees advanced spiritual training and teaches Darkspear priests tribal hexes and deep ancestral rites.",al={"who is ur'kyo","urkyo priest trainer","ur-kyo"},it="target"},{q="Where is the Valley of Spirits?",a="The Valley of Spirits is a secluded, swampy district in western Orgrimmar. It is the Darkspear trolls’ main home within the orcish fortress city, with their trainers, lodgings, and totems.",al={"valley of spirits location","where is ur'kyo","where to find ur'kyo"},it="place"},{q="What kind of magic does this training focus on?",a="Darkspear priests draw on the loa and ancient jungle troll traditions. They balance restorative spirit magic with weakening curses such as Hex of Weakness, rather than relying only on the Holy Light favored by humans or dwarves.",al={"troll priest magic","what are the old ways","hex lore"},it="power"},{q="Can non-trolls undertake this quest?",a="No. The rite belongs to Darkspear tradition and its unique spells. Undead priests go to their own mentors and shadow philosophies in Tirisfal and the Undercity.",al={"can undead do this","is this troll only"},gp=true},{q="Why does Tai'jin want this done?",a="Tai'jin recognizes that your basic training is complete and you are ready to delve deeper into the traditions of the Darkspear tribe. She sends you to Ur'kyo so you can be formally initiated into the circle and taught the ancient spiritual rites that define a true troll priest.",al={"taijin motive","why send me to urkyo","why learn hex of weakness"},it="motive",rc="Troll",add="f04dcf0d",nx={8}},{q="Why does Tai'jin send you instead of teaching you herself?",a="Tai'jin provides initial guidance to fledging priests in Razor Hill, but advanced spiritual instruction and tribal initiation are overseen by elder masters like Ur'kyo. To truly progress in the craft and master the deeper ways of your people, you must journey to the Valley of Spirits where the elders convene.",al={"why can't taijin teach me","why send me to orgrimmar","why must i go to urkyo"},it="why_me",rc="Troll",add="3c464e0c"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you leave novice lessons in Razor Hill and travel toward recognition as a Darkspear priest, learning curses passed down through generations.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you draw on communion with primal spirits, weaving tribal hexes with shadow and restorative spells. These traditions differ from the dogma of the Holy Light or the Forgotten Shadow.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see troll culture take root within the fortified walls of Thrall’s growing capital as you travel from Razor Hill to the Valley of Spirits."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","hex of weakness","loa","orgrimmar","sen'jin village","tai'jin","ur'kyo","valley of spirits"},rel={"npc:ur-kyo","npc:tai-jin","subzone:valley-of-spirits","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Tai'jin",["end"]="Ur'kyo",level="10",faction="Horde",cl={"PRIEST"},ra={"Troll"},id=5654,xg=5652},src={"Hex of Weakness (Durotar)"}}
E["quest:6062"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="durotar",s="In Razor Hill, Taming the Beast puts young Horde hunters to their first test with a taming rod. Thotar sends them to face a fierce dire mottled boar.",h="In Razor Hill, Taming the Beast puts young Horde hunters to their first test with a taming rod.",sec={{t="A Hunter's Rite of Passage",b="In Durotar, orc and Darkspear troll hunters must learn to command the wild as well as survive it. Thotar gives young hunters an enchanted taming rod and sends them against a fierce wild boar. They must subdue the beast without killing it, then make it a loyal ally.",sp=0},{t="The Boars of Durotar",b="Dire mottled boars roam the dry brush around Razor Hill. Their strength and temper make them a fitting first test for young hunters. The rod can subdue a charging boar, but using it takes patience and resolve. Every Horde tracker needs those qualities.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this trial?",a="The trial gives young hunters in Durotar their first practical lesson with a taming rod. They learn to subdue a wild creature instead of killing it.",al={"why do this quest","boar taming quest reason","taming the beast point"},it="purpose"},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Thotar, the hunter trainer in Razor Hill, gives you this trial after you prove your basic survival skills across Durotar.",al={"quest giver","who gives taming the beast","where to get boar quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the dire mottled boars found?",a="Dire mottled boars roam the dry scrublands outside Razor Hill’s palisades in central Durotar.",al={"boar location","where is dire mottled boar","where to find boar"},gp=true},{q="Do you keep the boar permanently after this quest?",a="No. The boar you tame is practice and leaves when you return to Thotar. You continue training with other creatures before you form a lasting bond.",al={"do i keep the boar","is the boar my permanent pet","keep dire mottled boar"},gp=true},{q="What comes after this task?",a="After you return to Thotar, he tests your command over other deadly Durotar predators, including surf crawlers and armored scorpid beasts.",al={"next quest","what after boar taming","taming chain next step"},it="next_step"},{q="Why use a taming rod instead of pure instinct?",a="Novice hunters have not yet gained the spiritual and physical discipline to bond directly with beasts. The enchanted rod focuses their will on a wild beast’s spirit until they master the art.",al={"why taming rod","what does the rod do","lore of taming rod"},it="power"},{q="Why does Thotar want you to tame a dire mottled boar?",a="Thotar is preparing you to become a true hunter of the Horde. In his eyes, commanding authority over nature and harnessing the inherent strength of wild beasts is essential to your discipline. He starts you with a local dire mottled boar so you can prove your determination and learn how to fight alongside a companion before moving on to fiercer predators.",al={"thotar motive","why tame boar thotar","why does thotar send you"},it="motive",add="97dfd1bd"},{q="What are dire mottled boars?",a="Dire mottled boars are rugged, aggressive swine indigenous to the dry plains of Durotar. Known for their thick hides, stubborn temperaments, and vicious tusks, they roam the crags and ravines near Razor Hill scavenging for food. Their stubborn nature makes them sturdy first partners for a novice hunter learning the art of beast mastery.",al={"dire mottled boar","what is a dire mottled boar","mottled boars durotar"},it="target",add="9ea8907b"},{q="Why does Thotar send you on this trial instead of handling it himself?",a="This is not an errand or an emergency for Razor Hill's defenders; it is your personal initiation as a hunter. Gaining control over a beast requires direct willpower, practice, and personal determination that no mentor or scout can perform on your behalf. Thotar's role is to guide your training, but mastering the wild is a burden you must shoulder alone.",al={"why me thotar","why do i have to tame it","why doesn't thotar tame it"},it="why_me",add="81608777"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you begin learning the bond with animal companions that marks a master of beasts.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you show strength of will by commanding a beast in Durotar’s harsh wilderness, your new home.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll hunter, you attune your spirit to Kalimdor’s rugged wildlife and continue your people’s ancient stalking traditions."},kw={"dire mottled boar","durotar","hunter quest","pet taming","razor hill","taming rod","thotar"},rel={"npc:thotar","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:6065","quest:6061","quest:6081","topic:troll"},m={start="Thotar",["end"]="Thotar",level="10",faction="Horde",cl={"HUNTER"},ra={"Orc","Troll"},id=6062},src={"Taming the Beast (Orc and Troll 1)"}}
E["quest:6069"] = {t="quest",n="The Hunter's Path",z="durotar",s="Thotar at Razor Hill can guide you toward earning a beast companion. You are sent to speak with him.",h="Thotar at Razor Hill can guide you toward earning a beast companion.",sec={{t="A Beast Companion",b="A trainer sees promise in your skill with beasts and sends you to Thotar at Razor Hill. He can guide you toward earning a pet of your own.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who should I speak with?",a="Speak with Thotar at Razor Hill.",al={"who do I talk to","where do I go","Thotar quest"}},{q="What can Thotar help me with?",a="Thotar can guide you toward earning a pet of your own.",al={"what does Thotar do","get a pet","hunter pet"}},{q="Why am I being sent to Thotar?",a="A trainer believes you are skilled enough to handle and train a beast as a companion.",al={"why Thotar","what's the point","hunter path"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you are judged skilled enough to handle a beast and train it as your companion."},kw={"beast","companion","hunter","hunter's path","pet","razor hill","thotar"},rel={"npc:thotar","subzone:razor-hill","topic:hunter"},m={faction="Horde",cl={"HUNTER"},ra={"Orc","Troll"},id=6069,xg=6068},src={"In-game quest text: The Hunter's Path"},fv=true}
E["quest:6081"] = {t="quest",n="Training the Beast",z="durotar",s="In Durotar, young orc and troll hunters are sent to learn from veteran master hunter Ormak Grimshot. After proving themselves with the plains beasts, they travel from Razor Hill to Orgrimmar. There they learn to care for, feed, and train a lifelong animal companion.",h="In Durotar, young orc and troll hunters are sent to learn from veteran master hunter Ormak Grimshot.",sec={{t="A Journey Beyond the Wilderness",b="In Durotar's arid canyons, skill with a bow and survival in the wild are only part of a hunter's duty. Young hunters first tame the plains beasts: fierce boars, crab scavengers, and armored scorpid stalkers. Once they prove their resilience, Thotar sends them from Razor Hill north through the red clay gulches to Orgrimmar's fortified gates. There, they must take responsibility for a companion.",sp=0},{t="The Valley of Honor",b="Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor is where veteran stalkers and warriors hone their craft. There, young hunters seek Ormak Grimshot, one of the Horde's revered master hunters. He looks beyond their youth to judge whether they have the patience to command a beast and care for it through famine, battle, and loss.",sp=0},{t="Bonding with the Wild",b="A beast won through force remains wild until hunter and companion understand one another. Ormak teaches the traditions that keep their bond: which foods nourish each creature's spirit, how discipline teaches a beast lethal techniques, and the spiritual focus needed to revive one that falls in the line of duty.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts the quest Training the Beast?",a="Thotar, the hunter trainer outside the barracks in Razor Hill, offers this training after you subdue all three test creatures across Durotar.",al={"quest giver","who gives training the beast","where to start training the beast"},gp=true},{q="Where can I find Ormak Grimshot?",a="Ormak Grimshot is in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, an eastern district, among veteran hunter and warrior mentors.",al={"ormak grimshot location","find ormak grimshot","where is ormak"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What skills does Ormak Grimshot teach you?",a="Ormak teaches you to train your companion with active and passive abilities, feed it to keep it loyal and content, and revive it if it dies in combat.",al={"what do i learn","quest reward skills","hunter pet abilities"},it="for_you",gp=true},{q="Why do orc and troll hunters have to visit Orgrimmar for this?",a="Local trainers like Thotar teach basic wilderness survival. The Horde's elder scouts and venerated trackers, including Ormak Grimshot, preserve advanced beast mastery in the capital.",al={"why go to orgrimmar","why orgrimmar","valley of honor visit"},it="purpose"},{q="Do other Horde races undertake this exact quest?",a="No. Orc and troll hunters starting in Durotar undertake this rite. Tauren hunters follow a parallel ritual in Mulgore under their own tribal masters.",al={"can tauren do this","is this orc only","undead hunter"},gp=true},{q="What happens if a hunter neglects to complete this training?",a="Without this training, a hunter cannot feed, properly train, or resurrect a companion. A captured beast grows unhappy and weak, and may ultimately abandon its hunter.",al={"do i need to do this","can i skip training the beast"},gp=true},{q="Why does Thotar send you to Ormak Grimshot?",a="Thotar guided you through the rites of taming Durotar's wild beasts, but knowing how to bond with a creature is only half the hunter's art. A beast captured in the wild will starve or abandon you if neglected. Thotar sends you onward to Ormak Grimshot so a veteran of the Valley of Honor can teach you how to feed, care for, and discipline your new companion properly.",al={"why does thotar want this done","thotar motive training the beast","why visit ormak"},it="motive",add="3f046eec"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, this training makes your pet a permanent, dependable ally rather than a fleeting summon. You learn the arts of Feed Pet and Revive Pet.",["race:Orc"]="For an orc, the bond with a hunting companion is a matter of martial honor and duty, tested in battle across Durotar's harsh frontiers.",["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls making a new home in Kalimdor, learning to commune with Durotar's savage creatures is vital to scouting and surviving on unfamiliar soil.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde relies on scouts and beasts to secure Durotar's and the Barrens' fragile borders against centaur, quilboar, and Alliance incursions."},kw={"durotar","hunter pet","orgrimmar","ormak grimshot","razor hill","thotar","training the beast","valley of honor"},rel={"quest:6061","quest:6065","npc:ormak-grimshot","npc:thotar","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:valley-of-honor","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},m={start="Thotar",["end"]="Ormak Grimshot",level="10",faction="Horde",cl={"HUNTER"},ra={"Orc","Troll"},id=6081},src={"Training the Beast (Orc and Troll)"}}
E["quest:6082"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="durotar",s="In Durotar, a young Horde hunter faces the last trial of Taming the Beast. Thotar in Razor Hill sends the hunter to tame an armored scorpid. Success grants the power to tame, call, and dismiss a lasting companion.",h="In Durotar, a young Horde hunter faces the last trial of Taming the Beast.",sec={{t="The Final Trial",b="A hunter must first prove they can command Durotar's harsh wildlife before traveling Kalimdor with an animal companion. Thotar trains hunters in Razor Hill and sends them to subdue three kinds of creature with an enchanted taming rod. Dire boars and swift surf crawlers have already tested them. Now they face an armored scorpid, a venomous predator with heavy plates, known for its resilience and speed.",sp=0},{t="Bonding with the Wild",b="Taming an armored scorpid tests focus and control under attack, not a hunter's skill at killing. Thotar urges hunters to meet the beast's quick, confident strikes. Once the scorpid is charmed, the hunter returns to Razor Hill and gives the taming rod back to Thotar. Then Thotar teaches the wild's innate techniques, so the hunter can seek out and bind a permanent companion of their choosing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creature do I need to tame for this trial?",a="For this trial, tame an armored scorpid with Thotar's taming rod. It roams Durotar's arid red crags.",al={"what beast to tame","target beast","scorpid quest"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Do I get to keep the armored scorpid after finishing the quest?",a="No. The armored scorpid is only a temporary companion and vanishes when you return the taming rod. Completing the trial teaches you to tame the wild beast of your choice permanently.",al={"keep scorpid","do i keep the pet","scorpid permanent"},gp=true},{q="Who initiates this rite of passage?",a="Thotar, the hunter trainer in Razor Hill, oversees this rite for young orc and troll hunters.",al={"quest giver","who gives taming the beast","thotar location"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why does Thotar want hunters to tame an armored scorpid specifically?",a="Thotar sees the armored scorpid as a model of confident, swift strikes and resilience. Taming such a dangerous predator proves a hunter can command wild beasts.",al={"why scorpid","purpose of scorpid"},it="motive"},{q="What skills do you learn upon completing this quest?",a="You learn Tame Beast, Call Pet, and Dismiss Pet.",al={"rewards","what spells do i get","taming skills unlocked"},it="power",gp=true},{q="What comes after this trial?",a="After learning to tame and call a companion, you can follow Thotar's direction to Training the Beast. There, you learn to feed and command your ally.",al={"next quest","what's next","after taming 3"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Thotar make you tame beasts yourself rather than doing it for you?",a="This is a rite of passage every burgeoning hunter must endure alone. Thotar's role in Razor Hill is to guide and instruct you, but mastering communion with the wild cannot be granted through words alone. Taming an aggressive, venomous creature like an armored scorpid proves you possess the will, patience, and resolve required to bend a fierce predator to your command before you are entrusted with a permanent companion.",al={"why must I tame the beast","why doesn't thotar tame it","why me thotar scorpid"},it="why_me",add="5a0a9a11"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, this rite marks an early milestone. It grants you the core skills to tame, call, and command animal companions.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde youth in Durotar, you face its harshest predators to earn a place among the faction's scouts and providers.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, subduing Durotar's scorpids honors the belief that harsh terrain is overcome through unyielding will and martial discipline.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you draw on keen instincts and a deep bond with wild spirits to pacify venomous predators that could strike others down."},kw={"armored scorpid","durotar","hunter trial","pet quest","razor hill","tame beast","taming rod","thotar"},rel={"npc:thotar","quest:6081","quest:6061","quest:6065","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},m={start="Thotar",level="10",faction="Horde",cl={"HUNTER"},ra={"Orc","Troll"},id=6082},src={"Taming the Beast (Orc and Troll 3)"}}
E["quest:6083"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="durotar",s="Along Durotar's coast, Taming the Beast sends young hunters to face their second trial. Thotar, the hunter trainer in Razor Hill, directs aspiring orc and troll hunters to tame a surf crawler near the Echo Isles and extend their bond to coastal wildlife.",h="Along Durotar's coast, Taming the Beast sends young hunters to face their second trial.",sec={{t="Bonding with the Coast",b="You have mastered a dire mottled boar, and now Thotar sends you toward the sea. Durotar's harsh shores are jagged, and shallow reefs teem with armored crustaceans. A surf crawler resists intrusion into its coastal domain. Taming one calls for patience and fortitude.",sp=0},{t="The Extension of Will",b="Thotar teaches that a bound beast should add to a hunter's strength. With the taming rod, you subdue a surf crawler and learn to command creatures of different temperaments in different surroundings. This trial proves you are ready for permanent companions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are surf crawlers found?",a="Surf crawlers skitter through the shallows along Durotar's eastern shores, across from Sen'jin Village and near the waters leading toward the Echo Isles.",al={"surf crawler location","where is surf crawler","crab location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of taming a surf crawler?",a="Thotar assigns you a surf crawler so you can learn to command different kinds of beasts. Taming an armored aquatic creature broadens your control and proves you can master animals from water as well as dry land.",al={"why tame crab","surf crawler quest purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Do I keep the surf crawler permanently?",a="No. The beasts you tame in these first trials are temporary practice subjects, subdued with Thotar's taming rod. Only after completing the full series do you learn the permanent taming skill.",al={"do i keep the crab","is surf crawler permanent"},gp=true},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Thotar, the hunter trainer in Razor Hill, gives you this trial after you prove you can tame a dire mottled boar.",al={"quest giver","who starts taming the beast 2"},it="identity"},{q="What comes after taming the surf crawler?",a="After you return the rod to Thotar, he gives you a third and final trial: track down and tame an Armored Scorpid. Then he teaches you permanent beast mastery.",al={"next quest","what's next in the chain"},it="next_step"},{q="Why use a taming rod instead of natural skills?",a="Novice hunters have not yet developed the spiritual authority to bond wild beasts permanently. The taming rod lets beginners safely practice channeling their will before they learn the true technique.",al={"why taming rod","what is taming rod"},it="item"},{q="Why does Thotar want me to tame a surf crawler?",a="Thotar is training you in the essential arts of being a hunter. Gaining control over beasts turns them into an extension of your own strength, granting you a distinct advantage over rivals. After testing you against land beasts, he wants you to turn toward the waters to broaden your command and prove you can master spirited aquatic creatures as well.",al={"thotar motive","why tame surf crawler","why does thotar want this"},it="motive",add="4f8a703d"},{q="What are surf crawlers?",a="Surf crawlers are spirited, hardy crabs native to the shallows along Durotar's eastern coast, frequently found scuttling in the waters between Sen'jin Village and the Echo Isles. Their armored carapaces and aquatic nature make them an ideal test for expanding a novice hunter's mastery beyond the terrestrial beasts of the plains.",al={"what is a surf crawler","surf crawlers durotar","about surf crawlers"},it="target",add="5da4eb39"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you learn the discipline needed to command defensive beasts. A creature's natural armor and tenacity can complement your skill as a ranged marksman.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc making a permanent home in Durotar, you reinforce your mastery of the rugged land by subduing its hardy shoreline wildlife.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you know the waters near the Echo Isles and Sen'jin Village well. This trial brings you face to face with wildlife from your coastal refuge."},kw={"durotar","echo isles","pet taming","razor hill","sen'jin village","surf crawler","taming rod","thotar"},rel={"npc:thotar","subzone:razor-hill","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:echo-isles","zone:durotar","quest:6061","quest:6081","quest:6065"},m={start="Thotar",level="10",faction="Horde",cl={"HUNTER"},ra={"Orc","Troll"},id=6083},src={"Taming the Beast (Orc and Troll 2)"}}
E["quest:6394"] = {t="quest",n="Thazz'ril's Pick",z="durotar",s="Foreman Thazz'ril needs his enchanted pick back from the northern cavern. Beasts now prowl the Burning Blade Coven, where the glowing tool lies.",h="Foreman Thazz'ril needs his enchanted pick back from the northern cavern.",sec={{t="A Lost Tool",b="Foreman Thazz'ril directs work in the Valley of Trials. He entered the northern cavern to search for mineral veins and left his favorite pick behind. When he returned, vicious beasts and hostile inhabitants had taken over. Now he seeks capable hands to bring back the tool.",sp=0},{t="Glow in the Dark",b="Thazz'ril enchanted his favorite pick to glow in the dark, making it easier to use in dim caverns. Its light marks the tool in a waterfall chamber inside the Burning Blade Coven. Dangerous creatures prowl the shadows. Thazz'ril hopes to put the pick back to work and find new mining prospects across the valley.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Foreman Thazz'ril?",a="Foreman Thazz'ril oversees labor and resource gathering in the Valley of Trials. He directs peons as they clear timber and prepare the land for mining.",al={"who is thazzril","thazzril role","foreman thazzril"}},{q="Why does Thazz'ril's pick glow?",a="Thazz'ril enchanted his favorite pick to glow in the dark, so it is easier to spot in pitch-black caverns.",al={"why is the pick special","glowing pick","enchanted pick"}},{q="Where is the Burning Blade Coven?",a="The Burning Blade Coven is a dark cave network north of the peon lumber camp in the Valley of Trials.",al={"where is burning blade coven","coven location","pick cave"}},{q="How did Thazz'ril lose his pick?",a="Thazz'ril left his favorite pick behind while surveying the northern cave for minerals. When he returned, vicious beasts and dark cultists had infested the cavern.",al={"how did thazzril lose his pick","why leave the pick","pick left behind"}},{q="Where inside the cave was the pick left?",a="Thazz'ril left the pick deep in the cave, in a subterranean chamber with waterfalls, where he had been surveying the rock walls.",al={"where inside cave","pick room","waterfall chamber"}},{q="What does Thazz'ril plan to do after getting his pick back?",a="Thazz'ril plans to find a productive cave to mine after his peons finish cutting down the surrounding timber in the Valley of Trials.",al={"thazzril future plans","what will thazzril mine"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you know why Foreman Thazz'ril relies on his enchanted pick to survey minerals across Durotar. He hopes to open new mining prospects once the local timber is cleared.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure basic tools and drive off threats like the Burning Blade Coven. That strengthens the Horde's foothold in the Valley of Trials."},kw={"burning blade coven","durotar","foreman thazz'ril","mining","pick","thazz'ril","valley of trials","waterfall"},rel={"npc:foreman-thazz-ril","subzone:burning-blade-coven"},m={faction="Horde",id=6394},src={"In-game quest text: Thazz'ril's Pick"},fv=true}
E["quest:784"] = {t="quest",n="Vanquish the Betrayers",z="durotar",s="At Tiragarde Keep, Kul Tiran forces still hold a foothold on Durotar's coast. Gar'Thok calls the Horde to strike at Lieutenant Benedict's garrison, whose presence has broken the fragile peace with Theramore.",h="At Tiragarde Keep, Kul Tiran forces still hold a foothold on Durotar's coast.",sec={{t="A Shattered Truce",b="Thrall led the Horde across the Great Sea to Kalimdor. There, he and Lady Jaina Proudmoore fought the Burning Legion at Mount Hyjal. Peace broke when Jaina's estranged father, Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore, brought Kul Tiras's navy to Durotar. He blamed every orc for the Old Horde's atrocities and seized coastal strongholds, among them Tiragarde Keep. Daelin died at Theramore, but remnants of his fleet still reject any pact and keep their hatred.",sp=0},{t="Benedict's Resurgence",b="Tiragarde Keep fell for a time after the Grand Admiral's defeat. Then Kul Tiras reserves under Lieutenant Benedict took it back. The fortress lies between Razor Hill and Sen'jin Village. From there, sailors and marines harass travelers and threaten Durotar's eastern sea approaches. Gar'Thok sees their presence as an immediate danger to Durotar's security. So he calls on Horde warriors to strike at Benedict's command.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are Kul Tiran humans attacking Durotar?",a="They are remnants of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's expeditionary fleet. Daelin rejected peace between humans and orcs and sought to destroy Durotar. Even after his death, his loyalists hold coastal strongholds such as Tiragarde Keep and defy the Horde.",al={"why are humans in durotar","kul tiras attacking","tiragarde keep humans lore"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Lieutenant Benedict?",a="Lieutenant Benedict commands the Kul Tiran reserves holding Tiragarde Keep. After Grand Admiral Proudmoore's defeat, Benedict rallied the surviving marines and sailors. He retook the coastal fortress and began persistent operations against the orcs.",al={"who is benedict","lieutenant benedict lore","leader tiragarde keep"},it="leader"},{q="Does Jaina Proudmoore support these humans?",a="No. Jaina made a pact with Warchief Thrall for their mutual survival and opposed her father's aggressive crusade to preserve peace. The troops at Tiragarde Keep are Kul Tiras remnants who reject Theramore's diplomacy and regard Jaina's truce as treason.",al={"does jaina support them","theramore kul tiras alliance","jaina proudmoore tiragarde"},it="ties"},{q="Why are they called 'betrayers'?",a="Gar'Thok calls them betrayers because their invasion broke the understanding Thrall and Jaina Proudmoore forged to defeat Archimonde in the Third War. Their continued military presence in Horde territory defies the post-war boundaries established on Kalimdor.",al={"why betrayers","who betrayed who","betrayers meaning"},it="name"},{q="Where is Tiragarde Keep located?",a="Tiragarde Keep is on Durotar's eastern coast, south of Razor Hill and just northeast of Sen'jin Village. Its high stone walls overlook the coastal waters and give the invaders a strategic base near Horde settlements.",al={"tiragarde keep location","where is tiragarde keep","where to find benedict"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Gar'Thok want Tiragarde Keep cleared?",a="Gar'Thok oversees the defense of Razor Hill and eastern Durotar. The reoccupation of Tiragarde Keep by hostile Kul Tiran forces directly threatens the security of the orcish homeland, defying the peace struck between Thrall and Jaina Proudmoore. Allowing an armed human fortress to fester on Durotar's coastline places nearby settlements and supply lines at immediate risk of invasion.",al={"gar'thok motive","why clear tiragarde keep","gar thok why attack humans"},it="motive",add="6a077d02"},{q="Who are you being sent to eliminate at Tiragarde Keep?",a="You are tasked with breaking the surviving Kul Tiran naval forces occupying Tiragarde Keep: sailors, marines, and their commanding officer, Lieutenant Benedict. These soldiers represent the remnants of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's fleet, maintaining an unauthorized armed beachhead deep within sovereign Horde territory.",al={"who to kill tiragarde keep","who are the targets","vanquish targets"},it="target",add="902328ad"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Kul Tiran forces still occupy Tiragarde Keep on Durotar's threshold. Driving out Benedict's forces shows the Horde can defend its newly settled home from foreign fleets.",["race:Orc"]="Orcs honor the truce with Jaina at Mount Hyjal, but Kul Tiras brings bitter memories of the Second War. Fighting Benedict's marines is a matter of survival and ancestral pride.",["race:Troll"]="Tiragarde Keep lies uncomfortably close to Sen'jin Village, the Darkspear settlement. Driving out its hostile sailors helps protect the trolls' vulnerable new home."},kw={"daelin proudmoore","durotar","gar'thok","kul tiras","lieutenant benedict","marines","razor hill","sailors","tiragarde keep","vanquish the betrayers"},rel={"subzone:tiragarde-keep","npc:gar-thok","quest:825","quest:830","subzone:razor-hill","topic:kul-tiras","npc:jaina-proudmoore","zone:durotar"},m={start="Gar'Thok",level="7",faction="Horde",id=784},src={"Vanquish the Betrayers"}}
E["quest:786"] = {t="quest",n="Thwarting Kolkar Aggression",z="durotar",s="Lar Prowltusk has uncovered a plan to strike Durotar's settlements and Orgrimmar. The Kolkar centaurs have divided the invasion plans among three leaders at Kolkar Crag, west of Sen'jin Village.",h="Lar Prowltusk has uncovered a plan to strike Durotar's settlements and Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Looming Invasion",b="Lar Prowltusk is a troll tracker scouting western Durotar. Under cover of night, he slipped into Kolkar Crag and found the Kolkar centaurs preparing more than scattered coastal raids. Three leaders hold the invasion plans. Their targets are the Valley of Trials, Sen'jin Village, and the gates of Orgrimmar.",sp=0},{t="Striking the Canyons",b="The Kolkar leaders hold three attack scrolls in their camps in the dry canyons of Kolkar Crag. You are sent to destroy the scrolls before the centaurs can strike. Lar Prowltusk believes the Horde could defeat a full invasion, but burning the plans can spare Durotar's defenders costly fighting as their young nation finds its footing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Thwarting Kolkar Aggression?",a="Lar Prowltusk, a Darkspear troll scout, offers the work just outside Sen'jin Village, along Durotar's southern bluffs.",al={"quest giver","who gives quest","lar prowltusk location"}},{q="What targets are the Kolkar centaur planning to attack?",a="The Kolkar plans name the Valley of Trials, Sen'jin Village, and Orgrimmar as targets.",al={"centaur targets","what are attack plans","three targets"}},{q="Where is Kolkar Crag located?",a="Kolkar Crag lies west of Sen'jin Village, beyond the rocky ridges in southern Durotar.",al={"kolkar crag location","where is the crag","centaur village durotar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where are the attack plans found inside the crag?",a="Three Kolkar leaders hold the invasion scrolls at campsites throughout the crag.",al={"attack plan locations","where are scrolls","centaur leaders"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Kolkar want to invade Durotar?",a="The Kolkar are an aggressive centaur clan native to Kalimdor's dry lands. They see the arriving orcs and Darkspear trolls as intruders on their territory and hunting grounds.",al={"why are centaur attacking","centaur motive","kolkar lore"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after the plans are destroyed?",a="Destroying the plans disrupts the Kolkar's coordinated attack and protects Durotar's settlements from a sudden siege.",al={"quest aftermath","does centaur attack stop"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Lar Prowltusk want the attack plans destroyed?",a="Lar Prowltusk scouted Kolkar Crag and discovered the centaur are preparing a three-pronged invasion targeting Sen'jin Village, the Valley of Trials, and Orgrimmar itself. While the Horde would ultimately crush such an assault, Prowltusk wants their operational plans burned to stop the invasion before it starts, sparing Durotar's defenders unnecessary bloodshed and disruption.",al={"why destroy attack plans","lar prowltusk motive","why thwart kolkar aggression"},it="motive",add="a839716d"},{q="Who are the Kolkar centaur in Kolkar Crag?",a="The Kolkar are a brutal clan of centaur who have established a stronghold in the crags along Durotar's western ridge. Fierce and territorial, they harbor deep hatred for the newly arrived orcs and Darkspear trolls, regularly launching raids from their encampment and scheming to drive the Horde completely out of the region.",al={"who are the kolkar here","kolkar crag centaur","why are kolkar in durotar"},it="target",add="4d134dbe"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Stopping the Kolkar offensive spares the young Horde an exhausting fight on several fronts at the threshold of its new home.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you know Sen'jin Village cannot fall to a centaur attack after your people lost their ancient island home.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know the Valley of Trials is where young orcs undergo their rites of adulthood. Centaur aggression there insults orcish warrior culture."},kw={"durotar","kolkar","kolkar crag","lar prowltusk","orgrimmar","sen'jin village","thwarting kolkar aggression","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:lar-prowltusk","subzone:kolkar-crag","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","topic:centaur","topic:horde"},m={start="Lar Prowltusk",level="8",faction="Horde",id=786},src={"Thwarting Kolkar Aggression"}}
E["quest:789"] = {t="quest",n="Sting of the Scorpid",z="durotar",s="At the Den in the Valley of Trials, Gornek sends new Horde recruits after scorpids northwest of camp. Ten tails will prove they can face danger in battle.",h="At the Den in the Valley of Trials, Gornek sends new Horde recruits after scorpids northwest of camp.",sec={{t="Trial of the Stinger",b="Gornek tests novice Horde recruits against the Valley of Trials' wildlife. Scorpid workers roam the rocks northwest of the Den. Their venom has humbled seasoned warriors and clumsy initiates alike. Recruits must face them and bring back ten tails as proof of their skill.",sp=0},{t="Venom and Vigilance",b="Scorpids are dangerous, yet their venom also helps save injured initiates. The Den keeps antivenom brewed from extracted scorpid venom to treat fallen novices. Gornek teaches recruits to stay watchful in battle. Even a small foe can wield enough venom to fell a mighty warrior.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who assigns Sting of the Scorpid?",a="Gornek oversees novice training at the Den in the Valley of Trials. He assigns the hunt to young warriors and adventurers.",al={"who gives sting of the scorpid","scorpid quest giver","gornek quest"}},{q="Where are the scorpids located?",a="Scorpid workers roam northwest of the Den in the Valley of Trials.",al={"where to find scorpids","scorpid location","valley of trials scorpids"}},{q="What does Gornek require from the hunt?",a="Gornek requires ten Scorpid Worker Tails as proof that a recruit has faced the venomous beasts and won.",al={"what do scorpids drop","scorpid quest item","scorpid tails"}},{q="How is the antidote for scorpid venom created?",a="The Den brews antivenom from venom extracted from scorpid stingers. It keeps stores on hand to treat novices who underestimate their prey.",al={"scorpid venom cure","antidote lore","how is scorpid antidote made"}},{q="What lesson does Gornek want recruits to learn?",a="Gornek teaches recruits that any opponent, large or small, can be lethal. Overconfidence against a seemingly minor foe can prove fatal.",al={"gornek lesson","why hunt scorpids","scorpid trial purpose"}},{q="Does Gornek offer further training after this hunt?",a="After you deliver the tails, Gornek says he has nothing left to teach you at the Den. He sends you onward into Durotar to serve the Horde.",al={"what after sting of the scorpid","gornek next quest","does gornek teach more"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As a young orc coming of age in the Valley of Trials, you face an essential test of endurance and battlefield awareness under Gornek's eye.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll training alongside the Horde in the Valley of Trials, you prove your skill against local scorpids before venturing deeper into Durotar.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you learn from Gornek that decisive strikes can overcome tough carapaces. Arrogance toward smaller foes invites defeat."},kw={"antidote","durotar","gornek","scorpid","scorpid worker","sting of the scorpid","the den","valley of trials","venom"},rel={"npc:gornek","topic:warrior"},m={faction="Horde",id=789},src={"In-game quest text: Sting of the Scorpid"},fv=true}
E["quest:791"] = {t="quest",n="Carry Your Weight",z="durotar",s="Atop the watchtower overlooking Razor Hill, Furl Scornbrow asks young Horde adventurers to gather canvas from human and centaur foes. Age and old injuries keep him from the front lines, so he makes supplies to help them on their way.",h="Atop the watchtower overlooking Razor Hill, Furl Scornbrow asks young Horde adventurers to gather canvas from...",sec={{t="A Veteran's Calling",b="Furl Scornbrow fought beside Warchief Thrall in Durotar and at Mount Hyjal. Age and old injuries have slowed him, and he no longer wields his axe in battle. From the watchtower above Razor Hill, Furl keeps a steady vigil and sounds the alarm when danger comes. Though he has left the front lines, he still serves the next generation of defenders from his post.",sp=0},{t="Scavenged Canvas",b="As the Horde's hold on the region grows stronger, signal horn alerts come less often. Furl has more hours to make useful gear, but sturdy canvas is scarce in Durotar's dry canyons. Along the eastern shore, Kul Tiran interlopers carry canvas in abundance. So do the nomadic Kolkar centaur roaming the plains. Furl salvages canvas from these hostile forces and stitches it into utility bags for active scouts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Furl Scornbrow?",a="Furl Scornbrow is an aging orc veteran stationed atop the watchtower above Razor Hill. He fought beside Thrall while the Horde founded Durotar and joined the ranks that defeated Archimonde at Mount Hyjal. Though he can no longer fight on the front lines, Furl keeps watch and crafts field equipment for young Horde warriors.",al={"who is furl","furl scornbrow lore","who gives carry your weight"},it="identity"},{q="Where can canvas scraps be found in Durotar?",a="Canvas scraps can be gathered from Kul Tiran humans along Durotar's eastern shore and from nomadic Kolkar centaur roaming the plains. Both carry sturdy canvas in abundance, which can be salvaged from their belongings.",al={"where to get canvas scraps","who drops canvas scraps","canvas scrap locations"},gp=true},{q="Where is the watchtower where Furl is located?",a="Furl's watchtower stands on the high rocky bluffs directly northwest of Razor Hill. A winding path behind the settlement climbs to the summit and its wooden lookout.",al={"where is furl scornbrow","razor hill watchtower location","find razor hill watchtower"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Furl craft with the canvas scraps?",a="Furl sews canvas scraps into utility bags for young adventurers traveling across Durotar. The extra carrying space helps them bring provisions, rations and salvaged arms through the harsh wilderness.",al={"what does furl make","what is the canvas used for","canvas scraps reward"},it="item"},{q="Why is an old warrior crafting bags instead of fighting?",a="Age and old injuries have left Furl unable to match the speed and strength needed in the field. He finds honor in retirement by keeping watch over Razor Hill and crafting gear to help younger fighters defend the realm.",al={"why is furl crafting","why does furl stay in the tower","why isn't furl fighting"},it="motive"},{q="What war did Furl fight in?",a="Furl fought under Warchief Thrall during the Third War, helping settle Durotar and fighting the Burning Legion at Mount Hyjal. He joined the temporary, necessary truce between the Horde, the night elves and the Alliance to defeat Archimonde.",al={"furl battle history","what did furl do before","archimonde furl"},it="history"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a young Horde soldier in Durotar, you rely on seasoned veterans like Furl Scornbrow. They remind newcomers that honoring the Horde means doing whatever duty the homeland requires, whether guarding an outpost or sewing canvas.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you see in Furl an elder who broke free from demonic corruption and crossed the sea with Thrall. Like others of his generation, he dedicates his final years to nurturing the future of his fledgling nation.",["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you can see Furl's rugged frontier craft in each bag. He turns discarded heavy canvas from human invaders and centaur raiders into durable gear for surviving the wilderness."},kw={"canvas scraps","carry your weight","durotar","furl scornbrow","kolkar","razor hill","razor hill watchtower","tiragarde"},rel={"npc:furl-scornbrow","subzone:razor-hill-watchtower","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:784","quest:786","topic:centaur","topic:horde"},m={start="Furl Scornbrow",level="7",faction="Horde",id=791,ri={"Canvas Scraps"}},src={"Carry Your Weight"}}
E["quest:792"] = {t="quest",n="Vile Familiars",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Vile Familiars pour from a nearby cavern. Zureetha Fargaze found a hidden Burning Blade coven while watching over the trials. Now recruits hunt the familiars spreading across Durotar's red earth.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Vile Familiars pour from a nearby cavern.",sec={{t="A Shadow in the Valley",b="Young orcs and Darkspear trolls face tests of strength, discipline, and loyalty to Thrall's Horde in the Valley of Trials. They were meant to face scorpids and boars, not demonic corruption. Yet a cave to the northeast shelters Burning Blade agents. They have formed a secret coven beneath the valley overseers' watch.",sp=0},{t="Culling the Imps",b="Zureetha Fargaze guides newcomers near the Den. She spotted the taint before it could overrun the canyon. Now Vile Familiars pour from the cave mouth and hurl fire at anyone who wanders too close. Before the Horde can root out the hidden masters, young recruits are sent to cut down these lesser servants and keep the valley secure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Vile Familiars?",a="Zureetha Fargaze gives the task. She waits just outside the Den's entrance in the center of the Valley of Trials.",al={"vile familiars quest giver","who gives vile familiars","where to pick up vile familiars"},it="identity"},{q="What are Vile Familiars?",a="Vile Familiars are small, imp-like demons summoned and bound by Burning Blade cultists. These lesser minions and pets wield fire against intruders.",al={"what are vile familiars","vile familiar lore","vile familiars mob type"},it="target"},{q="Where is the Burning Blade Coven located?",a="The Burning Blade coven hides in a cave in the northeastern Valley of Trials. It lies past the roaming Mottled Boars and Scorpid Workers.",al={"burning blade coven location","where is burning blade coven","cave in valley of trials"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the Burning Blade in the Valley of Trials?",a="The Burning Blade is a covert cult bent on undermining Thrall's new Horde and spreading demonic corruption. From the Valley of Trials, its members can hide while threatening the Horde's newest fighters as the Horde establishes its sovereignty.",al={"why is burning blade here","burning blade motives","what does burning blade want"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens after completing Vile Familiars?",a="Once the familiars outside the cavern are thinned out, Zureetha Fargaze sends you into the cave. There, you face the cultist leader and recover a Burning Blade Medallion.",al={"vile familiars follow up","what comes after vile familiars","burning blade medallion quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Do I have to go deep into the cave to find the familiars?",a="No. Vile Familiars dwell inside the cavern, but many swarm around the entrance and across the canyon floor outside the cave mouth.",al={"are vile familiars inside cave","where to kill vile familiars","farm vile familiars"},gp=true},{q="Why does Zureetha Fargaze want the Vile Familiars slain?",a="Zureetha Fargaze came to the Valley of Trials to guide new recruits, but discovered a growing corruption right at the Horde's doorstep. The covert Burning Blade cult has established a hidden coven in the nearby caves, and their summoned imps are spilling out across the valley. To protect the trial grounds and purge the demonic taint before it spreads further, she needs their vanguard eliminated.",al={"why kill vile familiars","zureetha fargaze motivation","why does zureetha want vile familiars dead"},it="motive",add="edfaf791"},{q="Why does Zureetha send you instead of dealing with the familiars herself?",a="You are in the Valley of Trials to prove yourself worthy of serving the Horde. While Zureetha coordinates the response against the covert cultists and keeps watch outside the Den, dispatching you serves a dual purpose: it curtails the demonic infestation threatening the valley while serving as a vital baptism of fire against the darker powers undermining your people.",al={"why send me","why doesn't zureetha fight","why do i have to kill familiars"},it="why_me",add="67a24c10"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you meet fel taint in your sacred training grounds. It is a bitter reminder that the Shadow Council's legacy still festers despite Thrall's rejection of demonic slavery.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face the Burning Blade's attempt to corrupt Durotar from within. The young Horde must firmly establish its sovereignty.",["class:Warlock"]="As an orc or troll warlock, you face rogue shadowcasters who use demonic pacts for destruction. You bend fel energies toward the Horde's survival."},kw={"burning blade","burning blade coven","durotar","imps","the den","valley of trials","vile familiars","zureetha fargaze"},rel={"npc:zureetha-fargaze","subzone:burning-blade-coven","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:the-den","zone:durotar","topic:horde","topic:troll"},m={start="Zureetha Fargaze",level="4",faction="Horde",cl={"DRUID","HUNTER","MAGE","PALADIN","PRIEST","ROGUE","SHAMAN","WARRIOR"},id=792},src={"Vile Familiars (Classic)"}}
E["quest:794"] = {t="quest",n="Burning Blade Medallion",z="durotar",s="Zureetha Fargaze sends young Horde initiates into the Valley of Trials cave, where the Burning Blade has gathered. They face a hidden cultist and seek the Burning Blade Medallion. Its presence points to demonic corruption near the Horde.",h="Zureetha Fargaze sends young Horde initiates into the Valley of Trials cave, where the Burning Blade has...",sec={{t="A Hidden Threat in the Valley",b="Young orcs and trolls face trials of combat and survival in the Valley of Trials. A menace gathers nearby. Through divination, the warlock Zureetha Fargaze senses that the vile familiars on the northern bluffs are only the vanguard of a darker presence. Deep in a nearby cavern, the Burning Blade cult has formed a hidden coven. Its followers practice dark arts and keep dangerous relics of demonic power.",sp=0},{t="Confronting Yarrog Baneshadow",b="Yarrog Baneshadow, an orc warlock and Burning Blade agent, holds the medallion. He waits on an elevated ledge deep in the underground den, commanding fel beasts and wielding dark magic beyond the Valley overseers’ watch. Defeating him and taking the medallion disrupts the cult’s local leadership before its rituals spread farther into Durotar.",sp=1},{t="The Lingering Shadow",b="The medallion confirms Zureetha Fargaze’s fears. The coven in the Valley of Trials has been dismantled, but the relic shows the Burning Blade is organized and deliberate. Its reach extends beyond the initiation grounds. The nascent Horde faces broader demonic conspiracies across Durotar.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do I find the Burning Blade Coven?",a="The Burning Blade Coven lies in a cave among the bluffs north and west of The Den in the Valley of Trials. Imp-like vile familiars surround it.",al={"coven cave location","where is the cave","burning blade cave valley of trials"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is carrying the Burning Blade Medallion?",a="Yarrog Baneshadow carries the medallion. He is deep in the cavern, on an elevated rock ledge beyond a shallow pool of water.",al={"who drops the medallion","yarrog baneshadow","medallion mob"},it="target"},{q="What is the Burning Blade?",a="The Burning Blade is a treacherous cult of fel-corrupted orcs and warlocks devoted to demonic powers. Its members scheme against Thrall’s new Horde from hidden dens and encampments.",al={"who are burning blade","burning blade cult","what is burning blade"},it="threat"},{q="Why is the medallion so important to Zureetha Fargaze?",a="Through divination, Zureetha Fargaze saw the medallion. The item of power fuels the cult’s dark rituals and proves demonic agents are infiltrating the Valley of Trials.",al={"why does zureetha want it","what is the medallion","zureetha fargaze medallion"},it="motive"},{q="Does defeating Yarrog finish off the cult in Durotar?",a="No. Yarrog’s defeat cleanses the cave in the Valley of Trials, but Zureetha warns that this coven is only a small cell. The Burning Blade has greater ambitions across Durotar.",al={"is the burning blade destroyed","are they gone","after burning blade medallion"}},{q="What happens after turning in the medallion?",a="After you slay Yarrog and recover the relic, you have proven your worth and are ready to leave the Valley of Trials. You are sent to report to Sen’jin Village on Durotar’s southern coast.",al={"next quest","what comes next","after this quest"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Burning Blade Medallion for?",a="Through her divinations, Zureetha Fargaze identified the medallion as a potent item of black magic harbored deep within the Burning Blade Coven. Possessed by Yarrog Baneshadow, it serves as an artifact of demonic power and an emblem of the shadow council's lingering influence right on the Horde's doorstep.",al={"burning blade medallion purpose","what does burning blade medallion do","why is medallion powerful"},it="item",add="29893710"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, recovering the tainted relic helps Zureetha Fargaze expose demonic corruption defiling Durotar’s earth.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, hunting Yarrog Baneshadow shows the new Horde’s struggle to purge the old ways’ lingering demonic taint from its training grounds.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, confronting Yarrog reminds you of the dangers of rogue demonic worship beyond the sanctioned, carefully hidden pacts forged under Thrall’s rule.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, this final trial marks your readiness to venture into Durotar’s broader wilds and defend the young nation."},kw={"burning blade","coven","durotar","medallion","the den","valley of trials","warlock","yarrog baneshadow","zureetha fargaze"},rel={"npc:zureetha-fargaze","subzone:burning-blade-coven","quest:792","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:the-den","zone:durotar"},m={start="Zureetha Fargaze",level="5",faction="Horde",id=794,ri={"Burning Blade Medallion"}},src={"Burning Blade Medallion (Classic)"}}
E["quest:804"] = {t="quest",n="Sarkoth",z="durotar",s="On the Valley of Trials' high bluffs, Hana'zua waits for help after Sarkoth's venom leaves him stranded. You have slain the scorpid that wounded him. Now Gornek needs word at the Den so aid can reach the scout.",h="On the Valley of Trials' high bluffs, Hana'zua waits for help after Sarkoth's venom leaves him stranded.",sec={{t="A Scout's Plight",b="Hana'zua, a Darkspear scout, lies stranded on the high bluffs of the Valley of Trials. Sarkoth's venom has left him too weak to descend the treacherous paths alone. You have avenged him by slaying the scorpid, but he still cannot cross the arid stones without help. So a passing initiate must carry word down to the training encampment.",sp=0},{t="Honor in the Den",b="Gornek waits at the Den for your report. When he hears of Hana'zua's plight, he recognizes the danger from Sarkoth and organizes aid for the scout. Horde commanders honor those who set aside their own training to defend and rescue a fallen stranger. Such conduct proves an initiate's worth before they march into Durotar proper.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hana'zua and why is he stranded?",a="Hana'zua is a young Darkspear troll scout stranded in the Valley of Trials' high reaches. Sarkoth ambushed and poisoned him, leaving him too weak to climb down alone.",al={"hanazua","who is hanazua","why is the troll hurt"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Gornek?",a="Gornek is an orc overseer at the Den in the Valley of Trials. He evaluates new recruits, assigns survival tasks, and coordinates aid when initiates face deadly threats in the ravine.",al={"gornek","where is gornek","den leader"},it="identity"},{q="What is Sarkoth?",a="Above the Valley of Trials, Sarkoth prowls the rocky bluffs as a notorious, overgrown scorpid. Its venom and ferocity make it a legendary danger to young orcs and trolls in the trials.",al={"sarkoth beast","what kind of monster is sarkoth"},it="target"},{q="Does Hana'zua survive his wounds?",a="Gornek promises to send aid to Hana'zua as soon as he hears your report. What becomes of the scout afterward is not told.",al={"does the troll live","is hanazua okay","hanazua saved"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Gornek praise this deed so highly?",a="Surviving the trials is expected. Setting aside your own tasks to defend a stranger's honor and help them survive reflects the values the new Horde seeks to forge in its warriors.",al={"why does gornek care","gornek honor speech"}},{q="Where is the Den located?",a="The Den is the central training cave and staging ground at the heart of the Valley of Trials in southwestern Durotar.",al={"where is the den","den location durotar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Hana'zua ask you to report to Gornek?",a="Though avenging his defeat against Sarkoth has steeled Hana'zua's resolve to survive, his grievous wounds leave him completely immobilized in the valley. He cannot make the trek back to the Den on his own strength. By sending you with word of his predicament, he hopes Gornek will dispatch aid before he succumbs to his injuries or the elements.",al={"why send to gornek","hanazua motive","why tell gornek"},it="motive",add="88c1d5d5"},{q="Why can't Hana'zua return to the Den himself?",a="Hana'zua was battered and left for dead by Sarkoth during his trial. He lacks the strength to stand, let alone crawl across the scorching canyon floor back to safety unassisted. With no other warriors nearby to assist him, you are his sole lifeline to relay word to Gornek before it is too late.",al={"why does hanazua need help","why cant hanazua walk","why me hanazua"},it="why_me",add="66b1c5a1"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know personal strength matters. Defending an incapacitated ally's honor shows the heart of a true warrior.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you can strengthen the young bond between the Darkspear tribe and Thrall's orcs by saving Hana'zua from a slow death by venom.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you learn that survival in a harsh, unforgiving land depends on mutual aid. Leaving no comrade behind is taught from an initiate's first steps."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","gornek","hana'zua","sarkoth","scorpid","the den","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:hana-zua","npc:gornek","subzone:the-den","zone:durotar"},m={start="Hana'zua",["end"]="Gornek",level="5",faction="Horde",id=804},src={"Sarkoth (2)"}}
E["quest:805"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Sen'jin Village",z="durotar",s="Zureetha Fargaze sends young initiates from the Valley of Trials to warn the Darkspear trolls in Sen'jin Village. Burning Blade cultists have been active in the valley. Master Gadrin tells them dark magic threatens the nearby Echo Isles.",h="Zureetha Fargaze sends young initiates from the Valley of Trials to warn the Darkspear trolls in Sen'jin...",sec={{t="Leaving the Den",b="After proving their combat mettle and recovering dark medallions from the Burning Blade Coven, young initiates leave the Valley of Trials. Zureetha Fargaze sees that demons in the sacred proving grounds are no isolated nuisance. They point to a blight spreading across Durotar. She sends the proven fighters east past the ravine's mouth, then south toward the coast, to warn the Darkspear tribe.",sp=0},{t="Shadows over the Coast",b="At Sen'jin Village, travelers bring their warning to Master Gadrin, the elder witch doctor guiding the Darkspear in exile. Gadrin says the Burning Blade has not marched on the village sands. Yet dark magic has taken root nearby on the Echo Isles, and betrayal threatens the trolls there. The young Horde's foothold remains fragile as allies hurry to defend one another while tribal divisions and fel corruption strike at their flanks.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Zureetha Fargaze sending people away from the Valley of Trials?",a="Demonic activity in the Valley of Trials makes Zureetha Fargaze fear the Burning Blade threatens all of Durotar. She sends proven initiates beyond the valley to warn allied settlements and learn how far the cult's influence has spread.",al={"why leave valley","why go to senjin","zureetha fargaze orders"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Master Gadrin?",a="Master Gadrin is an elder witch doctor and spiritual leader of the Darkspear trolls in Sen'jin Village. He advises chieftain Vol'jin and oversees tribal matters as threats close on their coastal refuge.",al={"master gadrin lore","who is gadrin"},it="identity"},{q="Has the Burning Blade attacked Sen'jin Village?",a="No, the Burning Blade has not attacked Sen'jin Village. Master Gadrin warns that dark magic and betrayal have taken root nearby on the Echo Isles, putting the trolls in danger.",al={"is burning blade in senjin","cult in senjin"},it="threat"},{q="Where is Sen'jin Village located?",a="Sen'jin Village lies east beyond the main canyon exit of the Valley of Trials, then south at the road's fork along Durotar's southeastern coast.",al={"how to get to senjin","senjin village direction"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threat does Master Gadrin mention on the Echo Isles?",a="Master Gadrin fears Zalazane, a fellow troll witch doctor, has betrayed the Darkspear. Zalazane used insidious hexes to enslave his brethren and seize control of the Echo Isles, driving the surviving Darkspear onto the mainland shores.",al={"echo isles trouble","what happened at echo isles"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after reporting to Master Gadrin?",a="After hearing your report and describing the trolls' plight, Gadrin asks you to help against the dangers threatening the coastline. Further orders then send you northwest to Orgnil Soulscar in Razor Hill.",al={"next quest after report to senjin","what to do after gadrin"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Zureetha Fargaze send you to Master Gadrin instead of a guard?",a="You have personally confronted the Burning Blade inside their coven in the Valley of Trials and recovered proof of their presence. Having proved your loyalty and strength through your trials, you are the most qualified messenger to provide Master Gadrin with an eyewitness account of the cult's infiltration.",al={"why send me","why me zureetha","why not send a runner to senjin"},it="why_me",add="54845e0f"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of Thrall's Horde, you see its founding races share warnings to protect one another's young settlements.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear adventurer, you return to Sen'jin Village to face your people's displacement and their struggle to reclaim the Echo Isles.",["race:Orc"]="As a young orc, you leave the Valley of Trials to aid the Darkspear, an early test of honor and solidarity with the allies who stood beside Thrall across the Great Sea."},kw={"burning blade","darkspear","durotar","echo isles","master gadrin","sen'jin village","valley of trials","zureetha fargaze"},rel={"npc:zureetha-fargaze","npc:master-gadrin","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:valley-of-trials","quest:823","subzone:burning-blade-coven","subzone:echo-isles","zone:durotar"},m={start="Zureetha Fargaze",["end"]="Master Gadrin",level="5",faction="Horde",id=805},src={"Report to Sen'jin Village (Classic)"}}
E["quest:806"] = {t="quest",n="Dark Storms",z="durotar",s="In Durotar, Burning Blade cultists corrupt the land from Thunder Ridge. Orgnil Soulscar in Razor Hill has learned that Fizzle Darkstorm leads them, and asks you to end his threat.",h="In Durotar, Burning Blade cultists corrupt the land from Thunder Ridge.",sec={{t="A Threat in the Ridge",b="Orgnil Soulscar has learned that dark magic has taken hold in Thunder Ridge, northwest of Razor Hill. Burning Blade cultists prowl its ravine while young Horde defenders guard Durotar’s borders. The cultists bring ruin to the wildlife and land.",sp=0},{t="Fizzle Darkstorm",b="Fizzle Darkstorm is a goblin warlock allied with the Burning Blade. He directs the cultists in Thunder Ridge and wields fel power for the cult, not for commerce or cartel interests. Slay him and bring back his twisted claw. Then Orgnil will know the ravine’s leaders have been struck down.",sp=0},{t="Rooting Out the Cult",b="The Burning Blade embodies demonic servitude, corruption, and bloodthirsty madness. Thrall’s new Horde seeks to leave that past behind. Fizzle’s death removes an active conspirator from Durotar’s interior. The shadow over the orcish homeland reaches beyond isolated encampments.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Fizzle Darkstorm?",a="Fizzle Darkstorm is a goblin warlock working for the Burning Blade cult. He and his followers shelter in Thunder Ridge and spread demonic chaos through the ravine. Orgnil Soulscar calls for his execution.",al={"who is fizzle","fizzle darkstorm lore","fizzle goblin"},it="target"},{q="Where is Thunder Ridge located?",a="Thunder Ridge lies in northwestern Durotar, north of Razor Hill and southwest of Orgrimmar. Lightning-infused beasts and Burning Blade cultists occupy its rugged canyon.",al={"where is thunder ridge","thunder ridge location","how to find thunder ridge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the Burning Blade in Durotar?",a="The Burning Blade seeks to undermine Thrall’s Horde and restore demonic dominance over the orcs. Its members hide in ravines, caves, and canyons across Durotar, sowing corruption from within.",al={"burning blade in durotar","why are cultists in durotar","burning blade motives"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Orgnil Soulscar want Fizzle's claw specifically?",a="Orgnil wants Fizzle’s claw as unmistakable proof that the warlock is dead. It confirms the head of the Thunder Ridge cultists can no longer direct their operations.",al={"why fizzle claw","fizzle's claw meaning","proof of death fizzle"},it="item"},{q="What happens after Fizzle is slain?",a="After Fizzle falls, you bring word to Orgnil Soulscar. He sends you to Margoz, a shaman who knows more about the Burning Blade’s corruption, so you can pursue further conspiracies.",al={"what comes after dark storms","dark storms follow up","next quest after dark storms"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why would a goblin work for the Burning Blade?",a="Some goblins are drawn to shadow magic for its power, influence, and dark arts. Fizzle embraced fel witchcraft and put his ruthless cunning at the cultists’ service.",al={"goblin in burning blade","why is fizzle with the cult","fizzle warlock"}},{q="Why does Orgnil Soulscar want Fizzle Darkstorm eliminated?",a="Orgnil fears that if the Burning Blade is allowed even a small foothold in Durotar, their corruption and demonic influence will spread uncontrollably. Fizzle Darkstorm and his coven have entrenched themselves in Thunder Ridge, actively sowing chaos right on the doorstep of the fledgling orc homeland. Striking them down immediately prevents a full-scale demonic infiltration from taking root.",al={"why kill fizzle darkstorm","orgnil soulscar motive","why dark storms quest"},it="motive",add="18f009de"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know the Burning Blade embodies the dark past your people struggle to overcome. Driving out infiltrators like Fizzle helps protect Thrall’s free nation.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you see how Fizzle’s reckless devotion to fel power makes him a danger and an embarrassment to disciplined Horde practitioners.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure Durotar’s heart from demonic subversion. Then the Horde can turn its defenses outward without collapsing from within.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you know Fizzle’s dark rites and minions disturb Thunder Ridge’s natural spirits and agitate its beasts. The elemental balance must be restored."},kw={"burning blade","dark storms","durotar","fizzle darkstorm","fizzle's claw","orgnil soulscar","razor hill","thunder ridge"},rel={"npc:orgnil-soulscar","subzone:thunder-ridge","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:823","topic:goblin"},m={start="Orgnil Soulscar",level="12",faction="Horde",id=806,ri={"Fizzle's Claw"}},src={"Dark Storms (quest)"}}
E["quest:808"] = {t="quest",n="Minshina's Skull",z="durotar",s="In Sen'jin Village, Master Gadrin hears his dead brother Minshina's desperate cries. Zalazane slew Minshina on the Echo Isles and bound his spirit to his severed skull. You can free him from torment by reclaiming the skull from Zalazane's ritual grounds.",h="In Sen'jin Village, Master Gadrin hears his dead brother Minshina's desperate cries.",sec={{t="A Plea from the Shadows",b="Master Gadrin is one of the Darkspear tribe's spiritual anchors in Sen'jin Village. Yet dark visions torment him. His brother Minshina fell when Zalazane betrayed the tribe and seized the Echo Isles. Minshina died in the conflict, but death brought him no peace. Troll tradition and voodoo mysticism hold that a spirit can remain bound after the body dies. Now Minshina's tormented voice reaches Gadrin in his dreams, pleading to be saved from a fate worse than death.",sp=0},{t="Zalazane's Circle of Power",b="Zalazane does more than kill his former brethren. He traps their souls to fuel his dark sorcery. He bound Minshina's spirit to his own skull, now set in a circle of power on the largest of the Echo Isles. Hexed trolls guard the circle as candles burn through the rites. The skull focuses Zalazane's twisted mojo. While it remains there, Minshina is captive to the witch doctor's will.",sp=0},{t="Freedom in Death",b="To free Minshina, you cross east from Sen'jin Village to the southern Echo Isles. You break into the ritual ring and take the skull from Zalazane's grasp. When you return Minshina's remains to Master Gadrin, the dark bindings break. Minshina's grateful spirit briefly appears and bows in reverence. Then he leaves for the realm of the ancestors.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Minshina?",a="Minshina was Master Gadrin's brother. Zalazane murdered him during the uprising on the Echo Isles, then defiled his remains with dark sorcery.",al={"minshina identity","who is minshina","gadrin brother"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Minshina's spirit trapped in his skull?",a="Zalazane uses dark voodoo and warlock magic to enslave the spirits of slain Darkspear trolls. He bound Minshina's soul to his physical skull and placed it in a circle of power. This denied Minshina passage to the afterlife and let Zalazane harness his spirit.",al={"why trap skull","zalazane soul trap","minshina soul"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the circle of power located?",a="The circle of power lies atop a hill on the southernmost and largest of the Echo Isles, off Durotar's southeastern coast. Ritual candles, dancing hexed trolls, and displays of skulls mark the site.",al={"where is skull","circle of power location","minshina skull spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens when the skull is brought back to Sen'jin Village?",a="When Master Gadrin receives the skull, the necromantic bindings shatter. Minshina's ghostly form appears before Gadrin and you, bows in gratitude, then vanishes to rest peacefully with the ancestors.",al={"quest turn in","what happens to minshina","does minshina appear"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who is Zalazane and why did he do this?",a="Zalazane was once a respected Darkspear witch doctor. Driven mad by lust for power, he turned on his tribe and used hexes to mind-control his brothers and sisters. He drove the remaining Darkspear refugees onto Durotar's mainland.",al={"who is zalazane","why zalazane evil","zalazane lore"},it="threat"},{q="Why can't Gadrin retrieve the skull himself?",a="Master Gadrin cannot leave Sen'jin Village unprotected. He holds the settlement together, guides the young Darkspear leadership, advises chieftain Vol'jin, and works to counter Zalazane's expanding hexes along the coast.",al={"why doesn't gadrin go","gadrin duties"},it="why_me"},{q="Why does Master Gadrin want this done?",a="Master Gadrin is tormented by the cries of his brother, Minshina, calling out to him in his dreams. Minshina was slain by the traitorous witch doctor Zalazane on the Echo Isles, but death offered no peace. Zalazane bound Minshina's soul directly to his severed skull, ensnaring him in dark magic. Gadrin cannot bear to leave his brother's spirit condemned to eternal slavery, and he desperately needs someone to break the warlock's hold and grant Minshina eternal rest.",al={"why does gadrin need minshina skull","master gadrin motive","why free minshina"},it="motive",add="2001e9be"},{q="What is Minshina's Skull used for?",a="Minshina's Skull serves as a magical vessel holding the trapped essence of Master Gadrin's murdered brother. Zalazane placed it within a ritual circle of power on the largest of the Echo Isles, using vile sorcery to enslave Minshina's spirit even beyond death. Removing the skull from the dark altar disrupts the warlock's binding magic, allowing Gadrin to finally free his brother's soul once you deliver it safely back to Sen'jin Village.",al={"what is minshina skull","purpose of minshinas skull","minshinas skull item"},it="item",add="5583848b"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you honor family and tribe by recovering Minshina's skull. You strike at Zalazane's corruption of ancestral voodoo traditions.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you know the sanctity of a departed soul and the horror of ritual necromancy that keeps a fallen brother from eternal peace.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you revere the spirits of the ancestors. Breaking Zalazane's circle releases a tortured soul and restores balance between the spirit world and the living.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you honor its bond with the Darkspear tribe by helping Master Gadrin. Your aid proves an ally's grief is shared by all."},kw={"circle of power","darkspear","echo isles","gadrin","minshina","sen'jin village","skull","voodoo","zalazane"},rel={"npc:master-gadrin","subzone:echo-isles","subzone:sen-jin-village","quest:826","topic:troll","zone:durotar","quest:817","subzone:razor-hill"},m={start="Master Gadrin",level="9",faction="Horde",id=808,ri={"Minshina's Skull"}},src={"Minshina's Skull (quest)"}}
E["quest:812"] = {t="quest",n="Need for a Cure",z="durotar",s="On Durotar’s northwestern cliffs, Rhinag is poisoned and far from the cure he needs. The Darkspear troll has little time before the venom kills him, so he sends a passing courier to Orgrimmar for Kor'ghan’s remedy.",h="On Durotar’s northwestern cliffs, Rhinag is poisoned and far from the cure he needs.",sec={{t="A Scorpid's Sting",b="Rhinag fought venomtail scorpids near Durotar’s border when one stung him. Their venom can kill in less than an hour. The poison keeps him from walking to Orgrimmar, leaving his survival to a traveler who reaches his remote camp in time.",sp=0},{t="Secrets in the Shadows",b="Rhinag sends you beneath Orgrimmar to the Cleft of Shadow, where Kor'ghan knows how to counter the poisons of Durotar’s wastes. Kor'ghan can brew a cure, though he rarely helps those who have not proved themselves.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rhinag?",a="Rhinag is a Darkspear troll adventurer clinging to life on Durotar’s northwestern cliffs. A venomtail scorpid stung him, and he fears his kin in Sen'jin Village will mock him if he returns in such a humbled state.",al={"rhinag lore","who is rhinag","rhinag the troll"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Kor'ghan in the Cleft of Shadow?",a="Kor'ghan makes his home in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar. Warlocks, rogues, and others who practice the dark arts work there beyond the eyes of Thrall’s honored warriors. Kor'ghan’s knowledge of venomous brews and grueling trials suits the caverns.",al={"where is korgan","who is korghan","kor'ghan location"}},{q="Why doesn't Rhinag just seek a shaman or healer in Sen'jin Village?",a="Rhinag says pride keeps him from seeking help in Sen'jin Village. He fears his fellow trolls will mock him for returning careless and stricken by venom, so he seeks a discreet remedy from Kor'ghan.",al={"why not go to senjin","why rhinag avoids senjin"},it="why_me"},{q="What happens after Rhinag receives the antidote?",a="Rhinag drinks the antidote and recovers, but Kor'ghan demands more of him. The curer expects him to face grueling trials, including slaying boars and gathering scorpid tails, before he earns Kor'ghan’s good graces again.",al={"does rhinag survive","rhinag aftermath"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where can Rhinag be found?",a="Rhinag can be found in the rugged bluffs of northwestern Durotar, near the border passes leading west toward the Barrens.",al={"rhinag location","where is rhinag"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is there such an urgent rush for this cure?",a="Without treatment, the venomtail scorpid’s poison can overwhelm a victim’s vital organs in less than an hour.",al={"why is it timed","rhinag poison timer"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Venomtail Antidote for?",a="The antidote counteracts the lethal poison of the venomtail scorpids lurking in northwestern Durotar. Rhinag was stung deeply during a careless skirmish with the beasts, and the toxin courses through his blood rapidly. Without this specific draught brewed by Kor'ghan in Orgrimmar, Rhinag has less than an hour before the venom claims his life.",al={"what is the antidote for","venomtail antidote use","why need venomtail antidote"},it="item",add="0710a7b2"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you can see how Rhinag fears the mockery of his kin in Sen'jin Village. Among the Darkspear, carelessness in wilderness survival invites harsh ridicule.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face Durotar’s rocky, unforgiving terrain, a trial for defenders newly arrived in Thrall’s young realm."},kw={"antidote","cleft of shadow","durotar","kor'ghan","need for a cure","orgrimmar","rhinag","scorpid","venomtail"},rel={"npc:rhinag","npc:kor-ghan","quest:813","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Rhinag",level="9",faction="Horde",id=812,ri={"Venomtail Antidote"}},src={"Need for a Cure"}}
E["quest:815"] = {t="quest",n="Break a Few Eggs",z="durotar",s="Cook Torka is waiting on fresh eggs from the Echo Isles before the next meal. You carry them back unbroken so the kitchen can keep to its schedule.",h="Cook Torka is waiting on fresh eggs from the Echo Isles before the next meal.",sec={{t="Endless Meals",b="At Razor Hill in Durotar, Cook Torka prepares meals from morning through evening. Breakfast gives way to lunch, then dinner, with little time to leave the stove for provisions. So Torka sends you to the Echo Isles for Taillasher eggs before the next meal service falls behind. Bring them back whole, and the cook can keep the kitchen working on time.",sp=0},{t="A Cook's Gratitude",b="Cook Torka has little time for praise while meals wait to be made. Eggs need a gentle touch, since a cracked shell spoils an ingredient the kitchen needs. When you bring the eggs back unbroken, Torka sends you on your way and returns to work over the fire.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Break a Few Eggs?",a="Cook Torka needs you to bring Taillasher eggs back unbroken from the Echo Isles, so the kitchen can keep to its schedule.",al={"break a few eggs quest","what is break a few eggs","egg quest"}},{q="Who is the cook in Break a Few Eggs?",a="Cook Torka prepares meals throughout the day at Razor Hill in Durotar. Torka speaks bluntly and is in a hurry, relying on you to fetch Taillasher eggs from the Echo Isles without cracking them before mealtime.",al={"who gives break a few eggs","egg quest cook","who is cooking"}},{q="Why does the cook need eggs?",a="Cook Torka needs eggs for meals prepared throughout the day, from breakfast through dinner. Fresh eggs keep the kitchen's work on schedule.",al={"why eggs","what are eggs for","why need eggs"}},{q="Why does the cook comment on not being clumsy?",a="Eggs can break on the way back. Cook Torka needs the shells and yolks intact for the coming meal service.",al={"why careful with eggs","dont break eggs","why not clumsy"}},{q="What does the title Break a Few Eggs refer to?",a="The title echoes the proverb about making an omelet and breaking eggs. It suits the work of carrying fragile ingredients to a busy kitchen.",al={"break a few eggs meaning","phrase meaning","why is it called break a few eggs"}},{q="Why is the cook so impatient?",a="Cook Torka is busy preparing meals from breakfast through dinner. With more cooking to do, Torka has little patience for chitchat and wants to return to the stove.",al={"cook attitude","why is the cook rude","grumpy cook"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you know the pressure of keeping people fed. Bringing fragile ingredients back unbroken is part of the work in any kitchen."},kw={"break a few eggs","breakfast","cook","cooking","eggs","kitchen","meals"},m={faction="Horde",id=815},src={"In-game quest text: Break a Few Eggs"},fv=true}
E["quest:816"] = {t="quest",n="Lost But Not Forgotten",z="durotar",s="Misha Tor'kren waits at her Durotar homestead for news of her son, Kron. He went west to hunt crocolisks along the Southfury River, and she fears the worst.",h="Misha Tor'kren waits at her Durotar homestead for news of her son, Kron.",sec={{t="A Mother's Dread",b="Misha Tor'kren lives at a farmstead northwest of Razor Hill. Days ago, her son Kron went west to hunt fierce crocolisks along the Southfury River, near the Barrens border. Misha warned him how deadly the beasts were, but pride drove him to prove his strength. No one has seen him since.",sp=0},{t="A Grim Confirmation",b="Misha asks you to search the Southfury River's banks for any sign of Kron, even inside the crocolisks. The Dreadmaw crocolisks hold the answer. Among their remains, you find Kron's swallowed amulet. When you bring it back, Misha knows her son did not survive. The keepsake gives her the closure she needs to begin mourning.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Misha Tor'kren?",a="Misha Tor'kren is an orc mother who lives at a homestead northwest of Razor Hill in Durotar. She fears for her missing son, Kron, and asks travelers to look for any sign of him.",al={"misha torkren","who gives lost but not forgotten","kron mother"},it="identity"},{q="Who was Kron?",a="Kron was Misha Tor'kren's headstrong son. He went to hunt dangerous crocolisks near the Southfury River, hoping to prove his strength, and died there.",al={"who is kron","what happened to kron","misha son"},sp=1,it="identity"},{q="Where did Kron go missing?",a="Kron went west across Durotar toward the Barrens border, to hunt along the banks of the Southfury River.",al={"where is kron","where to look for kron","kron location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How do you prove Kron's fate to Misha?",a="You find Kron's swallowed amulet among the remains of Dreadmaw crocolisks in the Southfury River. Bringing it to Misha confirms that he died.",al={"krons amulet","sign of krons fate","crocolisk stomach"},sp=1,it="item",gp=true},{q="What reward does Misha give?",a="Misha gives you a gift she had prepared for Kron's triumphant return from the hunt. After learning of his death, she cannot bear to look at it and gives it to you, the traveler who brought her closure.",al={"lost but not forgotten reward","misha gift"},sp=1,it="for_you",gp=true},{q="Why did Kron leave in the first place?",a="Kron left out of pride and a desire to prove his skill as a hunter. When Misha warned him about the dangerous crocolisks, he grew angry and stormed off to hunt them anyway.",al={"why did kron hunt","kron pride"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Misha Tor'kren want this done?",a="Misha is tormented by not knowing what became of her son. Kron stormed off days ago after an argument, determined to prove himself against dangerous beasts. While she fears the worst, she cannot begin to mourn or find closure until she has definite proof of his fate.",al={"why does misha need help","misha tor'kren motive","why look for kron"},it="motive",add="ad2ab742"},{q="What is Kron's Amulet for?",a="Kron's Amulet was a personal possession carried by Misha's son when he left to hunt. Recovered from the stomach of a river beast, it serves as grim, undeniable proof to his mother that Kron was slain along the Southfury River.",al={"krons amulet lore","what is the amulet","kron amulet purpose"},sp=1,it="item",add="a54100a0"},{q="What are the crocolisks along the Southfury River?",a="Dreadmaw crocolisks are aggressive, powerful reptiles native to the waterways and muddy banks separating Durotar from the Barrens. Vicious and opportunistic, they will devour any prey reckless enough to venture alone into their feeding grounds along the river.",al={"southfury crocolisks","why kill crocolisks","dreadmaw crocolisks"},it="target",add="a107a32d"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know pride and martial glory matter deeply in your culture. Kron's fate shows the cost of facing dangerous beasts without respect for their strength.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know a tracker must judge the prey's ferocity. Kron failed to do so, and the crocolisks killed him.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know life in Durotar is harsh. Families struggle against the unforgiving land and the deadly predators along its borders."},kw={"amulet","crocolisk","dreadmaw","kron","misha","razor hill","southfury","tor'kren"},rel={"npc:misha-tor-kren","subzone:southfury-river","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","zone:barrens"},m={start="Misha Tor'kren",level="11",faction="Horde",id=816,ri={"Kron's Amulet"}},src={"Lost But Not Forgotten (Classic)"}}
E["quest:817"] = {t="quest",n="Practical Prey",z="durotar",s="Vel'rin Fang calls for tiger hides from the Echo Isles to supply Sen'jin Village. The Darkspear's numbers grow, and their stores run low.",h="Vel'rin Fang calls for tiger hides from the Echo Isles to supply Sen'jin Village.",sec={{t="A Matter of Survival",b="Along Durotar's harsh coast, the Darkspear of Sen'jin Village make every resource last. Tiger pelts become tents, blankets and armor. Refugees arrive and scouts return, thinning the village stores. So leatherworker Vel'rin Fang sends hunters to bring back more hides.",sp=0},{t="Balance and the Hunt",b="The Darkspear hunt Durotar's tigers only when the tribe needs more supplies. Their hunters cross the water to the Echo Isles and track the predators there. For the trolls, each hunt also tests patience, discipline and skill in the wild.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Vel'rin Fang?",a="Vel'rin Fang is a Darkspear leatherworker in Sen'jin Village. He sends hunters for the hides the tribe needs to make clothing, shelter and gear.",al={"vel'rin fang","who gives practical prey","velrin fang"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Sen'jin Village need tiger furs?",a="Sen'jin Village uses tiger pelts for tents, blankets and armor. As the population grows, the village stores have come under strain.",al={"why tiger pelts","practical prey purpose","what are furs used for"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the Durotar tigers found?",a="Durotar's tigers roam the Echo Isles, just off the region's southeastern coast.",al={"where are the tigers","tiger location","echo isles tigers"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why don't the trolls hunt all the tigers nearby?",a="The Darkspear leave the tigers alone until they need more supplies. They take only what the tribe needs, allowing the predators to thrive.",al={"why let tigers thrive","culling the flock"}},{q="Is hunting tigers significant to Darkspear culture?",a="Yes. The Darkspear see tiger hunting as a test of patience and cunning. Vel'rin once waited nearly a day in the Echo Isles before claiming his first great hunting victory.",al={"tiger hunt tradition","first tiger hunt"}},{q="Why must hunters travel to the Echo Isles if Zalazane holds them?",a="Zalazane and his hexed minions hold much of the Echo Isles, but wild beasts remain plentiful. Hunting and scavenging along the outer shores still bring risks the Darkspear must take.",al={"tigers on echo isles","why go to echo isles"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the Durotar Tiger Fur used for?",a="The Darkspear craft the furs into essential goods to shelter and sustain their growing settlement. Vel'rin Fang uses the pelts to fashion sturdy leather armor, warm blankets, and weather-resistant tents, ensuring the villagers in Sen'jin Village remain protected and do not freeze as the seasons turn.",al={"durotar tiger fur use","what is tiger fur for","tiger fur practical prey"},it="item",add="b158745d"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you hunt across the Echo Isles and provide for your clan. The islands remind you bitterly of the home Zalazane took from your people.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know patience and precision matter. Vel'rin once tracked his prey in silence for a full day before springing his trap.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help supply the young Darkspear enclave and anchor the Horde's southern flank along the Great Sea."},kw={"darkspear","durotar tiger","echo isles","hunting","leatherworking","practical prey","sen'jin village","tiger fur","vel'rin fang"},rel={"subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:echo-isles","zone:durotar","quest:808","subzone:razor-hill"},m={start="Vel'rin Fang",level="8",faction="Horde",id=817,ri={"Durotar Tiger Fur"}},src={"Practical Prey"}}
E["quest:818"] = {t="quest",n="A Solvent Spirit",z="durotar",s="In Sen'jin Village, Master Vornal tests those who seek his teaching as his sight fades. He sends them to Durotar's coast for makrura eyes and crawler mucus, measuring their patience and resolve.",h="In Sen'jin Village, Master Vornal tests those who seek his teaching as his sight fades.",sec={{t="A Master's Fading Sight",b="Master Vornal lives in Sen'jin Village, where age has dimmed his sight. Primal magic once came easily to him, but now he relies on alchemy to sharpen his perceptions and weave his arts. His body weakens, yet the stubborn troll refuses an apprentice. He says neither the Darkspear nor Durotar's orcs have produced anyone worthy of his teaching.",sp=0},{t="Testing the Unproven",b="Vornal asks for raw materials from Durotar's harsh coast: intact makrura eyes and vials of crawler mucus. Taking undamaged eyes from armored, snapping makrura calls for careful strikes. Gathering enough mucus tests whether a would-be pupil can endure tedious work. For Vornal, the hunt is less about reagents than learning who can keep their focus.",sp=0},{t="A Measure of Will",b="For Master Vornal, time and patience measure strength. He expects brash youths to grow frustrated or abandon the work. Pristine ingredients brought back to Sen'jin Village show survival skills along the dangerous reefs of the Echo Isles channel. They also show the discipline needed to master alchemy's subtle arts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Master Vornal?",a="Master Vornal is an elderly troll alchemist and spellcaster who lives in Sen'jin Village. Age has dimmed his eyesight, so he uses alchemical solvents and brews to work magic that once came easily.",al={"master vornal","who is vornal","vornal lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Vornal need makrura eyes and crawler mucus?",a="Vornal uses alchemical mixtures to aid his magic and make up for his failing eyesight. He needs crawler mucus and intact makrura eyes as reagents, and gathering them tests those who seek his teaching.",al={"why crawler mucus","why makrura eyes","what does vornal make"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is Vornal so reluctant to teach an apprentice?",a="Vornal expects great dedication and patience, and has little tolerance for arrogance. He believes no troll or orc has shown the devotion he requires, and sees most would-be pupils as proud and easily discouraged.",al={"vornal apprentice","why no apprentice","is vornal looking for a student"},it="motive"},{q="Where are these creatures found around Sen'jin Village?",a="Crawlers and makrura roam the shallows along Darkspear Strand and the waterways between the mainland and the nearby Echo Isles.",al={"where are makrura","where are crawlers","darkspear strand beasts"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the makrura eyes need to be intact?",a="Vornal needs undamaged sensory organs for brews that sharpen perception. A forceful strike can crush a makrura's delicate eyes, so the hunter must act with precision and restraint.",al={"intact eye","makrura intact eyes","why intact eyes"},it="item"},{q="What lesson is Vornal trying to teach?",a="Vornal believes patience tests character. Repetitive, dirty gathering along the surf shows whether a novice gives in to haste or keeps an alchemist's calm focus.",al={"vornal lesson","meaning of the quest","patience test"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Master Vornal need an adventurer rather than gathering the reagents himself?",a="Master Vornal admits his eyesight is failing him with age, making dangerous fieldwork along the coast ill-advised. More importantly, he uses the chore as a deliberate test. Vornal has long refused to take on an apprentice, believing no troll or orc worthy has crossed his path. By sending you to harvest delicate reagents from hostile coastal wildlife, he measures your patience, strength, and will to see if your deeds match your confidence.",al={"why me vornal","why does vornal need me","why send an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="4926ebef"},{q="What are the makrura and surf crawlers threatening the Durotar coast?",a="Makrura are aggressive, crustacean humanoids native to the waters and shores of Durotar, while surf crawlers are wild, territorial crabs scuttling along the beaches and shallows near the Echo Isles. Both inhabit the waters off the Darkspear Strand, making the coast perilous for local fishers and gathering. For Master Vornal, however, they are valuable sources of specialized alchemical reagents needed to compensate for his failing senses.",al={"what are makrura","makrura durotar","surf crawlers senjin"},it="target",add="cab96330"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear rebuilding at Sen'jin Village, proving yourself to elder practitioners like Master Vornal helps carry the tribe's mystical and alchemical traditions forward.",["race:Orc"]="Vornal openly doubts that orcs have the quiet discipline alchemy demands. This work gives you a chance to show that Horde solidarity includes scholarly patience.",["faction:Horde"]="Coastal Durotar remains perilous for the fledgling Horde. Clearing aggressive makrura and surf crawlers helps secure the fishing shores around Sen'jin Village."},kw={"alchemy","crawler mucus","darkspear strand","durotar","intact makrura eye","makrura","master vornal","sen'jin village"},rel={"npc:master-vornal","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:darkspear-strand","subzone:echo-isles","zone:durotar","topic:troll","quest:99141"},m={start="Master Vornal",level="7",faction="Horde",id=818},src={"A Solvent Spirit"}}
E["quest:823"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Orgnil",z="durotar",s="Master Gadrin sends a warning from Sen'jin Village to Razor Hill about the Burning Blade. Demonic corruption is spreading through Durotar.",h="Master Gadrin sends a warning from Sen'jin Village to Razor Hill about the Burning Blade.",sec={{t="A Coordinated Defense",b="Sen'jin Village has troubles of its own, especially Zalazane's treachery on the Echo Isles. Yet the Burning Blade threatens more than the village. Demonic corruption has been uncovered in the Valley of Trials, and Master Gadrin knows the danger cannot be faced alone. So he sends you north along the road to Razor Hill, where orc authorities watch over Durotar.",sp=0},{t="Orgnil Soulscar",b="Orgnil Soulscar is at Razor Hill's military encampment, charged with rooting out evils in Durotar and guarding its central lands. When you bring Gadrin's warning, Orgnil joins the reports from Sen'jin Village and the Valley of Trials. The Burning Blade is dangerously close. He quickly gathers forces to break up the cultists before their rituals can unseat the young nation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Report to Orgnil?",a="Master Gadrin, the Darkspear witch doctor and spiritual leader in Sen'jin Village, sends you after you help the trolls with their first local troubles.",al={"who gives report to orgnil","where to get report to orgnil","quest giver report to orgnil"},gp=true},{q="Where is Orgnil Soulscar located?",a="Orgnil Soulscar is at Razor Hill, the fortified settlement north of Sen'jin Village in central Durotar.",al={"where is orgnil soulscar","orgnil soulscar location","find orgnil soulscar"},gp=true},{q="Why does Master Gadrin send you to Razor Hill?",a="Master Gadrin sees that demonic cult activity in the Valley of Trials and around Durotar threatens everyone, not only the trolls. He sends you to Orgnil Soulscar, the orc charged with guarding the region against the Burning Blade.",al={"why report to orgnil","why go to razor hill","purpose of report to orgnil"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Burning Blade mentioned in the quest?",a="The Burning Blade is a covert cult of demon worshippers working in Durotar's shadows and beyond. Its hidden presence in nearby canyons and caves threatens the young Horde's safety and stability.",al={"who are the burning blade","burning blade cult","what is burning blade"},it="threat"},{q="What quest follows Report to Orgnil?",a="After you deliver the report to Orgnil Soulscar at Razor Hill, he gives you Dark Storms. He sends you to investigate and fight the gathering cultist threat.",al={"next quest after report to orgnil","report to orgnil followup","what comes after report to orgnil"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What prerequisite must be completed before receiving this quest?",a="This follows your arrival in Sen'jin Village through Report to Sen'jin Village. It links what you found in the Valley of Trials to the wider Durotar campaign.",al={"prereq report to orgnil","how to unlock report to orgnil","previous quest report to orgnil"},gp=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you depend on cooperation between the newly allied Darkspear trolls and Durotar's orcs as they face shared threats.",["race:Troll"]="The Darkspear are caught up in their fight against Zalazane. Master Gadrin still shows the trolls' commitment to the Horde by warning orc leaders of dangers across the region.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you can look to Orgnil Soulscar as a defender of your homeland. He works to keep demonic corruption from taking root in Durotar."},kw={"burning blade","durotar","master gadrin","orgnil soulscar","razor hill","report to orgnil","sen'jin village"},rel={"npc:master-gadrin","npc:orgnil-soulscar","subzone:razor-hill","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","subzone:valley-of-trials"},m={start="Master Gadrin",["end"]="Orgnil Soulscar",level="7",faction="Horde",id=823},src={"Report to Orgnil"}}
E["quest:825"] = {t="quest",n="From The Wreckage....",z="durotar",s="Gar'Thok sends Horde scouts to the Scuttle Coast wrecks to recover Gnomish Tools. The Horde hopes to study Alliance engineering and put that knowledge to use.",h="Gar'Thok sends Horde scouts to the Scuttle Coast wrecks to recover Gnomish Tools.",sec={{t="Echoes of the Fleet",b="Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore brought Kul Tiras's fleet to Kalimdor. Its ships crowded the shore near Tiragarde Keep. After his defeat, broken hulls sank along the Scuttle Coast. The surviving Kul Tiran soldiers fortify the keep, while the wrecks lie scattered on the shoals beneath the tide.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Contraptions",b="Alliance ingenuity can give its enemies an edge over orcish strength, iron, and blood. Gnomish technicians sailed with the expeditionary fleet and fitted its ships with complex machinery and precise tools. Gar'Thok wants the Horde to recover those tools from the wrecks. Then its craftspeople can learn how they work.",sp=0},{t="Destined for Orgrimmar",b="Gar'Thok sends the salvaged tools by caravan from Razor Hill to Orgrimmar. There, Horde craftspeople and tacticians hope to study the gnomish instruments. They seek ways to counter Alliance devices in future conflicts and strengthen their own industries.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Horde salvaging tools from these wrecks?",a="The Horde wants to understand the Alliance's advanced technology. Gnomes make intricate machinery for human forces. Studying their tools may show Horde tacticians how to counter Alliance devices and adapt useful designs for their own craftspeople.",al={"why get gnomish tools","why salvage wreck","gar'thok reason for tools"},it="motive"},{q="Whose ships are wrecked off the Scuttle Coast?",a="The wrecked ships belonged to Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's Kul Tiras fleet. After landing in Durotar to fight Thrall's newly founded nation, several ships were destroyed along the coast just east of Tiragarde Keep.",al={"whose ships are these","who wrecked ships durotar","proudmoore fleet wreckage"},it="origin"},{q="Where do the recovered tools go after Razor Hill?",a="Gar'Thok sends the recovered Gnomish Tools by caravan from Razor Hill to Orgrimmar. Engineers and craftspeople there can study them to strengthen the capital's defenses and industry.",al={"what happens to tools","where do gnomish tools go","who gets the salvage"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are gnomish tools found on human warships?",a="Gnomes are close allies of the humans in the Grand Alliance. They often bring mechanical skill, siege gear, and precision tools to keep human warships working.",al={"why gnomes with humans","gnomes on proudmoore ships","alliance gnomish tech"},it="item"},{q="What is the Scuttle Coast?",a="The Scuttle Coast is Durotar's eastern shore, running past Tiragarde Keep. Its shallow waters hold half-submerged and sunken ships left after the battles against Proudmoore's expedition.",al={"where is scuttle coast","scuttle coast location","durotar sunken ships area"},it="place"},{q="How does this task relate to the threat at Tiragarde Keep?",a="After the assault on Tiragarde Keep clears out Kul Tiran marines, Gar'Thok seizes the chance to claim the remaining Alliance resources. The Horde can profit from the defeat by stripping nearby wrecks before scavengers or the tide take everything.",al={"tiragarde keep connection","vanquish the betrayers link","why do this after tiragarde"},it="conflict"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As a tinker, you can see in the Gnomish Tools the early clash between Alliance mechanical precision and the Horde's growing craft industries.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Gar'Thok sees Alliance metal as knowledge for defeating future invasions and material for building Durotar.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you leave your mark wherever the Alliance sails. The Horde respects your sophisticated gear enough to send scouts to recover it."},kw={"durotar","gar'thok","gnomish tools","proudmoore","razor hill","salvage","scuttle coast","tiragarde keep","wreckage"},rel={"npc:gar-thok","quest:784","subzone:scuttle-coast","subzone:tiragarde-keep","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","topic:gnome"},m={start="Gar'Thok",level="8",faction="Horde",id=825,ri={"Gnomish Tools"}},src={"From The Wreckage...."}}
E["quest:826"] = {t="quest",n="Zalazane",z="durotar",s="On the Echo Isles, dark magic has driven Zalazane mad and turned him against his tribe. Master Gadrin of Sen'jin Village calls Horde champions to end the witch doctor's rule. Zalazane enslaved his fellow tribesmen, seized the Darkspear trolls' rightful home, and drove them into exile on Durotar's coast.",h="On the Echo Isles, dark magic has driven Zalazane mad and turned him against his tribe.",sec={{t="Betrayal on the Isles",b="After fleeing their sunken island, the Darkspear followed Thrall across the Great Sea and settled on the Echo Isles, just off Durotar's southeast coast. Zalazane was once a respected and powerful witch doctor, but he hungered for power. His hexes enslaved the minds of his kin, and violence followed. Vol'jin led those who remained free, yet they were driven from their ancestral camps and forced to build a temporary refuge at Sen'jin Village.",sp=0},{t="A Tribe's Torment",b="From his hilltop stronghold on the largest Echo Isle, Zalazane still sends raiding parties across the channel. They seize more Darkspear and bring them under his control. The captured trolls become mindless voodoo and hexed thralls, lost to their tribe. Master Gadrin sees a threat to more than Darkspear land: Zalazane endangers the tribe's survival. Until his severed head is brought before the elders, no Darkspear can be safe.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zalazane?",a="Zalazane was once a prominent witch doctor among the Darkspear trolls. Hunger for dark power corrupted him, and he turned on his kin, using mind-controlling voodoo to enslave them and seize the Echo Isles.",al={"zalazane lore","who is the boss on echo isles","witch doctor zalazane"},it="target"},{q="Why did the Darkspear flee the Echo Isles?",a="The Darkspear fled after Zalazane staged a surprise coup on the islands and used sorcery to turn their kin into mindless thralls. Vol'jin and the free Darkspear were too few to face their enchanted kin, so they retreated to mainland Durotar and founded Sen'jin Village as a temporary refuge.",al={"why are trolls in sen'jin village","echo isles backstory","how did trolls lose echo isles"},it="history"},{q="What happens to the trolls under Zalazane's control?",a="Hexes have robbed the trolls under Zalazane's control of their minds. They serve him, patrol the islands, and raid the mainland to capture more victims. Master Gadrin considers them lost to the tribe, with execution their only mercy.",al={"hexed trolls","voodoo trolls","can zalazane's thralls be cured"},it="threat"},{q="Where is Zalazane located?",a="Zalazane makes his lair on the largest Echo Isle, just east of Durotar's southern coast. He patrols from the high summit of its central hill down to the cluster of troll huts beneath it.",al={"zalazane location","find zalazane","where is zalazane"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who gives the quest to kill Zalazane?",a="Master Gadrin, a tribal elder in Sen'jin Village on Durotar's southern shore, asks you to kill Zalazane. You meet him after handling local threats and arriving from the Valley of Trials.",al={"who starts zalazane","where to get zalazane quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Vol'jin not lead the assault himself?",a="Vol'jin rules the tribe and coordinates the Darkspear's defense alongside Warchief Thrall in Orgrimmar. In Sen'jin Village, elders such as Master Gadrin guide local survival, and Gadrin enlists capable adventurers to strike back at Zalazane.",al={"where is vol'jin","why isn't vol'jin fighting zalazane"},it="leader"},{q="Why does Master Gadrin want Zalazane killed?",a="Zalazane is not content with stealing the Echo Isles; he continually dispatches his enthralled trolls across the water to raid the mainland, enslaving more Darkspear to bolster his ranks. Master Gadrin knows that Sen'jin Village will never be safe as long as the rogue witch doctor lives to torment and abduct their people.",al={"gadrin zalazane why","why kill zalazane","why does master gadrin want this"},it="motive",add="ae6e25c2"},{q="What is Zalazane's Head for?",a="Master Gadrin demands Zalazane's severed head as undeniable proof of the witch doctor's demise. Only by seeing the head with his own eyes can Gadrin be certain that Zalazane's dark influence is broken and that the Darkspear tribe can finally sleep in peace.",al={"zalazanes head purpose","why bring zalazanes head","zalazane head quest item"},it="item",add="a3c2387d"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you have a personal duty to punish the betrayer who stole your people's home and enslaved your kin.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help defend the displaced Darkspear. Allies from across Durotar rally to their cause in one of the young Horde's first major tests of unity.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you know the spiritual crafts and primal powers practiced by troll shamans and witch doctors. Zalazane twists binding magic against his own kin."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","echo isles","hexed troll","master gadrin","sen'jin village","vol'jin","voodoo troll","zalazane"},rel={"npc:master-gadrin","subzone:echo-isles","subzone:sen-jin-village","quest:808","topic:darkspear-tribe","npc:vol-jin","zone:durotar","quest:817"},m={start="Master Gadrin",level="10",faction="Horde",id=826,ri={"Zalazane's Head"}},src={"Zalazane (quest)"}}
E["quest:827"] = {t="quest",n="Skull Rock",z="durotar",s="Margoz sends you east of Orgrimmar, where Burning Blade cultists hold Skull Rock. They bind themselves to dark magic with painful demonic devices. Margoz needs the cursed artifacts to study the cult near the capital.",h="Margoz sends you east of Orgrimmar, where Burning Blade cultists hold Skull Rock.",sec={{t="A Den of Shadows",b="In northeastern Durotar, Burning Blade cultists gather close to Orgrimmar's gates. Their cave lies among the hills, away from the open roads but near the Warchief's seat. The cult has long plagued orcish society, and now its followers perform rituals in the tunnels. Nearby, the Warchief's scouts keep watch.",sp=0},{t="Demonic Attunement",b="Burning Blade cultists wear Searing Collars around their necks. The metal bands scorch and brand their flesh. Margoz believes the pain and fel sorcery attune their wearers to demonic power. He asks you to recover the collars so he can study the spells and bindings that empower them.",sp=0},{t="The Looming Threat",b="The Searing Collars reveal how the Burning Blade has organized itself in Durotar. Its sorcery threatens the Horde's newly established territories. Margoz studies the collars, then pursues further inquiries among Orgrimmar's hidden circles.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Skull Rock located?",a="Skull Rock lies in northeastern Durotar, east of Orgrimmar and north of Sen'jin Village. Its entrance sits in a craggy cliffside along the shore.",al={"skull rock location","where is skull rock","skull rock cave durotar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is the Burning Blade?",a="The Burning Blade is a cult of orcs and fel-worshipers devoted to demons and dark magic. The modern Horde broke from demonic servitude, but splinter groups like the Burning Blade still practice forbidden rites and seek to corrupt the Horde from the shadows.",al={"what is burning blade","who are burning blade cultists","burning blade lore"},it="threat"},{q="What do the cultists use the Searing Collars for?",a="Cultists wear Searing Collars around their necks, where the fiery metal burns their flesh. Margoz suspects the pain and demonic enchantment help them channel and attune themselves to dark fel energies.",al={"searing collars purpose","why wear searing collars","what are searing collars"},it="item"},{q="Who is Margoz?",a="Margoz is an orcish hermit who lives in a small camp atop Durotar's bluffs, near Skull Rock. He watches cultist movements along the coast and works to dismantle the Burning Blade's operations.",al={"who is margoz","margoz durotar","margoz questgiver"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the Horde allow the cult so close to Orgrimmar?",a="The Horde does not knowingly tolerate the cult near Orgrimmar. Burning Blade followers hide in caves and desolate ravines beyond regular patrols, and adventurers investigate when the cult's rituals reveal its footholds.",al={"why is skull rock near orgrimmar","orgrimmar burning blade nearby"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after Margoz examines the collars?",a="Margoz plans to examine the Searing Collars. His investigation continues with Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar.",al={"next quest after skull rock","where do collars lead","margoz spell"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Margoz want the Searing Collars?",a="Margoz believes that by burning their flesh with these collars, the cultists attune themselves to demonic forces. He needs a collection of intact collars to study and inspect with his magic, hoping to uncover the dark secrets behind the Burning Blade and expose how deep their demonic corruption runs.",al={"why does margoz need collars","margoz searing collars motive","why collect searing collars"},it="motive",add="cfe1a49d"},{q="Who are you sent against in Skull Rock?",a="You are dispatched against the cultists of the Burning Blade hiding inside Skull Rock, a cavern east of Orgrimmar. They have gathered there beneath the Horde's nose to perform vile rituals, bind themselves to demonic masters, and plot against the safety of Durotar.",al={"who is in skull rock","skull rock enemies","burning blade cultists skull rock"},it="target",add="50396613"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you face the Burning Blade as a remnant of your people's dark past. Driving the cult from Durotar's rocks is a matter of survival and honor.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can see how Searing Collars bind their wearers with fel magic. Their crude enchantments show how the cult turns demonic sacrifice into power.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face a demonic cult entrenched just beyond Orgrimmar's walls. It threatens the heart and security of your people."},kw={"burning blade","cultists","demonic","durotar","fel","margoz","orgrimmar","searing collar","skull rock"},rel={"quest:828","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Margoz",level="12",faction="Horde",id=827,ri={"Searing Collar"}},src={"Skull Rock (Classic)"}}
E["quest:828"] = {t="quest",n="Margoz",z="durotar",s="In northern Durotar, Margoz keeps watch for the Burning Blade's growing threat. After the clash with fel corruption at Thunder Ridge, Orgnil Soulscar sends champions to seek the shaman at his lonely camp before they strike a nearby cultist stronghold. Margoz's counsel reveals Skull Rock as the Burning Blade's concealed cavern base.",h="In northern Durotar, Margoz keeps watch for the Burning Blade's growing threat.",sec={{t="A Hermit's Vigil",b="After Thunder Ridge revealed the depth of fel taint, Orgnil Soulscar sees that strength alone cannot cleanse Durotar. So he sends champions to Margoz, an experienced orc shaman at a lonely camp in the crags northeast of Razor Hill. Between Drygulch Ravine and the eastern sea, Margoz watches the northern reaches for dark omens that Orgrimmar's busy warriors often miss.",sp=0},{t="The Threat of Skull Rock",b="Margoz knows where the Burning Blade has built its power in northern Durotar: Skull Rock, a concealed cavern system carved into the mountain cliffs outside Orgrimmar's southern gates. The cultists are closer to Thrall's capital than the Warchief's guards realize. Hidden passages there could shelter a demonic ambush, so Margoz gives counsel to those sent against the coven before they enter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Margoz?",a="Margoz is an experienced orc shaman loyal to the Horde, keeping a lonely camp in northeastern Durotar. He studies dark magic and watches the demonic corruption spreading through the region.",al={"margoz lore","who is margoz","margoz npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I find Margoz?",a="You can find Margoz at his camp in the rugged hills of northeastern Durotar, between Drygulch Ravine and the eastern coastline, southeast of Orgrimmar.",al={"margoz location","find margoz","where is margoz"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Orgnil Soulscar send me to Margoz?",a="Orgnil Soulscar sends you to Margoz because the shaman has studied the local Burning Blade cultists. Before you assault their stronghold, Orgnil wants you to hear Margoz's spiritual wisdom and practical counsel.",al={"why speak with margoz","orgnil soulscar margoz"},it="motive"},{q="What is Skull Rock?",a="Skull Rock is a concealed system of mountain caves just south of Orgrimmar's eastern walls. There, Burning Blade cultists worship demons and conduct rituals close to the Horde's capital.",al={"skull rock lore","what is skull rock"},it="place"},{q="What happens after finding Margoz?",a="When you report to Margoz, he acknowledges your growing strength and sends you into Skull Rock to slay the cultists and recover their corrupted insignia.",al={"next quest after margoz","margoz follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Is Margoz part of the Burning Blade?",a="No. Margoz is a devoted Horde shaman who works to purge demonic influence and guide young champions along an honorable, uncorrupted path.",al={"is margoz evil","is margoz a cultist"},it="side"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can see Margoz's patient wisdom in his watch along the wilderness margins. He senses spiritual corruption before it becomes war.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you hear Margoz's warning: demon cults lurk within striking distance of Orgrimmar.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, meeting Margoz reminds you that fel power still tempts your people. He urges the new generation toward a pure, honorable path."},kw={"burning blade","drygulch ravine","durotar","margoz","orgnil soulscar","orgrimmar","shaman","skull rock"},rel={"npc:orgnil-soulscar","quest:827","zone:durotar","subzone:drygulch-ravine","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Orgnil Soulscar",["end"]="Margoz",level="12",faction="Horde",id=828},src={"Margoz (Classic)"}}
E["quest:829"] = {t="quest",n="Neeru Fireblade",z="durotar",s="In Orgrimmar, Neeru Fireblade studies dark arts he claims can guard the Horde. Margoz sends you from Durotar with a Searing Collar taken from the Burning Blade, hoping the warlock can explain its demonic power.",h="In Orgrimmar, Neeru Fireblade studies dark arts he claims can guard the Horde.",sec={{t="A Shaman's Limits",b="Margoz has reached the edge of shamanic craft. The collars taken from Burning Blade cultists at Skull Rock bear demonic sorcery he cannot unravel. Shamans draw on the elements and ancestral spirits. So Margoz sends you to a warlock in the capital to learn what the collars do.",sp=0},{t="Into the Cleft of Shadow",b="Beneath Orgrimmar's red cliffs lies the Cleft of Shadow. Warlocks and other practitioners of forbidden magic work there beneath Thrall's wary eye. Neeru Fireblade lives in the cavern and says he studies fel power to thwart demonic threats. When you bring him the collar, his curiosity turns Durotar's investigation toward the warlock enclave.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Margoz send me to a warlock?",a="Margoz is a shaman who draws power from the elements and ancestral spirits. The Searing Collars from Skull Rock carry demonic magic, so he needs someone trained in fel magic and the dark arts to understand their enchantments and origins.",al={"why warlock","why neeru","margoz warlock"},it="motive"},{q="Where can I find Neeru Fireblade?",a="You can find Neeru Fireblade in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar, where warlocks, rogues, and shadow casters gather.",al={"neeru location","where is neeru fireblade","cleft of shadow neeru"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Can Neeru Fireblade be trusted?",a="Margoz doubts Neeru's claim that his occult research is benign and meant to fight demons. Thrall permits warlocks in Orgrimmar under strict watch, but whether Neeru can be trusted remains uncertain.",al={"is neeru evil","neeru trustworthy","can i trust fireblade"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Example Collar?",a="The Example Collar is one of the Searing Collars taken from Burning Blade cultists at Skull Rock. Margoz gives it to you to bring to Neeru Fireblade for magical study.",al={"example collar","what is the collar","searing collar quest item"},it="item"},{q="What happens after giving the collar to Neeru?",a="Neeru examines the collar closely and sends you deeper into the investigation of the cult's presence in Durotar. The search turns toward Ak'Zeloth.",al={"next quest after neeru","what does neeru do","quest chain after neeru"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does the Horde allow warlocks in Orgrimmar?",a="Thrall allows warlocks in Orgrimmar out of practical need. He keeps them in the Cleft of Shadow, where their dangerous research can be watched, controlled, and sometimes used to understand demonic enemies.",al={"why are warlocks allowed","warlocks in cleft of shadow","thrall warlocks"},it="history"},{q="Why does Margoz send you instead of going himself?",a="Margoz remains stationed outside Razor Hill keeping watch over Durotar's spiritual unrest. You are the adventurer who recovered the Searing Collars from Skull Rock in the first place, proving your capability in dealing with the cult's dark artifacts. Because he cannot divine their demonic workings through shamanism alone, he relies on you to carry a sample swiftly to the Cleft of Shadow.",al={"why me margoz","why send me to neeru","why doesn't margoz go to orgrimmar"},it="why_me",add="273c9fa7"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you know the elements will not answer fel artifacts. Margoz has reached the bounds of his craft and needs a warlock's help.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you meet Neeru Fireblade in the Cleft of Shadow, Orgrimmar's most prominent warlock. Your forbidden craft can serve the Horde.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see a fragile truce in Orgrimmar. The Warchief's shamans sometimes rely on the shadowy outcasts of the Cleft of Shadow to protect Durotar."},kw={"burning blade","cleft of shadow","durotar","margoz","neeru fireblade","orgrimmar","searing collar","skull rock","warlock"},rel={"quest:827","quest:828","quest:809","quest:924","quest:806","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:orgrimmar","zone:durotar"},m={start="Margoz",["end"]="Neeru Fireblade",level="12",faction="Horde",id=829},src={"Neeru Fireblade (quest)"}}
E["quest:830"] = {t="quest",n="The Admiral's Orders",z="durotar",s="On Durotar’s coast, the Admiral’s Orders carry word of a threat to the young Horde. Sealed by the late Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore, they show that the Kul Tiran garrison is organized and entrenched. Gar'Thok in Razor Hill needs to know what they contain.",h="On Durotar’s coast, the Admiral’s Orders carry word of a threat to the young Horde.",sec={{t="A Sealed Legacy",b="On the upper floors of Tiragarde Keep, a heavy chest holds an aged envelope under Lieutenant Benedict’s watch. Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore sealed it with his crest. Its parchment gives naval commands from Kul Tiras’s bloody invasion of Durotar. Though the Grand Admiral fell at Theramore, his officers still hold their fortifications and cling to their mission against the Horde settlement.",sp=0},{t="Alarm in Razor Hill",b="Gar'Thok commands Razor Hill’s local defense force. When you bring him the recovered papers, they confirm that the Kul Tiran soldiers on the eastern shore are an established force awaiting reinforcements. They are no mere castaways. Gar'Thok sees that Durotar’s survival depends on breaking Tiragarde’s command structure.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where are the Admiral's Orders found?",a="The orders lie in an aged envelope inside a locked chest on Tiragarde Keep’s third floor. Lieutenant Benedict guards the second floor and carries the key.",al={"orders location","where is aged envelope","find admirals orders"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who was Admiral Proudmoore?",a="Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore ruled Kul Tiras and commanded the Alliance naval fleet during the Second War. He refused to believe orcs could live in peace, so he sailed to Kalimdor to wage a war of extermination against Durotar. He died at Theramore.",al={"who is the admiral","daelin proudmoore lore","who issued orders"},it="identity"},{q="Why are Kul Tiran soldiers still in Tiragarde Keep?",a="Daelin Proudmoore built fortified coastal footholds such as Tiragarde Keep during his invasion of Durotar. After his defeat, surviving officers and marines under Lieutenant Benedict held their posts and continued his campaign against the Horde.",al={"why are humans in durotar","tiragarde keep soldiers","kul tiras in durotar"},it="why_here"},{q="Why is Gar'Thok so concerned about these orders?",a="Gar'Thok commands Razor Hill and guards central Durotar. The orders show that Tiragarde Keep is an active, deliberate military threat to the orcish homeland, not a band of stranded survivors.",al={"gar'thok reaction","why does garthok care"},it="danger"},{q="Who holds the key to the Admiral's chest?",a="Lieutenant Benedict, the Kul Tiran officer commanding on Tiragarde Keep’s second floor, carries the key to the strongbox with the aged envelope.",al={"benedict key","who drops key"},it="in_charge",gp=true},{q="What happens after giving the orders to Gar'Thok?",a="Gar'Thok sees that Proudmoore’s plans were made before his death, and more of his men may land on Durotar’s shores. He sends the orders to Orgrimmar at once, so the Warchief’s council can be warned.",al={"admirals orders follow up","next quest"},it="next_step"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Proudmoore’s orders show that the Alliance presence on Durotar’s shores was an organized campaign of extermination. The Horde must defend its new home with care.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs building a future in Durotar, these papers recall Daelin Proudmoore’s hatred and the remnants who still seek their destruction."},kw={"admirals orders","aged envelope","daelin proudmoore","gar'thok","kul tiras","lieutenant benedict","razor hill","tiragarde keep"},rel={"npc:gar-thok","subzone:tiragarde-keep","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar"},m={start="Aged Envelope",["end"]="Gar'Thok",level="7",faction="Horde",id=830},src={"The Admiral's Orders"}}
E["quest:831"] = {t="quest",n="The Admiral's Orders",z="durotar",s="Gar'Thok sends you to carry Admiral Proudmoore's Orders to Nazgrel in Orgrimmar. The orders raise fears of another human landing on Horde shores.",h="Gar'Thok sends you to carry Admiral Proudmoore's Orders to Nazgrel in Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Warning for Nazgrel",b="Gar'Thok in Durotar fears that Admiral Proudmoore's plans still threaten the Horde. He sends you with the admiral's orders to Nazgrel in Thrall's chamber in Orgrimmar.",sp=0},{t="In Thrall's Chamber",b="Nazgrel receives the orders and says the Warchief must hear of the matter at once. He thanks you for serving the Horde honorably, then turns to counsel Thrall.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends me to Orgrimmar?",a="Gar'Thok sends you from Durotar to deliver Admiral Proudmoore's Orders to Nazgrel.",al={"who gave me this","Gar'Thok orders"}},{q="Who should receive the orders?",a="Nazgrel is to receive Admiral Proudmoore's Orders in Thrall's chamber in Orgrimmar.",al={"deliver to who","Nazgrel orders"}},{q="Why are the orders urgent?",a="Gar'Thok fears that Admiral Proudmoore's plans may bring more of his men to Horde shores.",al={"why urgent","human threat"}},{q="What does Nazgrel do with the warning?",a="Nazgrel says he must counsel Thrall about the matter.",al={"what does Nazgrel do","counsel Thrall"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you carry a warning that Gar'Thok believes concerns the safety of Horde shores."},kw={"admiral proudmoore","gar'thok","horde","human landing","nazgrel","orders","orgrimmar","thrall"},rel={"quest:830","item:admiral-proudmoore-s-orders","npc:gar-thok","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","topic:horde","npc:thrall"},m={start="Gar'Thok",["end"]="Nazgrel",level="7",faction="Horde",id=831},src={"Classic quest text: The Admiral's Orders","In-game quest text: The Admiral's Orders"}}
E["quest:832"] = {t="quest",n="Burning Shadows",z="durotar",s="In Skull Rock, the Eye of Burning Shadow carries warnings from the Burning Blade. Its voice threatens Gazz'uz with Neeru Fireblade's wrath.",h="In Skull Rock, the Eye of Burning Shadow carries warnings from the Burning Blade.",sec={{t="A Voice in the Stone",b="After Gazz'uz falls deep within Skull Rock, the Eye of Burning Shadow is found among his remains. The stone carries a voice into the mind of anyone who holds it. The speaker demands a report from Gazz'uz. His secret work east of Orgrimmar has been compromised.",sp=0},{t="A Curious Threat",b="The voice gives Gazz'uz an ultimatum. Answer, or Neeru Fireblade will be told to hunt him down with swift brutality. Neeru lives openly in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, where he practices dark arts under Thrall's strict oversight. When the pendant reaches him, the warlock feigns surprise and wonders why the cult used his name to frighten Gazz'uz.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Eye of Burning Shadow?",a="The Eye of Burning Shadow is an enchanted pendant found among the Burning Blade leader Gazz'uz's remains inside Skull Rock. It carries two-way telepathic messages between cult operatives and their unseen masters.",al={"eye of burning shadow","what is this pendant","gazz'uz eye"},it="item"},{q="Who is speaking through the pendant?",a="An unidentified superior in the Shadow Council or Burning Blade hierarchy is trying to contact Gazz'uz, unaware he has already been slain in Skull Rock.",al={"who spoke to me","voice in the pendant","who talks through eye"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the voice threaten Gazz'uz with Neeru Fireblade?",a="The voice says Neeru Fireblade will come after Gazz'uz with brutal force if he fails to report. Neeru says he is known for hunting the Warchief's enemies, though he finds it strange that the voice singled him out.",al={"why mention neeru","neeru fireblade threat","neeru connection"},it="purpose"},{q="Where do I take the Eye of Burning Shadow?",a="Take the pendant to Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, where he hovers over cauldrons and tomes.",al={"where to turn in burning shadows","where is neeru fireblade"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="How does Neeru Fireblade react when given the eye?",a="Neeru is intrigued that the voice singled out his name, and finds it stranger still that the Burning Blade cultists bear a name so close to his own. He keeps the pendant to study it and ponder its message.",al={"neeru reaction","what does neeru say"},sp=1},{q="Where is Gazz'uz located?",a="Gazz'uz lurks at the deepest point of Skull Rock, a cavern hidden among the crags on Durotar's eastern coastline, just east of Orgrimmar.",al={"where is gazz'uz","gazz'uz location","skull rock boss"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does the voice in the Eye of Burning Shadow want a report?",a="The voice whispering through the pendant is trying to contact Gazz'uz, a Burning Blade leader in Skull Rock. News has reached the cult hierarchy that their hidden enclave has been discovered by the Horde, and the unseen commander urgently seeks to rally Gazz'uz to prepare defenses before an inevitable assault wipes out their foothold.",al={"why does the pendant speak","why eye of burning shadow report","eye of burning shadow voice motive"},it="motive",add="286b7c01"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock training in the Cleft of Shadow, you hear the Burning Blade invoke another practitioner's name. The threat shows how thin the line is between state-sanctioned fel study and open treason.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you uncover whispers between cultists just outside the capital's gates. The demonic corruption of the Old Horde still festers uncomfortably close to Durotar's heart.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know the Burning Blade's presence in Durotar desecrates your new homeland. Orcs fought alongside Thrall to purge the Legion's taint."},kw={"burning blade","burning shadows","cleft of shadow","durotar","eye of burning shadow","gazz'uz","neeru fireblade","orgrimmar","skull rock"},rel={"quest:827","quest:829","zone:durotar"},m={start="Eye of Burning Shadow",["end"]="Neeru Fireblade",level="12",faction="Horde",id=832},src={"Burning Shadows"}}
E["quest:834"] = {t="quest",n="Winds in the Desert",z="durotar",s="Rezlak waits in Durotar for a stolen supply caravan. Dustwind harpies ambushed it in Razorwind Canyon and scattered the building materials among the cliffs.",h="Rezlak waits in Durotar for a stolen supply caravan.",sec={{t="A Goblin on a Deadline",b="Rezlak came from Ratchet at Chief Engineer Gazlowe's command, to help the Horde build across Durotar. The harsh, barren land makes fortification work hard enough. Now shipments vanish before they reach the building sites, and without the cargo, work stops. The irritable goblin supervisor has nothing to build with.",sp=0},{t="Ambush in the Canyon",b="Dustwind harpies ambushed the latest supply run in Razorwind Canyon. They roost in the high ravines beside the road from Razor Hill to Orgrimmar, then swoop on passing wagons. They neither eat nor destroy the freight. Instead, they hoard crates and sacks near their nests, where the supplies wait for anyone willing to fight through their territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rezlak?",a="Rezlak is a goblin worker employed by Gazlowe, the boss of Ratchet. Gazlowe sent him to Durotar to help the orcs build outside Orgrimmar's gates.",al={"rezlak","who is rezlak","who gave this quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why are goblins helping build in Durotar?",a="Gazlowe and the Steamwheedle Cartel have a commercial and engineering partnership with Warchief Thrall. Goblin engineers and machines helped lay Orgrimmar's foundations. Gazlowe still supplies contracted labor and materials to the Horde.",al={"why are goblins helping orcs","gazlowe durotar","goblin horde cooperation"},it="purpose"},{q="Where did the supplies come from?",a="Rezlak does not say where the shipment began. He says only that a caravan carried supplies for his work with the orcs in Durotar.",al={"where are the supplies from","caravan origin"},it="origin"},{q="What are the harpies doing in Durotar?",a="Dustwind harpies are aggressive, predatory scavengers that infest the cliffs and ravines of central Durotar. They harass travelers, raid trade along Razorwind Canyon, and gather anything bright or useful for their nests.",al={"why harpies in durotar","dustwind harpies lore","razorwind harpies"},it="threat"},{q="Where is Razorwind Canyon located?",a="Razorwind Canyon branches from the main southern gorge between Orgrimmar and Razor Hill. Ravines cut into both cliff walls, giving Dustwind harpies high roosts where they stash stolen cargo.",al={"razorwind canyon location","where to find supplies","sacks of supplies location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why didn't the orc guards protect the caravan?",a="Rezlak says caravans are hard to keep safe and that this shipment was promised safe passage. He does not say what guards went with it or why they failed to stop the Dustwind harpies.",al={"why failed caravan","durotar security","orc caravans"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Rezlak want this done?",a="Rezlak was sent directly by Gazlowe to oversee engineering and construction work for the Horde in Durotar. Without these essential materials, his work has ground to a complete standstill, leaving him empty-handed and frustrated. He cannot fulfill his contract or finish his assigned projects until the cargo is recovered.",al={"rezlak motive","why does rezlak need supplies","why does rezlak care"},it="motive",add="5ac1923e"},{q="What is the Sack of Supplies for?",a="These sacks contain engineering and building provisions intended for Horde construction across Durotar. Rezlak and his crew require them to complete their building projects for the orcs, but the material was scattered through Razorwind Canyon when Dustwind harpies intercepted the delivery caravan.",al={"sack of supplies use","what are the sacks of supplies","rezlak supply sacks"},it="item",add="ef031f2c"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Each shipment lost to canyon beasts threatens the Horde's rapid expansion and the fortification of its stronghold in Durotar.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you rely on goblin skill and foreign supplies to make Durotar's harsh, dry soil a fortified homeland.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can understand why Rezlak prizes sound plans and on-time deliveries, even when local wildlife causes trouble."},kw={"caravan","durotar","dustwind harpies","gazlowe","orgrimmar","ratchet","razorwind canyon","rezlak","supplies"},rel={"npc:rezlak","quest:835","subzone:razorwind-canyon","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:razor-hill"},m={start="Rezlak",faction="Horde",id=834,ri={"Sack of Supplies"}},src={"Winds in the Desert"}}
E["quest:835"] = {t="quest",n="Securing the Lines",z="durotar",s="Near Razorwind Canyon, Rezlak needs the goblin supply routes through Durotar kept safe. Harpies in Drygulch Ravine intercept and plunder caravans, so he hires help to drive them out.",h="Near Razorwind Canyon, Rezlak needs the goblin supply routes through Durotar kept safe.",sec={{t="A Route Plagued by Harpies",b="Dustwind harpies make travel through Durotar’s dry valleys dangerous. Rezlak oversees regional supply operations for his boss, Gazlowe. From their roost in Drygulch Ravine, the harpies raid caravans in Razorwind Canyon and seize shipments before they reach their destinations.",sp=0},{t="Business and Bloodshed",b="Rezlak believes the right price can get anything done. He hires adventurers to break the roost by eliminating Dustwind Savages and Dustwind Storm Witches, rather than entering the canyon himself. Clearing the harpies keeps trade corridors open and secures shipments of engineering gadgets. It also points helpful travelers toward greater opportunities in Ratchet.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rezlak working for?",a="Rezlak works for Gazlowe, chief engineer and boss of Ratchet, the neutral goblin port town. Gazlowe oversees extensive commerce and infrastructure projects throughout Durotar and the Barrens.",al={"rezlak boss","who does rezlak work for","rezlak employer"},it="ties"},{q="Why are the harpies attacking caravans?",a="The Dustwind harpies roost in Drygulch Ravine, which runs alongside Razorwind Canyon’s main transit routes. They attack intruders and plunder nearby wagons and goods.",al={"why do harpies attack","dustwind harpies motive","why drygulch ravine"},it="conflict"},{q="Where is Drygulch Ravine located?",a="Drygulch Ravine lies deep in the eastern reaches of Razorwind Canyon in northern Durotar, carved into the arid crimson hills.",al={"drygulch ravine location","where is drygulch ravine","how to find drygulch"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after helping Rezlak?",a="Once the Dustwind harpies are culled and the supply route is secure, Rezlak points adventurers across the border to Ratchet in the Barrens. He encourages them to seek out Gazlowe for more profitable contracts.",al={"after securing the lines","rezlak follow up","what next after rezlak"},it="next_step"},{q="Why doesn't the Horde handle the harpies instead of goblins?",a="The Horde has outposts in Durotar, but its resources are stretched thin by centaur, quilboar, and the needs of its settlements. Goblin merchants like Rezlak often find it quicker and cheaper to hire independent adventurers to protect their private enterprise.",al={"why goblins hiring","why isn't orgrimmar handling this","horde and harpies"},it="why_me"},{q="What kinds of harpies reside in Drygulch Ravine?",a="Drygulch Ravine’s roost includes feral Dustwind Savages, who attack at close range, and Dustwind Storm Witches, who wield wind and lightning against trespassing caravans.",al={"harpy types","dustwind harpy types","drygulch enemies"},it="target"},{q="Why does Rezlak want the harpies cleared out?",a="Rezlak is responsible for keeping cargo moving through Durotar, but the Dustwind harpies in Drygulch Ravine have been ambushing and raiding his supply caravans. Every lost wagon costs gold, delays vital materials, and jeopardizes upcoming shipments—including some specialized equipment he is personally awaiting from Ratchet.",al={"rezlak motive","why kill drygulch harpies","rezlak caravan problem"},it="motive",add="bafa495b"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Keeping Rezlak’s shipments safe helps goblin components move from Ratchet into the hands of local tinkerers.",["faction:Horde"]="Clearing the harpies in eastern Razorwind Canyon keeps goods and reinforcements moving between Durotar’s frontier outposts and coastal trade hubs."},kw={"drygulch ravine","dustwind savage","dustwind storm witch","gazlowe","ratchet","razorwind canyon","rezlak","securing the lines"},rel={"npc:rezlak","subzone:drygulch-ravine","subzone:razorwind-canyon","subzone:ratchet","zone:durotar"},m={start="Rezlak",level="11",id=835},src={"Securing the Lines (Classic)"}}
E["quest:837"] = {t="quest",n="Encroachment",z="durotar",s="At Razor Hill in central Durotar, Gar'Thok sends you west against Razormane camps. Their fortified dens still threaten the young orc homeland.",h="At Razor Hill in central Durotar, Gar'Thok sends you west against Razormane camps.",sec={{t="A Thorn in Durotar's Side",b="When Thrall brought the orcs to Kalimdor and founded Durotar, the Razormane already ranged across much of the harsh, arid land. These aggressive, boar-like quilboar became a constant danger to the new settlement. The Horde drove most of them back through sustained military efforts. Yet fortified pockets remain in thorned redoubts west of Razor Hill.",sp=0},{t="Gar'Thok's Offensive",b="Gar'Thok, an officer at Razor Hill, leads the effort to remove the remaining Razormane. He sends seasoned defenders into the western bramble camps to kill their scouts, warriors, and dustrunners. Gar'Thok and the Horde leadership fear any quilboar foothold near Razor Hill could bring disaster. They see this strike as the first step toward securing Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="Clearing the Brambles",b="Once the quilboar defenders are gone, Horde forces can burn the bramble dens and keep the Razormane from reclaiming the western foothills. The fire destroys an enduring menace and secures Durotar's western perimeter. It also protects the vital supply roads between Razor Hill and the wider realm.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Encroachment?",a="Gar'Thok, an orc officer stationed at Razor Hill in central Durotar, gives the order.",al={"who gives encroachment","where to get encroachment","encroachment questgiver"}},{q="Why is the Horde fighting the Razormane quilboar in Durotar?",a="When the orcs arrived in Durotar, the Razormane quilboar held much of the region. The Horde drove most of them back, but fortified pockets remain west of Razor Hill and threaten the safety of the new orc homeland.",al={"why fight quilboar durotar","why attack razormane","quilboar conflict durotar"}},{q="Where are the Razormane camps located?",a="The Razormane camps lie west of Razor Hill, among dense tangles of thorny brambles.",al={"where are the quilboar camps","how to find razormane camps","encroachment location"}},{q="Who are the Razormane?",a="The Razormane are a hostile tribe of quilboar native to Kalimdor's arid plains. They build defensive bramble dens and fiercely resist the Horde's settlement of Durotar and the Barrens.",al={"who are the razormane","razormane lore","what is razormane"}},{q="What happens once the quilboar are defeated?",a="After the quilboar are defeated, Gar'Thok sends word to burn their cleared brambles and structures. This strengthens Horde control of the area and secures Durotar's borders.",al={"what happens after encroachment","encroachment turn in","fate of quilboar camps"}},{q="What is Razor Hill's role in this conflict?",a="Razor Hill is a fortified orc settlement in central Durotar. It is a military and logistical hub between the Valley of Trials and Orgrimmar.",al={"where is razor hill","what is razor hill"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you need to secure Durotar from the native Razormane quilboar to establish a safe, lasting homeland.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you claim Durotar as your new homeland. The Razormane bramble dens still threaten your settlements."},kw={"brambles","durotar","encroachment","gar'thok","quilboar","razor hill","razormane"},rel={"npc:gar-thok","subzone:razor-hill","topic:quilboar","zone:durotar"},m={faction="Horde",id=837},src={"In-game quest text: Encroachment"},fv=true}
E["quest:840"] = {t="quest",n="Conscript of the Horde",z="durotar",s="Along Durotar’s western road, recruits head toward the Barrens under the name Conscript of the Horde. Takrin Pathseeker watches beyond Razor Hill and gives them a letter for Kargal Battlescar, whose outpost guards the crossing.",h="Along Durotar’s western road, recruits head toward the Barrens under the name Conscript of the Horde.",sec={{t="Crossing the Southfury",b="You have proved your strength around Razor Hill, and now you are called west to serve the wider Horde. Takrin Pathseeker watches the road out of Durotar for his friend, veteran Kargal Battlescar. He gives capable travelers a recruitment letter to carry across the Southfury River. For a recruit, it marks a first formal assignment beyond the orcs’ new homeland.",sp=0},{t="Border Defense",b="Kargal Battlescar holds the outpost beyond the bridge, between Durotar’s red canyons and the dry Barrens. He gathers recruits to guard the frontier, where centaur, quilboar, and Alliance expeditions test the border. Yet the Horde needs more than guards there. Raw manpower is also bound for the settlement of the Crossroads.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I take the recruitment letter?",a="Take the western road out of Razor Hill and cross the wooden bridge over the Southfury River. Kargal Battlescar waits at the Horde watchtower just across the border, on the Barrens side.",al={"where do i go","kargal battlescar location","turn in location"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Who is Takrin Pathseeker?",a="Takrin Pathseeker is a Horde scout on the western road outside Razor Hill. He watches the road and sends capable warriors west to his comrade Kargal Battlescar.",al={"takrin role","who gives quest","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Kargal Battlescar?",a="Kargal Battlescar is a gruff veteran officer at the eastern Barrens watchpost. He inspects arriving volunteers, signs their conscription papers, and directs them west across the savanna to aid the Crossroads.",al={"who is kargal","battlescar lore"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after Kargal signs the letter?",a="After Kargal accepts the letter, he enlists you for further service and sends you west along the main road to report to Sergra Darkthorn at the Crossroads.",al={"next quest","what after conscript of the horde","where next"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is the Horde recruiting soldiers for the Barrens?",a="The Barrens is an open frontier that connects Orgrimmar with Mulgore. Fierce quilboar tribes, centaur marauders, and Alliance incursions threaten supply routes, so the Horde needs every able hand to keep the roads secure.",al={"why conscript","barrens danger","why recruit"},it="purpose"},{q="Is this quest available to Alliance players?",a="No. This service is only for Horde members moving from the early Durotar story into the Barrens.",al={"can alliance do this","is this horde only"},gp=true},{q="Why does Takrin Pathseeker want me to deliver the recruitment letter?",a="Takrin Pathseeker serves as an advanced scout watching the road from Durotar into the arid plains. His old comrade Kargal Battlescar commands the border outpost just across the river and faces a constant shortage of capable warriors. Seeing promise in your strength, Takrin wants to steer fresh blood directly into the Barrens garrison to bolster Horde defense rather than let able hands idle in Razor Hill.",al={"why does takrin send me","takrin pathseeker motive","why recruit for kargal"},it="motive",add="dfa16f64"},{q="Why does Takrin send an adventurer instead of reporting to Kargal himself?",a="Takrin is assigned to watch the vital crossroads between Durotar and the western frontier, keeping eyes on travelers and threats moving along the highway. Leaving his post to ferry individual messages would abandon his duty. More importantly, he is scouting for potential soldiers to aid Kargal, and having you report directly to the outpost commander proves your willingness and initiative to serve the Horde.",al={"why doesn't takrin go","why send me to kargal","why me conscript of the horde"},it="why_me",add="788e36ab"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, this conscription marks your move from protecting Durotar to defending Horde lands across Kalimdor.",["race:Orc"]="As a young orc leaving the Valley of Trials and Razor Hill, answering Kargal Battlescar’s call is a rite of passage in service to the Warchief.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you join your orc allies in this deployment to aid the Horde’s expansion and secure the lands bordering the Great Sea."},kw={"barrens","conscript of the horde","crossroads","kargal battlescar","razor hill","recruitment letter","southfury river","takrin pathseeker"},rel={"quest:842","npc:kargal-battlescar","zone:barrens","subzone:razor-hill","subzone:crossroads","topic:horde"},m={start="Takrin Pathseeker",["end"]="Kargal Battlescar",level="12",faction="Horde",id=840},src={"Conscript of the Horde (Classic)"}}
E["quest:8670"] = {t="quest",n="Runetotem the Elder",z="durotar",s="In Razor Hill, travelers can honor Runetotem the Elder during the Lunar Festival. This ancestral spirit waits beneath a beam of heavenly light and offers blessings and festival tokens to those who remember the past.",h="In Razor Hill, travelers can honor Runetotem the Elder during the Lunar Festival.",sec={{t="A Spirit in Razor Hill",b="During the Lunar Festival, ancient elders appear across Azeroth to commune with the living. Elder Runetotem waits just inside Razor Hill's southern entrance. Starlight falls on her as she watches over the orcish settlement. Travelers may pause to honor the wisdom of those who came before.",sp=0},{t="Guidance Across the Lands",b="Pay Elder Runetotem homage and she gives you a festival token of fortune. She also tells you where other spirits can be found. Her directions lead to Elder Darkhorn and Elder High Mountain elsewhere across the continent.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Elder Runetotem located?",a="Elder Runetotem waits inside Razor Hill in Durotar, just to the right after you enter through the southern entrance.",al={"elder runetotem location","where is elder runetotem","find elder runetotem"}},{q="Why is there a beam of light shining on her?",a="A shaft of celestial light marks Elder Runetotem as an honored elder, as it does the ancestral spirits who appear during the Lunar Festival.",al={"light beam elder","why is runetotem glowing","elder beam of light"}},{q="What do you receive for honoring Elder Runetotem?",a="You receive a festival token for honoring Elder Runetotem, and she gives directions to spirits such as Elder Darkhorn and Elder High Mountain.",al={"runetotem reward","what does runetotem give","elder runetotem turn in"}},{q="Can Alliance players visit Elder Runetotem?",a="Elder Runetotem welcomes homage from all mortals, whatever their allegiance, but Razor Hill is a guarded Horde outpost that can be perilous for Alliance travelers to reach.",al={"alliance elder runetotem","can alliance talk to runetotem"}},{q="Which elders does Runetotem mention?",a="Elder Runetotem gives directions to Elder Darkhorn and Elder High Mountain.",al={"runetotem directions","who does runetotem tell you to find"}},{q="Is Elder Runetotem a living tauren or a ghost?",a="Elder Runetotem is an ancestral spirit who appears during the Lunar Festival to bless those whose spirits burn with life.",al={"is runetotem dead","is runetotem a ghost"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, meeting a spirit of the Runetotem family beyond Mulgore recalls your people's deep spiritual heritage across Kalimdor.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can honor Elder Runetotem inside Razor Hill, making her one of the safest and most convenient ancestors to visit early in your travels.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you must cross enemy lines into Durotar to honor Elder Runetotem, risking the anger of Razor Hill's orcish guards."},kw={"durotar","elder darkhorn","elder high mountain","elder runetotem","lunar festival","razor hill","runetotem"},rel={"npc:elder-runetotem","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:light"},m={start="Elder Runetotem",id=8670},src={"Runetotem the Elder"}}
E["quest:96102"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Tailoring",z="durotar",s="Tailoring training teaches you to make a Rallying Banner. Its test belongs in the wilderness, where a camp needs a campfire.",h="Tailoring training teaches you to make a Rallying Banner.",sec={{t="A Campfire First",b="You can now craft a Rallying Banner, and its completion note calls for a wilderness test. A camp needs a campfire before you set it up. Most cooks can teach you to make one, so ask a cooking trainer for the basics if you have not learned them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What can I make after this?",a="Tailoring training teaches you to craft your own Rallying Banner.",al={"what do i craft","banner recipe","tailoring banner"}},{q="Where should I test the banner?",a="Test your Rallying Banner in the wilderness. The completion note says townsfolk generally do not care for camps in the center of town.",al={"where to test it","camping where","test banner"}},{q="What does a camp need?",a="Before you set up a camp, you need a campfire.",al={"camp needs what","campfire needed","camping basics"}},{q="Who can teach me to make a campfire?",a="Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. A cooking trainer can teach you the basics.",al={"campfire trainer","who teaches fire","cooking fire"}}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you can craft a Rallying Banner for a camp.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can teach others to make a campfire."},kw={"campfire","camping","cooking","rallying banner","tailoring","wilderness"},m={faction="Horde",id=96102},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Tailoring"},fv=true}
E["quest:96604"] = {t="quest",n="The Great Outdoors",z="durotar",s="Brakk welcomes travelers beside his Basic Campfire and teaches them to rest in the wild. From there, they turn to practical crafts.",h="Brakk welcomes travelers beside his Basic Campfire and teaches them to rest in the wild.",sec={{t="Lessons in the Wild",b="Brakk greets aspiring adventurers with a hearty “Lok-tar” and welcomes those seeking fortune and glory. The road through Azeroth’s wilds asks for more than skill at arms; travelers must also endure the elements. Learning to make camp and regain strength is a first step toward surviving out there.",sp=0},{t="From Hearth to Craft",b="Rest beside Brakk’s Basic Campfire brings a restorative pause in the open air and teaches travelers how to recover. Once they know these basics, novice adventurers can visit craftsmen in a nearby village. There, they can study tradeskills and learn to build camp fixtures suited to their chosen craft.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is The Great Outdoors?",a="Brakk’s lesson teaches new adventurers to rest beside a campfire before taking up a profession.",al={"what is the great outdoors","the great outdoors quest"}},{q="Who is Brakk?",a="Brakk welcomes restless travelers seeking fortune and glory and teaches practical ways to survive in the wild and rest by a campfire.",al={"who is brakk","quest giver"}},{q="What is the Boosted Rest buff?",a="Resting near Brakk’s Basic Campfire grants the Boosted Rest buff and shows how an open flame can help an adventurer recover in the wild.",al={"boosted rest buff","campfire buff"}},{q="What should you do after completing the quest?",a="After learning how to rest in the wild, visit trainers in the nearby village to study a tradeskill and learn to build camp fixtures suited to that craft.",al={"next step after quest","what to do after campfire"}},{q="What are camp fixtures?",a="Camp fixtures are campsite installations taught by profession trainers in nearby villages. They let travelers adapt their camps to support their chosen tradeskills.",al={"camp fixtures","what are camp fixtures"}},{q="Who is this training intended for?",a="This lesson is for restless souls seeking fortune and glory in the wild, especially those just beginning their journey and preparing to choose a trade.",al={"who should do this quest","is this for horde"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="A traditional Orcish “Lok-tar” greets new Horde adventurers as they learn the basics of survival before setting out across treacherous territories."},kw={"boosted rest","brakk","camp fixture","campfire","the great outdoors","tradeskill","wilderness survival"},m={faction="Horde",id=96604},src={"In-game quest text: The Great Outdoors"},fv=true}
E["quest:96652"] = {t="quest",n="The Adventurer",z="durotar",s="On Durotar’s red wastes, The Adventurer finds a lost journal meant for Brakk near Razor Hill. Its pages remember quiet travels and nights beneath the stars.",h="On Durotar’s red wastes, The Adventurer finds a lost journal meant for Brakk near Razor Hill.",sec={{t="A Wanderer's Notes",b="A lost journal lies in Durotar’s red dirt, far from the battles and campaigns that mark the land. An unknown traveler fills its pages with daily journeys and the pleasure of making camp beneath the open sky. The journal offers a quiet glimpse of life on the road through harsh country.",sp=0},{t="Delivery to Brakk",b="The journal is meant for Brakk, an adventurer camped near Razor Hill. Its pages link an unknown traveler to someone watching the dusty roads. Carrying it to Brakk may keep the writer’s travels remembered.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the lost journal?",a="The journal holds daily entries about an obscure adventurer’s travels, with fond notes about camping in the wilderness.",al={"what does the journal say","lost journal contents","journal text"},it="item"},{q="Who wrote the journal?",a="The recovered pages do not name their author. They describe an unfamiliar adventurer’s life and travels.",al={"who is the adventurer","author of lost journal","who wrote this book"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Brakk?",a="Brakk is an adventurer camped near Razor Hill in central Durotar, and the journal is meant for him.",al={"brakk razor hill","who is brakk","where is brakk"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the journal found?",a="The journal lies abandoned in Durotar’s red dirt, where a passing Horde traveler can find it.",al={"where do i find the journal","lost journal location","adventurer quest start"},gp=true},{q="Why does Brakk care about this journal?",a="The journal gives no reason for Brakk to care about it. He is an adventurer camped just outside Razor Hill who teaches newcomers the basics of camping, and the journal tells of camping.",al={"why bring it to brakk","brakk purpose","brakk journal"},it="motive"},{q="Is the adventurer who wrote it in danger?",a="The pages give no sign of foul play and recall camping fondly. The writer may have lost the journal by mistake or moved on unexpectedly.",al={"is the author alive","did the adventurer die","lost adventurer status"},it="threat"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Many new recruits walk Durotar’s arid trails. Bringing lost belongings to wanderers like Brakk near Razor Hill helps keep order along the central frontier.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know how to live off the land. The journal’s fond notes about wilderness camping may feel familiar."},kw={"adventurer","brakk","camping","durotar","journal","lost journal","razor hill"},rel={"zone:durotar","subzone:razor-hill"},m={start="Object #654925",["end"]="Brakk",level="6",faction="Horde",id=96652},src={"The Adventurer (Durotar)"},fv=true}
E["quest:96655"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Cooking",z="durotar",s="In Razor Hill, Cook Torka shows travelers how to cook and make a campfire. With those skills, they can establish camps in the wild.",h="In Razor Hill, Cook Torka shows travelers how to cook and make a campfire.",sec={{t="The Hearth of the Wild",b="Beyond a settlement's gates, surviving in the wild takes more than sharp steel and sturdy armor. In Razor Hill, Cook Torka teaches budding adventurers to cook. Across Durotar and beyond, cooking means more than preparing a hot meal. It also teaches travelers to light a reliable campfire, the heart of any campsite.",sp=0},{t="Building and Furnishing a Camp",b="Once travelers know the basics, they can pitch a modest camp almost anywhere on the frontier. A novice campfire supports only a few essential furnishings. Greater cooking skill lets travelers build larger blazes. Other trades teach them to craft what they need to furnish and improve a camp into a reliable shelter from the wild.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Camping 101: Cooking?",a="Camping 101: Cooking teaches adventurers the basics of outdoor survival. Learning to cook and make a campfire lets them establish camps in the wild.",al={"what is camping 101 cooking","camping 101 cooking quest","what does this quest do"}},{q="Who is Cook Torka?",a="Cook Torka is the Horde cooking trainer in Razor Hill, Durotar. He teaches aspiring adventurers cooking basics and how to light a campfire.",al={"who teaches cooking razor hill","who is cook torka","where is cook torka"}},{q="Why is cooking required for camping?",a="Cooking teaches travelers to build the campfire at the heart of a campsite. Without a fire, they cannot maintain a proper campsite in the wilderness.",al={"why do i need cooking for camping","cooking campfire connection","does camping require cooking"}},{q="Where can an adventurer set up a campsite?",a="Once you learn the basics of cooking and making a campfire, you can set up a small campsite almost anywhere in the open wilderness. At first, it supports only a few furnishings.",al={"where can i camp","how does camping work","campsite placement"}},{q="How do you upgrade your campfire?",a="As you improve your cooking skill, you can learn to build larger, longer lasting campfires and expand what your campsite can support.",al={"bigger campfires","upgrade campfire","how to improve campsite"}},{q="How do you obtain furnishings for a campsite?",a="Cooking provides the campfire foundation, while other trade trainers across the world teach adventurers to craft and place furnishings for their campsites.",al={"campsite decorations","furnishing camp","camp furnishings trainers"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Cooking is needed to build a basic campfire, the foundation for surviving in the wild and setting up a campsite.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer starting out in Durotar, you can visit Cook Torka in Razor Hill to learn the basics of cooking."},kw={"campfire","camping 101","camping 101: cooking","campsite","cook torka","cooking","durotar","furnishings","razor hill"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill"},m={faction="Horde",id=96655},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Cooking"},fv=true}
E["quest:96821"] = {t="quest",n="Legging It",z="durotar",s="The peons have halted their southward travel because dangers line the road. Their work waits until the way is safe again.",h="The peons have halted their southward travel because dangers line the road.",sec={{t="Securing the Line",b="Peons have left their assigned work undone and stopped traveling south. Perils along the road have made the journey too dangerous. Once the threats are pushed back, overseers can send their crews to work again.",sp=0},{t="Labor and Route Security",b="Peons do much of the Horde’s hard labor, from harvesting timber and quarrying to building outposts. They have little skill in battle, so roadside predators or hostile scouts can halt the movement of supplies. Clear routes keep settlements supplied and let the work continue.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Legging It?",a="Dangers along the road have frightened peons away from traveling south. Their duties wait until the way is safe.",al={"what is legging it","legging it quest info","legging it quest"}},{q="Why were the peons afraid to travel south?",a="The peons fear the dangers along the southern road. Without protection or a clear path, they refuse to travel to their assignments, bringing local work to a halt.",al={"why were peons scared","peon fear","why peons stopped working"}},{q="What is accomplished by completing the task?",a="When the southern route is clear and immediate dangers are pushed back, overseers can send peons to gather resources and work in the field.",al={"what happens after legging it","legging it outcome","clearing path result"}},{q="Who are the peons mentioned in the task?",a="Peons are the Horde’s labor force. They harvest lumber, mine, and build fortifications. They are essential to settlements but poorly suited to combat, and readily retreat from danger.",al={"who are the peons","peon role","what do peons do"}},{q="Where were the peons traveling?",a="The peons were traveling south along a path toward outlying work areas and resource deposits that need regular care. The journey had become dangerous enough to stop all traffic.",al={"where does the path lead","southern path","heading south"}},{q="Why do peons require adventurers to clear their routes?",a="Peons lack military training and combat gear, leaving them vulnerable to wilderness predators and hostile forces. Overseers rely on experienced adventurers to clear threats and keep work routes safe.",al={"why do peons need protection","peon safety","guarding peons"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Horde construction and resource gathering rely heavily on peons, so their routes need to stay safe.",["race:Orc"]="Peons do much of the work in orcish settlements. Overseers rely on warriors to clear threats from their paths so work can continue."},kw={"cleared the path","horde labor","legging it","overseer","peon labor","peons","southern path"},m={faction="Horde",id=96821},src={"In-game quest text: Legging It"},fv=true}
E["quest:96822"] = {t="quest",n="For Honor",z="durotar",s="Fallen warriors live on in memory through For Honor. Their sacrifices endure in the minds of those who remember them.",h="Fallen warriors live on in memory through For Honor.",sec={{t="A Duty of Remembrance",b="Those who outlive fallen warriors carry their memory forward. Remembering those who gave everything is a duty.",sp=0},{t="Preserving the Legacy",b="Your efforts keep the fallen fighters alive in memory. Those who remember them continue to honor their sacrifices.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest For Honor about?",a="For Honor asks you to remember fallen fighters. Your efforts keep their sacrifices from fading.",al={"what is for honor","for honor quest overview"}},{q="Who are the warriors mentioned upon completion?",a="The warriors are fallen fighters honored for their deeds. Your actions preserve their memory and the service they gave.",al={"who are the warriors","who is remembered"}},{q="Why is honoring these warriors important?",a="Remembering fallen warriors gives their sacrifice dignity. It keeps their courage acknowledged.",al={"why do this quest","for honor meaning"}},{q="Who asks for this task to be done?",a="Someone seeking to remember fallen comrades directs the work. When you return, they confirm it is done and acknowledge the warriors' memory.",al={"who gives for honor","quest giver for honor"}},{q="Does this quest lead to other tasks?",a="Nothing points to further work. For Honor honors fallen fighters and their sacrifices.",al={"is for honor part of a chain","what follows for honor"}},{q="What does the title For Honor signify?",a="For Honor names the duty of remembering fallen soldiers. Keeping their sacrifice and battlefield memory alive is a solemn duty for any fighter.",al={"what makes it honorable","meaning of for honor"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you know the weight of battlefield sacrifice. Remembering fallen combatants keeps their deeds alive."},kw={"fallen warriors","for honor","honor","memorial","quest","remembrance","warrior"},rel={"topic:warrior"},m={faction="Horde",id=96822},src={"In-game quest text: For Honor"},fv=true}
E["quest:96825"] = {t="quest",n="This Fruit Could Bite Back",z="durotar",s="In Durotar, prickly pears feed Orgrimmar and promise more food ahead. Gathered with care, these hardy fruits can nourish the Horde capital and provide seeds for future crops.",h="In Durotar, prickly pears feed Orgrimmar and promise more food ahead.",sec={{t="Harvesting the Arid Wastes",b="Durotar is rugged and sun-baked, where traditional farming is nearly impossible. Its hardy prickly pears thrive in the arid soil, so inhabitants gather them to help feed Orgrimmar. Their protective spines call for care, and their fruit brings needed nourishment.",sp=0},{t="Cultivation and Sustenance",b="Prickly pears feed people now and can help supply food in the years ahead. Their flesh is prepared for dishes, while their seeds are carefully preserved for planting. The aim is to grow this resilient crop around Orgrimmar, creating a lasting food source close outside the fortress walls.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is This Fruit Could Bite Back?",a="You gather wild prickly pears in Durotar for cooking and save their seeds to plant across the dry land around Orgrimmar.",al={"what is this fruit could bite back","this fruit could bite back quest","bite back fruit quest"}},{q="Why are prickly pears being gathered?",a="Prickly pears provide food for local meals, and their seeds are saved for planting. The aim is to grow them across the arid land around Orgrimmar.",al={"why gather prickly pears","prickly pear purpose","what are prickly pears for"}},{q="Where will the seeds be planted?",a="The seeds are meant to be planted throughout the outskirts and lands around Orgrimmar, where they can help establish a resilient food supply in the harsh desert soil.",al={"where grow prickly pears","prickly pear planting orgrimmar"}},{q="Who wants these fruits gathered?",a="A local resident wants the harvest to improve local food stores, feed travelers, and grow crops suited to Durotar's harsh desert climate.",al={"who wants the prickly pears","quest giver bite back"}},{q="Why does the fruit 'bite back'?",a="Prickly pears have sharp spines and needles like other hardy desert cacti, so gatherers must take care.",al={"why bite back","why does fruit bite back"}},{q="Why is planting fruit around Orgrimmar important?",a="Durotar is mostly arid and rocky, making conventional farming difficult. Drought-tolerant prickly pears could help provide a lasting food supply for Orgrimmar.",al={"does orgrimmar lack food","orgrimmar agriculture","durotar farming"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know sustainable food sources like hearty desert fruits can help feed Orgrimmar and the Horde's growing population.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can prepare prickly pears into dishes, and the fruit can also supply city residents.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you know how hardy desert plants can be and how much effort it takes to gather spiny wild fruits for cultivation."},kw={"cactus fruit","durotar","fruit","orgrimmar","prickly pear","prickly pears","seeds","this fruit could bite back"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar"},m={faction="Horde",id=96825},src={"In-game quest text: This Fruit Could Bite Back"},fv=true}
E["quest:96873"] = {t="quest",n="A Pain in the Neck",z="durotar",s="Pa'zula asks you to strip the binding magic from pendants used by Zalazane to control trolls in the Echo Isles. The residue may free their spirits from the witchdoctor's hold.",h="Pa'zula asks you to strip the binding magic from pendants used by Zalazane to control trolls in the Echo...",sec={{t="Pa'zula's Request",b="Pa'zula in Sen'jin Village needs the residue from Hexed Pendants. Zalazane uses binding spells on the pendants to keep his prisoners under control. You are to remove that magic and bring Pa'zula what remains. The trolls' freedom is at stake.",sp=0},{t="The Pendants",b="Pa'zula says the binding spells hold the trolls' minds, and warns you against wearing a pendant yourself. When you return with the residue, Pa'zula says the spells are removed and the slain trolls' spirits can rest.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the residue?",a="Pa'zula in Sen'jin Village asks you to bring the residue from Hexed Pendants.",al={"who wants residue","pa'zula request"}},{q="What does Zalazane do with the pendants?",a="Zalazane uses binding spells on the pendants to keep his prisoners' minds under control.",al={"zalazane pendants","hexed pendants"}},{q="Where are the Hexed Pendants found?",a="The Hexed Pendants are carried by trolls in the Echo Isles.",al={"pendant location","where pendants"}},{q="What is Luminous Residue?",a="Luminous Residue is obtained by stripping the magic from Hexed Pendants.",al={"residue from pendants","luminous stuff"}},{q="Why does Pa'zula want the pendant magic removed?",a="Pa'zula says removing the binding spells lets the slain trolls' spirits rest.",al={"why disenchant pendants","free troll spirits"}}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="As an enchanter, you practice your craft by stripping binding magic from Hexed Pendants for Pa'zula."},kw={"a pain in the neck","binding spells","echo isles","hexed pendants","luminous residue","pa'zula","sen'jin village","zalazane"},rel={"quest:826","subzone:echo-isles","subzone:sen-jin-village","topic:troll"},m={faction="Horde",id=96873},src={"In-game quest text: A Pain in the Neck"},fv=true}
E["quest:96876"] = {t="quest",n="Ukor's Lost Pack",z="durotar",s="In southern Durotar, Ukor's Lost Pack lies abandoned in the wilds. Its owner fled a huge spider and left his supplies behind.",h="In southern Durotar, Ukor's Lost Pack lies abandoned in the wilds.",sec={{t="A Lost Belonging",b="In southern Durotar, you find a traveling bag with Ukor's name crudely stitched across its flap. In these harsh lands, discarded gear may point to trouble nearby.",sp=0},{t="Fleeing the Wilds",b="Ukor receives his pack in southern Durotar and tells how he lost it. A huge spider ambushed him, and he fled in panic, certain his supplies were gone. Finding the bag intact earns you Ukor's heartfelt gratitude and praise.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ukor?",a="Ukor lives in southern Durotar. When a huge spider confronted him in the wilds, he abandoned his belongings to escape.",al={"who is ukor","ukor durotar"}},{q="Why did Ukor lose his pack?",a="Ukor dropped his pack while fleeing a huge spider in Durotar. He thought his belongings were gone for good until you found the bag.",al={"why was pack lost","where did ukor lose pack"}},{q="Where does the pack need to be taken?",a="Take the recovered pack to Ukor in southern Durotar, where he waits to greet returning travelers.",al={"where to return pack","ukor turn in"}},{q="How is the pack identified?",a="Ukor's name is crudely stitched across the bag's flap.",al={"how is pack identified","pack stitching"}},{q="What kind of creature chased Ukor?",a="A huge spider ambushed Ukor in southern Durotar. Terrified, he dropped his possessions and ran for safety.",al={"spider in durotar","what spider attacked ukor"}},{q="What happens when you return the pack to Ukor?",a="Ukor is astonished and deeply grateful to see his belongings again. He calls you a true hero for retrieving the bag.",al={"ukor reward","how does ukor react"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a young Horde adventurer in southern Durotar, you can help locals like Ukor by recovering belongings lost to dangerous wildlife."},kw={"durotar","horde","lost pack","southern durotar","spider","ukor","ukor's lost pack"},rel={"npc:ukor","zone:durotar"},m={faction="Horde",id=96876},src={"In-game quest text: Ukor's Lost Pack"},fv=true}
E["quest:96877"] = {t="quest",n="Halikor's Hoof",z="durotar",s="In the wilds, Halikor's Hoof is carried to Orgrimmar as proof of a hunter's triumph. The enormous severed hoof honors the hunter's victory over the formidable lizard.",h="In the wilds, Halikor's Hoof is carried to Orgrimmar as proof of a hunter's triumph.",sec={{t="Trophy of a Mighty Beast",b="Halikor's vast size is plain in the hoof taken from its remains. Hunters and warriors in the wilds have long claimed a piece of a formidable beast to prove the kill. The hoof leaves no doubt of the lizard's great size and strength.",sp=0},{t="Proof for the Capital",b="The heavy hoof is carried to Orgrimmar to announce the beast's defeat to the Horde. Strength and survival against the land's harsh predators matter in this warrior society. Presenting the trophy honors the hunter and assures the capital that a dangerous creature has been slain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Halikor?",a="Halikor is a formidable lizard of immense size. Hunters claim its severed hoof as proof that the beast was slain.",al={"what is halikor","who is halikor","halikor lizard"}},{q="Why must the hoof be delivered to Orgrimmar?",a="The hoof is carried to Orgrimmar as proof of the beast's defeat and the hunter's triumph.",al={"why bring hoof to orgrimmar","halikor hoof deliver","where does the hoof go"}},{q="How is Halikor's Hoof obtained?",a="You claim Halikor's Hoof from the lizard's body after tracking down and slaying it in combat.",al={"how to get halikors hoof","halikor drop"}},{q="Why does a lizard have a hoof?",a="Halikor is a mighty beast of the wilds, and its enormous hoof proves you brought it down. No one has said why it bears a hoof.",al={"does halikor have hooves","why does a lizard have hooves"}},{q="Who in Orgrimmar wants Halikor's Hoof?",a="You carry the hoof to Orgrimmar as proof of your victory. No particular hunter or official is named to receive it.",al={"who accepts halikors hoof in orgrimmar","turn in halikor hoof orgrimmar"}},{q="What is the story behind the quest Halikor's Hoof?",a="The mighty lizard Halikor is slain, and its enormous severed hoof is carried to Orgrimmar. The trophy shows the hunter's prowess and brings the Horde word of the beast's death.",al={"what is halikors hoof quest","halikors hoof story"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Carrying proof of a mighty beast's defeat to Orgrimmar honors Horde traditions of strength and hunting prowess.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, bringing down the enormous Halikor shows the skill of the tracker and the thrill of the hunt."},kw={"halikor","halikor's hoof","horde","hunt","lizard","orgrimmar","trophy"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar"},m={faction="Horde",id=96877},src={"In-game quest text: Halikor's Hoof"},fv=true}
E["quest:97223"] = {t="quest",n="Bloodtalon Matriarch",z="durotar",s="Near Sen'jin Village, handlers face a threat from the Bloodtalon Matriarch as they seek her young. Her pack is prized for speed and cunning, but adults resist taming. The Darkspear seek to secure her clutch and raise loyal companions from the egg.",h="Near Sen'jin Village, handlers face a threat from the Bloodtalon Matriarch as they seek her young.",sec={{t="The Bloodtalon Lineage",b="Along Durotar's coast, Bloodtalon raptors are prized for speed and cunning. Handlers in Sen'jin Village value those traits in dependable mounts and companions for the Darkspear tribe. Yet full-grown raptors have stubborn, violent instincts. Once grown, wild adults are scarcely tamed.",sp=0},{t="Preserving the Bloodline",b="Repeated attempts to capture and train the Matriarch have only made her more aggressive. Now she threatens the surrounding territory. The trolls seek to protect their tribe and preserve her bloodline. They must quell the dangerous mother and save her clutch, so the next generation can be raised from the egg as loyal allies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is the Bloodtalon Matriarch?",a="The Bloodtalon Matriarch is a fierce adult raptor whose pack is known for speed and cunning. Attempts to capture and train her failed as she grew too dangerous to handle. The Darkspear trolls seek to secure her eggs.",al={"who is bloodtalon matriarch","bloodtalon raptor matriarch","matriarch raptor"}},{q="Why must the Bloodtalon Matriarch be dealt with?",a="The Matriarch has become a danger to the surrounding territory, and adult raptors are difficult to tame. By quelling her and securing her clutch, handlers in Sen'jin Village can protect the tribe and preserve her bloodline.",al={"why kill matriarch","why capture eggs","why hunt the matriarch"}},{q="Why not tame the Matriarch instead?",a="Full-grown raptors have stubborn, violent instincts and are nearly impossible to tame. Handlers can raise the young from eggs as loyal companions instead.",al={"can you tame adult raptors","train adult raptor"}},{q="What will happen to the Matriarch's offspring?",a="The captured clutch is brought to Sen'jin Village to be incubated and raised. The trolls plan to train the young raptors from infancy as reliable allies and mounts for the tribe.",al={"what happens to the eggs","matriarch children","raptors in senjin"}},{q="Where is this quest centered?",a="The work centers near Sen'jin Village on the coast of Durotar. There, handlers seek to raise loyal raptors for the Darkspear tribe.",al={"where is this quest handed in","senjin village raptor quest"}},{q="What makes the Bloodtalon pack special?",a="The Bloodtalon pack is prized for speed and cunning. Those traits make its young desirable as companions and mounts, while full-grown raptors resist taming.",al={"bloodtalon raptor traits","why bloodtalon raptors"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you know Sen'jin Village's handlers prize raptors as agile companions and war mounts. The Bloodtalon line is valued for cunning and speed.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know that raising local predators as loyal allies helps protect the Darkspear settlement and strengthen the Horde's presence on the Durotar coast.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know how hard it is to tame a seasoned adult beast. Raising a predator from birth can forge a true bond."},kw={"bloodtalon","darkspear","matriarch","raptor","raptor eggs","raptors","sen'jin village","senjin","troll mounts"},rel={"subzone:sen-jin-village"},m={faction="Horde",id=97223},src={"In-game quest text: Bloodtalon Matriarch"},fv=true}
E["quest:97225"] = {t="quest",n="Forgotten Loa Idols",z="durotar",s="The Darkspear seek the Forgotten Loa Idols so their sacred rites can continue. The relics preserve the tribe’s bond with its patron spirits.",h="The Darkspear seek the Forgotten Loa Idols so their sacred rites can continue.",sec={{t="Sacred Remnants of the Loa",b="The Darkspear honor the loa through sacred rites. These primal animal spirits and wild gods belong to the trolls’ ancestral heritage. The lost idols are needed for ceremonies in their honor. Without them, spiritual leaders cannot perform the rites that keep the tribe in harmony with its divine guardians.",sp=0},{t="The Darkspear Bond",b="The Darkspear approach the loa with respect and humble reverence. Other hostile troll factions across Azeroth practice blood sacrifice or try to command spirits by force. Losing their patrons’ favor would be a grave catastrophe for the Darkspear. So restoring the idols is vital to preserving the tribe.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Forgotten Loa Idols?",a="The Darkspear need the missing sacred idols so their tribal rituals can resume and they can honor their wild spirits.",al={"forgotten loa idols","what is this quest","what is forgotten loa idols"}},{q="What are loa?",a="The loa are powerful, ancient primal spirits and animal deities revered by trolls. Trolls honor them with offerings, prayer, and ritual ceremonies, seeking protection, favor, and spiritual guidance.",al={"what are loa","troll gods","who are the loa"}},{q="How do the Darkspear view their loa compared to other troll tribes?",a="The Darkspear meet the loa with deep reverence, mutual respect, and a sense of spiritual duty. They believe their survival depends on keeping the spirits’ favor.",al={"darkspear loa relationship","why revere loa","other tribes loa"}},{q="Why are the idols needed for tribal rituals?",a="The idols are sacred objects needed for tribal rites. Without them, elders and spiritual leaders cannot properly commune with and honor their patron spirits.",al={"why need idols","loa idols purpose","why are idols important"}},{q="Why is keeping the loa's favor so vital to the Darkspear?",a="The Darkspear fear that without proper rites and offerings, they could lose the loa’s favor and protection, leaving the tribe vulnerable in a perilous world.",al={"what happens if not returned","falling out of favor","darkspear loa favor"}},{q="Who seeks the return of the Forgotten Loa Idols?",a="A Darkspear spiritual guide seeks the idols’ return and is anxious to resume communal ceremonies and secure blessings from the tribe’s ancestral patrons.",al={"who gives forgotten loa idols","quest giver","who asks for idols"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, communion with the loa is central to your spiritual life. Lost idols let vital rituals continue and help keep the tribe in the spirits’ good graces.",["class:Priest"]="As a troll priest, you rely on rituals and sacred items from your ancestors to channel spiritual power and honor the loa.",["class:Shaman"]="As a troll shaman, you invoke elemental forces while honoring the wild gods and ancestral loa tied to your tribe’s survival.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you belong to a faction whose foundational members include the Darkspear. Helping their holy elders preserve vital religious artifacts strengthens tribal unity."},kw={"darkspear","forgotten loa idols","idols","loa","reverence","rituals","spirits","troll"},m={faction="Horde",id=97225},src={"In-game quest text: Forgotten Loa Idols"},fv=true}
E["quest:97279"] = {t="quest",n="Wayward Weapons",z="durotar",s="At the Valley of Trials, Gornek sends fresh arrivals to recover weapons for the encampment. Young warriors keep coming to serve the Horde, and Kzan Thornslash needs old arms returned to use.",h="At the Valley of Trials, Gornek sends fresh arrivals to recover weapons for the encampment.",sec={{t="Arming the New Blood",b="Young recruits face harsh trials in Durotar's red wastes. Many arrive ready to pledge their blades to the warchief, leaving the encampment short of weapons. Weaponsmith Kzan Thornslash struggles to meet demand. Early lessons can end in death or humiliation for those unready.",sp=0},{t="A Test of Resourcefulness",b="Overseer Gornek turns the shortage into a practical trial. He sends fresh arrivals to recover abandoned blades and blunt training weapons left by recruits who fell or fled. Kzan can repair and temper the recovered arms for the next wave. The recruits learn that survival in the Horde calls for scavenging as well as swinging steel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there so many abandoned training weapons lying around?",a="Some recruits lack the strength or resolve the Horde demands. Careless or frightened newcomers leave their gear behind, while others fall to local boars and scorpids, scattering their issued arms across the dirt.",al={"why are weapons on the ground","abandoned weapons durotar","failed recruits weapons"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Kzan Thornslash?",a="Kzan Thornslash is the weaponsmith inside the Den in the Valley of Trials. He outfits new recruits, repairs battered training gear, and maintains the Horde's martial supplies in the starting valley.",al={"kzan thornslash lore","who is kzan","weaponsmith kzan"},it="identity"},{q="Who issues this task?",a="Gornek, the overseer outside the Den, sends new recruits to help. He watches incoming aspirants, judges their basic potential, and assigns them immediate needs around the trial grounds.",al={"who gives wayward weapons","gornek quest"},gp=true},{q="What will Kzan do with these salvaged weapons?",a="Kzan repairs, sharpens, and restores the battered practice weapons. With resources in Durotar sparse and recruits arriving constantly, he reuses salvaged iron and wood to train the next wave.",al={"what happens to the training weapons","repairing weapons kzan"},it="next_step"},{q="Where is this quest taking place?",a="You are in the Valley of Trials, an isolated canyon in southern Durotar where young orcs and Darkspear trolls begin their path as warriors for the Horde.",al={"valley of trials location","where is wayward weapons"},it="place"},{q="Why doesn't the Horde just forge entirely new weapons?",a="Durotar is rugged and arid, with few easily reached iron deposits, and the young Horde cannot afford waste. Reusing practice blades from recruits who fail saves raw metal for frontline troops.",al={"why salvage weapons","durotar metal shortage"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Gornek want the abandoned weapons collected?",a="A fresh influx of recruits into the Valley of Trials has strained the camp's armory. The weaponsmith, Kzan, is running short on practice gear, and Gornek needs to keep supplies moving to train the next wave. Asking you to scour the grounds solves the shortage while letting Gornek test your diligence and survival skills out in the valley.",al={"gornek motive","why does gornek want weapons","why collect abandoned training weapons"},it="motive",add="c966be67"},{q="What is the Abandoned Training Weapon for?",a="These crude blades and bludgeons were carried by past recruits who proved unworthy or perished before finishing their trials. Left scattered in the dirt, they are still sturdy enough to be restored. Once you deliver them to Kzan Thornslash, he repairs and sharpens them so future recruits have gear to fight with.",al={"abandoned training weapon use","what are abandoned weapons used for","purpose of abandoned training weapon"},it="item",add="42aac14b"},{q="Why does Gornek send a recruit instead of guards?",a="The trial grounds exist to separate capable warriors from the weak. Sending seasoned guards to clean up after failed recruits wastes veteran manpower, whereas sending you serves a dual purpose: you cut your teeth hunting boars in the wilds while proving you can follow orders and maintain the camp's necessities.",al={"why not send guards","why me gornek","why send recruits for weapons"},it="why_me",add="056af0db"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="In Durotar, every scrap of metal counts. As a blacksmith, you reclaim ruined gear and rework battered edges into tools of war.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you learn to respect your weapons. Recovering arms left by failed recruits calls for discipline and self-reliance before combat begins.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you endure in Durotar through grit and resourcefulness, saving weapons even when those unfit to carry them cast them aside."},kw={"durotar","gornek","kzan thornslash","recruits","salvage","the den","training weapons","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:gornek","npc:kzan-thornslash","subzone:the-den","zone:durotar"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Kzan Thornslash",level="2",faction="Horde",id=97279,ri={"Abandoned Training Weapon"}},src={"Wayward Weapons"},fv=true}
E["quest:97281"] = {t="quest",n="A Simmering Storm",z="durotar",s="In Durotar, the Dull Stormy Orb has caught Rezlak's attention. The goblin tinker sees reason to study the relic, recovered from the Dustwind harpies of Drygulch Ravine.",h="In Durotar, the Dull Stormy Orb has caught Rezlak's attention.",sec={{t="A Spark in the Dust",b="Travelers who contend with the Dustwind harpies of Drygulch Ravine may find the Dull Stormy Orb among their strange trinkets. Its worn surface gives off a steady electrical vibration. Dark mist churns within, split now and then by sharp sparks. The relic shows the harpies have handled storm magic.",sp=0},{t="Goblin Curiosity",b="Rezlak waits at the entrance to Drygulch Ravine, where the orb has caught his eye. Its discovery brings to mind advice from his employer, Chief Engineer Gazlowe of Ratchet. What the harpies meant to do with the miniature storm remains unknown. Now the orb is in goblin hands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Dull Stormy Orb?",a="The Dull Stormy Orb is a magical curiosity recovered from a harpy in Durotar. Its dull surface hides a faint electrical buzz, swirling dark mist, and occasional sparks.",al={"what is dull stormy orb","stormy orb","orb from harpies"}},{q="Who wants the Dull Stormy Orb?",a="Rezlak wants the Dull Stormy Orb. He is a goblin scout stationed just outside Drygulch Ravine in Durotar, with an eye for peculiar curiosities and salvage.",al={"who takes dull stormy orb","turn in stormy orb","where to bring orb"}},{q="Why did the harpies have this orb?",a="The harpies' purpose for the orb is unknown. The Dustwind harpies of Drygulch Ravine were using it to channel or contain electrical and stormy elemental forces.",al={"what were harpies doing with orb","why do harpies have storm orb","harpy orb purpose"}},{q="Who is Rezlak?",a="Rezlak is a goblin operative near Drygulch Ravine in northern Durotar. He is affiliated with the Steamwheedle Cartel and Chief Engineer Gazlowe of Ratchet.",al={"who is rezlak","rezlak durotar","goblin near drygulch"}},{q="Where is Drygulch Ravine?",a="Drygulch Ravine is a rugged canyon system in northern Durotar. Hostile Dustwind harpies infest it, harassing travelers and disrupting local trade and settlements.",al={"where is drygulch ravine","drygulch location","harpy canyon durotar"}},{q="What does Rezlak think of the orb?",a="The orb brings to Rezlak's mind lessons and remarks from his boss, Chief Engineer Gazlowe, about peculiar oddities that might prove profitable.",al={"what does rezlak say about gazlowe","rezlak gazlowe connection"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer, you help Rezlak secure mysterious magical artifacts recovered from hostile harpies threatening Durotar's canyons.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you recognize the miniature electrical storm as a reflection of primal elemental forces. Its crude vessel raises questions about the harpies' methods.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you share Rezlak's interest in odd curiosities that spark with erratic electrical charges and swirling internal mists."},kw={"a simmering storm","drygulch ravine","dull stormy orb","durotar","dustwind","gazlowe","harpy","rezlak"},rel={"subzone:drygulch-ravine","npc:rezlak","topic:harpy"},m={faction="Horde",id=97281},src={"In-game quest text: A Simmering Storm"},fv=true}
E["quest:97282"] = {t="quest",n="Stormy Potential",z="durotar",s="Near Drygulch Ravine, Rezlak looks for a way to protect his caravan from harpies. He hopes to charge a drained orb with the electrical organs of Durotar's thunder lizards.",h="Near Drygulch Ravine, Rezlak looks for a way to protect his caravan from harpies.",sec={{t="Seizing Opportunity",b="Near Drygulch Ravine in Durotar, harpies threaten Rezlak's caravan, and a sound magical orb has lost its power. Gazlowe, Ratchet's chief engineer, once advised Rezlak to seize opportunity when it knocks. Now the goblin plans to charge the dormant orb and answer both troubles at once.",sp=0},{t="Harnessing the Storm",b="Rezlak needs strong electricity to restore his drained orb. Thunder lizards live in the gorge west of Drygulch Ravine, and their organs generate and conduct deadly lightning. He asks you to bring him those charged organs. Rezlak hopes to channel their volatile current into the orb and defend his supply wagons from harpy ambushes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Stormy Potential?",a="Rezlak, a goblin merchant and tinkerer near Drygulch Ravine in Durotar, asks for your help. Gazlowe, Ratchet's chief engineer, taught him to seize opportunity, and Rezlak hopes to restore a drained orb with the charge in local beasts' electrical organs.",al={"who gives stormy potential","where is rezlak","rezlak quest giver"}},{q="What is Rezlak trying to charge with the organs?",a="Rezlak hopes to charge an intact orb that has lost all its power. He plans to use thunder lizard organs to defend his caravan from harpies harassing the area.",al={"what is rezlak charging","why need thunder lizard organs","rezlak orb purpose"}},{q="Where are the thunder lizards found?",a="Thunder lizards live in a gorge west of Rezlak's position near Drygulch Ravine in Durotar. You can bring their electrical organs back to him.",al={"where find thunder lizards","thunder lizard location durotar","where are the organs"}},{q="Why are thunder lizards dangerous to harvest?",a="Thunder lizards are dangerous because they release bolts of lightning. Their electrical blasts can teach travelers a painful lesson they may get only once.",al={"why thunder lizards lightning","do thunder lizards use lightning"}},{q="Why does Rezlak fear the harpies?",a="Harpies from Drygulch Ravine ambushed Rezlak's caravan. He hopes the charged orb will deter them or serve as a weapon against further attacks on his shipments.",al={"why rezlak need defense","who attacked rezlak","harpy caravan attack"}},{q="What is Rezlak's connection to Gazlowe?",a="Rezlak looks to Gazlowe, Ratchet's chief engineer, as a mentor and business inspiration. Gazlowe's advice to seize opportunity guides Rezlak's plan for the orb.",al={"who is gazlowe to rezlak","rezlak gazlowe advice"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Using thunder lizard organs to power dormant devices shows goblin ingenuity, though the safety margins are nearly nonexistent.",["faction:Horde"]="Rezlak's work supports the Horde's foothold and travel through Durotar, where marauding harpies from Drygulch Ravine threaten travelers and supply caravans."},kw={"charged organs","drygulch ravine","durotar","gazlowe","harpies","orb","rezlak","stormy potential","thunder lizard"},rel={"npc:rezlak","subzone:drygulch-ravine"},m={faction="Horde",id=97282},src={"In-game quest text: Stormy Potential"},fv=true}
E["quest:97899"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Alchemy",z="durotar",s="An alchemist in Orgrimmar can learn to craft a Mana Well for a camp. It offers healers and spellcasters a refreshing drink, while setting it up calls for a campfire.",h="An alchemist in Orgrimmar can learn to craft a Mana Well for a camp.",sec={{t="A Well for Camp",b="Someone in Orgrimmar asks you to speak with Whuut once you have shown skill in alchemy. Whuut can teach you to craft a Mana Well, a camping item that draws healers and spellcasters seeking refreshment. To set up camp in the wilderness, you also need a campfire. A cooking trainer can teach you how to make one.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who can teach me to make a Mana Well?",a="Whuut in Orgrimmar can teach you to craft a Mana Well once you have shown proficiency in alchemy.",al={"mana well trainer","whuut alchemy","who is whuut"}},{q="What does a Mana Well do?",a="A Mana Well is a camping item that offers a refreshing taste to healers and spellcasters.",al={"mana well use","what is mana well","camp mana"}},{q="Can I set up camp in town?",a="Most people do not care for camps set up in the center of town, so the completion text points you toward the wilderness to try out your Mana Well.",al={"camp in orgrimmar","mana well town","camping town"}},{q="What else do I need for a camp?",a="A campfire is needed as the basis of a camp. A cooking trainer can teach you to make one.",al={"campfire needed","camp setup","fire for camp"}}},kw={"alchemist","alchemy","campfire","camping","healers","mana well","orgrimmar","spellcasters","whuut"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar"},m={faction="Horde",id=97899},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Alchemy"},fv=true}
E["quest:97900"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Blacksmithing",z="durotar",s="In Razor Hill, Dwukk can teach you a camp craft suited to your blacksmithing skill. A Sharpening Wheel gives nearby fighters a way to hone their weapons.",h="In Razor Hill, Dwukk can teach you a camp craft suited to your blacksmithing skill.",sec={{t="A camp craft",b="Dwukk teaches you to craft a Sharpening Wheel once you show skill in blacksmithing. Set it up at a wilderness camp, where nearby fighters and rogues can hone their weapons.\n\nYou need a campfire to start your camp. Cooks can teach you how to make one.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches me to make a Sharpening Wheel?",a="Dwukk in Razor Hill teaches you to craft a Sharpening Wheel once you show skill in blacksmithing.",al={"sharpening wheel trainer","dwukk blacksmithing","who teaches camping blacksmithing"}},{q="What does the Sharpening Wheel do?",a="Nearby fighters and rogues can use a Sharpening Wheel at your camp to hone their weapons.",al={"sharpening wheel use","what's the wheel for","hone weapons camp"}},{q="Where can I try out my camp?",a="Try out your camp in the wilderness. Camps should not be set up in the center of town.",al={"where to set up camp","camping location","camp in town"}},{q="Do I need a campfire?",a="Yes. You need a campfire to start your camp, and cooks can teach you how to make one.",al={"campfire needed","how start camp","fire for camping"}}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can learn from Dwukk to craft a Sharpening Wheel for a wilderness camp.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can hone your weapons at a nearby Sharpening Wheel set up at camp."},kw={"blacksmithing","campfire","camping","dwukk","razor hill","rogues","sharpening wheel","weapons"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","topic:rogue"},m={faction="Horde",id=97900},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Blacksmithing"},fv=true}
E["quest:97901"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Enchanting",z="durotar",s="You can make an Enchanted Lute, but townsfolk dislike camps in town centers. To set up camp in the wilderness, you need a fire.",h="You can make an Enchanted Lute, but townsfolk dislike camps in town centers.",sec={{t="A Campfire First",b="A campfire gives you the basis for your camp. Most cooks can show you how to make one, so seek a cooking trainer if you have not learned the basics.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What can I craft?",a="You can craft an Enchanted Lute.",al={"enchanted lute","make a lute","camping lute"}},{q="Where can I try it out?",a="You need to head into the wilderness to try it out. Most folks dislike camps in town centers.",al={"where to camp","camping spot","try the lute"}},{q="Why do I need a campfire?",a="Your camp begins with a campfire.",al={"need campfire","camp fire","camping fire"}},{q="Who can teach me to make a fire?",a="Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. Ask a cooking trainer if you have not learned the basics.",al={"learn fire","cooking trainer","make campfire"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can teach others to make a fire for the basis of a camp."},kw={"campfire","camping","cooking","enchanted lute","fire","wilderness"},m={faction="Horde",id=97901},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Enchanting"},fv=true}
E["quest:97902"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Engineering",z="durotar",s="A teacher points you to Mukdrak in Razor Hill, who can teach you to craft a Reagent Bot after you prove your engineering skill. The bot helps keep a camp supplied with materials for spells.",h="A teacher points you to Mukdrak in Razor Hill, who can teach you to craft a Reagent Bot after you prove your...",sec={{t="A Bot for Camp",b="An engineer can learn to make a Reagent Bot from Mukdrak in Razor Hill once you show proficiency in your skill. The automaton helps keep you and your allies supplied with materials used to fuel spells. To try it at camp, head into the wilderness; townsfolk do not welcome camps in the center of town.",sp=0},{t="Ready the Fire",b="A camp also needs a campfire before it can be set up. Most cooks can teach you how to make one, so you can seek out someone who trains cooks if you need the basics.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches me to make a Reagent Bot?",a="Mukdrak in Razor Hill can teach you to craft a Reagent Bot after you show proficiency in engineering.",al={"mukdrak bot","who teaches reagent bot","reagent bot trainer"}},{q="What does the Reagent Bot do?",a="The Reagent Bot helps keep you and your allies supplied with materials used to fuel spells.",al={"what bot do","reagent bot use","bot for camp"}},{q="Where should I set up my camp?",a="The completion text advises heading into the wilderness to try the bot, since most folk dislike camps set up in the center of town.",al={"camp where","camping location","where test bot"}},{q="What else do I need before setting up camp?",a="You need a campfire before starting your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make one.",al={"campfire needed","camp setup","fire for camp"}},{q="Who can teach me the basics of making a campfire?",a="Someone who trains cooks can teach you the basics of making a campfire.",al={"campfire teacher","learn make fire","cooking fire"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can learn to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp after showing proficiency in your skill."},kw={"camp","campfire","camping 101","engineering","mukdrak","razor hill","reagent bot"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill"},m={faction="Horde",id=97902},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Engineering"},fv=true}
E["quest:97903"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: First Aid",z="durotar",s="At Rawrk's camp in Razor Hill, capable travelers learn to make a First Aid Kit for the wilderness. The lesson covers where to camp and why a fire matters.",h="At Rawrk's camp in Razor Hill, capable travelers learn to make a First Aid Kit for the wilderness.",sec={{t="Survival on the Frontier",b="Rawrk in Razor Hill teaches capable travelers to make a First Aid Kit. With one, you can tend wounds far from an apothecary or infirmary, where help may be hard to find.",sp=0},{t="The Art of the Campfire",b="Rawrk warns you against pitching a tent in the middle of Razor Hill or another settlement. Find an open place in the wild instead. A camp also needs a fire to see you through the night. Learn basic firemaking from a cooking instructor before you set out.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rawrk and where is he found?",a="Rawrk teaches survival campcraft in Razor Hill, Durotar. He shows capable travelers how to make First Aid Kits for the wilderness.",al={"who teaches camping first aid","where is rawrk","camping 101 trainer"}},{q="What is required before setting up a wilderness camp?",a="Choose an open place in the wild and build a proper campfire. Rawrk warns against camping within town limits and advises you to learn firemaking from a cooking instructor first.",al={"what do i need to camp","how to make a camp","campfire requirement camping"}},{q="Can camps be pitched inside towns or settlements?",a="No. Residents object to tents in the middle of settlements, so find an open place in the wild for your camp.",al={"can i camp in razor hill","camping inside cities","where can i place my camp"}},{q="What does this training teach adventurers to craft?",a="The training teaches you to make a personal First Aid Kit for tending wounds on wilderness journeys.",al={"camping 101 first aid reward","what item does this teach","first aid kit crafting"}},{q="Why does Rawrk recommend learning cooking?",a="A proper camp needs a fire. Cooking instructors teach basic firemaking, so Rawrk recommends learning from one before you set out.",al={"why do i need cooking for camping","cooking campfire camping"}},{q="What prerequisites are needed before learning this craft?",a="You need to show basic proficiency in medical and survival skills before Rawrk teaches you to make a field First Aid Kit.",al={"prerequisites for camping 101 first aid","skill needed for camping first aid"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler, you can learn this training in Razor Hill, Durotar, to help sustain yourself across Kalimdor's rugged frontiers.",["profession:Cooking"]="As someone who knows Cooking, you know campcraft needs fire. Rawrk says a proper camp requires a fire, a skill taught by cooking trainers."},kw={"campfire","camping 101","durotar","first aid kit","rawrk","razor hill","survival","wilderness camp"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill"},m={faction="Horde",id=97903},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: First Aid"},fv=true}
E["quest:97904"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Fishing",z="durotar",s="At your camp, fishing can bring comfort to you and your companions. Near Sen'jin Village, Lau'Tiki can teach you to make a Fish Bowl.",h="At your camp, fishing can bring comfort to you and your companions.",sec={{t="A Camp Comfort",b="Once you have shown skill in fishing, speak with Lau'Tiki near Sen'jin Village. Lau'Tiki can teach you to make a Fish Bowl, a fixture for camp meant to bring joy to you and your fellow adventurers. A happier camp, the giver hopes, makes for stronger fighters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What can fishing do for my camp?",a="Your fishing skill can help you learn to make a Fish Bowl for your camp.",al={"fishing camp item","camping fishing"}},{q="Who teaches me to make a Fish Bowl?",a="Lau'Tiki near Sen'jin Village can teach you to make a Fish Bowl once you have shown skill in fishing.",al={"fish bowl teacher","Lau'Tiki fishing"}},{q="What is the Fish Bowl for?",a="The Fish Bowl is a camping fixture meant to bring joy to you and your fellow adventurers.",al={"fish bowl use","camp fish fixture"}},{q="Where can I find Lau'Tiki?",a="Lau'Tiki is near Sen'jin Village.",al={"Lau'Tiki location","Sen'jin fishing"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a fisher, you can learn to make a Fish Bowl for your camp once you have shown skill in fishing."},kw={"camp fixture","camping","fish bowl","fisherman","fishing","lau'tiki","sen'jin village"},rel={"subzone:sen-jin-village"},m={faction="Horde",id=97904},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Fishing"},fv=true}
E["quest:97905"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Herbalism",z="durotar",s="You learn to make incense candles from wild plants in Camping 101: Herbalism. First, though, a proper camp needs a fire, and your campsite belongs in the wilderness beyond town.",h="You learn to make incense candles from wild plants in Camping 101: Herbalism.",sec={{t="Aromatic Craft of the Wild",b="Herbalism lets you turn gathered plants into incense candles for comfort on the trail. Townsfolk frown on tents pitched in city streets, so these candles are meant for camps beyond guarded settlements.",sp=0},{t="The Heart of the Campsite",b="A campfire belongs at the heart of every campsite. Set one before you use an incense candle. Herbalists provide the aromatic burn, while cooking trainers across the land teach travelers the basics of starting a fire.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is an incense candle?",a="Herbalists craft incense candles from wild plants. Burn one at a wilderness campsite beside a campfire.",al={"what is incense candle","incense candle use","camping herbalism item"}},{q="Where can you set up a camp?",a="You can set up camp in the open wilderness. Townsfolk object to tents spread across town thoroughfares.",al={"where to make camp","can i camp in town","camping in cities"}},{q="Why do you need a campfire to set up a camp?",a="A camp needs a campfire at its heart. Cooking trainers across Azeroth teach basic fire-building techniques.",al={"how to make campfire","campfire needed for camp","cook campfire camping"}},{q="Who teaches how to make a campfire?",a="Cooking trainers teach you to kindle a simple campfire. Learn the basics of cooking before you head into the wild.",al={"who teaches campfires","learn to build fire","cooking trainer fire"}},{q="How does herbalism tie into camping?",a="Herbalism provides the plants and resins for incense candles. Gathered from the wilds, they bring soothing aromas to your campsite.",al={"herbalism connection to camping","why herbalism camping","what does herbalism give for camps"}},{q="Do you need a campfire to use an incense candle?",a="A camp needs a proper campfire. Set one before you settle in to use an incense candle.",al={"can i light incense candle without fire","incense candle campfire requirement"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you learn to make incense candles from gathered plants for use at wilderness camps.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you learn to kindle the campfire at the heart of every camp."},kw={"camp","campfire","camping","cooking","herbalism","incense candle","wilderness"},m={faction="Horde",id=97905},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Herbalism"},fv=true}
E["quest:97906"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Leatherworking",z="durotar",s="In Orgrimmar, Karolek can teach you to craft a leatherworker’s tent once you have shown skill in your profession. A tent offers shelter on your travels, though setting camp also calls for a campfire.",h="In Orgrimmar, Karolek can teach you to craft a leatherworker’s tent once you have shown skill in your...",sec={{t="A Place to Camp",b="A leatherworker in Orgrimmar points you to Karolek, who can teach you to make a tent for your travels. It offers shade on hot days and shelter from rain, giving you a place to rest while journeying. Once you have shown proficiency in leatherworking, Karolek can teach you to craft this camping item.",sp=0},{t="Campfire First",b="Your tent is ready, but a campfire completes the camp. Cooks can teach you to make one, and a cooking trainer can show you the basics. To try your tent, leave the center of town and set it up in the wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who can teach me to make a leatherworker’s tent?",a="Karolek in Orgrimmar can teach you to craft a tent after you show proficiency in leatherworking.",al={"tent trainer","who teaches leatherworking tent","karolek tent"}},{q="What does the tent do?",a="The tent gives you shelter from rain and shade on hot days, and offers a place to rest on your travels.",al={"what is the tent for","leatherworking camping item","tent use"}},{q="Can I set up my tent in town?",a="The completion text says most people do not care for tents set up in the center of town, so you need to go into the wilderness to try it out.",al={"tent in town","where can i camp","camping location"}},{q="What else do I need to start a camp?",a="You need a campfire as well as a tent. Cooks can teach you to make a fire.",al={"need campfire","camp fire how","what completes a camp"}},{q="Who can teach me the basics of cooking?",a="Someone who trains cooks can teach you the basics of the culinary arts.",al={"cooking trainer","learn culinary arts","campfire trainer"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can learn to make the campfire needed to complete a camp."},kw={"campfire","camping 101","camping item","cooking","karolek","leatherworking","orgrimmar","tent"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar"},m={faction="Horde",id=97906},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Leatherworking"},fv=true}
E["quest:97907"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Mining",z="durotar",s="In Durotar, skilled miners can learn to forge a Lodestone for camps in the wild. Krunn in Razor Hill teaches the craft.",h="In Durotar, skilled miners can learn to forge a Lodestone for camps in the wild.",sec={{t="The Miner's Camp",b="Mining yields materials for travel and survival in the wild. With skill in pick and ore, you can learn to make gear for a campsite. In Durotar, Krunn in Razor Hill teaches skilled miners to forge a Lodestone for their travels.",sp=0},{t="Campfire Camaraderie",b="At a wilderness camp, a Lodestone gives the gathered fighters greater strength in battle. Set it beside the campfire, and martial fighters around the flames gain an edge. Townsfolk frown on tents pitched in city squares, so you need the open wild to put your craft to use.",sp=0},{t="Fire and Fieldcraft",b="A sturdy Lodestone needs a fire at the heart of camp. You need a basic campfire before setting up a resting place. If you do not know how to build one, seek a cooking instructor. Cooking teaches the basics for warmth and sustenance on expeditions beyond town walls.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Mining?",a="Skilled miners can seek Krunn in Razor Hill and learn to craft a Lodestone for a campsite.",al={"what is camping 101 mining","camping mining quest","mining lodestone quest"}},{q="Who is Krunn?",a="Krunn trains skilled miners in Razor Hill, in Durotar. Once they show enough skill, he teaches them to make camp items such as the Lodestone.",al={"who is krunn","where is krunn","razor hill trainer"}},{q="What is a Lodestone used for?",a="Miners make Lodestones to place beside a wilderness campfire. Physical fighters gathered around it gain greater martial strength.",al={"what does a lodestone do","lodestone benefit","why craft lodestone"}},{q="Can you set up camp inside Razor Hill?",a="No. Townsfolk and settlement authorities frown on camps in populated streets. Head into the surrounding wilderness to pitch camp and place your Lodestone.",al={"can i camp in town","why cant i camp in razor hill","camping inside cities"}},{q="Why do you need a campfire before setting up camp?",a="A campfire forms the center of a working campsite. Cooking instructors teach you to build a basic fire, and cooking helps prepare you for camps in the wild.",al={"do i need a campfire","how to start camp","fire requirement camping"}},{q="Who can learn to craft a Lodestone?",a="Miners who show enough skill can learn to craft a Lodestone from Krunn in Razor Hill.",al={"who can make lodestones","can anyone make a lodestone"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can unearth raw minerals and make field gear such as a Lodestone to support your allies at camp.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can learn from cooking instructors to build the basic campfire at the heart of a wilderness campsite.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde miner traveling through Durotar, you can visit Krunn in Razor Hill to learn how to make Lodestones for your expeditions."},kw={"camp","campfire","camping 101: mining","cooking","durotar","krunn","lodestone","mining","razor hill"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill"},m={faction="Horde",id=97907},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Mining"},fv=true}
E["quest:97908"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Skinning",z="durotar",s="In Orgrimmar, new skinners are sent to Thuwd to learn the craft of camping. You make a Camp Chair from hides and pelts, then carry it beyond the city to open country.",h="In Orgrimmar, new skinners are sent to Thuwd to learn the craft of camping.",sec={{t="Comfort in the Wild",b="In Orgrimmar, Thuwd teaches capable skinners to make a Camp Chair from cured hides. The pelts and hides of fallen beasts can serve beyond armorcraft. A skinner can put them to use in the wild.",sp=0},{t="Rules of the Trail",b="Thuwd warns that guards and townsfolk frown on camps along busy city streets. A chair belongs in open country, away from settlement walls. A proper campsite needs a warm campfire, too. Cooks across Kalimdor teach the basics of making one.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches skinners how to make camp items?",a="In Orgrimmar, Thuwd teaches skinners how to make camp items. Skinners speak with him after showing basic skill in their craft.",al={"who gives camping 101 skinning","who to speak to in orgrimmar","who is thuwd"}},{q="What camping item can skinners craft?",a="Skinners can make a Camp Chair from the hides and pelts of fallen beasts. It offers a comfortable seat while they rest in the wild.",al={"what do skinners make for camp","skinning camping craft","camp chair skinning"}},{q="Can you set up a camp chair inside a city?",a="City residents and guards frown on campsite equipment in town. Travel beyond settlement gates into the wilderness to pitch camp and set out your chair.",al={"can i camp in orgrimmar","camps in city","where to pitch camp"}},{q="What else is required to complete a camp?",a="A proper campsite needs a fire for warmth, visibility, and cooking. Before you pitch camp, ask a cooking trainer how to build a simple campfire.",al={"why need campfire","camp prerequisites","how to set up camp"}},{q="Why should an adventurer craft a camp chair?",a="A comfortable chair gives you a place to rest between hunts and recover from the road before your next skirmish.",al={"skinning benefit camping","why rest in camp chair","camp chair benefits"}},{q="When does Thuwd teach the Camp Chair pattern?",a="Thuwd shares the Camp Chair pattern after skinners prove basic skill at harvesting skins and hides from fallen beasts.",al={"when can i learn camp chair","camping 101 requirements","skinning skill needed"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Thuwd trains skinners in Orgrimmar, so Horde adventurers traveling from Durotar can learn this wilderness craft there.",["profession:Cooking"]="A proper campsite needs both a seat and heat. As a new skinner, you are encouraged to study cooking basics and learn to build a campfire."},kw={"camp chair","campfire","camping","camping 101: skinning","orgrimmar","skinning","thuwd"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar"},m={faction="Horde",id=97908},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Skinning"},fv=true}
E["quest:98575"] = {t="quest",n="Tainted Tablet",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Tainted Tablet calls new practitioners to Nartok inside the Den. He teaches warlocks to command the Nether and shape their own fate, though its powers must be kept guarded.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Tainted Tablet calls new practitioners to Nartok inside the Den.",sec={{t="A Dark Summons",b="A stone message passes through uneasy camp caretakers to newly arrived practitioners in the Valley of Trials. Nartok, a warlock trainer who makes his home inside the Den, calls them to him. He invites you to leave ordinary tribal duties and study deeper, forbidden magic.",sp=0},{t="Commanding the Nether",b="Nartok speaks plainly about the troubled history between orcs and the Nether. He says the strong should command these volatile powers instead of rejecting them from shame or fear. Where ordinary chieftains falter, he believes those who cunningly master Nether entities can rise to prominence. Yet fearful minds strike at what they cannot understand, so these powers must be guarded closely.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Tainted Tablet?",a="Tainted Tablet is a written summons for an aspiring practitioner in the Valley of Trials. It directs you to Nartok, your trainer inside the Den.",al={"what is tainted tablet","tainted tablet quest","tablet purpose"}},{q="Who sent the Tainted Tablet?",a="Nartok sent Tainted Tablet. He is an orc warlock trainer inside the Den in the Valley of Trials, and calls newly arrived practitioners to instruction.",al={"who wrote the tablet","who is nartok","who sent the tablet"}},{q="Where can Nartok be found?",a="Nartok lives inside the Den, a cavern in the Valley of Trials where darker arts and specialized training take place out of sight.",al={"where is nartok","where is the den","how to find nartok"}},{q="Why does Nartok warn to guard your powers closely?",a="Nartok warns you to guard your powers because ordinary folk may lash out in fear at what they do not understand. Orcs also remember the deep harm demonic corruption caused in their past, so warlocks keep their arts guarded and tread carefully.",al={"why hide warlocks","why guard powers","why secrecy warlocks"}},{q="What is Nartok's view on practicing fel magic?",a="Nartok believes those who master Nether entities can forge their own path and shape their people's fate. Where conventional leaders falter, warlocks can seize power instead of being enslaved by it.",al={"what is nartoks goal","nartok philosophy","why use nether powers"}},{q="Who gives you the Tainted Tablet?",a="A local in the Valley of Trials passes you the tablet. They admit unease with fel spellcasters, but know Nartok's summons must be delivered.",al={"who delivered the tablet","who handed me the tablet"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you receive your first call to Nartok, your trainer in Durotar. He urges you to master the Nether instead of fearing it.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know demonic pacts brought catastrophe to Draenor. Fel magic remains controversial, so Durotar's warlocks counsel both secrecy and boldness.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Thrall's new people are wary of demonic corruption. Warlocks in places like the Den say they can command Nether powers safely and secure their people's future."},kw={"durotar","nartok","nether","tainted tablet","the den","valley of trials","warlock"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials"},m={faction="Horde",cl={"WARLOCK"},ra={"Troll"},id=98575},src={"In-game quest text: Tainted Tablet"},fv=true}
E["quest:98576"] = {t="quest",n="Glyphic Parchment",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Gornek sends young mages to Mai'ah for their first lessons. A runed notice points them to the mage near the Den, where their study of the arcane begins.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Gornek sends young mages to Mai'ah for their first lessons.",sec={{t="A Summons to Study",b="New recruits face Durotar's local pests, but those drawn to magic need more than strength. Gornek gives them a notice marked with runes. It directs novice spellcasters to Mai'ah, who guides the Horde's newest recruits through their first lessons in magic.",sp=0},{t="The Way of the Arcane",b="Just outside the Den, Mai'ah teaches young spellweavers to temper ambition with patience and thought. She urges them to choose their moment instead of casting raw sorcery without care. Her novices learn to weave delicate strands of the cosmos rather than unleash an unruly tempest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends the Glyphic Parchment?",a="Mai'ah sends the parchment, and Gornek hands it to you. The mage trainer waits near the Den in the Valley of Trials.",al={"who wrote glyphic parchment","who sent this","parchment author"}},{q="Where can Mai'ah be found?",a="Mai'ah waits just outside the Den in the Valley of Trials, Durotar, alongside the other class mentors.",al={"where is maiah","mai'ah location","find mai'ah"}},{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="The parchment introduces novice mages to their trainer. Speaking with Mai'ah begins your formal arcane instruction and opens the way to new spells and foundational training.",al={"what does glyphic parchment do","why do this quest","quest goal"}},{q="What is Mai'ah's philosophy on magic?",a="Mai'ah teaches that arcane magic calls for intellect, restraint, and patience. A mage watches carefully, then responds at the right moment.",al={"what does maiah teach","mai'ah lore"}},{q="Why is a troll training mages in the Valley of Trials?",a="The Valley of Trials welcomes young orcs and Darkspear trolls into the Horde. Darkspear spellcasters such as Mai'ah teach their knowledge of cosmic forces to emerging mages.",al={"why troll mage","trolls and arcane","troll trainer in orc area"}},{q="Who delivers the parchment to the player?",a="Gornek, the trial overseer at the Valley of Trials' central camp, gives you the parchment when you return to him during your early duties.",al={"who gives glyphic parchment","gornek quest"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, this missive sends you to Mai'ah to begin your studies and add new spells to your spellbook.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you learn that the Valley of Trials teaches even volatile arts like the arcane with discipline, to strengthen the Horde's future.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you can look to Mai'ah and the Darkspear's growing arcane traditions. She shares her understanding of cosmic forces with fellow trolls and allied recruits."},kw={"arcane","durotar","glyphic parchment","gornek","mage","mai'ah","the den","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:mai-ah","npc:gornek","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","subzone:the-den"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Mai'ah",level="1",faction="Horde",cl={"MAGE"},ra={"Orc"},id=98576},src={"Glyphic Parchment (Forever)"},fv=true}
E["quest:99048"] = {t="quest",n="A Missing Hand",z="durotar",s="In Durotar, reports from Tiragarde Keep have fallen silent around Heglan Shadeeye. The Shattered Hand scout watched the human garrison occupying the keep, and now an investigator seeks her post.",h="In Durotar, reports from Tiragarde Keep have fallen silent around Heglan Shadeeye.",sec={{t="Silent Reports",b="Heglan Shadeeye's reports from Tiragarde Keep have stopped. A Shattered Hand scout, she watched the hostile human garrison occupying the keep from a post in Durotar. Her superiors doubt the soldiers detected and captured her. They fear something more dangerous may have intervened, and send you north of the keep to find her post and learn what happened.",sp=0},{t="The Cold Hut",b="At her observation post north of Tiragarde Keep, Heglan Shadeeye lies dead in the wreckage of a ruined hut. The evidence shows her attacker was not human. What creature or force struck down a trained operative so close to Horde lands?",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the quest A Missing Hand?",a="In Durotar, Heglan Shadeeye's sudden silence has prompted an investigation. The Shattered Hand scout's regular reports from her post north of Tiragarde Keep stopped without explanation.",al={"what is a missing hand","missing hand quest overview"}},{q="Who is Heglan Shadeeye?",a="Heglan Shadeeye is a Shattered Hand operative who covertly watches Tiragarde Keep from a nearby post. Her reports have stopped, prompting an investigation into her whereabouts.",al={"who is heglan","where is heglan shadeeye","missing scout"}},{q="What happened to Heglan Shadeeye?",a="Heglan Shadeeye's reports from a post north of Tiragarde Keep stopped without warning. Her superior doubts the humans caught her and fears something more dangerous may have intervened.",al={"what happened to heglan shadeeye","is heglan dead","heglan fate"}},{q="What is the Shattered Hand?",a="The Shattered Hand is the Horde's organization of subtle operatives, assassins, and spies. Its members carry out covert surveillance and intelligence work to protect Horde territories.",al={"what is shattered hand","who are the shattered hand"}},{q="Did the humans at Tiragarde Keep kill Heglan?",a="Heglan's superior doubts the humans caught her. She watched the hostile Kul Tiras humans at Tiragarde Keep, but the one who sends you fears something more dangerous may have intervened.",al={"did humans kill heglan","did tiragarde soldiers kill her"}},{q="Why was Tiragarde Keep being watched?",a="Heglan watched Tiragarde Keep, an outpost of hostile Kul Tiras sailors and soldiers threatening Durotar's coast. She kept watch nearby and relayed intelligence to the Horde.",al={"why was heglan watching tiragarde keep","tiragarde keep surveillance"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you know the Shattered Hand as the Horde's covert backbone and intelligence guild. A vanished operative shows the danger of field surveillance.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know that watching the Kul Tiras remnants at Tiragarde Keep matters to Durotar's security. A scout's unexplained silence signals a possible threat near Orgrimmar.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know Durotar as newly secured orcish territory. A scout going silent within sight of nearby human squatters raises alarm for the realm's safety."},kw={"a missing hand","durotar","heglan shadeeye","rogue","scout","shattered hand","tiragarde keep"},rel={"quest:1858","subzone:tiragarde-keep","topic:human"},m={faction="Horde",id=99048},src={"In-game quest text: A Missing Hand"},fv=true}
E["quest:99049"] = {t="quest",n="Threat from Below",z="durotar",s="Along Durotar’s eastern shore, Threat from Below begins with an ambush on scout Heglan Shadeeye. The Horde searches her ruined post for clues to the attackers and what they find puts Razor Hill’s defenses at risk.",h="Along Durotar’s eastern shore, Threat from Below begins with an ambush on scout Heglan Shadeeye.",sec={{t="Ambush on the Durotar Coast",b="Heglan Shadeeye’s post on the Durotar coast lies shattered after a fierce skirmish. A Shattered Hand scout, she was keeping watch when an unseen enemy ambushed her. The wreckage shows she fought back and wounded her attackers. With hostile forces moving along the eastern shore, the Horde needs to learn who struck her. You search the campsite and nearby ground for clues.",sp=0},{t="The Serpent Threat",b="The wreckage holds a torn banner and a broken piece of an exotic blade, both belonging to the naga. These serpent-like creatures seem to have moved south along the Durotar coast from Azshara. Razor Hill already faces human invaders from Tiragarde Keep to the south and quilboar in the western canyons. A new attack from the north could overwhelm the settlement’s defenses.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Threat from Below?",a="The Horde investigates the ambush on scout Heglan Shadeeye along Durotar’s coast. You search the damaged site for clues to the unknown attackers, then bring what you find to Orgnil Soulscar in Razor Hill so he can judge the danger to the region.",al={"threat from below quest","what is threat from below","threat from below overview"}},{q="Who is Heglan Shadeeye?",a="Heglan Shadeeye is a Shattered Hand scout who watched Tiragarde Keep from a hut north of it. An enemy ambushed her at her coastal post while she kept watch, and the wreckage shows she fought fiercely. Razor Hill’s leaders need to know who attacked her.",al={"heglan shadeeye","who is heglan","heglan shadeeye lore"}},{q="Who attacked Heglan Shadeeye?",a="Naga attacked Heglan Shadeeye along Durotar’s shore. A torn banner and a broken blade fragment found at the site identify the serpent-like attackers, and the fierce fight left them wounded.",al={"who ambushed heglan","heglan attackers","what attacked heglan shadeeye"}},{q="Who is Orgnil Soulscar?",a="Orgnil Soulscar is an orc authority stationed at Razor Hill in central Durotar. He organizes the region’s defense and coordinates Horde scouts. When Heglan Shadeeye fails to report, he relies on returning scouts and travelers to identify the attackers and protect the settlement.",al={"who is orgnil","orgnil soulscar","orgnil in razor hill"}},{q="Why are the naga a danger to Razor Hill?",a="Razor Hill faces human marines from Kul Tiras to the south and hostile quilboar to the west. If naga establish a permanent foothold on the northern coast, the outpost could be caught between its enemies, its small garrison stretched thin, and Durotar’s reinforcement routes cut off.",al={"why are naga dangerous here","naga threat razor hill","razor hill naga danger"}},{q="Where did the attacking naga come from?",a="The recovered remnants suggest the naga came south along the coast from northern waters, perhaps from Azshara or the Great Sea shelf. They used the waterways to evade inland patrols and strike isolated coastal posts before Durotar’s defenders could organize a perimeter.",al={"where did naga come from","naga origin durotar","how did naga get to durotar"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Searching the coast helps defend Durotar and keep the young Horde from being flanked along its shores.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you see the ambush on scout Heglan Shadeeye as an intolerable intrusion into your settled homeland. It calls for an immediate investigation and retaliation.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you know the naga’s treachery well. Your people have faced sea witches and horrors of the Great Sea."},kw={"durotar","heglan shadeeye","horde","naga","orgnil soulscar","razor hill","scout","threat from below"},rel={"topic:naga","subzone:razor-hill","npc:orgnil-soulscar"},m={faction="Horde",id=99049},src={"In-game quest text: Threat from Below"},fv=true}
E["quest:99051"] = {t="quest",n="Threat from Below",z="durotar",s="Naga scouts are raising camps nearby, and Threat from Below sends you against them. Horde defenders hope to drive the invaders north and keep the area safe.",h="Naga scouts are raising camps nearby, and Threat from Below sends you against them.",sec={{t="Serpentine Incursion",b="Naga raiders have begun raising camps nearby. Local defenders send you to strike before the intruders gain a foothold. You are to slay the scouts and bring back naga spinefins as proof that their camp has been crushed.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Borders",b="The serpentfolk have troubled the area before, and local command will not abide their presence. After you strike the scout camps, surviving naga are expected to flee north. Horde grunts will watch for stragglers and sudden ambushes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Threat from Below?",a="You are sent to slay naga scouts who have begun raising camps nearby. Bring back naga spinefins as proof that you struck the encroaching serpentfolk.",al={"what is threat from below","threat from below quest"}},{q="Who are the snakes mentioned in the orders?",a="The snakes, or snake scum, are naga: amphibious serpentine humanoids who have emerged from coastal or aquatic depths to scout local positions.",al={"who are the snakes","snakes in threat from below"}},{q="Why must the naga scouts be eliminated?",a="Their camps point to an organized scouting effort, not wandering creatures. The local commander wants swift retaliation before the naga can mount a larger assault or strengthen their position.",al={"why kill naga scouts","naga motive"}},{q="Why are naga spinefins collected?",a="Naga spinefins provide physical proof that the scout camps were found and broken. They confirm that the immediate pressure along the border has eased.",al={"why spinefins","naga proof"}},{q="Where are the naga expected to retreat?",a="The commander hopes the strike will send surviving naga north. Grunts will watch for stragglers and suspicious movements.",al={"where do naga go","naga north"}},{q="Who keeps watch after the scouts are slain?",a="Horde grunts are ordered to watch the area for stragglers and further naga incursions.",al={"who watches for naga","grunts naga watch"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help defend Horde-held territory from encroaching naga scouts. Horde grunts will watch for stragglers."},kw={"grunts","naga","naga spinefins","scouts","snake scum","spinefins","threat from below"},rel={"topic:naga"},m={faction="Horde",id=99051},src={"In-game quest text: Threat from Below"},fv=true}
E["quest:99052"] = {t="quest",n="Threat from Below",z="durotar",s="Along Durotar's northern coast, Threat from Below puts travelers and the nearby waters in danger. A sea giant prowls the shore, and defeating it earns the respect of Durotar's warriors.",h="Along Durotar's northern coast, Threat from Below puts travelers and the nearby waters in danger.",sec={{t="The Northern Coastline",b="A sea giant prowls Durotar's northern coast, where the Great Sea meets jagged sand and rocky shores. Scavengers and crabs usually roam there. Now the giant moves through the shallows, threatening coastal travelers and those who secure the waters beside the Horde's new homeland.",sp=0},{t="A Titan of the Waves",b="Sea giants can shatter longboats and crush warriors beneath their fists. Bringing one down is a hard fight for young adventurers. Those who succeed earn deep respect among the orcs. Their cry of “blood and thunder” rings across Durotar's dry red bluffs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Threat from Below?",a="Horde warriors are called to hunt a dangerous sea giant along Durotar's northern coast and bring back proof of the deed.",al={"what is threat from below","threat from below quest","sea giant quest durotar"}},{q="Where is the sea giant found?",a="The sea giant roams the waters and shores along Durotar's north coast.",al={"where is sea giant","durotar sea giant location","threat from below location"}},{q="What kind of creature is a sea giant?",a="Sea giants are massive, ancient coastal behemoths created to dredge the oceans and shape Azeroth's coastlines. Few wanderers survive facing one directly.",al={"what is a sea giant","sea giant lore","who are sea giants"}},{q="Why does the sea giant need to be eliminated?",a="A huge creature prowling so close to Durotar endangers coastal travelers, fishermen, and Horde encampments along the shore.",al={"why kill sea giant","is sea giant dangerous","threat to durotar"}},{q="What does the quest giver mean by 'blood and thunder'?",a="“Blood and thunder” is a traditional orcish battle cry honoring martial strength, ferocity, and glory in victory against dangerous foes.",al={"blood and thunder meaning","orc greeting blood and thunder"}},{q="What proof is required to complete the task?",a="Proof of the sea giant's fall must be brought back from Durotar's north coast to verify that the beast has been slain.",al={"threat from below proof","proof of accomplishment"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Defeating the sea giant removes a dangerous colossus from the shore beside the Horde's heartland.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know honor means facing titanic foes and answering “blood and thunder” against overwhelming might.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face a test of endurance in direct combat with one of the coast's heaviest brutes."},kw={"blood and thunder","coastal monster","durotar","horde quest","north coast","sea giant","threat from below"},rel={"zone:durotar"},m={faction="Horde",id=99052},src={"In-game quest text: Threat from Below"},fv=true}
E["quest:99123"] = {t="quest",n="Lost in the Shadows",z="durotar",s="Pal'juh is lost in dangerous country after setting out alone. Her rescue shows why a hunter needs courage and patience.",h="Pal'juh is lost in dangerous country after setting out alone.",sec={{t="A Reckless Scout",b="Pal'juh went into hostile territory alone because she would not wait for help. A talented hunter, she soon found herself in over her head. Someone had to bring her safely back.",sp=0},{t="Patience of the Hunt",b="After Pal'juh is rescued, her overseers see promise in her as a scout and tracker. Yet she charges like a raptor instead of stalking with a tiger's patience. The wilderness offers little mercy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Pal'juh?",a="Pal'juh is a promising young hunter who heads into danger alone. She has talent, but acts rashly and can be overwhelmed by beasts and the wilds.",al={"who is paljuh","paljuh lore","pal'juh"}},{q="What happens during the quest 'Lost in the Shadows'?",a="Pal'juh went out alone and got into trouble again. Someone had to track her down and help her before she came to serious harm.",al={"what happened in lost in the shadows","lost in the shadows quest lore","lost in the shadows story"}},{q="Why does the quest giver say Pal'juh acts more like a raptor than a tiger?",a="A raptor lunges without caution, while a tiger waits, stalks, and strikes with precision. The comparison warns that Pal'juh needs patience and discipline as a hunter.",al={"why raptor tiger","raptor than a tiger meaning","hunter raptor tiger"}},{q="Who receives the report for Lost in the Shadows?",a="Someone who knows Pal'juh and expects her recklessness receives the report. They are relieved that help came to the headstrong tracker.",al={"who turns in lost in the shadows","lost in the shadows questgiver"}},{q="Does Pal'juh learn her lesson from this misadventure?",a="Pal'juh survived because someone intervened. Her overseers remain watchful to see whether she learns the danger of wandering off alone.",al={"did paljuh learn her lesson","is paljuh okay"}},{q="Is Pal'juh considered a skilled hunter?",a="Pal'juh has raw talent and courage as a hunter. Her mentors warn that instinct cannot replace patience when tracking dangerous prey.",al={"is paljuh a good hunter","paljuh skill"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you need patience and careful stalking, not a reckless charge like a hungry raptor.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you may recognize Pal'juh's eagerness to prove herself in the wilderness before she has mastered restraint."},kw={"hunter","lost in the shadows","pal'juh","paljuh","raptor","tiger"},rel={"topic:hunter"},m={faction="Horde",id=99123},src={"In-game quest text: Lost in the Shadows"},fv=true}
E["quest:cutting-teeth"] = {t="quest",n="Cutting Teeth",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, fresh recruits face their first test against mottled boars. Overseer Gornek sends warriors and spellcasters to thin the herds around the cactus dirt farms and prove they can fight for the Horde.",h="In the Valley of Trials, fresh recruits face their first test against mottled boars.",sec={{t="A Measure of Backbone",b="Young recruits may dream of hunting great beasts in the Barrens or winning glory on a battlefield. Overseer Gornek starts them at the farms instead. Thinning the mottled boars tests their first skill with a weapon or spell. It shows whether they can face a wild attacker and survive their first skirmish.",sp=0},{t="Taming the Red Dust",b="Feral swine roam the dirt farms north and northeast of camp. They root through cactus patches and threaten the few supplies grown in Durotar’s harsh soil. Clearing them keeps local pests in check. It also shapes young orcs and trolls into defenders of their new nation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Gornek send recruits after boars instead of bigger beasts?",a="Gornek sends recruits after boars because the Horde needs them alive. The Barrens hold mighty kodo and predators, but an untried recruit could be needlessly killed facing them. Boars test basic fighting skill without throwing lives away.",al={"why boars","why kill boars","gornek boar hunt"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the mottled boars located?",a="Mottled boars root through scrub and dirt farms north and northeast of the central clearing in the Valley of Trials.",al={"boar location","where are boars","find mottled boars"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the significance of the phrase 'cutting teeth'?",a="“Cutting teeth” means gaining a first practical experience in a craft or calling. For an aspiring Horde defender, it means leaving training dummies and idle talk behind and drawing blood in a fight for survival.",al={"what does cutting teeth mean","meaning of cutting teeth"},it="name"},{q="Who assigns this trial?",a="Gornek assigns the trial. He is an overseer at the heart of the Valley of Trials, where he evaluates and directs new recruits entering Durotar’s training grounds.",al={"who gives cutting teeth","quest giver cutting teeth","gornek trial"},it="in_charge"},{q="Does this complete the training in the Valley of Trials?",a="No. Gornek warns that fighting boars is only a warm-up. More dangerous challenges follow, including facing humanoid intruders and gathering vital valley resources.",al={"is this the last quest","what comes after cutting teeth"},it="next_step"},{q="Why do the boars pose a problem in the valley?",a="Feral boars roam the local dirt farms and brush patches. They endanger workers and eat the few hardy crops, such as cactus fruit, that sustain the encampment.",al={"boar problem","valley of trials boars"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Gornek send me instead of the seasoned warriors?",a="The Valley of Trials exists solely to weed out the weak and forge green recruits into capable defenders of the Horde. Seasoned veterans have far more pressing duties safeguarding Durotar and fortifying Orgrimmar. For an untested novice, battling the local wildlife proves you possess the mettle and backbone required before anyone entrusts you with real military responsibility.",al={"why send me cutting teeth","why does gornek need recruits","why not seasoned guards"},it="why_me",add="852f533a"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Every young champion who enters Durotar starts in the dirt. The Horde’s future rests on their blood and sweat, not unearned prestige.",["race:Orc"]="Orcish culture prizes practical survival and martial honor. Even culling boars is a sacred first step into adulthood and service to Thrall’s new nation.",["race:Troll"]="As the Darkspear tribe rebuilds alongside its orc allies, young troll scouts and mystics prove their self-reliance among Durotar’s unforgiving predators."},kw={"barrens","boars","cutting teeth","durotar","gornek","horde","mottled boar","recruits","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:gornek","quest:your-place-in-the-world","zone:durotar","zone:barrens"},m={start="Gornek",faction="Horde",id=788,ri={"Mottled Boar"}},src={"Cutting Teeth"}}
E["quest:galgar-s-cactus-apple-surprise"] = {t="quest",n="Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise",z="durotar",s="In the Valley of Trials, Galgar sends new recruits to gather cactus apples for a cooling treat. Foraging helps them learn to live in Durotar's dry land.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Galgar sends new recruits to gather cactus apples for a cooling treat.",sec={{t="Surviving the Red Wastes",b="Young orcs and Darkspear trolls begin their work as defenders of the Horde in the Valley of Trials. Combat drills and fierce trials against native beasts leave them tired and thirsty. Learning to live off the land matters as much as learning to swing an axe. Across the valley, cacti bear ripe apples rich with water, a welcome relief from the desert sun.",sp=0},{t="A Valley Delicacy",b="Galgar cooks in the training grounds and knows how to forage. His Cactus Apple Surprise is said to cool a person faster than a plunge into river water. He sends eager recruits to gather prickly fruit from nearby cacti. That keeps his kitchen stocked and ensures new wanderers do not set out into Durotar hungry.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Galgar?",a="Galgar is an orc stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. He prepares cooling provisions and treats such as Cactus Apple Surprise for recruits in the desert heat, rather than overseeing formal combat drills.",al={"who is galgar","galgar lore","who gives cactus apple quest"},it="identity"},{q="What is Cactus Apple Surprise?",a="Cactus Apple Surprise is a popular local sweet Galgar makes with fresh apples gathered from wild desert cacti. Trainees prize the refreshing snack for quick relief and hydration beneath Durotar's blistering sun.",al={"cactus apple surprise food","what is the surprise","galgars recipe"},it="item"},{q="Where are cactus apples found?",a="Cactus apples grow in small clusters on the ground at the base of flowering cacti scattered through the Valley of Trials' red cliffs and canyons.",al={"where are cactus apples","find cactus apples","how to get cactus apples"},gp=true},{q="Why does Galgar ask recruits to gather them?",a="The Valley of Trials is intensely hot, and Galgar cannot leave his post to search the desert himself. He offers portions of his prized treat to passing novices who gather its raw ingredients from the brush.",al={"why gather cactus apples","why does galgar need apples"},it="why_me"},{q="Does this quest connect to a larger storyline?",a="No. The foraging acquaints new recruits with gathering local resources as they complete their first trials for the Horde.",al={"is there a chain","cactus apple follow up","what comes after cactus apple surprise"}},{q="Why is foraging important in the Valley of Trials?",a="Durotar is a harsh land of arid rock and scrub. Horde leaders believe that learning to survive on its sparse natural resources prepares recruits to endure the trials of the wider world.",al={"why forage","survival in durotar"}},{q="Why does Galgar want cactus apples gathered?",a="The sweltering heat of the Valley of Trials is relentless, and Galgar is looking for relief. He craves his signature recipe, cactus apple surprise, which he claims is the best treat to cool someone off under the blazing Durotar sun. By gathering the fruit, you allow him to prepare a batch to beat the heat and share the refreshing food with you.",al={"why does galgar want apples","galgar motive","why gather cactus apples"},it="motive",add="e97f8b04"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Galgar's dish shows the resourcefulness needed to make nourishing food and refreshing treats from tough, prickly desert plants.",["race:Orc"]="Settling Durotar meant adapting to an arid landscape. Dishes made from native cacti show the orcs' practical ability to thrive in their new home.",["faction:Horde"]="Every fresh recruit who enters the Valley of Trials quickly learns that enduring Durotar's punishing sun is part of training, alongside combat."},kw={"cactus","cactus apple","durotar","food","foraging","galgar","horde","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:galgar","subzone:valley-of-trials","quest:cutting-teeth","zone:durotar"},m={start="Galgar",faction="Horde",id=4402,ri={"Cactus Apple"}},src={"Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise"}}
E["quest:lazy-peons"] = {t="quest",n="Lazy Peons",z="durotar",s="Foreman Thazz'ril sends new Horde recruits across the Valley of Trials to rouse sleeping peons. Their labor keeps timber moving to Durotar's settlements.",h="Foreman Thazz'ril sends new Horde recruits across the Valley of Trials to rouse sleeping peons.",sec={{t="Slacking in the Sun",b="Durotar's new homes need timber, stone, and hard labor. Peons have little skill in battle, so they carry much of that burden and keep the Horde supplied with workers. In the Valley of Trials, heat and grueling work drive Foreman Thazz'ril's crews beneath the trees for unauthorized naps.",sp=0},{t="A Swift Wake-Up Call",b="Foreman Thazz'ril gives new Horde recruits his blackjack and sends them across the valley to wake the sleeping workers. Startled, the peons return to chopping wood. Their labor keeps lumber flowing for Durotar's survival.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the peons falling asleep?",a="Hauling heavy lumber beneath Durotar's punishing sun is exhausting work. When no supervisor is near, peons slip beneath large trees to rest.",al={"why are peons lazy","sleeping peons","peons sleeping on job"}},{q="Who is Foreman Thazz'ril?",a="Foreman Thazz'ril oversees the labor crews in the Valley of Trials. They harvest lumber and supplies for the Horde's new construction.",al={"thazzril","who gives lazy peons","thazz'ril"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the Foreman's Blackjack?",a="The Foreman's Blackjack is a heavy leather sap Thazz'ril uses to discipline workers who shirk their duties. A blow to the head wakes a sleeping peon without causing permanent injury.",al={"blackjack","peon club","blackjack tool"},it="item"},{q="What role do peons have in the Horde?",a="Peons make up the laboring class of orcish society. Though physically stout, they are considered unfit for war and instead build, mine, and cut wood for Horde settlements and its war machine.",al={"orc peons role","what are peons","peon caste"},it="people"},{q="Where do I find the sleeping peons?",a="You can find sleeping peons throughout the Valley of Trials, both north and south of the Den. Look beneath wide tree canopies where workers seek shade.",al={"lazy peon locations","where are lazy peons","find sleeping peons"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What happens after the peons are awakened?",a="After you return the blackjack to Foreman Thazz'ril, he sends you to recover his lost mining pick from a nearby cave.",al={"after lazy peons","what follows lazy peons","next quest after peons"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Foreman Thazz'ril want the peons awakened?",a="Foreman Thazz'ril is responsible for keeping the Valley of Trials supplied with timber, and construction demands constant labor. When the peons slack off and nap under the trees, lumber gathering grinds to a halt. Thazz'ril needs them disciplined and actively chopping wood so the Horde's encampment can maintain its supplies and fortifications.",al={"thazzril motive","why wake the peons","why hit peons"},it="motive",add="a41786ab"},{q="Who are you sent after?",a="You are sent after the Valley of Trials' peons, the lowest-ranking laborers of the Horde assigned to harvest lumber from the valley's trees. Rather than working, many have abandoned their axes to nap in the shade. While essential to the valley's supply lines, their notorious lack of motivation requires a harsh reminder to keep them at their posts.",al={"who do I hit","who are lazy peons","target of lazy peons"},it="target",add="088600b8"},{q="Why does Foreman Thazz'ril need you to discipline the peons?",a="Foreman Thazz'ril oversees multiple operations across the Valley of Trials and cannot leave his post to scour every copse of trees for shirkers. With the valley's warrior trainers and guards busy training recruits or guarding against local threats, handing a blackjack to a capable young recruit like you is the quickest way to enforce order among the laborers.",al={"why me lazy peons","why doesn't thazzril hit them","why not guards"},it="why_me",add="94fa6eb4"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As a young orc coming of age, you learn the hard truths and practical discipline of building a nation from the wilderness by disciplining your kin's workers.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll training alongside your allies, you see the brute strength and exasperation behind orcish construction.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know every Durotar outpost depends on timber harvested by peons. Keeping the workers on the job matters to all."},kw={"blackjack","durotar","foreman thazz'ril","lazy peons","lumber","peon","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:foreman-thazz-ril","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","subzone:the-den"},m={start="Foreman Thazz'ril",faction="Horde",id=5441},src={"Lazy Peons"}}
E["quest:sarkoth"] = {t="quest",n="Sarkoth",z="durotar",s="On a southern plateau in the Valley of Trials, Sarkoth has left a young Darkspear hunter near death. Beneath a tree, Hana'zua asks a passing warrior to kill the scorpid and bring back its mangled claw, so his last strike will count for something.",h="On a southern plateau in the Valley of Trials, Sarkoth has left a young Darkspear hunter near death.",sec={{t="A Matter of Honor",b="The Valley of Trials puts aspiring Horde warriors against Durotar's harsh desert. While hunting its venomous creatures, young troll scout Hana'zua met a scorpid far larger and deadlier than the rest. He struck hard enough to mangle one pincer. Then Sarkoth drove its tail into his chest. Now Hana'zua bleeds in the red dirt and fears his life is near its end. He wants the beast dead before it outlives him.",sp=0},{t="The Plateau Terror",b="Sarkoth roams a high mesa above the southern Valley of Trials. Hana'zua shattered one claw, but the scorpid still rules the ridge and attacks anyone climbing the rocky path. Bring the scarred claw back to the wounded scout. Then he will know his last strike weakened the monster enough for someone to bring it down.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Sarkoth?",a="Sarkoth roams the high plateau south of Hana'zua's hiding place. Follow the dirt ramp winding up the canyon wall to the ridge.",al={"sarkoth location","where is sarkoth","how to get to sarkoth"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Hana'zua?",a="Hana'zua is a young Darkspear troll on his hunting trials in the Valley of Trials. Sarkoth mauled and envenomed him, and he lies beneath a tree asking a passing adventurer to avenge him before his wounds claim him.",al={"hanazua","dying troll valley of trials","quest giver sarkoth"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Hana'zua want Sarkoth's claw?",a="Hana'zua shattered Sarkoth's claw with a fierce blow before the scorpid stung him. The mangled claw proves the beast is dead and gives Hana'zua pride in his final fight.",al={"why sarkoths claw","mangled claw proof","hanazua honor"},it="item"},{q="Does Hana'zua die from the venom?",a="Though gravely wounded and bitter over what he sees as failure, Hana'zua finds hope when Sarkoth falls. He sends you to the Den for medical aid.",al={"does hanazua survive","hanazua fate","is hanazua dead"},sp=1,it="history"},{q="What makes Sarkoth different from other scorpids?",a="Sarkoth is larger and more aggressive than the scorpid workers on the lower valley floor. One claw bears the mark of Hana'zua's blow.",al={"sarkoth differences","why is sarkoth special","scorpid boss durotar"},it="target"},{q="What is the follow-up task after killing Sarkoth?",a="After you bring Sarkoth's claw to Hana'zua, he urges you to hurry to the Den. Tell the camp leaders of his plight and bring help before the venom proves fatal.",al={"quest after sarkoth","next step hanazua","back to the den quest"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Hana'zua want Sarkoth dead?",a="Hana'zua believes his life is fading beneath the scorpid's venom, and he refuses to die in disgrace. His father always told him he would amount to little, and perishing alone in the dirt without slaying his opponent would prove those bitter words true. Avenging his defeat is his final chance to uphold his warrior's honor and ensure his last enemy does not outlive him.",al={"why kill sarkoth","hanazua motive","why does hanazua want sarkoth dead"},it="motive",add="2909716d"},{q="Why can't Hana'zua kill Sarkoth himself?",a="Hana'zua is severely crippled and bleeding out beneath a tree. In their clash atop the southern plateau, he managed to strike Sarkoth's claw, but the beast drove its stinger deep into his chest. Poisoned and too weak to stand or return to the Den for aid, he relies entirely on you to finish the hunt before his life seeps away.",al={"why does hanazua need me","why can't hanazua fight","why me sarkoth"},it="why_me",add="3ecf0257"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear, you answer Hana'zua's plea as kin. You see that a tribe member's honorable stand is recognized across Durotar's sands.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know the pain of dying without victory. Avenging Hana'zua lets an untested scout see his foe brought low.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you come to a fallen comrade's aid in the Valley of Trials. That bond gives strength to Thrall's people."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","hana'zua","mangled claw","sarkoth","scorpid","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:hana-zua","quest:804","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},m={start="Hana'zua",faction="Horde",id=790,ri={"Sarkoth's Mangled Claw"}},src={"Sarkoth (quest)"}}
E["quest:your-place-in-the-world"] = {t="quest",n="Your Place In The World",z="durotar",s="Kaltunk sends new recruits in the Valley of Trials to Gornek for training. There, young orcs and Darkspear trolls begin their service to the Horde and learn what honor and survival demand in Durotar.",h="Kaltunk sends new recruits in the Valley of Trials to Gornek for training.",sec={{t="Coming of Age in Durotar",b="Young orcs and Darkspear trolls prove their worth in Durotar's arid Valley of Trials before they enter the wider world. Under Warchief Thrall, life demands strength, vigilance, and discipline. Kaltunk tests each eager recruit and turns their dreams of wrestling demons and dragons toward the practical duties ahead. In the canyon, training begins with humility before glory.",sp=0},{t="Reporting to Gornek",b="Gornek waits beside the camp fire, only steps from Kaltunk. The gruff veteran regards fresh arrivals with a skeptical eye and grumbles about the meager stock reaching camp. He hardens young fighters through trials, beginning with the vermin that threaten the encampment's supplies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="This rite marks a young recruit's entry into Horde service in the Valley of Trials. You go straight to Gornek, who begins your basic combat training and assigns your first duties.",al={"why do this quest","first horde quest","what is your place in the world"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Kaltunk?",a="Kaltunk is an orc overseer at the Valley of Trials entrance. He evaluates recruits coming of age and directs them to the proper trainers and leaders in camp.",al={"kaltunk role","who gives this quest"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Gornek?",a="Gornek is an experienced Horde trainer seated near the campfire in the Valley of Trials. He tests incoming recruits and hardens them into capable soldiers before they leave the canyon.",al={"gornek role","where is gornek"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this quest lead next?",a="Reporting to Gornek leads straight to the trial called 'Cutting Teeth'. Recruits head into the dirt to cull mottled boars and prove their basic martial skill.",al={"what quest is next","next after your place in the world"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are recruits kept in the Valley of Trials?",a="The Valley of Trials is a secluded, protected canyon in Durotar. Recruits train, face evaluation, and are weeded out there before meeting the territory's deadlier beasts, quilboar, and enemy scouts.",al={"why valley of trials","why start here"},it="why_here"},{q="Does this quest differ between orcs and trolls?",a="Young orcs and Darkspear trolls begin training together in the Valley of Trials. Kaltunk gives them the same call to arms.",al={"troll intro quest","orc intro quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Kaltunk send you to Gornek?",a="You have finally come of age to fight for the Horde and win glory for Warchief Thrall. While Kaltunk sees potential in you, he knows eager recruits often dream of slaying dragons before learning the basics. He directs you to Gornek so you can be tested with duties appropriate for a novice, ensuring you survive long enough to become a true asset to the Valley.",al={"why does kaltunk want this done","kaltunk motive","why kaltunk sends you"},it="motive",add="4ca14302"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Every young Horde recruit in Durotar must prove their grit in defense of their fledgling nation before taking up arms in the Warchief's name.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, coming of age and reporting for duty in the Valley of Trials marks a cultural milestone. It centers on personal honor and readiness for battle.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you settled in Durotar alongside your orc allies. Here, you train with your brethren to forge unity and survive together."},kw={"cutting teeth","durotar","gornek","horde","kaltunk","recruits","valley of trials","warchief"},rel={"npc:kaltunk","npc:gornek","quest:cutting-teeth","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},m={start="Kaltunk",["end"]="Gornek",faction="Horde",id=4641},src={"Your Place In The World"}}
E["subzone:bladefist-bay"] = {t="subzone",n="Bladefist Bay",z="durotar",s="Along Durotar’s eastern coast, Bladefist Bay opens onto the Great Sea just beyond Orgrimmar’s gates. Craggy bluffs rise above the shore, with Azshara’s southern coast across the water.",h="Along Durotar’s eastern coast, Bladefist Bay opens onto the Great Sea just beyond Orgrimmar’s gates.",sec={{t="A Bay on the Great Sea",b="Bladefist Bay meets the Great Sea on Durotar’s northeastern edge, east of Orgrimmar, the Horde capital. Rocky cliffs rise above its treacherous surf. Across the water to the north, Azshara’s ancient red cliffs and ruins mark the far shore. Here, Durotar meets the open sea.",sp=0},{t="Shadow of the Shattered Hand",b="Kargath Bladefist gave the bay its name. Chieftain of the Shattered Hand clan, he severed his own hand and replaced it with a blade during the old Horde’s trials on Draenor. Nearby, Skull Rock shelters cultists and hidden rogue networks. The coast recalls the fierce and ruthless legacy of the clan’s chieftain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bladefist Bay named after?",a="Bladefist Bay is named for Kargath Bladefist, chieftain of the Shattered Hand clan. During the old Horde’s trials on Draenor, he replaced his severed hand with a lethal scythe blade.",al={"who is bladefist","bladefist namesake","kargath bladefist bay"},it="name"},{q="Where is Bladefist Bay located?",a="Bladefist Bay runs along Durotar’s northeastern coast, east of Orgrimmar’s main gates. Azshara lies across the water to the north.",al={"bladefist bay location","where is bladefist bay","how to get to bladefist bay"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threats lurk around Bladefist Bay?",a="Skull Rock lies beside the shoreline. Its caverns harbor warlocks, demons, and members of the Burning Blade cult.",al={"bladefist bay danger","dangers at bladefist bay","enemies in bladefist bay"},it="danger"},{q="Why is the bay sometimes called a midden heap?",a="No account from this era calls the bay a midden heap. It is a rocky stretch of Durotar’s coast east of Orgrimmar, facing Azshara across the water.",al={"midden heap","bladefist flotsam","ocean trash bay"}},{q="What is Bladefist Bay?",a="Bladefist Bay is a coastal inlet of the Great Sea along the northeastern shores of Durotar, sitting east of Orgrimmar and south of Azshara.",al={"what is bladefist bay","bladefist bay durotar","about bladefist bay"},it="place",add="6e8d698f"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know the bay bears Kargath Bladefist’s proud and brutal name. It recalls the Shattered Hand clan’s trials on Draenor.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know the Shattered Hand operates in Orgrimmar’s shadows as the Horde’s guild of thieves and assassins. This coast carries a quiet resonance for covert operatives."},kw={"bay","bladefist","durotar","great sea","kargath","orgrimmar","shattered hand","skull rock"},rel={"zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","quest:827","zone:azshara","quest:1858"},src={"Bladefist Bay"}}
E["subzone:burning-blade-coven"] = {t="subzone",n="Burning Blade Coven",z="durotar",s="In the northern cliffs of the Valley of Trials, the Burning Blade Coven threatens new Horde recruits. Cultists and summoned demons haunt the old mineral caves, using them to practice dark magic on Durotar’s doorstep.",h="In the northern cliffs of the Valley of Trials, the Burning Blade Coven threatens new Horde recruits.",sec={{t="A Shadow Over the Proving Grounds",b="Dark rituals now trouble the caves along the Valley of Trials’ northern edge. Imps and lesser fiends spill from the cavern mouth, stirring chaos among the young orcs and Darkspear trolls training here for the Horde. Yarrog Baneshadow leads the Burning Blade cult from deep inside the caves. What was once a testing wilderness is now a battleground against demonic corruption.",sp=0},{t="Corruption in the Rocks",b="Before demons took root, local overseers hoped to harvest the caves’ raw materials for the settlement. Foreman Thazz'ril went inside to survey the minerals, but cultists drove him out in haste, leaving valuable equipment behind.\n\nNow, driving Baneshadow’s coven from the caves is the final proving trial for aspiring warriors, rogues, and spellcasters before they venture into greater Durotar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Burning Blade Coven located?",a="The Burning Blade Coven occupies caves in the high red rock ridges along the Valley of Trials’ northern edge in Durotar.",al={"coven location","where is burning blade coven","valley cave location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who leads the cultists here?",a="The warlock Yarrog Baneshadow leads the coven, directs its rituals, and commands its summoned demons.",al={"coven leader","who leads burning blade coven","yarrog"},it="leader"},{q="What kinds of enemies lurk inside?",a="The caves hold rogue imps, minor demonic servitors, and mortal acolytes aligned with the Burning Blade cult.",al={"what mobs are in the cave","coven monsters","demons in valley of trials"},it="threat"},{q="Why do new recruits go into the cave?",a="New orc and troll adventurers brave the cave’s depths to recover lost tools such as Foreman Thazz'ril's pick. They also slay Yarrog Baneshadow as their final initiation rite before leaving the valley.",al={"why go to coven","coven purpose","coven final test"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Burning Blade Coven?",a="The Burning Blade Coven is a dark cavern carved into the northern red mountains of the Valley of Trials. Once an abandoned cave surveyed for minerals, it has been claimed by demonic cultists who threaten the very proving grounds of the Horde.",al={"what is burning blade coven","burning blade coven lore","what is this cave"},it="place",add="8ab36280"},{q="Is the Burning Blade Coven dangerous?",a="It poses a severe threat to the Valley of Trials. Mischievous imps and dangerous demons have begun spilling out from the cave's mouth, and sinister members of the Burning Blade lurk within its depths. Venturing into the cavern to face these perils serves as the final trial for aspiring orc and troll adventurers before they are permitted to journey into Durotar.",al={"is burning blade coven dangerous","how dangerous is the coven","is it safe here"},it="danger",add="7f26a7cc"},{q="Why is it called the Burning Blade Coven?",a="The cavern takes its name from the Burning Blade cult whose members have secretly occupied its tunnels. They use its secluded hollows as a coven to consort with demonic entities and plot against the young Horde right under the noses of its mentors.",al={"why is it called burning blade coven","burning blade coven name origin","who named burning blade coven"},it="name",add="5cf26a24"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you see an early warning in the demonic imps and dark rituals here, where fel power is wielded recklessly.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you can see the Burning Blade cult near the Valley of Trials as an intolerable insult to Thrall's new Horde. Their presence recalls the demon worship the orcs fought to leave behind."},kw={"burning blade coven","demon","durotar","imps","thazz'ril","valley of trials","yarrog baneshadow"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Burning Blade Coven"}}
E["subzone:darkspear-strand"] = {t="subzone",n="Darkspear Strand",z="durotar",s="Darkspear Strand shelters the trolls who fled the Echo Isles. They came ashore on Durotar’s southern coast and built Sen'jin Village nearby under Vol'jin’s leadership.",h="Darkspear Strand shelters the trolls who fled the Echo Isles.",sec={{t="A Shore of Exile",b="The Darkspear trolls came ashore here after losing the Echo Isles. Witch doctor Zalazane seized their home, so the survivors crossed the narrow waters and landed on this coast. They gathered just yards inland rather than scatter through Durotar’s hostile red wastes. There, they built Sen'jin Village. The strand looks across the surf toward the islands they still hope to reclaim.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened at Darkspear Strand?",a="The Darkspear trolls landed on this coast after fleeing the Echo Isles. When Zalazane turned against his people, the survivors crossed the water and gathered nearby to establish Sen'jin Village.",al={"why is it called darkspear strand","darkspear strand lore","what is this beach"},it="history"},{q="Why did the Darkspear leave the Echo Isles?",a="The Darkspear left the Echo Isles after witch doctor Zalazane betrayed his kin and enslaved his fellow tribesfolk’s minds with dark voodoo. Chief Vol'jin led the remaining uncorrupted trolls away to escape total subjugation, and they landed on this strand.",al={"why did trolls leave echo isles","zalazane exile","echo isles evacuation"},it="origin"},{q="What settlement is located next to Darkspear Strand?",a="Sen'jin Village sits just yards inland from the beach. Refugees founded it after landing, and it is the Darkspear’s main outpost and spiritual center in Durotar.",al={"village near darkspear strand","town next to beach","sen'jin village location"}},{q="What is Darkspear Strand?",a="Darkspear Strand is the stretch of Durotar's coastline situated directly opposite the Echo Isles, lying just outside Sen'jin Village. It serves as the primary shore where the Darkspear trolls washed ashore and regrouped after their tragic retreat from their island home.",al={"what is darkspear strand","darkspear strand lore","about darkspear strand"},it="place",add="88a2cf68"},{q="Why is it called Darkspear Strand?",a="The shoreline bears the name of the Darkspear tribe, honoring their landing here during their evacuation from the Echo Isles. It marks the first safe ground the tribe reached on Kalimdor's mainland after fleeing the treacherous coup of Zalazane.",al={"why darkspear strand","how did darkspear strand get its name","darkspear strand name origin"},it="name",add="504bffc1"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, this shore recalls Zalazane’s betrayal and your escape to found Sen'jin Village.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, this strand marks where the Darkspear made their place on Kalimdor’s southern coast beside their Orc allies after losing their island home."},kw={"darkspear","darkspear strand","durotar","echo isles","sen'jin village","vol'jin","zalazane"},rel={"subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:echo-isles","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Darkspear Strand"}}
E["subzone:deadeye-shore"] = {t="subzone",n="Deadeye Shore",z="durotar",s="Along Durotar’s eastern edge, Deadeye Shore stretches east of Drygulch Ravine. Its barren sands take their name from Kilrogg Deadeye, the Bleeding Hollow chieftain, while raptors, scorpids, and feral boars roam the coast.",h="Along Durotar’s eastern edge, Deadeye Shore stretches east of Drygulch Ravine.",sec={{t="A Shoreline of the Bleeding Hollow",b="Beneath central Durotar’s red bluffs, Deadeye Shore runs past sand and rocky outcrops shaped faintly like a skull with one empty eye socket. The coast is named for Kilrogg Deadeye, the one-eyed Bleeding Hollow chieftain who fought in the First and Second Wars.\n\nNo great settlement or military outpost holds this shore. Aggressive beasts roam the sands, and Burning Blade cultists from nearby ravine hideouts have been seen prowling toward the water.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is it called Deadeye Shore?",a="Kilrogg Deadeye, the famed Bleeding Hollow chieftain, gave the shore its name. Its rocky outcrops also faintly resemble a skull with one empty eye socket.",al={"who is deadeye","why deadeye shore","origin of name"},it="name"},{q="Who lives along Deadeye Shore?",a="No permanent settlements occupy Deadeye Shore. Raptors, scorpids, and boars roam the coast, while fishermen and travelers sometimes pass through and may meet hidden Burning Blade cultists.",al={"who is here","settlements deadeye shore","npcs deadeye"},it="residents"},{q="What threats are found around Deadeye Shore?",a="Aggressive beasts roam Deadeye Shore, and Burning Blade cultists from neighboring Drygulch Ravine sometimes descend from its rocky canyons. They ambush unwary travelers and fishermen.",al={"dangers deadeye shore","enemies here","burning blade deadeye"},it="danger"},{q="What is Deadeye Shore?",a="Deadeye Shore is a rugged stretch of coastline on the eastern edge of Durotar, sitting directly east of Drygulch Ravine. It is characterized by its stark, sun-bleached sands and rocky bluffs looking out over the Great Sea, largely isolated from the settled settlements of the Horde.",al={"what is deadeye shore","deadeye shore overview","where is deadeye shore"},it="place",add="46f1927a"},{q="What happened at Deadeye Shore?",a="Beyond receiving its name in honor of Kilrogg Deadeye, chieftain of the Bleeding Hollow clan, this stretch of coastline has seen little recorded history. Its isolation still makes it risky for wanderers, with raptors, scorpids and boars roaming the sands.",al={"deadeye shore history","what happened here","deadeye shore events"},it="history",add="01a709cb"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you see a shore named for Kilrogg Deadeye. It recalls the old chieftains who shaped the Horde’s history during the wars on Azeroth."},kw={"bleeding hollow","deadeye shore","drygulch ravine","durotar","kilrogg deadeye"},rel={"zone:durotar","subzone:drygulch-ravine"},src={"Deadeye Shore"}}
E["subzone:drygulch-ravine"] = {t="subzone",n="Drygulch Ravine",z="durotar",s="Dustwind harpies prey on supply caravans at Drygulch Ravine in eastern Durotar. Reach their rocky refuge through a cave from Razorwind Canyon or by a perilous leap from above.",h="Dustwind harpies prey on supply caravans at Drygulch Ravine in eastern Durotar.",sec={{t="A Bandit Haven in the Red Rocks",b="East of Orgrimmar, Drygulch Ravine lies sheltered among Durotar's rocky crags. A cramped natural tunnel from Razorwind Canyon is the only way in at ground level. Dustwind harpies roost along the steep cliffs, where they keep their broods and pile up goods stolen from Horde supply trains on the regional trails.",sp=0},{t="A Thorn in Durotar's Side",b="The Dustwind harpies are the ravine's chief danger. Their matriarchs fiercely guard eggs tucked along the high ledges. Horde scouts often send young warriors to thin the flock, recover stolen trade crates, and break the harpies' hold on the ravine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do you get into Drygulch Ravine?",a="You can reach the ravine by leaping from the high cliffs above, if you survive, or through the small cave entrance in neighboring Razorwind Canyon.",al={"drygulch entrance","how to enter drygulch","where is the cave to drygulch"},gp=true},{q="What creatures live in Drygulch Ravine?",a="Dustwind harpies rule the ravine. They nest, lay eggs, and stash stolen caravan supplies along its craggy rock shelves.",al={"drygulch mobs","what is in drygulch ravine","who lives in drygulch"},it="residents"},{q="Why does the Horde care about this ravine?",a="Dustwind harpies raid Durotar's trade trails and hoard stolen cargo in the gorge. Authorities in Razor Hill regularly send recruits to recover provisions and thin the flock.",al={"why kill harpies drygulch","drygulch ravine quests","horde interest in drygulch"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Drygulch Ravine?",a="Drygulch Ravine is a secluded, steep-sided canyon nestled within the rugged crags of Durotar. Accessed primarily through a narrow cave opening off Razorwind Canyon, it offers a sheltered crevasse away from the open plains. It has become a secluded roost for nesting Dustwind harpies, isolated from the major settlements of the Horde.",al={"what is drygulch ravine","drygulch ravine lore","drygulch ravine info"},it="place",add="7b842580"},{q="Is Drygulch Ravine dangerous?",a="Drygulch Ravine is perilous for unescorted travelers and supply caravans. The high cliffs are dominated by the aggressive Dustwind harpies, who swoop down from their roosts to attack intruders and raid passing Horde transports. Navigating the sheer drops and tight crevices invites ambush, especially near their high nests where the fiercest harpies aggressively guard their brood.",al={"is drygulch ravine dangerous","drygulch ravine threats","how dangerous is drygulch"},it="danger",add="c29d93c1"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Securing the harpies' roosts and recovering stolen supplies helps protect Durotar's trade routes from constant banditry.",["race:Orc"]="As a young orc, you can prove your mettle against the fierce harpies perched on your homeland's rocky bluffs."},kw={"drygulch ravine","durotar","dustwind harpies","harpy nests","orgrimmar","razorwind canyon","stolen supplies"},rel={"subzone:razorwind-canyon","quest:834","quest:835","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Drygulch Ravine"}}
E["subzone:dustwind-cave"] = {t="subzone",n="Dustwind Cave",z="durotar",s="High above Razorwind Canyon, Burning Blade initiates train in Dustwind Cave, northeast of Razor Hill. The cave shelters the cult as well as its training ground in Durotar.",h="High above Razorwind Canyon, Burning Blade initiates train in Dustwind Cave, northeast of Razor Hill.",sec={{t="A Shadow in the Cliffs",b="Dustwind Cave looks down on Razorwind Canyon, close to Razor Hill and a danger to the town. Here, the Burning Blade trains recruits beyond the notice of Horde authorities. Cultists teach forbidden dark magic and demonology, preparing initiates to weaken the young orcish realm from within Durotar's borders.",sp=0},{t="Tainted Bloodlines",b="Those who enter Dustwind Cave risk the Burning Blade's corruptions. Cultists wield volatile dark arts, including felblood afflictions. Their work shows the cult's hold on the demonic legacy Thrall fought to banish. Clearing the cabal from the cave matters to Durotar's fragile peace.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Dustwind Cave located?",a="Dustwind Cave lies high on the clifftops of Razorwind Canyon, northeast of Razor Hill in Durotar.",al={"dustwind cave location","where is dustwind cave","how to find dustwind cave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who occupies Dustwind Cave?",a="Burning Blade cultists and initiates occupy Dustwind Cave. The demonic cult spreads fel corruption and seeks to destabilize the Horde.",al={"who is in dustwind cave","dustwind cave enemies","mobs in dustwind cave"},it="residents"},{q="Why is the Burning Blade operating here?",a="The Burning Blade uses Dustwind Cave as a secluded training outpost. Seasoned cultists teach new recruits demonic arts beyond the immediate gaze of guards in Orgrimmar and Razor Hill.",al={"why are cultists in dustwind cave","burning blade purpose durotar"},it="motive"},{q="Why does the Horde want this cave cleared?",a="Demon-worshiping cultists near Razor Hill threaten traveling recruits and Durotar's defenses.",al={"why clear dustwind cave","horde threat dustwind cave"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Dustwind Cave?",a="Dustwind Cave is a small cavern carved into the high cliffs above Razorwind Canyon, sitting just northeast of Razor Hill. Hidden away from the watchful eyes of Orgrimmar's grunts, it serves as a clandestine training ground and safe haven for initiates of the shadow-worshiping Burning Blade cult.",al={"what is dustwind cave","dustwind cave lore","about dustwind cave"},it="place",add="580d7a1c"},{q="Is Dustwind Cave dangerous?",a="It is quite dangerous, particularly for unseasoned adventurers. The cavern crawls with fanatical Burning Blade cultists and their eager trainees. Beyond steel blades and ruthless ambush, these zealots wield corrupting shadow and demonic magic, seeking to spread their dark influence across Durotar.",al={"is dustwind cave safe","threats in dustwind cave","how dangerous is dustwind cave"},it="danger",add="c011eaae"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a Horde warlock, you may recognize the dark rituals in Dustwind Cave. The Burning Blade turns its fel gifts against Thrall's new order.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, Dustwind Cave is a dangerous breach within your borders. It shelters demon cultists within shouting distance of Razor Hill."},kw={"burning blade","cultists","durotar","dustwind cave","felblood","razor hill","razorwind canyon"},rel={"subzone:razorwind-canyon","subzone:razor-hill","quest:827","zone:durotar"},src={"Dustwind Cave"}}
E["subzone:echo-isles"] = {t="subzone",n="Echo Isles",z="durotar",s="The Darkspear seek to reclaim the Echo Isles, now held by Zalazane. They first made their home there after crossing the Great Sea with Thrall.",h="The Darkspear seek to reclaim the Echo Isles, now held by Zalazane.",sec={{t="A Fractured Sanctuary",b="The Darkspear made the Echo Isles their home after crossing the Great Sea with Thrall. Their peace ended when Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's naval forces invaded Durotar during Kul Tiras' attack. The trolls drove back Proudmoore's fleet, but danger rose within their own tribe.\n\nZalazane, one of their witch doctors, took up dark arts and enslaved the minds of his kin. Chieftain Vol'jin and the free Darkspears fled again. Across the narrow strait, they found temporary refuge at Sen'jin Village.",sp=0},{t="Zalazane's Grip",b="Aggressive predators, tainted wildlife, and Zalazane's thralls now overrun the tropical islands. The rogue witch doctor uses malevolent hexes, voodoo fetishes, and ju-ju heaps to bend beasts and captive trolls to his will. Vol'jin's scouts and warriors set out often from their camp at Darkspear Strand. On these frequent sorties, they seek the remains of their fallen and a chance to strike down the mystic who stole their home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why don't the Darkspear trolls live here right now?",a="Zalazane betrayed the Darkspear and used dark magic to strip his kin of their free will, turning them into obedient servitors. Chieftain Vol'jin ordered the tribe to evacuate to Durotar's mainland coast, where they founded Sen'jin Village as a base while they fight to reclaim their home.",al={"why abandoned","why did trolls leave","troll home"},it="ruin"},{q="Who is Zalazane?",a="Zalazane is a Darkspear witch doctor who turned against his tribe. His powerful voodoo and dark magic laid hexes over the islands, corrupted local wildlife, and enslaved fellow trolls as mindless thralls.",al={"who is zalazane","boss on echo isles","witch doctor zalazane"},it="in_charge"},{q="What threats are on the islands?",a="Wild raptors, tigers, and corrupted beasts roam the islands. Zalazane's voodoo heaps and mind-controlled troll minions are there too, including hexed and voodoo trolls.",al={"echo isles mobs","what is on the islands","echo isles dangers"},it="danger"},{q="How did the Darkspear tribe end up on these islands originally?",a="Thrall and the Horde rescued the Darkspear from a sinking island and hostile naga in the Great Sea. The trolls journeyed to Kalimdor, where they were granted the Echo Isles to settle beside their orc allies.",al={"how did trolls get here","darkspear origin","echo isles history"},it="origin"},{q="What are the Echo Isles?",a="The Echo Isles are a tropical archipelago resting just off the southeastern shores of Durotar. Originally claimed by the Darkspear tribe as their new homeland in Kalimdor, the islands are now heavily contested, plagued by wild beasts, hexed trolls, and dark magic.",al={"what is echo isles","echo islands","where are the echo isles"},it="place",add="7222f2f6"},{q="What happened to the Echo Isles?",a="After escaping their sinking homeland with Thrall's Horde, the Darkspear settled the Echo Isles. They were soon forced to evacuate when Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's fleet attacked. Though Proudmoore was eventually defeated and the trolls returned, the witch doctor Zalazane betrayed them, using dark sorcery to enslave his brethren and drive Vol'jin's people onto the Durotar coast.",al={"history of echo isles","echo isles lore","what happened at echo isles"},it="history",add="2c6446a5"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For the Darkspear, the Echo Isles are their promised home in Kalimdor and a reminder of Zalazane's betrayal. Reclaiming them is a matter of tribal survival and personal honor.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, securing the Echo Isles means stabilizing Durotar's southern coast, protecting Sen'jin Village, and holding its borders against naval threats and rogue mystics."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","echo isles","sen'jin village","trolls","vol'jin","voodoo","zalazane"},rel={"topic:darkspear-tribe","quest:826","npc:vol-jin","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","subzone:darkspear-strand","quest:808","topic:kul-tiras"},src={"Echo Isles"}}
E["subzone:hidden-path"] = {t="subzone",n="Hidden Path",z="durotar",s="In Durotar, young shaman climb the Hidden Path toward Spirit Rock. Its high reaches look west across the Barrens.",h="In Durotar, young shaman climb the Hidden Path toward Spirit Rock.",sec={{t="A Sacred Ascent",b="Above the Valley of Trials, the Hidden Path climbs through red peaks and is hard to see from the canyon floor. Mentors send young shaman along it to test their awareness and discipline. Then they commune with the spirits at Spirit Rock. From the highest reaches, you can see west across the rolling savannas of the Barrens.",sp=0},{t="Strategic Vulnerability",b="The Hidden Path cuts through the natural defenses around the valley. A low pass leads toward Ratchet and the road to Orgrimmar. It goes around the usual canyon checkpoints. So defenders fear Alliance infiltrators could take the quiet trail to the Horde's proving grounds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Hidden Path lead?",a="The Hidden Path climbs from the Valley of Trials into the crags and reaches Spirit Rock, where shaman commune with the elements. Its mountain passes also connect toward the Barrens and the coastline.",al={"hidden path destination","where does hidden path go","hidden path leads to"},it="place"},{q="Why is the path significant to shaman?",a="Young shaman in the Valley of Trials take the Hidden Path as part of their early elemental trials. The climb leads to Spirit Rock, where they drink Sapta to commune with the spirits.",al={"shaman path valley of trials","spirit rock path","shaman quest path"},it="purpose"},{q="Could enemies use the Hidden Path to attack the Valley of Trials?",a="Yes. Low gaps along the Hidden Path go around the valley's usual guarded entrances. An Alliance strike force from Ratchet or the coast could slip past Horde scouts and enter the training grounds unseen.",al={"hidden path alliance invasion","is valley of trials vulnerable","valley of trials back door"},it="threat"},{q="What can you see from the top of the path?",a="From the Hidden Path's highest point, you can look west over the Barrens and across Durotar's red canyons.",al={"hidden path view","lookout point hidden path"}},{q="What is the Hidden Path?",a="The Hidden Path is a secluded mountain trail winding through the crags bordering the Valley of Trials in Durotar. Kept largely out of plain sight, it serves as a secret passage leading up to Spirit Rock, a sacred site where fledgling shaman commune with the elemental spirits. From its higher ridges, it overlooks the rugged frontier stretching toward the Barrens.",al={"hidden path durotar","what is hidden path","about hidden path"},it="place",add="d2b4f0e1"},{q="Why is it called the Hidden Path?",a="The path earns its name from its obscurity. Tucked into the crags framing the Valley of Trials, it is not an obvious road or marked route, but a concealed way through the rocky barrier. Finding it is traditionally part of an initiate's trial, testing their perception before they reach Spirit Rock.",al={"why called hidden path","hidden path name meaning","hidden path name origin"},it="name",add="46af627a"},{q="Is the Hidden Path dangerous?",a="The path itself is quiet and free of permanent settlements or monster camps, but its isolation poses a strategic concern. Because a lower gap along the trail provides unmonitored passage out toward the coast, Ratchet, or even northward toward Orgrimmar, it represents an unguarded flank where Alliance infiltrators could theoretically slip into the Valley of Trials.",al={"is hidden path safe","hidden path danger","enemies hidden path"},it="danger",add="a83f5cf6"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you make your first true physical and spiritual climb on the Hidden Path. It tests your perception before you commune with the earth spirits at Spirit Rock.",["faction:Horde"]="Though sacred to shaman, the Hidden Path is an unfortified passage above the Valley of Trials. It leaves a blind spot that calls for a watchful eye."},kw={"barrens","durotar","hidden path","shaman","spirit rock","valley of trials"},rel={"subzone:spirit-rock","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","zone:barrens","subzone:ratchet","topic:alliance","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Hidden Path"}}
E["subzone:jaggedswine-farm"] = {t="subzone",n="Jaggedswine Farm",z="durotar",s="South of Orgrimmar’s main gate, Jaggedswine Farm raises swine to feed the capital. Its shed, pen, and watering hole supply the nearby stronghold.",h="South of Orgrimmar’s main gate, Jaggedswine Farm raises swine to feed the capital.",sec={{t="Provisions for the Capital",b="Feeding Orgrimmar is hard work. Durotar’s red soil supports little farming, so hardy livestock helps feed the city’s warriors and laborers. A timber storehouse, broad wooden pen, and natural watering hole anchor the farm. Here, swine are herded, bred, and butchered to keep the Horde’s granaries supplied.",sp=0},{t="A Quiet Frontier",b="Swineherds and patrolling Orgrimmar Grunts visit the farm, though dry heat can leave it looking half-tended. Wild and mature swine roam inside and beyond the enclosures, sometimes testing nearby guards. At the edge of the valley approach to the capital, the farm is an unassuming but necessary part of Durotar’s daily supply work.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Jaggedswine Farm?",a="Jaggedswine Farm raises swine for meat and lard, feeding the people and garrison of nearby Orgrimmar.",al={"what is jaggedswine farm","why is there a pig farm in durotar","jaggedswine farm purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Where exactly is Jaggedswine Farm located?",a="Jaggedswine Farm lies in northern Durotar, just outside the southern approach and grand gates leading into Orgrimmar’s Valley of Strength.",al={"where is jaggedswine farm","how to get to jaggedswine farm","pig farm durotar location"},gp=true},{q="Why does the farm look somewhat deserted?",a="Orcish livestock farming in Durotar is utilitarian and unglamorous. Free-roaming boars and sparse timber buildings leave the farm without grand homesteads, but Horde supply lines still use it.",al={"is jaggedswine farm abandoned","who lives at jaggedswine farm","why no farmers"},it="ruin"},{q="Are the pigs here dangerous to travelers?",a="The domesticated swine inside the pens are docile, but wild and mature boars on the outskirts can turn aggressive if startled by young travelers or careless foragers.",al={"are swine hostile","do pigs attack here","swine dangerous"},it="danger"},{q="What is Jaggedswine Farm?",a="Jaggedswine Farm is one of several swine-breeding homesteads situated just south of the gates of Orgrimmar in northern Durotar. Established to supply essential provisions to the Orcish capital, the modest settlement consists of an enclosure for livestock, a storage house, and a nearby watering pond. While practical for the Horde's sustenance, it stands exposed in the harsh, dry terrain outside the city walls.",al={"what is jaggedswine farm","jaggedswine farm info","tell me about jaggedswine farm"},it="place",add="62544dd9"},{q="Why is it called Jaggedswine Farm?",a="The farm takes its name from the distinctive, bristled swine raised here to feed the growing population of Orgrimmar. Like much of the wildlife surviving in Durotar's unforgiving landscape, these hardy beasts sport rugged hides and sharp features suited to the barren clay and rock of the canyon plains.",al={"why called jaggedswine","jaggedswine farm name origin","why jaggedswine"},it="name",add="00bf6885"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a Horde cook learning the trade in Durotar, you can find tender ribs, pork cuts, and cooking grease among the swine raised around Jaggedswine Farm, a primary local source.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know steady meat supplies in Durotar’s arid wastes mean survival. Jaggedswine Farm helps sustain Orgrimmar’s military strength."},kw={"boars","durotar","horde provisions","jaggedswine farm","orgrimmar","pig pen","pigs","swine"},rel={"zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:gates-of-orgrimmar","topic:horde"},src={"Jaggedswine Farm"}}
E["subzone:kolkar-crag"] = {t="subzone",n="Kolkar Crag",z="durotar",s="Kolkar centaur watch the southern Durotar flats from Kolkar Crag and launch raids from the gorge. Warlord Kolkanis leads them against nearby Horde settlements.",h="Kolkar centaur watch the southern Durotar flats from Kolkar Crag and launch raids from the gorge.",sec={{t="A Thorn in Durotar's Side",b="Kolkar centaur hold a fortified gorge in southern Durotar. They guard its narrow passages and watch the flats for openings in orc and Darkspear holdings. From the crag, scouts and marauders probe those defenses. For young warriors training in the Valley of Trials and patrols along the southern coast, this is the nearest organized centaur threat.",sp=0},{t="Schemes of Invasion",b="Warlord Kolkanis commands the centaur at Kolkar Crag, and their plans reach beyond skirmishes. Recovered attack plans name the Valley of Trials, Sen'jin Village, Razor Hill, and even the gates of Orgrimmar as targets. To stop the assaults, Horde forces must strike deep into the ravine, kill Kolkanis, and break the centaur muster before their war parties sweep through the valleys.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who lives in Kolkar Crag?",a="Kolkar centaur live in Kolkar Crag under Warlord Kolkanis. They use the canyon as a camp and raiding post against Horde outposts throughout Durotar.",al={"who is at kolkar crag","kolkar crag inhabitants","who owns kolkar crag"},it="residents"},{q="Why is the Horde concerned about this ravine?",a="Centaur in the gorge have planned coordinated assaults on Durotar's vital settlements: the Valley of Trials, Sen'jin Village, Razor Hill, and Orgrimmar.",al={"why care about kolkar crag","is kolkar crag dangerous","kolkar threat"},it="threat"},{q="Who leads the centaur here?",a="Warlord Kolkanis commands the centaur encampment. He directs their scouting and plans attacks against the orcs and trolls.",al={"kolkar crag boss","who leads kolkar crag","warlord kolkanis"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is Kolkar Crag?",a="Kolkar Crag is a rugged, craggy gorge located in southern Durotar. It serves as an entrenched stronghold for the hostile Kolkar centaur, who have carved out a base within its natural canyons dangerously close to vital Horde settlements.",al={"kolkar crag location","what is kolkar crag","kolkar crag overview"},it="place",add="e91c2682"},{q="What happened at Kolkar Crag?",a="Following the Third War, Kolkar centaur fortified themselves within this ravine, using it as a staging ground to plan coordinated attacks against Durotar settlements, including Sen'jin Village, Razor Hill, the Valley of Trials, and Orgrimmar itself.",al={"kolkar crag history","history of kolkar crag","events at kolkar crag"},it="history",add="b1f68783"},{q="Is Kolkar Crag dangerous?",a="Yes, it is exceptionally dangerous. The gorge is teeming with aggressive Kolkar centaur led by Warlord Kolkanis, all organized and preparing raids against nearby settlements. Unwary travelers wandering into the ravine will quickly find themselves ambushed and outnumbered.",al={"how dangerous is kolkar crag","is kolkar crag safe"},it="danger",add="a74eb943"},{q="Why is it called Kolkar Crag?",a="The ravine takes its name directly from the Kolkar clan of centaur that claimed and established their stronghold within the rocky gorge.",al={"kolkar crag name meaning","why kolkar crag"},it="name",add="86a855ff"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Centaur near the Valley of Trials threaten the initiation of young orcs. Pacifying Kolkar Crag is an urgent matter of territorial defense.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing southern Durotar against centaur incursions protects the supply lines between Sen'jin Village and the road to Orgrimmar."},kw={"centaur","durotar","kolkanis","kolkar","kolkar crag","sen'jin village","valley of trials","warlord kolkanis"},rel={"quest:786","topic:centaur","zone:durotar","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:razor-hill","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Kolkar Crag"}}
E["subzone:orgrimmar"] = {t="subzone",n="Orgrimmar",z="durotar",s="In northern Durotar, Orgrimmar shelters the New Horde as its warrior capital. Warchief Thrall founded the city in memory of Orgrim Doomhammer. Its red canyons shelter the orcs’ renewal and their struggle to survive on Kalimdor.",h="In northern Durotar, Orgrimmar shelters the New Horde as its warrior capital.",sec={{t="A Stronghold in the Stone",b="After the victory at Mount Hyjal, Warchief Thrall led his surviving people south to make a homeland in Durotar. They built Orgrimmar among steep mountain crags, with spiked timber walls, stone watchtowers, and caverns cut deep into the mountains.\n\nDarkspear trolls, tauren stonemasons, and goblin engineers helped raise the fortress. Its defenses turned the wilderness into a stronghold built to withstand a siege.",sp=0},{t="Heart of the New Horde",b="Freed from the demonic bloodlust that once bound them, the orcs built Orgrimmar as a beacon of honor, community, and survival. Orcs and Darkspear trolls live in the city. Emissaries from the tauren of Mulgore and the newly allied Forsaken are welcomed there.\n\nShamans teach the next generation ancestral balance. In gladiatorial rings, veterans clash to hone the army that guards Kalimdor’s fragile peace.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Orgrimmar named after?",a="Warchief Thrall named Orgrimmar for his mentor and predecessor, the legendary orc Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer. Doomhammer fell in the Eastern Kingdoms while freeing the orc internment camps. He gave Thrall his iconic warplate and battle hammer.",al={"orgrimmar name origin","why called orgrimmar","who was orgrimmar named for"},it="name"},{q="Who helped build the city?",a="Orcs, Darkspear trolls, tauren, hired goblin sappers and engineers, and the wandering champion Rexxar rapidly raised Orgrimmar. They carved and fortified its natural stone walls to provide swift, defensible shelter in Durotar’s harsh terrain.",al={"who built orgrimmar","how was orgrimmar made","orgrimmar builders"},it="origin"},{q="Which races call Orgrimmar home?",a="Orcs and Sen'jin's Darkspear trolls share Orgrimmar’s districts. Tauren travelers often reside there as steadfast allies. Envoys of the recently accepted Forsaken have begun establishing a quiet foothold.",al={"who lives in orgrimmar","orgrimmar residents","races in orgrimmar"},it="residents"},{q="Where does Warchief Thrall reside?",a="Thrall resides in Grommash Hold, a central stronghold in Orgrimmar’s Valley of Wisdom. The hold honors his fallen friend, Grom Hellscream.",al={"where is thrall","thrall location orgrimmar","warchief seat"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is Orgrimmar?",a="Orgrimmar is the mighty capital city of the orcs and the primary seat of the entire Horde. Carved deep into the jagged red-rock canyons on the northern border of Durotar, it stands as an imposing warrior fortress guarded by towering wooden ramparts, iron gates, and natural mountain barriers. For travelers and heroes of the Horde, it serves as the beating heart of trade, training, and leadership.",al={"what is orgrimmar","about orgrimmar","orgrimmar overview"},it="place",add="4128ed5a"},{q="What is the history behind the founding of Orgrimmar?",a="Following the Third War and the Battle of Mount Hyjal, Warchief Thrall led the orcs to Kalimdor to claim a new homeland free of demonic corruption. Aided by the tauren, the Darkspear trolls, and Rexxar, the Horde rapidly carved the fortress city into the rocky valleys of Durotar. Despite violent skirmishes with native centaur, harpies, and quilboar, the stronghold endured and established the Horde's enduring presence on the continent.",al={"orgrimmar history","how was orgrimmar founded","founding of orgrimmar"},it="history",add="96f2b3eb"},{q="Is Orgrimmar dangerous?",a="For loyal members of the Horde, Orgrimmar is a secure and welcoming sanctuary, fiercely guarded by seasoned warriors and Kor'kron protectors. However, any Alliance trespasser foolish enough to step near its gates will be hunted down and slain on sight. Beyond its outer walls, the surrounding canyons of Durotar also harbor lurking threats like hostile quilboar, harpies, and rogue cultists.",al={"is orgrimmar dangerous","orgrimmar threats","threats in orgrimmar"},it="danger",add="98ddc713"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As the Horde’s supreme seat of leadership, Orgrimmar is the center for military campaigns, clan alliances, and diplomacy across Kalimdor and beyond.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you can see Orgrimmar as the realization of your people’s redemption. There, they cast off the demonic curse’s legacy and build an honorable, independent future."},kw={"darkspear","doomhammer","durotar","grommash hold","new horde","orgrimmar","tauren","thrall"},rel={"zone:durotar","npc:thrall","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","subzone:grommash-hold","subzone:drag","topic:new-horde","topic:darkspear-tribe","topic:tauren"},src={"Orgrimmar"}}
E["subzone:razor-hill"] = {t="subzone",n="Razor Hill",z="durotar",s="At Razor Hill, young orc and troll warriors train before setting out into Durotar. The fortified barracks stand at a crossroads linking the Valley of Trials, the Barrens, and Orgrimmar.",h="At Razor Hill, young orc and troll warriors train before setting out into Durotar.",sec={{t="Heart of Durotar",b="Razor Hill joins northern Durotar to the southern coast and the Barrens across the Southfury River. Stone-and-timber barracks and orcish burrows fill the settlement, founded early in Durotar's settlement. After the Third War, human forces from Kul Tiras lured the Horde here with a false offer of an emissary summit. Rexxar went in Thrall's stead and stopped their ambush. Razor Hill is fortified now against further attacks from the coast.",sp=0},{t="Watch on the Frontier",b="Veteran officers such as Gar'Thok direct Razor Hill's defenses against nearby threats. Human marines still hold Tiragarde Keep on the eastern shore, while quilboar and harpy tribes harass supply lines. Investigators such as Orgnil Soulscar track the Burning Blade cult. Its rituals and corrupted agents lurk in nearby crags, and the investigators work to stamp them out.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Razor Hill's purpose in Durotar?",a="Razor Hill is Durotar's main administrative and defensive outpost. It links the southern shores and Valley of Trials with Orgrimmar to the north and the Barrens to the west. It also supplies and trains young adventurers.",al={"why is razor hill here","razor hill purpose","what is razor hill"},it="purpose"},{q="What happened here during the Kul Tiras invasion?",a="After the Third War, Kul Tiras forces offered Warchief Thrall a peaceful summit at Razor Hill. Rexxar suspected treachery and went in Thrall's place. He uncovered the ambush and defeated the human assassins.",al={"kul tiras ambush","rexxar razor hill","what happened at razor hill summit"},it="history"},{q="Who commands the settlement?",a="The orc veteran Gar'Thok commands Razor Hill's garrison from the town barracks. He oversees patrols against human remnants and local wild beasts.",al={"razor hill leader","who runs razor hill","gar'thok"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the Burning Blade doing near Razor Hill?",a="The Burning Blade cult has infiltrated hidden crags and canyons in central Durotar. Horde scouts working from Razor Hill follow Orgnil Soulscar's direction as they uncover its covens and try to end its influence.",al={"burning blade durotar","orgnil soulscar","cultists near razor hill"},it="threat"},{q="What is Razor Hill?",a="Razor Hill is the principal orcish settlement in central Durotar. Built around a major crossroads, it connects the road north to Orgrimmar, south to Sen'jin Village and the Valley of Trials, and west toward the Barrens. Dominated by its stout military barracks and watchtower, the fortified outpost serves as both a thriving civic hub for local orc laborers and farmers and a vital defensive bulwark defending the heart of Durotar.",al={"about razor hill","razor hill overview","what kind of town is razor hill"},it="place",add="77896146"},{q="Is Razor Hill dangerous?",a="Within its walls, Razor Hill is well defended by Horde guards and watchful grunts, making it a safe haven for weary travelers. However, the surrounding territory is fraught with peril. Human marine scouts from Tiragarde Keep frequently probe near the roads, foul cultists of the Burning Blade lurk in nearby canyons, and venomous wildlife like scorpid and raptors prowl just outside the town's perimeter.",al={"is razor hill safe","threats to razor hill","razor hill danger"},it="danger",add="413cce6a"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For Horde soldiers, Razor Hill is the first true town after the training grounds. Here, young recruits set out to prove their loyalty to Thrall's new nation.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you can see the life your people have carved out in Durotar: sturdy burrows, hard-won survival, and freedom from demonic servitude."},kw={"barracks","burning blade","durotar","gar'thok","kul tiras","orgnil soulscar","razor hill"},rel={"zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:tiragarde-keep","npc:gar-thok","npc:orgnil-soulscar","zone:barrens"},src={"Razor Hill"}}
E["subzone:razor-hill-watchtower"] = {t="subzone",n="Razor Hill Watchtower",z="durotar",s="Furl Scornbrow watches Durotar from the Razor Hill Watchtower. From the red stone bluffs, he keeps watch over the plains and coast, guarding the settlement below.",h="Furl Scornbrow watches Durotar from the Razor Hill Watchtower.",sec={{t="Eyes Over Durotar",b="Above Razor Hill, the watchtower looks out across the settlement and the surrounding canyons. Thick timber and iron hold the outpost firm. Durotar faces Kul Tiras marines along the eastern shore, quilboar raiders across the scrublands, and Burning Blade cultists in nearby crags. From the ridgeline, a lookout can spot warbands, smoke signals, and incursions before they reach the gates.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Razor Hill Watchtower?",a="The Razor Hill Watchtower is the main lookout for Razor Hill and central Durotar. From its height, scouts watch the trails for hostile beasts and troop movements from nearby Alliance camps or centaur raiding parties.",al={"why is the watchtower here","watchtower purpose","razor hill tower"},it="purpose"},{q="Who guards the watchtower?",a="Furl Scornbrow, an aging orc, watches for invaders and sounds his signal horn when needed. As Durotar has grown more settled, he has also taken to making bags for young adventurers.",al={"who is at the tower","watchtower guards"},it="in_charge"},{q="What threats can be seen from up here?",a="Scouts watch for aggressive quilboar of the Razormane tribes, human infiltrators from Tiragarde Keep along the eastern coast, and wild beasts in the dry valleys.",al={"threats to razor hill","what are they looking for"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Razor Hill Watchtower?",a="Perched on the red bluffs high above the settlement of Razor Hill, this wooden Horde fortification commands a sweeping view across Durotar. It serves as an early warning post for the nearby crossroads, letting sentries monitor the dusty canyon roads, the southern coastline, and any movement of hostile quilboar, centaur, or Alliance infiltrators creeping inland from the Great Sea.",al={"what is razor hill watchtower","razor hill tower","watchtower razor hill"},it="place",add="e22a9f25"},{q="Is the Razor Hill Watchtower dangerous?",a="The watchtower is a Horde lookout above Razor Hill. Furl Scornbrow keeps watch for invaders, though he says the need to sound his signal horn has grown less frequent as Durotar has become settled.",al={"is razor hill watchtower safe","danger razor hill watchtower"},it="danger",add="9138eaa5"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For young warriors and scouts leaving the Valley of Trials, the watchtower is a reassuring sign of the fledgling Horde’s safety and strength.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can use the watchtower’s high, open vantage point to track quarry and watch the beasts move across Durotar."},kw={"durotar","lookout","razor hill","razor hill watchtower","sentry","watchtower"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Razor Hill Watchtower"},nf=true}
E["subzone:razormane-grounds"] = {t="subzone",n="Razormane Grounds",z="durotar",s="Razormane quilboar press east from the Barrens into central Durotar. Their thorn-choked camp marks the front of a long struggle with Orgrimmar's orcs.",h="Razormane quilboar press east from the Barrens into central Durotar.",sec={{t="A Thorn in Durotar's Side",b="At the Southfury River, Razormane Grounds threaten travelers beneath central Durotar's red cliffs. Here the quilboar have spread farther east from the Barrens than anywhere else. Captain Flat Tusk of the Battleguard and Geolord Mottle lead raids on nearby orc settlements and passing supply lines. Patrols leave Razor Hill and nearby outposts, yet the Razormane replenish their ranks among the briars faster than the Horde can clear them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Razormane Grounds?",a="Razormane Grounds is a fortified quilboar camp in central Durotar, where the Razormane press east from the Barrens.",al={"razormane grounds","quilboar camp durotar","where are razormane"},it="place"},{q="Why are the quilboar attacking Durotar?",a="The Razormane claim neighboring lands and seek to expand their thorny thickets and hunting grounds at the expense of the Horde's new settlements.",al={"why quilboar attack","why are razormane here","quilboar invasion"},it="conflict"},{q="Who leads the quilboar at the Razormane Grounds?",a="Captain Flat Tusk leads the Razormane Battleguard alongside Geolord Mottle, an earth-shaping geomancer.",al={"razormane bosses","who leads the razormane grounds","captain flat tusk"},it="leader"},{q="Why are there so many bones around the camp?",a="The Razormane hunt and scavenge aggressively, stripping local wildlife to the bone to feed their raiders. They leave the carcasses around the camp as markers of their territory.",al={"bones in camp","razormane animal carcasses","why dead animals"}},{q="What happened at the Razormane Grounds?",a="When the orcs founded Durotar, the Razormane quilboar pushed eastward out of the Barrens to expand their territory. The Razormane Grounds became the front line of that invasion. The orcs have fought relentlessly to hold them back from Durotar's heartland, but for every quilboar slain among the brambles, more seem to emerge from the thickets to press the assault.",al={"razormane grounds history","what happened at razormane grounds","razormane invasion durotar"},it="history",add="cce0af6c"},{q="Who lives at the Razormane Grounds?",a="The encampment is home to an aggressive war band of Razormane quilboar pushing into Durotar. The camp is commanded by Captain Flat Tusk, who leads their battleguard, alongside the geomancer Geolord Mottle, who commands earth magic among the brambles.",al={"who lives at razormane grounds","razormane grounds inhabitants","who is at razormane grounds"},it="residents",add="8556a3c9"},{q="Is the Razormane Grounds dangerous?",a="Yes. It serves as an active forward war camp crawling with hostile quilboar warriors and geomancers. The Razormane fiercely butcher intruders and local wildlife alike, littering the area with stripped bones, and the dense thorn brambles make any retreat perilous.",al={"is razormane grounds dangerous","danger razormane grounds","how dangerous are razormane grounds"},it="danger",add="b58c6eb9"},{q="Why is it called the Razormane Grounds?",a="The grounds are named after the Razormane tribe of quilboar, who established this sprawling encampment as a staging area for their territorial push into Durotar.",al={"why is it called razormane grounds","razormane grounds name meaning","where did razormane grounds get its name"},it="name",add="a76ef142"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For orcs in Durotar, Razormane Grounds threaten the heart of their new homeland. Young warriors prove their mettle by culling the quilboar.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, suppressing Razormane Grounds helps secure travel and supply lines between the Barrens and Orgrimmar."},kw={"captain flat tusk","durotar","geolord mottle","quilboar","raggaran","razormane","razormane grounds"},rel={"zone:durotar","topic:quilboar","zone:barrens"},src={"Razormane Grounds"}}
E["subzone:razorwind-canyon"] = {t="subzone",n="Razorwind Canyon",z="durotar",s="Dustwind harpies threaten travelers on Razorwind Canyon’s road between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar. The rocky gulch cuts through Durotar, making the route north toward the Horde capital dangerous.",h="Dustwind harpies threaten travelers on Razorwind Canyon’s road between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Threat on the High Road",b="Razorwind Canyon follows the main road from Razor Hill to Orgrimmar. Its gullies reach east into the bluffs and west toward Tor'kren Farm. Dustwind harpies roost among the rocks and attack travelers who stray too close. With the canyon so near the capital’s trade route, Durotar’s defenders must watch its gullies.",sp=0},{t="Passages and Ravines",b="Razorwind Canyon’s winding passages cut through Durotar’s red rock hills. One eastern branch runs deep into the crags, through a cavern, and into Drygulch Ravine. Harpies roost on high perches, then descend in flocks. Travelers crossing the passes can be surrounded and cut down.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Razorwind Canyon located?",a="Razorwind Canyon runs along both sides of the main road between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar in central Durotar. Entrances lie north of Razor Hill, near Tor'kren Farm, and through a cave leading to Drygulch Ravine.",al={"razorwind canyon location","where is razorwind canyon","how to find razorwind canyon"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What creatures inhabit Razorwind Canyon?",a="Dustwind harpies inhabit Razorwind Canyon. They nest in its gullies and rocky outcroppings, preying on unwary travelers.",al={"razorwind mobs","what lives in razorwind canyon","harpy canyon durotar"},it="residents"},{q="Why is the Horde concerned about this canyon?",a="The Horde is concerned because Razorwind Canyon borders the main trade and travel route between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar. Nesting harpies harass couriers, supply caravans, and other travelers on the central road.",al={"why care about razorwind","orgrimmar threat razorwind"},it="threat"},{q="Does Razorwind Canyon connect to other areas?",a="Yes. Razorwind Canyon opens onto the main road and has trails west toward Tor'kren Farm. An eastern cavern leads into Drygulch Ravine.",al={"canyon connections","where does razorwind lead"},gp=true},{q="What is Razorwind Canyon?",a="Razorwind Canyon is a jagged canyon flanking the main road between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar in central Durotar. Split into eastern and western ravines, the crags serve as the primary nesting grounds for the savage Dustwind harpies, posing a constant danger to travelers journeying along the Horde's vital overland routes.",al={"razorwind canyon lore","about razorwind canyon","what is razorwind"},it="place",add="8d215d8c"},{q="Is Razorwind Canyon dangerous?",a="Yes, it is very dangerous. Razorwind Canyon swarms with aggressive Dustwind harpies who fiercely defend their nesting perches. Their overwhelming numbers and vicious nature make it easy for unwary travelers or lone wanderers to be swarmed, subdued, and killed if they venture off the road into the canyon depths.",al={"is razorwind dangerous","razorwind canyon danger","danger in razorwind"},it="danger",add="851d9326"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know clearing Dustwind harpies from Razorwind Canyon helps keep the main road between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar safe for couriers and fresh recruits.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know harpies nesting beside Durotar’s central road threaten your homeland’s security. Young warriors must cull their numbers."},kw={"drygulch ravine","durotar","dustwind harpies","razor hill","razorwind canyon","tor'kren farm"},rel={"zone:durotar","subzone:razor-hill","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:drygulch-ravine","subzone:tor-kren-farm","quest:835","quest:834"},src={"Razorwind Canyon"}}
E["subzone:rocktusk-farm"] = {t="subzone",n="Rocktusk Farm",z="durotar",s="At Rocktusk Farm, swine feed Orgrimmar from just beyond the city gates in northern Durotar. Dry, stony ground makes crops hard to grow, so the farm sends meat and provisions to the capital.",h="At Rocktusk Farm, swine feed Orgrimmar from just beyond the city gates in northern Durotar.",sec={{t="Provisions for the Capital",b="Rocktusk Farm raises hardy swine on Durotar’s dry, stony ground. Crops are hard to grow here, so the farm helps feed Orgrimmar’s growing population. Near the capital’s fortified perimeter, it is safer than homesteads out in the wild red canyonlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Rocktusk Farm used for?",a="Rocktusk Farm raises swine for meat and provisions for Orgrimmar, where arable land is scarce.",al={"what is this place","rocktusk farm purpose","why are there pigs here"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Rocktusk Farm located?",a="Rocktusk Farm sits in northern Durotar, just southwest of Orgrimmar’s main gates along the road, beside rocky bluffs.",al={"where is rocktusk farm","rocktusk farm location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is the farm safe from wild beasts?",a="Orgrimmar’s closeness and nearby Horde patrols make the farm safer than most outlying homesteads. Wild beasts and roaming pests still prowl its outskirts.",al={"is rocktusk farm safe","dangers at rocktusk farm"},it="danger"},{q="What is Rocktusk Farm?",a="Rocktusk Farm is a swine-breeding homestead situated along the western road just outside the gates of Orgrimmar in Durotar. Operating in the rugged shadow of the capital's defenses, the farm raises pigs to help provide vital sustenance and provisions for the growing Horde.",al={"what is rocktusk farm","rocktusk farm durotar","about rocktusk farm"},it="place",add="38585a5d"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see how swine from this farm help feed the warriors and laborers stationed in Orgrimmar.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can use the farm’s pigs for fresh pork, ribs, and savory cuts to roast."},kw={"durotar","horde provisions","orgrimmar","pig farm","rocktusk farm","swine"},rel={"zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","topic:horde","subzone:gates-of-orgrimmar"},src={"Rocktusk Farm"}}
E["subzone:scuttle-coast"] = {t="subzone",n="Scuttle Coast",z="durotar",s="Along Durotar’s eastern shore, wreckage from Daelin Proudmoore’s fleet recalls the recent naval war. Now the Horde scavenges among the sunken ships between Razor Hill and Tiragarde Keep.",h="Along Durotar’s eastern shore, wreckage from Daelin Proudmoore’s fleet recalls the recent naval war.",sec={{t="Wreckage of the Fleet",b="Sunken warships line Durotar’s eastern edge, where the shore meets the Great Sea. During Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore’s invasion, the Kul Tiras fleet attacked the young nation of Durotar. Fierce battles with the Horde drove many human warships onto jagged shoals, where they broke apart. Barnacled timber, broken rigging, cargo barrels, and sunken ships still mark the coast. For the encampments at Razor Hill, the wreckage recalls how close the Kul Tiran threat remains.",sp=0},{t="Scavengers and Tides",b="The name Scuttle Coast may point to warships scuttled or grounded in the fighting. It may also come from crabs and makrura picking through the wreckage. Shoreline beasts and dangerous tides keep casual travelers away.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where did all these shipwrecks come from?",a="The shattered ships belonged to Kul Tiras’s fleet under Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore. During his failed campaign against the newly founded Horde, they smashed against Durotar’s rocky shallows.",al={"why are there ships here","who owns the wrecked ships","sunken ships durotar"},it="history"},{q="Why is it called the Scuttle Coast?",a="No one is certain why it is called the Scuttle Coast. The name may refer to warships scuttled during naval combat, or to makrura and crabs scuttling across the rocky sands.",al={"why is it called scuttle coast","scuttle coast name origin"},it="name"},{q="Is the Scuttle Coast safe to travel?",a="No. Treacherous waves and jagged rocks line the shore, while makrura and other hostile coastal beasts prowl the surf. Armed Kul Tiras survivors remain entrenched just to the south at Tiragarde Keep.",al={"scuttle coast dangers","is scuttle coast dangerous"},it="danger"},{q="What is Scuttle Coast?",a="The Scuttle Coast is the rocky eastern shoreline of Durotar, facing the Great Sea just southeast of Razor Hill and north of Tiragarde Keep. It is a windswept stretch of beach and jagged shoals infamous for maritime disasters and treacherous waters.",al={"what is scuttle coast","scuttle coast lore","tell me about scuttle coast"},it="place",add="d351211f"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, the broken hulls on this beach recall Durotar’s defense against Daelin Proudmoore’s invading navy."},kw={"daelin proudmoore","durotar","kul tiras","makrura","razor hill","scuttle coast","shipwrecks","tiragarde keep"},rel={"zone:durotar","subzone:tiragarde-keep","subzone:razor-hill","topic:kul-tiras","npc:jaina-proudmoore","topic:alliance"},src={"Scuttle Coast"}}
E["subzone:sen-jin-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Sen'jin Village",z="durotar",s="Sen'jin Village shelters the Darkspear on Durotar's southern shore. Vol'jin led them there after Zalazane seized the Echo Isles, and gave the refuge his fallen father's name. Across the shallows, their lost home waits.",h="Sen'jin Village shelters the Darkspear on Durotar's southern shore.",sec={{t="A Refugee Shore",b="The Darkspear survivors have made their refuge on Durotar's shore. After Zalazane betrayed the tribe and seized the Echo Isles, Chieftain Vol'jin led them across the strait to the mainland. They raised crude huts beneath coastal cliffs, with the water and their lost home in view.\n\nThe village bears the name of Sen'jin, Vol'jin's father. Murlocs captured and sacrificed him during the Third War. Though the Darkspear are closely allied with Thrall's Horde, exile remains their burden. The lost isles lie just across the shallows.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on the Isles",b="Preparation and defense shape life in Sen'jin Village. Quilboar raids, aggressive sea beasts, and Zalazane's hexes from across the sea threaten the villagers. Herbal remedies and potent alchemical spirits help sustain them.\n\nVol'jin coordinates the tribe's wider defense from the Horde capital. Meanwhile, local shamans, hunters, and scouts gather recruits arriving from the Valley of Trials. The Darkspear seek resources, guard Durotar's southern flank, and plan Zalazane's downfall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why did the Darkspear build Sen'jin Village here?",a="Zalazane seized the Darkspear home on the Echo Isles, so they crossed the strait to Durotar's coast. Vol'jin founded Sen'jin Village as a refuge and gathering place across the water from their lost land.",al={"why is senjin village here","why are trolls in durotar","why did trolls leave echo isles"},it="origin"},{q="Who was Sen'jin?",a="Sen'jin was a respected witch doctor and chieftain of the Darkspear, and Vol'jin's father. During the Third War, he foresaw Thrall's arrival, but murlocs captured and sacrificed him to their Sea Witch before Thrall could save him.",al={"who was senjin","who is senjin named after","senjin lore"},it="name"},{q="Why are there so many herbalists and alchemists here?",a="Local witch doctors and medicine men use Durotar's coastal plants and scorpok venoms to make charms, antidotes, and ritual brews. These remedies tend the wounded and ward against hexes from the Echo Isles.",al={"senjin village trainers","professions in senjin village","why alchemy here"}},{q="Can you reach the Echo Isles from Sen'jin Village?",a="The Echo Isles lie across the eastern water from Sen'jin Village. You can swim or wade across the shallow channel to confront Zalazane's voodoo cultists, recover stolen artifacts, or gather resources for the village defenders.",al={"how to get to echo isles","isles off senjin coast","swimming to echo isles"},gp=true},{q="What is Sen'jin Village?",a="Sen'jin Village is a coastal fishing settlement on the southern shore of Durotar, serving as the primary mainland refuge for the Darkspear trolls. Founded after the tribe was driven from the Echo Isles, it is a modest cluster of huts, docks, and raptor pens where troll refugees, witch doctors, and scouts maintain a watch over their lost homeland.",al={"what is senjin village","senjin village overview","sen'jin village lore"},it="place",add="8cd2719d"},{q="What happened at Sen'jin Village?",a="When the witch doctor Zalazane betrayed the Darkspear tribe and seized control of the Echo Isles with dark voodoo, Vol'jin led the surviving trolls across the water to Durotar's southern coast. There, they raised this village as a temporary sanctuary and military foothold, naming it in honor of Vol'jin's fallen father while plotting to reclaim their home.",al={"sen'jin village history","history of senjin village","how was senjin village founded"},it="history",add="fb8d4411"},{q="Who lives in Sen'jin Village?",a="The settlement is populated almost entirely by exiled Darkspear trolls. Local hunters, shadow hunters, herbalists, and alchemists work out of its huts and docks, defending the coast and gathering resources to support the broader Darkspear war effort under Chieftain Vol'jin's leadership.",al={"who lives in senjin village","who runs senjin village","sen'jin village leader"},it="residents",add="f928ac6d"},{q="Is Sen'jin Village dangerous?",a="The village itself is heavily guarded by Sen'jin axe throwers and shamans, offering safety within its borders. However, danger lies just beyond: Zalazane's mind-controlled trolls inhabit the nearby Echo Isles, while the surrounding shores are plagued by aggressive wildlife and encroaching sea creatures.",al={"is sen'jin village safe","threats to senjin village","senjin village dangers"},it="danger",add="5cc89452"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll emerging from the Valley of Trials, you find refuge among your displaced people. The village holds memories of your lost chieftain and the sting of Zalazane's betrayal.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you can learn natural medicine in Sen'jin Village. Coastal Peacebloom, Silverleaf, and Earthroot help local witch doctors treat venom and curses."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","echo isles","sen'jin village","senjin","vol'jin","zalazane"},rel={"topic:darkspear-tribe","subzone:echo-isles","npc:vol-jin","quest:826","zone:durotar","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:razor-hill","topic:third-war"},src={"Sen'jin Village"}}
E["subzone:shrine-of-the-dormant-flame"] = {t="subzone",n="Shrine of the Dormant Flame",z="durotar",s="Horde shaman climb to the Shrine of the Dormant Flame, atop Durotar’s highest peak northwest of the Valley of Trials. Telf Joolam keeps this secluded sanctuary, where initiates prove their spiritual mastery.",h="Horde shaman climb to the Shrine of the Dormant Flame, atop Durotar’s highest peak northwest of the Valley of...",sec={{t="A Summit of Trial and Flame",b="A narrow trail climbs from the Southfury River at the Southfury Watershed’s southwestern edge. At the summit, Durotar’s red cliffs fall away beneath a wide view, and one misstep near the precipice means certain death. Telf Joolam, a solitary hermit, oversees the sacred rites here.\n\nOrc and troll shaman come to answer the Call of Fire. At the shrine’s brazier, they kindle sleeping coals with the ember of a defeated elemental. The trial proves they can commune with fire and respect its destructive spirits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do you reach the Shrine of the Dormant Flame?",a="Begin at the Southfury River, on the southwestern edge of the Southfury Watershed, just northwest of the Valley of Trials. A narrow, winding trail climbs around the peak to the summit.",al={"how to get to shrine of the dormant flame","path to dormant flame","climb dormant flame mountain"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Why is this shrine important to shaman?",a="The shrine is sacred to Horde shaman learning to understand and command fire. For the Call of Fire, initiates climb to the summit to prepare a ritual draft and kindle the dormant brazier.",al={"shrine of dormant flame purpose","why do shaman go here","call of fire shrine"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Telf Joolam?",a="Telf Joolam is a solitary troll hermit who keeps the shrine. He guides young shaman through their trials, preparing a fire draught to awaken their spiritual sight and test their resolve.",al={"who is telf joolam","dormant flame npc","shrine keeper"},it="in_charge"},{q="What happens when you kindle the brazier?",a="After gathering the ritual components and defeating a hostile fire elemental, shaman place its burning ember in the brazier. The offering proves their strength and discipline in taming the volatile spirit of flame.",al={"brazier of dormant flame","igniting the flame","shrine brazier quest"},gp=true},{q="What is the Shrine of the Dormant Flame?",a="Perched atop the highest mountain peak northwest of the Valley of Trials, the Shrine of the Dormant Flame is a sacred place of communion for Horde shaman. Reached only by a winding, narrow trail above the Southfury River, it is where initiates prove their spiritual authority over elemental fire by kindling its sacred brazier.",al={"what is shrine of the dormant flame","what is dormant flame shrine","shrine of dormant flame durotar"},it="place",add="9edb20fb"},{q="What happened at the Shrine of the Dormant Flame?",a="For generations since the Horde settled Durotar, young orc and troll shaman have climbed to this windswept peak to undergo their trials. Here, aspirants bring captured embers won from defeated fire elementals to ignite the mountain's ceremonial brazier, proving their mastery over the primal flame and earning their fire totems under the watch of its keeper.",al={"history of shrine of dormant flame","shrine of dormant flame past","what happened at dormant flame shrine"},it="history",add="0def2f7d"},{q="Is the Shrine of the Dormant Flame dangerous?",a="The shrine itself is peaceful, but the journey to reach it is treacherous. The spiral path clinging to the mountain's cliffs is narrow and dizzying, and a single misstep can send you plunging to your death on the rocks far below. Additionally, summoning and binding elemental fire upon the peak requires absolute focus to avoid being consumed.",al={"danger shrine of dormant flame","is dormant flame shrine safe","is it dangerous up here"},it="danger",add="b2d73685"},{q="Why is it called the Shrine of the Dormant Flame?",a="The peak takes its name from the sacred brazier that rests cold and quiet until a worthy shaman awakens it. The flame remains asleep—dormant—waiting to be kindled by an ember won from elemental combat, bursting to life only when invoked during the trials of fire.",al={"why dormant flame","shrine dormant flame name origin","why is it called shrine of the dormant flame"},it="name",add="a82c700c"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a young orc or troll shaman, you climb this crag to kindle your spiritual connection with fire and earn your Fire Totem.",["faction:Horde"]="Above Durotar, this isolated shrine preserves ancient elemental rites vital to the spiritual heart of the new Horde."},kw={"call of fire","dormant flame","durotar","fire totem","shrine","southfury watershed","telf joolam","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:1524","npc:telf-joolam","subzone:southfury-river","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:merchant-coast","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},src={"Shrine of the Dormant Flame"}}
E["subzone:skull-rock"] = {t="subzone",n="Skull Rock",z="durotar",s="At Skull Rock, Burning Blade cultists gather in Durotar's eastern coastal cliffs. East of Orgrimmar, they plot against Thrall's Horde.",h="At Skull Rock, Burning Blade cultists gather in Durotar's eastern coastal cliffs.",sec={{t="A Den of Cultists",b="In northeastern Durotar, Burning Blade cultists gather beneath the crags at Skull Rock. Dark cultists, fel-worshipping orcs, and summoners meet in its winding tunnels. There they practice demonic arts and plot against the young Horde. The warlock Gazz'uz leads them, and their work threatens Orgrimmar's nearby gates and travelers along the eastern shore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Skull Rock?",a="Skull Rock is a cave system along northeastern Durotar's coast. Burning Blade cultists use its natural cover to plot against Thrall's Horde.",al={"skull rock cave","where is skull rock","what is in skull rock"},it="place"},{q="Who controls Skull Rock?",a="The Burning Blade controls Skull Rock. The orc warlock Gazz'uz leads the cult from the cave's deepest chamber.",al={"who leads skull rock","who runs skull rock","skull rock boss"},it="residents"},{q="Why does the Horde care about this cave?",a="Skull Rock lies close to Orgrimmar and threatens the Horde's security. The Burning Blade seeks to undermine Thrall's new realm and return the orcs to demonic servitude.",al={"why clear skull rock","why is skull rock dangerous"},it="danger"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can see demonic influence spreading through Skull Rock. Thrall's Horde seeks to root it out and control the cave.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know clearing Skull Rock's cultists helps secure Durotar's coastal approaches. It also protects Orgrimmar from subversion within."},kw={"burning blade","cultists","durotar","gazz'uz","orgrimmar","skull rock"},rel={"quest:827","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Skull Rock"}}
E["subzone:spirit-rock"] = {t="subzone",n="Spirit Rock",z="durotar",s="Above the Valley of Trials in Durotar, Horde initiates climb Spirit Rock to commune with the elements. The Hidden Path winds up to the sacred crag.",h="Above the Valley of Trials in Durotar, Horde initiates climb Spirit Rock to commune with the elements.",sec={{t="A Sanctuary of the Elements",b="Spirit Rock looks down on the red canyon where young Horde warriors and scouts train. From the canyon floor, the Hidden Path winds up the rocky ridgeline to a quiet altar. There, aspiring shaman drink sapta, a traditional brew that opens their senses beyond the physical world. They listen for the earth's rumblings and whispers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Spirit Rock used for?",a="Horde shaman initiates go to Spirit Rock to commune with the spirits of the earth. Novices drink Earth Sapta there to gain the spiritual vision needed to reach them.",al={"spirit rock purpose","what happens at spirit rock","spirit rock use"},it="purpose"},{q="How do you reach Spirit Rock?",a="Climb the Hidden Path from the Valley of Trials in southwestern Durotar. The narrow trail winds from the canyon floor into the cliffs above.",al={"how to get to spirit rock","path to spirit rock","spirit rock location"},gp=true},{q="What is a sapta?",a="Sapta is a ceremonial elemental brew prepared by shaman trainers. Drinking it changes a seeker's perception and reveals elemental manifestations hidden from ordinary senses.",al={"earth sapta","what is sapta","sapta drink"},it="item"},{q="What is Spirit Rock?",a="Spirit Rock is a secluded sanctuary perched high in the rocky bluffs overlooking the Valley of Trials in Durotar. Reached by a winding, hidden path up the hills, it serves as a sacred gathering ground where aspiring shaman seek communion with the spirits of the world.",al={"what is spirit rock","spirit rock durotar","about spirit rock"},it="place",add="5b9df982"},{q="Is Spirit Rock dangerous?",a="The rock itself is a place of solemn spiritual reflection rather than a den of monsters. However, the path leading up into the jagged crags borders the rough wilderness of Durotar, and communing directly with elemental spirits carries its own trials for the unprepared.",al={"spirit rock danger","is spirit rock safe","enemies at spirit rock"},it="danger",add="383a79b2"},{q="Why is it called Spirit Rock?",a="It earned its name because it is a consecrated natural focal point where the veil between the physical realm and the elemental spirits is thin. It is here that shaman drink specially prepared saptas to perceive and speak with the spirits of the earth.",al={"why spirit rock","spirit rock name origin"},it="name",add="57276d06"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a young orc or troll shaman, you climb the Hidden Path to Spirit Rock and drink Earth Sapta. There, you begin your bond with the spirits of stone and soil."},kw={"call of earth","durotar","earth spirits","hidden path","sapta","shaman","spirit rock","valley of trials"},rel={"subzone:hidden-path","subzone:valley-of-trials","quest:1520","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},src={"Spirit Rock"}}
E["subzone:the-den"] = {t="subzone",n="The Den",z="durotar",s="In southwestern Durotar, young orcs and trolls gather at the sheltered Den in the heart of the Valley of Trials. It is their main base, where they train in arms and magic before setting out into the wider world.",h="In southwestern Durotar, young orcs and trolls gather at the sheltered Den in the heart of the Valley of...",sec={{t="Cradle of the Horde",b="The Den is an austere proving ground, carved into the red canyon walls of the Valley of Trials. Inside its shadowed halls, novice fighters, spellcasters, and hunters answer to veterans such as Gornek and Zureetha Fargaze. They receive their first combat lessons, supplies, and rites of passage, preparing for Durotar's harshness and the struggles facing the new Horde.",sp=0},{t="A Watchful Outpost",b="The Den houses class trainers and merchants who provide provisions. From this field outpost, overseers send recruits to cull local beasts and aggressive quilboars. They keep a strict watch over the valley.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Den?",a="The Den is the central base and training ground in the Valley of Trials. Novice orcs and Darkspear trolls learn basic class techniques, buy provisions, and receive assignments meant to prove their loyalty and readiness to fight for the Horde.",al={"what is the den","why is the den here","purpose of the den"},it="purpose"},{q="Who runs things inside the Den?",a="Veteran overseers such as Gornek and Foreman Thazz'ril supervise the Den. Spiritual and magical mentors, including Zureetha Fargaze and Canaga Earthcaller, instruct the newest warriors and mystics.",al={"who leads the den","who is in charge","den overseer"},it="in_charge"},{q="Can you learn primary professions here?",a="No. The Den has basic class trainers and general equipment merchants. To study primary trades such as Blacksmithing, Leatherworking, or Mining, travel north to Razor Hill or continue to Orgrimmar.",al={"profession trainers den","can i learn blacksmithing here","train mining in den"},gp=true},{q="What is the Den?",a="The Den is the cavernous base of operations in the Valley of Trials, nestled in the southwestern corner of Durotar. It serves as the primary muster camp for young orc novices seeking to prove themselves worthy of the Horde. Inside, trainers teach the basics of various arts, merchants sell essential supplies, and local leaders hand out trials to test incoming recruits before they venture into the wider world.",al={"what is the den","the den durotar","about the den"},it="place",add="e0991dfb"},{q="Is the Den dangerous?",a="The Den itself is heavily guarded and quite safe for members of the Horde, protected by Den Grunts and experienced overseers. The real dangers lie outside, where beasts and quilboar roam the Valley of Trials.",al={"is the den dangerous","is it safe in the den","the den threats"},it="danger",add="ac46dd9b"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Every young orc begins at the Den, leaving behind the complacency of the internment camps and blood haze. Discipline and labor are how you earn your place.",["race:Troll"]="After the Darkspear Isles were devastated, young Darkspear trolls began training in the Den beside their orc allies. Under the Horde's banner, you must prove your mettle."},kw={"durotar","gornek","starting cave","the den","trainers","valley of trials","zureetha fargaze"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","npc:gornek","npc:zureetha-fargaze","subzone:razor-hill","npc:magga","npc:mai-ah","topic:troll"},src={"The Den"}}
E["subzone:thunder-ridge"] = {t="subzone",n="Thunder Ridge",z="durotar",s="Southwest of Orgrimmar, Thunder Ridge lies along the Southfury River in western Durotar. Thunder lizards roam its stripped canyon, where human logging and dark sorcery ruined a former grove. Agitated beasts and lingering cultists threaten nearby settlements.",h="Southwest of Orgrimmar, Thunder Ridge lies along the Southfury River in western Durotar.",sec={{t="A Scarred Sanctuary",b="Once, ancient trees shaded Thunder Ridge and made it a green haven in arid Durotar. Shortly after the Third War, humans from Kul Tiras began felling its timber. As the trees fell, the thunder lizards grew wild. Then the Burning Blade used fel sorcery to destroy what remained of the canopy. Now the gorge lies barren and exposed, and angry beasts that spew lightning roam its crags.",sp=0},{t="Cultists and Tests of Strength",b="Orgrimmar's people watch Thunder Ridge with care. The Burning Blade keeps cultists there under the warlock Fizzle Darkclaw, whose demonic magic spreads chaos through Durotar. Horde veterans such as Orgnil Soulscar send scouts to hunt them. Warrior trainers like Uzzek also send aspiring fighters into the crags to test themselves against the enraged thunder lizards.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to the trees in Thunder Ridge?",a="Thunder Ridge was once dense woodland, but two waves of destruction stripped away its trees. Shortly after Durotar was founded, Kul Tiran forces felled the ancient trees for lumber. Later, the Burning Blade used dark, demonic magic to raze the surviving groves and wipe out the forest.",al={"why is thunder ridge barren","thunder ridge forest","deforestation thunder ridge"},it="ruin"},{q="Why are the thunder lizards so aggressive here?",a="Thunder lizards once lived peacefully among Thunder Ridge's ancient trees. Human logging brought noise and destruction to their home, and lingering fel corruption from the Burning Blade cultists worsened their agitation. Now they attack anyone who enters the canyon.",al={"angry lizards thunder ridge","thunder lizards durotar"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Fizzle Darkclaw?",a="Fizzle Darkclaw leads a Burning Blade cult and established an encampment in Thunder Ridge. He and his followers use dark rituals to destabilize the region. Horde leaders such as Orgnil Soulscar have placed a bounty on his head.",al={"fizzle darkclaw lore","who is darkclaw","burning blade thunder ridge"},it="threat"},{q="Did Rexxar fight in Thunder Ridge?",a="Yes. Shortly after Durotar was founded, Rexxar came to Thunder Ridge to gather shimmerweed for the farseer Drek'Thar. He found the human lumber camp driving the lizards wild. Then he culled the frenzied beasts and salvaged their eggs for Drek'Thar to study.",al={"rexxar thunder ridge","drek'thar thunder ridge"}},{q="What is Thunder Ridge?",a="Thunder Ridge is a deep, deforested gorge nestled in northwestern Durotar, located just southwest of Orgrimmar. Once a flourishing ancient forest, it served as a traditional sanctuary for massive herds of thunder lizards. Today, its lush canopy is gone, replaced by barren cliffs, roaming beasts, and encroaching dark cultists.",al={"what is thunder ridge","thunder ridge durotar","where is thunder ridge"},it="place",add="d8d2e909"},{q="What happened at Thunder Ridge?",a="Shortly after Durotar was founded, humans from Kul Tiras established an illegal logging operation here, cutting down the ancient timber and enraging the thunder lizards until Rexxar and Drek'Thar intervened. Later, demonic corruption wielded by the Burning Blade cult severed the remaining trees, stripping the valley bare and agitating the native beasts into a violent frenzy.",al={"history of thunder ridge","thunder ridge lore","what happened here thunder ridge"},it="history",add="675c5d12"},{q="Who lives in Thunder Ridge?",a="No peaceful settlement exists within the ridge. Aside from herds of agitated thunder lizards and lightning hides, a coven of Burning Blade cultists led by the warlock Fizzle Darkclaw has established a camp in the ravine, using dark magic to sow chaos across Durotar.",al={"who lives in thunder ridge","thunder ridge inhabitants","thunder ridge factions"},it="residents",add="ea9b6430"},{q="Is Thunder Ridge dangerous?",a="Yes. The native thunder lizards are naturally territorial, and recent dark meddling has driven them into an erratic, hostile fury capable of shocking intruders with lightning. In addition, the Burning Blade cultists lurking in the gorge will readily strike down anyone investigating their ritual sites.",al={"how dangerous is thunder ridge","thunder ridge hazards","is thunder ridge safe"},it="danger",add="e9504f5d"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="Warrior mentors such as Uzzek send their trainees into Thunder Ridge to test their defensive skill against the strength and lightning shocks of wild thunder lizards.",["faction:Horde"]="Just beyond Orgrimmar's western bluffs, Thunder Ridge must be kept clear of Burning Blade agents such as Fizzle Darkclaw. His demonic schemes threaten the capital."},kw={"burning blade","durotar","fizzle darkclaw","orgnil soulscar","rexxar","southfury river","thunder lizards","thunder ridge","uzzek"},rel={"zone:durotar","quest:806","quest:1498","npc:orgnil-soulscar","npc:uzzek","subzone:southfury-river","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:drygulch-ravine"},src={"Thunder Ridge"}}
E["subzone:tiragarde-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Tiragarde Keep",z="durotar",s="Kul Tiran marines still garrison Tiragarde Keep on Durotar’s Scuttle Coast, south of Razor Hill. Built during Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore’s invasion, the ruined stronghold remains under Lieutenant Benedict, a hostile presence in Horde territory.",h="Kul Tiran marines still garrison Tiragarde Keep on Durotar’s Scuttle Coast, south of Razor Hill.",sec={{t="Proudmoore's Bastion",b="Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore’s fleet used Tiragarde Keep as a beachhead on Durotar’s red shores. He raised it during his campaign to destroy Thrall’s newly founded realm. The Horde broke the siege and killed Proudmoore at Theramore Isle, yet the keep was never fully abandoned.\n\nResupply forces under Lieutenant Benedict reclaimed its shattered stone walls. They follow the late Admiral’s standing orders to wage unyielding war against the orcs. They reject the peace Lady Jaina Proudmoore forged.",sp=0},{t="A Thorn in Durotar's Flank",b="White battlements rise above Durotar’s crimson cliffs, patrolled by Kul Tiran sailors and marines. The garrison raids supply lines near Razor Hill. For the Horde, the keep remains a security crisis and a proving ground.\n\nOrc and troll commanders send young warriors to assault the fortress and cut down Benedict’s soldiers. They seek to contain the garrison before the humans push farther inland.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there humans in Durotar?",a="The humans in Durotar are Kul Tiran sailors and marines who arrived with Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore during his invasion after the Third War. They reject peace with the Horde and keep the garrison to harass the orcs.",al={"why are alliance here","who are the humans in tiragarde","human soldiers durotar"},it="why_here"},{q="Are these humans part of Jaina's forces in Theramore?",a="No. Jaina Proudmoore rules Theramore Isle and maintains an uneasy truce with Thrall. These soldiers follow invasion orders left by her late father, Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore, and regard peace with orcs as unacceptable treason.",al={"is tiragarde theramore","are they jaina proudmoore's men","theramore soldiers here"},it="ties"},{q="Who commands Tiragarde Keep?",a="Lieutenant Benedict commands Tiragarde Keep under posthumous invasion orders from Admiral Proudmoore to secure the coast and attack the Horde.",al={"tiragarde boss","who leads tiragarde keep","lieutenant benedict"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why hasn't the Horde simply wiped them out?",a="Tiragarde Keep is fortified and held by disciplined, well-armed Kul Tiran troops. Defenders from Razor Hill often skirmish with the garrison and send new recruits there to prove themselves. A full siege would cost many lives and draw resources away from securing the rest of Durotar.",al={"why not destroy tiragarde","why is the keep still here"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Tiragarde Keep?",a="Tiragarde Keep is an Alliance coastal fortification situated along the Scuttle Coast in southeastern Durotar. Built out of pale stonework that clashes sharply with the surrounding red canyons, it serves as a fortified beachhead for human forces hostile to the Horde. Even in its battered condition, the keep provides Kul Tiras soldiers a fortified base to harass nearby settlements like Razor Hill.",al={"tiragarde keep what is it","what is this keep","tell me about tiragarde keep"},it="place",add="975f81a6"},{q="What happened at Tiragarde Keep?",a="Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore hastily constructed the keep during his invasion of Durotar to wage war against the nascent Horde. The Horde struck back, assaulting and battering the fortress until it fell. Although Proudmoore was later slain, reserve forces under Lieutenant Benedict were dispatched to reclaim the ruined keep and carry on the fallen Admiral's campaign.",al={"tiragarde keep history","what happened here","battle of tiragarde keep"},it="history",add="6c9a5200"},{q="Why is Tiragarde Keep ruined?",a="The fortress lies in ruins because the Horde stormed and shattered it during Grand Admiral Proudmoore's initial invasion of Durotar. While Lieutenant Benedict and his Kul Tiran reinforcements successfully reoccupied the site, they hold it as a crumbling, patched stronghold rather than a pristine castle, constantly under siege and pressure from nearby orcish outposts.",al={"why is tiragarde keep destroyed","why is the keep damaged","who destroyed tiragarde keep"},it="ruin",add="79c67834"},{q="Is Tiragarde Keep dangerous?",a="Yes, deeply so for members of the Horde. The keep is occupied by well-trained Kul Tiras Marines and Sailors who carry deep hatred for orcs and strike at travelers along the coast. They launch raids toward Razor Hill and fiercely defend their ramparts against any Horde warriors sent to dislodge them.",al={"is tiragarde keep safe","tiragarde keep danger","are the humans in tiragarde keep dangerous"},it="danger",add="246e91e1"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, Tiragarde Keep is an Alliance invasion base on Durotar’s doorstep. Raiding its ramparts and defeating Lieutenant Benedict is a rite of passage for young soldiers serving Razor Hill.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see the garrison’s stubborn legacy of Kul Tiras and Admiral Proudmoore. Its soldiers wage a guerrilla war against the Horde despite Jaina Proudmoore’s diplomacy."},kw={"daelin proudmoore","durotar","kul tiras","lieutenant benedict","razor hill","scuttle coast","tiragarde keep"},rel={"zone:durotar","subzone:scuttle-coast","subzone:razor-hill","quest:784","topic:kul-tiras","subzone:theramore-isle","npc:jaina-proudmoore","npc:thrall"},src={"Tiragarde Keep"}}
E["subzone:tor-kren-farm"] = {t="subzone",n="Tor'kren Farm",z="durotar",s="At Tor'kren Farm in northwestern Durotar, Misha Tor'kren anxiously waits for news of Kron. Her son has not returned from a hunting trip.",h="At Tor'kren Farm in northwestern Durotar, Misha Tor'kren anxiously waits for news of Kron.",sec={{t="A Lonely Homestead",b="Tor'kren Farm struggles to raise pigs in Durotar's dry red dirt. The homestead lies southeast of Thunder Ridge, near the Southfury River. Feed and water run short, and nearby bluffs leave the farm isolated. Its yields are meager.",sp=0},{t="A Mother's Worry",b="Several days ago, Kron went west to hunt crocolisks along the Southfury River. Misha Tor'kren warned him about the vicious predators, but he left in anger. Now she asks passing travelers to search for him or bring back a sign of his fate. She fears the worst, yet cannot begin mourning without knowing what happened.",sp=0},{t="A Mother's Loss",b="Misha Tor'kren recognizes Kron's Amulet when an adventurer brings it back from the river's crocolisks. Now she knows her son is dead. At last, Misha can begin to mourn.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Tor'kren Farm located?",a="Tor'kren Farm lies in northwestern Durotar, southeast of Thunder Ridge and east of the Southfury River.",al={"tor'kren farm location","where is torkren farm","find tor'kren farm"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who lives at Tor'kren Farm?",a="Misha Tor'kren tends the swine farm. Her son Kron is missing after setting out to hunt along the Southfury River.",al={"who runs tor'kren farm","tor'kren farm npcs","who is misha tor'kren"},it="residents"},{q="What happened to Misha's son?",a="Kron went to hunt crocolisks along the Southfury River several days ago and has not returned. Misha asks travelers to find him or bring back a sign of his fate.",al={"misha son","kron tor'kren death","who is kron"},it="history"},{q="What does Tor'kren Farm produce?",a="Tor'kren Farm raises swine, but harsh terrain and isolation leave its profits leaner than those of other livestock operations in Durotar.",al={"torkren farm business","what kind of farm is torkren","tor'kren pigs"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Tor'kren Farm?",a="Tor'kren Farm is a modest homestead situated in northwestern Durotar, tucked between Thunder Ridge and the Southfury River. It serves as a working pig farm, though it struggles to achieve the success and profit of other settlements in the region. Maintained under the harsh desert sun, it represents the quiet, grinding effort of everyday orcs trying to carve out a livelihood on Durotar's unforgiving frontier.",al={"what is torkren farm","torkren farm lore","about torkren farm"},it="place",add="13fe9b16"},{q="Is Tor'kren Farm dangerous?",a="The farmstead itself offers relative safety, but its surroundings are fraught with peril. It lies near the Southfury River and its watershed, waters infested with vicious crocolisks that have claimed lives in the past. In addition, the rugged terrain nearby harbors aggressive wildlife, meaning travelers and workers must always keep their guard up when venturing beyond the homestead's immediate perimeter.",al={"is torkren farm safe","torkren farm threats","danger at torkren farm"},it="danger",add="11f4c018"},{q="Why is it called Tor'kren Farm?",a="The farm takes its name from the Tor'kren family who built and maintain it. Misha Tor'kren settled the land to raise swine alongside her son Kron, lending their family name to the small, enduring patch of farmland.",al={"why is it called torkren farm","torkren farm name origin","who is torkren"},it="name",add="65c8d3ec"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="At Tor'kren Farm, you see the hardships ordinary Horde settlers face as they try to tame Durotar's wild frontier.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know how dangerous Durotar's riverbanks can be. Misha warned Kron about the Southfury's crocolisks."},kw={"durotar","kron","misha tor'kren","pig farm","southfury river","thunder ridge","tor'kren farm"},rel={"npc:misha-tor-kren","subzone:southfury-river","subzone:thunder-ridge","zone:durotar"},src={"Tor'kren Farm"}}
E["subzone:valley-of-trials"] = {t="subzone",n="Valley of Trials",z="durotar",s="The Valley of Trials, in the south of Durotar, is where young orcs and Darkspear trolls are put to the test. Chieftains and trainers watch over them from The Den, a shelter cut into the cliffs. Out in the sunlit gulch, the recruits hunt scorpids and cull the angry boars. They keep the lazy peons in line as well, while they gather the valley's scarce timber.",h="The Valley of Trials, in the south of Durotar, is where young orcs and Darkspear trolls are put to the test.",sec={{t="A Crucible of Sand and Stone",b="The trial is hard. Only those who prove their mettle earn the right to leave as soldiers of the Horde, ready to defend their people. Those who fail are left beneath the desert sun.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow in the North",b="The northern caves have brought a new danger to the Valley of Trials. Cultists of the Burning Blade have settled in the natural caves along the cliffs and summon minor demonic familiars into the valley. Trainers use the intruders to give fresh recruits live combat practice. But fel magic so close to Orgrimmar’s threshold fuels rumors that the Shadow Council is trying to regain its hold over the orcish people.",sp=1,bt={"q5726.3"}}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Valley of Trials?",a="The Valley of Trials is where young orcs and Darkspear trolls prove themselves to the Horde. In its sheltered canyons, recruits face demanding trials of martial skill, survival, and loyalty before they may leave for the rest of Durotar.",al={"why are orcs here","what is this place","valley of trials purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="What is The Den?",a="The Den is a cave carved into the cliffs near the center of the valley. Class trainers, vendors, and overseers such as Gornek gather there to direct, equip, and watch over new recruits during their first trials.",al={"the den","cave in valley of trials","who is in the den"},it="place"},{q="Why are there demons in a beginner's training ground?",a="Cultists of the Burning Blade have taken root in the northern caves and summon weak demonic familiars. Trainers use the familiars to test recruits, while the cult’s presence suggests the Shadow Council is seeking a foothold on Durotar’s doorstep.",al={"why demons in valley of trials","burning blade in durotar","demons north cave"},sp=1,it="threat",bt={"q5726.3"}},{q="Who is Sarkoth?",a="Sarkoth is an unusually large, venomous scorpid that lives in the rocky heights of the valley. Instructors send promising recruits to hunt him, testing their courage and asking them to bring back his mangled claw as proof.",al={"sarkoth lore","giant scorpid","sarkoth quest"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Valley of Trials?",a="The Valley of Trials is a rugged, canyon-sheltered proving ground in southern Durotar. Surrounded by towering red cliffs, it serves as the essential proving ground for young orcs and Darkspear trolls seeking to earn their place in the Horde. Here, recruits endure trials of combat, survival, and discipline under harsh sun and craggy rocks before stepping beyond the valley walls into the wider world.",al={"where am i","what is this place","valley of trials lore"},it="place",add="7f52c0d9",nx={6,7}},{q="Why is it called the Valley of Trials?",a="It takes its name from the strict rites of passage held within its walls. Every aspiring recruit must prove their strength, resolve, and loyalty to the Horde by completing dangerous trials against the land's beasts and threats. Those who prove worthy are granted passage out into Durotar; those who fail and fall in the attempt are left to bake in the scorching desert sun.",al={"why valley of trials","meaning of valley of trials name","why is it named valley of trials"},it="name",add="341e719f"},{q="Is the Valley of Trials part of Durotar?",a="Yes, it lies in the southern reaches of Durotar. Durotar itself is a dry, rocky realm on the eastern coast of Kalimdor, founded and named by Thrall in memory of his father, Durotan. The Valley of Trials is the protected staging ground where recruits prepare before entering the harsher wilds of the broader territory.",al={"is this in durotar","is valley of trials part of durotar","valley of trials durotar"},it="place",add="5bae7ae4"},{q="Who is in charge here?",a="The valley's trials and training are managed locally by Horde veteran taskmasters and class trainers. Taskmaster Gornek directs the new arrivals and evaluates their progress, ensuring every novice proves their worth to the New Horde before they are allowed to venture into greater Durotar.",al={"who leads the valley of trials","who runs the valley of trials","who is the boss here"},it="in_charge",add="9914b36c",nx={9}},{q="Who is Gornek?",a="Gornek is an orc taskmaster stationed right in front of The Den in the Valley of Trials. He oversees recruits from the moment they report for duty, issuing foundational trials to test your mettle, culling wild beasts, and directing proven warriors and spellcasters to their respective trainers.",al={"gornek","who is gornek","what does gornek do"},it="leader",add="aa4d1f31"},{q="What is the New Horde?",a="The New Horde is a coalition of disparate cultures founded by Warchief Thrall upon principles of survival, honor, and freedom. Bound together by an alliance of mutual protection in a hostile world, it stands centered on the orcs, joined by allies like the Darkspear trolls and the tauren, dedicated to building a future free from demonic corruption.",al={"new horde","what is the horde","thrall's horde"},it="purpose",add="4fde55c9"},{q="Why are orcs living in a desert now?",a="After escaping human captivity in the Eastern Kingdoms and crossing the Great Sea, Thrall brought the orcs to Kalimdor to claim a land of their own. Durotar's cracked red soil, rugged canyons, and arid heat remind the orcs of their ancient homeworld of Draenor, offering a harsh beauty where their strength can endure.",al={"why durotar","why are orcs in the desert","why did orcs settle durotar"},it="arrival",rc="Orc",add="3a67b133"},{q="Why is my troll starting in an orc camp?",a="The Darkspear tribe owes their very survival to Thrall, who helped rescue them when their island home was lost during the exodus to Kalimdor. Allied in gratitude and friendship, young Darkspear trolls train shoulder-to-shoulder with orc recruits in the Valley of Trials to prove their shared devotion to the Horde.",al={"why do trolls start in valley of trials","troll starting area","why are trolls with orcs"},it="arrival",rc="Troll",add="e4c91867",nx={13}},{q="What happened to the Darkspear tribe?",a="Driven from their ancestral islands in the Great Sea after fighting murlocs and a sea witch, the Darkspear followed Thrall to Kalimdor and colonized the Echo Isles off Durotar's coast. However, the treachery of the witch doctor Zalazane and attacks by human forces drove them from the isles, forcing them onto the Durotar mainland at Sen'jin Village.",al={"darkspear history","what happened to darkspear","echo isles darkspear"},it="history",rc="Troll",add="3629ab9f"},{q="Who are the Burning Blade?",a="The Burning Blade is a dark cult associated with demonic corruption and whispers of the treacherous Shadow Council. Rather than seeking honor under Thrall's Horde, their warlocks and followers traffic with fel powers and harbor sinister designs against the safety of Durotar.",al={"burning blade","who is the burning blade","burning blade cult"},it="threat",add="9ca718af",nx={15}},{q="Why are the Burning Blade in the valley?",a="Members of the cult have secretly moved into the natural cavern network along the valley's northern cliffs, now known as the Burning Blade Coven. Led by the warlock Yarrog Baneshadow, their presence allows demonic imps to spill into the training grounds, testing recruits who must eradicate the corruption before departing.",al={"why is burning blade here","burning blade in valley of trials","why are they in the coven"},it="why_here",add="d2b83034"},{q="What is Sen'jin Village and why am I being sent there?",a="Sen'jin Village is a Darkspear troll settlement established along the southern coast of Durotar on Darkspear Strand. Founded by Vol'jin after Zalazane seized the Echo Isles, it serves as the tribe's staging post and your natural destination once you prove yourself worthy of leaving the Valley of Trials.",al={"sen'jin village","why go to sen'jin village","what is senjin village"},it="next_step",add="3ff6b15f"},{q="How did I end up in Valley of Trials?",a="You arrived here to test yourself. Tucked away within the southern crags of Durotar, the Valley of Trials serves as the proving ground for new recruits of the Horde. Whether answered out of a sense of duty, tribal tradition, or the raw urge to fight for your people, all who wish to serve Thrall's realm must first brave this arid gorge. You entered on foot, reporting to the recruiters and taskmasters of The Den to begin your rite of passage.",al={"how did i get here","how did i end up here","why did i wake up here"},it="arrival",add="b9026890"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Valley of Trials?",a="You are here to prove your strength and earn your place among the Horde. Under the harsh sun, Taskmaster Gornek and the valley's mentors demand that you toughen yourself by slaying local beasts, harvesting vital supplies, and honing your combat craft. As your final challenge, you must face the growing corruption brewing in the northern caverns. Once your instructors judge you capable of surviving Durotar's perils, you will be permitted to pass through the northern gate and journey deeper into the wild lands beyond.",al={"what should i do here","what am i doing here","why am i here"},it="purpose",add="f72f3f76"},{q="Why does a new Orc start here, in Valley of Trials?",a="For an orc, coming to the Valley of Trials is an essential rite of passage. In this new homeland that Thrall carved from the dust and named after his father, Durotan, old traditions live on in a new form. Every aspiring orc must undergo these trials to demonstrate honor, discipline, and battle readiness before they can join the grunts guarding Orgrimmar or roam the frontier. You were sent here to prove that you possess the spirit needed to defend the New Horde.",al={"why do orcs start here","why are orcs in the valley","why do i start in the valley of trials as an orc"},it="arrival",rc="Orc",add="5263efa6"},{q="Why does a new Troll start here, in Valley of Trials?",a="Your people, the Darkspear tribe, recently suffered a bitter betrayal. Driven from your home on the Echo Isles by the traitor Zalazane and his hexed minions, the survivors gathered along the coast at Sen'jin Village. Lacking proper proving grounds of your own, your chieftain Vol'jin relies on his alliance with Thrall, sending eager Darkspear youth here to Durotar's valley alongside the orcs. By proving your strength in this harsh canyon, you prepare to serve the Horde and eventually help reclaim your home.",al={"why do trolls start here","why is a troll in an orc camp","why am i here as a troll"},it="arrival",rc="Troll",add="576a24aa"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For a young orc seeking honor, the valley is a rite of passage that carries on Draenor’s warrior traditions in a newly forged homeland.",["race:Troll"]="After losing their home on the Echo Isles to Zalazane, Darkspear trolls train beside their orc allies in this canyon to earn their place in the Horde."},kw={"burning blade coven","durotar","gornek","orcs","peons","sarkoth","the den","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:gornek","zone:durotar","subzone:the-den","subzone:burning-blade-coven","subzone:echo-isles","topic:horde","topic:darkspear-tribe","topic:shadow-council"},src={"Valley of Trials"}}
E["topic:grommash-hellscream"] = {t="topic",n="Grommash Hellscream",z="durotar",s="Grommash Hellscream's sacrifice has freed his people from the blood curse. The warsong chieftain once bound the orcs to the Burning Legion, but gave his life to slay mannoroth in ashenvale and free them.",h="Grommash Hellscream's sacrifice has freed his people from the blood curse.",sec={{t="The First Drink and the Iron Will",b="Before the Dark Portal opened, Grom Hellscream led the warsong clan with fierce resolve. His pitch-black tattooed jaw and the deadly sweep of Gorehowl, his two-handed axe, set him apart. On Draenor, Gul'dan and the Shadow Council offered the orcs demonic strength. Grom was the first chieftain to drink the blood of the pit lord mannoroth. The draught bound the orcs to demonic service and filled them with burning bloodlust.\n\nMany chieftains perished or lost themselves to the bloodlust, but Grom kept his fierce spirit through the old Horde's horrors. He carried a quiet ache for what his people had surrendered.",sp=0},{t="A Brotherhood in the Wilds",b="Left behind on Draenor during the Second War, Grom later crossed the Dark Portal. The rift was shattered, and he was stranded. For nearly fifteen years, he and the surviving warsong warriors evaded the Alliance of Lordaeron. They endured lethargy and despair as the demon blood faded.\n\nThen a young fugitive named Thrall found Grom in the wilderness, and hope returned. Grom saw Thrall's strength and noble heart, and taught him the proud heritage of their people. With Orgrim Doomhammer, they rallied the scattered clans, broke open the human internment camps, and began the New Horde.",sp=0},{t="Fall and Final Redemption",b="During the Third War, Grom's aggression rose again in ashenvale's ancient forests. The night elves and the demigod Cenarius pressed his clan hard. To save them, Grom drank from a fountain corrupted with mannoroth's blood. Bound again to the demon lord, he turned against his own people.\n\nThrall and Jaina Proudmoore captured Grom and cleansed his spirit with ancient shamanic and arcane rites. Restored to his senses and burdened with guilt, he pursued mannoroth into Demon Fall Canyon. There Grom drove Gorehowl into the demon lord's chest, ending the demonic curse forever. Hellfire took Grom's life.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Grommash Hellscream?",a="Grommash Hellscream led the Warsong clan and served as Thrall's trusted lieutenant. Famous for Gorehowl, he was the first orc to drink Mannoroth's blood and accept the demonic pact. He redeemed his legacy by slaying Mannoroth in Kalimdor and freeing the orcs from the Blood Curse.",al={"who is grom","who was hellscream","grom hellscream backstory"},it="identity"},{q="How did Grom die?",a="Grom died in Demon Fall Canyon in Ashenvale, where he faced the pit lord Mannoroth. He leapt into the air and cleaved the demon's chest with Gorehowl, shattering its heart. The burst of demonic hellfire fatally wounded him, and Grom died declaring that he had freed himself and his people.",al={"grom death","how did grom hellscream die","who killed grom"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Grom's connection to Thrall?",a="Grom was the first clan chieftain Thrall met after escaping the internment camp of Durnholde. He took the young orc under his wing, teaching him orcish traditions, language, and culture. Thrall saw Grom as an older brother and spiritual guide, while Grom saw Thrall as the visionary who could lead their shattered race back to honor.",al={"thrall and grom","how did thrall know grom","were thrall and grom friends"},it="ties"},{q="Why was Grom's jaw tattooed black?",a="Grom's lower jaw bore a solid black tattoo that set him apart among the orcish chieftains and made him easy to recognize in battle. The tales told of him do not record what the mark meant.",al={"grom black jaw","why is groms jaw black","grom tattooed lower jaw"},it="origin"},{q="Why did Grom drink demon blood a second time?",a="Grom drank demon blood again to save his clan after night elves and the demigod Cenarius decimated it while it harvested lumber in Ashenvale. Cenarius was nearly invincible against mortal weapons. Grom found a pool corrupted by Mannoroth's blood and drank, knowing the dreadful cost, to gain the demonic fury to defeat him.",al={"why did grom drink again","grom chaos orcs","grom drank blood twice"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Grommash buried?",a="Grommash rests in Demon Fall Canyon in southeastern Ashenvale, where he struck down Mannoroth. A stone monument marks his burial site, with an epitaph by Thrall honoring Grom's courage and ultimate sacrifice for the Horde.",al={"grom grave","grom monument","where is groms tomb"},it="place"},{q="What is the history of Grommash Hellscream?",a="Grommash rose to lead the Warsong clan on Draenor and became the first chieftain to drink the blood of the demon Mannoroth, binding the orcs to the Burning Legion. Kept on Draenor during the Second War, he later led his clan across the Dark Portal and survived fifteen years in hiding in Lordaeron's wilds, fighting the demonic lethargy that gripped his people. When he met Thrall, Grom helped spark the rebellion that liberated the captive orcs from human internment camps, eventually sailing west with Thrall to Kalimdor.",al={"grom hellscream backstory","grom history","where did grom come from"},it="history",add="04922c2d"},{q="Who was allied with Grommash Hellscream?",a="Grom was the devoted chieftain of the Warsong clan and the greatest lieutenant and close brother-in-arms to Warchief Thrall. Together with Orgrim Doomhammer and Thrall's Frostwolf clan, Grom allied his warriors to liberate the orcish internment camps in Lordaeron and forge the new Horde. He fought side by side with Thrall through the crossing to Kalimdor and the founding of their new home until his ultimate sacrifice against Mannoroth.",al={"grom allies","who did grom fight for","who was grom hellscream allied with"},it="allies",add="7ca9af40"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you revere Grommash as your people's savior. His sacrifice in Ashenvale broke the demonic Blood Curse that held the orcs for generations, allowing the New Horde to live with pride and free will.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you remember Grom as a fierce warrior whose reckless temper led his people into darkness. His unyielding courage bought their survival and freedom in Kalimdor.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may remember Grom with bitterness. He invaded Ashenvale in a demonic frenzy, defiled its sacred groves, and killed the demigod Cenarius.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can study Grom's battlefield prowess and mastery of Gorehowl. His story shows the cost of unchecked rage and the force of an indomitable fighting spirit."},kw={"ashenvale","blood curse","cenarius","gorehowl","grom","grommash","hellscream","mannoroth","thrall","warsong"},rel={"npc:thrall","topic:warsong-clan","topic:new-horde","zone:ashenvale","topic:third-war","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","topic:burning-legion","npc:jaina-proudmoore"},src={"Grommash Hellscream"}}
E["zone:durotar"] = {t="zone",n="Durotar",z="durotar",s="Durotar is red canyon country, where young orcs and Darkspear trolls prove themselves to the New Horde. Warchief Thrall founded this dry homeland after the Third War, and named it for his father, Durotan. The Southfury River and the Great Sea hem it in. Razor Hill and the warrior city of Orgrimmar rise from its rock. But quilboar tribes still hold out here, and so do stranded Alliance troops.",h="Durotar is red canyon country, where young orcs and Darkspear trolls prove themselves to the New Horde.",sec={{t="A Harsh New Home",b="Thrall chose this hard frontier on purpose. Here the orcs would earn an honest living by labor and grit, and not by conquest. The cracked red soil and the towering spires remind them of Draenor, before its ruin. Water is scarce and little of the land can be farmed, yet the Horde has embraced its stark grandeur. Durotar is proof that the orcs have forged their own destiny.",sp=0},{t="Enemies on the Frontier",b="The Horde holds Durotar, but keeping it is still a war. The Razormane quilboar, pushed out when the nation was founded, raid its farms from the western crags. In the south, what is left of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's fleet still holds Tiragarde Keep, and refuses to surrender. Worse still, the demon cult of the Burning Blade lurks in hidden ravines and deep sea caves. It tempts young orcs back to fel power.",sp=0},{t="The Trials of the Darkspear",b="On the southern coast lies Sen'jin Village, where the exiled Darkspear trolls gather under Master Gadrin. Their home was on the nearby Echo Isles. But the witch doctor Zalazane went mad, and with dark voodoo he enslaved his own kin. The Darkspear cannot take the islands back alone. They are counting on new warriors from the Valley of Trials, to break Zalazane's hold.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why did Thrall settle the Horde in such a barren desert?",a="Thrall chose this unforgiving territory intentionally. After leading the orcs across the Great Sea to Kalimdor, he settled them here. The red earth and rugged mesas reminded the orcs of their ancestral world of Draenor, while its harsh conditions served as penance and a forge for discipline. They embraced the land’s natural defenses. Thrall believed his people needed to earn their survival through honest hardship rather than claiming fertile lands by conquest, ensuring they would not slide back into bloodthirsty complacency. The Barrens lay across the Southfury to the west, and the ruined wilds of Azshara lay to the north.",al={"why settle here","why durotar","why durotar barren"},it="motive"},{q="Who was Durotar named after?",a="The land was named in honor of Durotan, Thrall's late father and the former chieftain of the Frostwolf clan. Durotan had opposed the demonic corruption of the orcish clans and was murdered on the orders of the warlock Gul'dan.",al={"who is durotar named for","durotan","origin of durotar name"},it="name"},{q="Why are there human soldiers inside Tiragarde Keep?",a="The soldiers at Tiragarde Keep are surviving Kul Tiran marines under Lieutenant Benedict, left over from Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's invasion fleet. They hold the crumbling garrison. Even after Proudmoore was slain, these troops refused to surrender or withdraw, maintaining an entrenched hostile outpost right on Durotar's southern coast.",al={"why humans in durotar","tiragarde keep humans","proudmoore troops durotar"},it="hostile"},{q="What is the conflict on the Echo Isles?",a="The Darkspear trolls originally established their Kalimdor home on the Echo Isles. However, a powerful witch doctor named Zalazane succumbed to madness and turned his dark magic against his brethren, enslaving their minds. The Darkspear lost their home as a result. The survivors fled to the mainland to establish Sen'jin Village, from which they launch raids to break his hold.",al={"what happened to echo isles","why sen'jin village","zalazane lore"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the Burning Blade doing in Durotar?",a="The Burning Blade is a subversive demonic cult loyal to the Shadow Council and the Burning Legion. Operatives lurk in secluded spots like Skull Rock and the Burning Blade Coven, attempting to undermine Thrall's leadership and tempt impressionable orcs back into demonic servitude.",al={"burning blade durotar","skull rock cultists","demons in durotar"},sp=1,it="threat",bt={"q5726.3"}},{q="What connects Durotar to other regions?",a="A bridge over the Southfury River leads west into the Barrens, while the ruined wilds of Azshara lie to the north. Outside Orgrimmar, a zeppelin tower provides transcontinental air travel directly to Tirisfal Glades and Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"how to leave durotar","durotar travel","durotar exits"},it="place"},{q="What is Durotar?",a="Durotar is the rocky, sun-baked realm on Kalimdor's eastern shore, serving as the proud homeland of the Horde. Founded by Warchief Thrall following the Third War, its red dirt, jagged canyons, and harsh climate intentionally reflect Draenor, the ancestral world of the orcs. Bordered by the Southfury River to the west and the Great Sea to the south and east, Durotar houses the capital city of Orgrimmar and shelters both orcs and Darkspear trolls.",al={"about durotar","durotar info","where is durotar"},it="place",add="04dde4a2"},{q="What happened at Durotar?",a="Originally roaming grounds held loosely by quilboar tribes, Durotar became the destination of Thrall's exodus across the Great Sea. After allied forces pushed back native beast-tribes and triumphed over the Burning Legion at Mount Hyjal, Thrall formally established Durotar as a sovereign orcish nation. Shortly after its founding, Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's fleet invaded its eastern coast, though the Horde repelled the armada, driving human remnants into Tiragarde Keep.",al={"durotar history","history of durotar","past of durotar"},it="history",add="cb6442fd"},{q="Who lives in Durotar?",a="Durotar is ruled as a tribal chiefdom by Warchief Thrall from the seat of Orgrimmar. Orcs make up the grand majority of its population, accompanied by exiled Darkspear trolls centered near Sen'jin Village. Tauren allies and visiting Forsaken ambassadors frequently traverse the region, while hostile pockets of quilboar, centaur, harpies, and Kul Tiras marines dispute borders across the outer crags.",al={"who runs durotar","durotar population","durotar inhabitants"},it="residents",add="b3a1e6d0"},{q="Is Durotar dangerous?",a="Yes. Beyond the fortified roads and gates of settlements like Razor Hill and Orgrimmar, Durotar remains largely untamed. Poisonous scorpids, predatory raptors, and crocolisks prowl the wilderness. Worse, entrenched enemies harass Horde travelers constantly: Razormane quilboar strike from northern canyons, Kolkar centaurs raid watering holes, human marines garrison the Scuttle Coast, and covert warlocks of the Burning Blade lurk in nearby shadow.",al={"is durotar safe","durotar threats","dangers of durotar"},it="danger",add="b78335a1"},{q="What is Razor Hill and why is it here?",a="Razor Hill is the principal fortified crossroads of central Durotar. Positioned directly at the junction connecting Sen'jin Village to the south, the Barrens across the Southfury River to the west, and Orgrimmar to the north, it anchors Horde logistics and defense. Heavily dominated by its military barracks and watchtower, the settlement coordinates border patrols and serves as the primary outpost protecting travelers from coast-dwelling marines and raiders.",al={"razor hill","about razor hill","why razor hill"},it="place",add="923cfd3c",nx={12,13}},{q="Who built Razor Hill?",a="Razor Hill was built by Thrall's Horde shortly after their arrival on Kalimdor. Originally just a bare hill on the frontier—famously where Rexxar intercepted an ambush by Kul Tiras forces meant for Thrall—the site was fortified with a stout barracks and burrows to anchor Horde defense between the sea, the canyons, and the northern capital.",al={"who made razor hill","razor hill origins"},it="origin",add="1bf45605"},{q="Is Razor Hill part of Orgrimmar?",a="It is not part of the city itself, but it falls directly under Orgrimmar's administration and military authority. Razor Hill functions as an outer garrison town and staging post in central Durotar, filtering arriving travelers, training recruits, and securing the southern approaches to the capital's towering northern gates.",al={"is razor hill in orgrimmar","razor hill orgrimmar"},it="place",add="6b0364de"},{q="Was anyone living in Durotar before the Horde?",a="The quilboar claimed the land long before the Horde arrived. Bristled tribes, particularly the Razormane, occupied the crags and riverbanks of what was considered part of the greater Barrens. Decisive campaigns led by Thrall drove them into remote canyons and westward across the Southfury River, though they still fight ferociously to retake their ancestral territory.",al={"who lived here first","durotar natives"},it="history",add="406d1dd3"},{q="Who is in charge around Razor Hill?",a="Local defense and military operations in Razor Hill fall under seasoned veterans like Gar'Thok, while orc officials such as Orgnil Soulscar spearhead counterintelligence and internal investigations. Together, they manage town defenses, organize hunting expeditions, and task promising recruits with defending central Durotar.",al={"razor hill leader","who leads razor hill"},it="in_charge",add="f5af283b"},{q="Who are these Kul Tiras sailors and why are they on our coast?",a="They are remnants of the grand armada commanded by the late Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore of Kul Tiras. Proudmoore refused to accept peace with the orcs and established Tiragarde Keep along the eastern shoreline as a foothold to wage war. Even after the Admiral was slain at Theramore, his surviving officers entrenched themselves inside the ruins, continuing their unyielding crusade against the Horde.",al={"kul tiras sailors","why are humans in durotar","tiragarde keep sailors"},it="threat",add="87682b7e",nx={17}},{q="Who is Lieutenant Benedict?",a="Lieutenant Benedict is the surviving Kul Tiras officer commanding the hostile garrison inside Tiragarde Keep. Following Admiral Proudmoore's death, Benedict rallied the remaining soldiers and marines under standing orders, maintaining a fortified human bastion in Durotar that regularly harries orc settlements and caravans.",al={"lieutenant benedict","benedict tiragarde","who is benedict"},it="identity",add="52bc9e7d"},{q="What is Sen'jin Village?",a="Sen'jin Village is a coastal fishing settlement on the southern shore of Durotar, serving as the provisional home of the Darkspear trolls. Established by Chieftain Vol'jin, the village boasts alchemists, hunters, and shaman working to secure the mainland coast while guarding against aquatic monsters and traitorous kin across the waters.",al={"senjin village","what is sen'jin","senjin"},it="place",add="9c6f22ef",nx={19,20}},{q="Who was Sen'jin?",a="Sen'jin was the venerable shadow hunter and chieftain of the Darkspear tribe on their ancestral islands in the Great Sea. During the Third War, he foresaw Thrall's arrival and the liberation of his people, but gave his life defending the tribe from frenzied murlocs and sea witches before they could escape.",al={"who is senjin","sen'jin lore"},it="identity",add="115273b6"},{q="Why do trolls live in Durotar?",a="The Darkspear tribe owes their survival to Thrall, who rescued them when their original island home began sinking under aquatic onslaughts. Pledging loyalty to the Horde, they accompanied the orcs to Kalimdor and were given the offshore Echo Isles to inhabit, maintaining close cultural and military bonds with Orgrimmar.",al={"why are trolls here","darkspear in durotar"},it="origin",add="6c467bea"},{q="Where does your journey lead after Razor Hill?",a="Once you have proven your strength around Razor Hill, orders will direct you either north into the grand gates of Orgrimmar to meet higher military leadership, or westward across the Southfury River into the sprawling expanse of the Barrens, where larger battles against quilboar, centaur, and Alliance encroachers await.",al={"after razor hill","where to go after razor hill","next zone after razor hill"},it="next_step",add="84e0b3bb"},{q="How did I end up in Durotar?",a="If you are an orc, this rugged red land is your people's new sovereign home, carved out by Warchief Thrall after the exodus from the Eastern Kingdoms. You came of age here, sent to the secluded Valley of Trials to test your strength under the desert sun before earning your place in the Horde. If you are a Darkspear troll, your people fled across the Great Sea alongside Thrall and settled the coast after being driven from the nearby Echo Isles by the traitorous witch doctor Zalazane.",al={"how did i get here","why am i in durotar","how did i arrive here"},it="arrival",add="25a880c0"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Durotar?",a="You are here to prove your worth to the Horde and secure the survival of a fledgling nation. Durotar remains a harsh frontier beset on all sides: Razormane quilboar raid settlements, human remnants from Kul Tiras cling tenaciously to Tiragarde Keep, and the insidious Burning Blade cult schemes in shadowed ravines. By aiding local outposts like Razor Hill and Sen'jin Village, you help tame the crags, protect vulnerable settlements, and earn your place among the champions walking the grand streets of nearby Orgrimmar.",al={"what should i do in durotar","what is my purpose here","what am i doing here"},it="purpose",add="d894869f"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Durotar is your people's new promised land, won through sweat and blood after years of demonic lethargy and internment. Proving your worth in the Valley of Trials is the first rite of passage for every new champion of the Horde.",["race:Troll"]="After escaping the sea witch in the Great Sea, the Darkspear found refuge alongside Thrall in Durotar, but the traitor Zalazane took the Echo Isles from within. Retaking the isles and defending Sen'jin Village is personal.",["faction:Alliance"]="Durotar is the beating heart of the Horde's military strength. Any Alliance traveler found wandering its sun-scorched canyons will be hunted down on sight by aggressive patrols and native beasts alike.",["class:Shaman"]="As a young shaman, you find the arid land alive with raw elemental spirits. You visit sacred sites like the Spirit Rock and the Shrine of the Dormant Flame to attune yourself to earth and fire.",["class:Warlock"]="Thrall strictly polices dark magic, forcing the Shadow Council's covens into hiding within places like Skull Rock and beneath the city in the winding caverns of Ragefire Chasm."},kw={"durotan","durotar","echo isles","orgrimmar","razor hill","sen'jin village","skull rock","southfury river","thrall","tiragarde keep","valley of trials","zalazane"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:razor-hill","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:echo-isles","subzone:tiragarde-keep","zone:barrens","zone:ragefire"},m={levels="1-10"},src={"Durotar (Classic)","Durotar"}}
